], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 34, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.069, 0.488, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.264, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Bard Spells"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.069, 0.488, 0.202], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Special School</td></tr><tr><td>Antipathy/Sympathy</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Befuddlement</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Dominate Monster</td><td>C Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Glibness</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Mind Blank</td><td>Abjuration</td></tr><tr><td>Power Word Stun</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.104, 0.235, 0.488, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.217, 0.264, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Bard Spells"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.104, 0.235, 0.488, 0.349], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>School Special</td></tr><tr><td>Foresight</td><td>Divination</td></tr><tr><td>Power Word Heal</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Power Word Kill</td><td>Enchantment</td></tr><tr><td>Prismatic Wall</td><td>Abjuration</td></tr><tr><td>True Polymorph</td><td>C Transmutation</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.359, 0.261, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bard Subclass:"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.377, 0.272, 0.395], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "College of Lore"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.4, 0.388, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plumb the Depths of Magical Knowledge"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.42, 0.49, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bards of the College of Lore collect spells and secrets from diverse sources, such as scholarly tomes, mystical rites, and peasant tales. The college’s members gather in libraries and universities to share their lore with one another. They also meet at festi vals or affairs of state, where they can expose corruption, unravel lies, and poke fun at self-important figures of authority."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.551, 0.357, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3: Bonus Proficiencies"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.568, 0.49, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain proficiency with three skills of your choice."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.739, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3: Cutting Words"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.911, 0.223], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You learn to use your wit to supernaturally distract, confuse, and otherwise sap the confidence and competence of others. When a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself makes a damage roll or succeeds on an ability check or attack roll, you can take a Reaction to expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration; roll your Bardic Inspiration die, and subtract the number rolled from the creature’s roll, reducing the damage or potentially turning the success into a failure."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.23, 0.781, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6: Magical Discoveries"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.247, 0.91, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You learn two spells of your choice. These spells can come from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list or any combination thereof (see a class’s section for its spell list). A spell you choose must be a cantrip or a spell for which you have spell slots, as shown in the Bard Features table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.339, 0.908, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You always have the chosen spells prepared, and whenever you gain a Bard level, you can replace one of the spells with another spell that meets these requirements."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.408, 0.732, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 14: Peerless Skill"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.426, 0.902, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make an ability check or attack roll and fail, you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration; roll the Bardic Inspiration die, and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning a failure into a success. On a failure, the Bardic Inspiration isn’t expended."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.033, 0.952, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "35"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 35, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.192, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cleric"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.098, 0.488, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.082, 0.258, 0.098], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Core Cleric Traits"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.098, 0.488, 0.343], "content": "<table><tr><td>Primary Ability</td><td>Wisdom</td></tr><tr><td>Hit Point Die</td><td>D8 per Cleric level</td></tr><tr><td>Saving Throw Proficiencies</td><td>Wisdom and Charisma</td></tr><tr><td>Skill Proficiencies</td><td>Choose 2: History, Insight, Medicine, Persuasion, or Religion</td></tr><tr><td>Weapon Proficiencies Simple weapons</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Armor Training</td><td>Light and Medium armor and Shields</td></tr><tr><td>Starting Equipment</td><td>Choose A or B: (A) Chain Shirt, Shield, Mace, Holy Symbol, Priest&#x27;s Pack, and 7 GP; or (B) 110 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.353, 0.33, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Becoming a Cleric …"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.378, 0.315, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Level 1 Character"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.395, 0.473, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Gain all the traits in the Core Cleric Traits table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.411, 0.481, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Gain the Cleric’s level 1 features, which are listed in the Cleric Features table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.761, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Multiclass Character"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.904, 0.114], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Gain the following traits from the Core Cleric Traits table: Hit Point Die and training with Light and Medium armor and Shields."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.524, 0.114, 0.904, 0.177], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Gain the Cleric’s level 1 features, which are listed in the Cleric Features table. See the multiclassing rules in “Character Creation” to determine your available spell slots."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.183, 0.754, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cleric Class Features"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.206, 0.886, 0.254], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Cleric, you gain the following class features when you reach the specified Cleric levels. These features are listed in the Cleric Features table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.261, 0.71, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1: Spellcasting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.279, 0.901, 0.356], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have learned to cast spells through prayer and meditation. See “Spells” for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Cleric spells, which appear on the Cleric spell list later in the class’s description."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.356, 0.902, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrips.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know three cantrips of your choice from the Cleric spell list. Guidance, Sacred Flame, and Thaumaturgy are recommended."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.401, 0.901, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you gain a Cleric level, you can replace one of your cantrips with another cantrip of your choice from the Cleric spell list."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.082, 0.48, 0.215, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cleric Features"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.083, 0.501, 0.935, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.083, 0.501, 0.935, 0.92], "content": "<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Level</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Proficiency Bonus</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Class Features</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Channel Divinity</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Cantrips</td><td rowspan=\"2\">Prepared Spells</td><td rowspan=\"2\"></td><td colspan=\"7\">-Spell Slots per Spell Level-</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>2 3 4 5 6 7 8</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>9</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>+2</td><td>Spellcasting, Divine Order</td><td></td><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>+2</td><