"Wizard Subclass: Evoker"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.633, 0.35, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create Explosive Elemental Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.653, 0.489, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your studies focus on magic that creates powerful elemental effects such as bitter cold, searing flame, rolling thunder, crackling lightning, and burning acid. Some Evokers find employment in military forces, serving as artillery to blast armies from afar. Others use their power to protect others, while some seek their own gain."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.758, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3: Evocation Savant"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.912, 0.115], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose two Wizard spells from the Evocation school, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.522, 0.115, 0.91, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one Wizard spell from the Evocation school to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.523, 0.199, 0.74, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3: Potent Cantrip"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.217, 0.912, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your damaging cantrips affect even creatures that avoid the brunt of the effect. When you cast a cantrip at a creature and you miss with the attack roll or the target succeeds on a saving throw against the cantrip, the target takes half the cantrip’s damage (if any) but suffers no additional effect from the cantrip."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.332, 0.718, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6: Sculpt Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.349, 0.908, 0.474], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can create pockets of relative safety within the effects of your evocations. When you cast an Evocation spell that affects other creatures that you can see, you can choose a number of them equal to 1 plus the spell’s level. The chosen creatures automatically succeed on their saving throws against the spell, and they take no damage if they would normally take half damage on a successful save."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.48, 0.816, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 10: Empowered Evocation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.498, 0.9, 0.545], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you cast a Wizard spell from the Evocation school, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of that spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.552, 0.73, 0.568], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 14: Overchannel"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.57, 0.911, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can increase the power of your spells. When you cast a Wizard spell with a spell slot of levels 1–5 that deals damage, you can deal maximum damage with that spell on the turn you cast it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.631, 0.908, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first time you do so, you suffer no adverse effect. If you use this feature again before you finish a Long Rest, you take 2d12 Necrotic damage for each level of the spell slot immediately after you cast it. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.708, 0.909, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each time you use this feature again before finishing a Long Rest, the Necrotic damage per spell level increases by 1d12."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "82"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 82, "blocks": [{"type": "doc_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.113, 0.05, 0.479, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Character Origins"}], "level": 1}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.095, 0.435, 0.118], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Character Backgrounds"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.488, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your character’s background is a collection of characteristics that represent the place and occupation that were most formative before your character embarked on a life of adventure."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.189, 0.343, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parts of a Background"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.212, 0.423, 0.23], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A background includes the following parts."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.236, 0.235, 0.253], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.253, 0.481, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A background lists three of your character’s ability scores. Increase one by 2 and another one by 1, or increase all three by 1. None of these increases can raise a score above 20."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.323, 0.15, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.34, 0.479, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A background gives your character a specified Origin feat (described in “Feats”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.379, 0.265, 0.395], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skill Proficiencies"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.397, 0.47, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A background gives your character proficiency in two specified skills."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.436, 0.254, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tool Proficiency"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.453, 0.487, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each background gives a character proficiency with one tool—either a specific tool or one chosen from the Artisan’s Tools category. Tools are detailed in “Equipment.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.523, 0.207, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.54, 0.487, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each background offers a choice between a package of equipment and 50 GP."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.578, 0.374, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Background Descriptions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.603, 0.179, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Acolyte"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.623, 0.445, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Feat:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Magic Initiate (Cleric) (see “Feats”) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Skill Proficiencies:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Insight and Religion "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tool Proficiency:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Calligrapher’s Supplies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.689, 0.488, 0.738], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose A or B: (A) Calligrapher’s Supplies, Book (prayers), Holy Symbol, Parchment (10 sheets), Robe, 8 GP; or (B) 50 GP"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.745, 0.187, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Criminal"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.101, 0.764, 0.474, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Feat:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Alert (see “Feats”)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.797, 0.437, 0.83], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skill Proficiencies:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Sleight of Hand and Stealth "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tool Proficiency:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Thieves’ Tools"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.83, 0.461, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose A or B: (A) 2 Daggers, Thieves Tools, Crowbar, 2 Pouches, Traveler’s Clothes, 16 GP; or (B) 50 GP"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.573, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sage"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.07, 0.887, 0.087], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.086, 0.828, 0.103], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feat:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Magic Initiate (Wizard) (see “Feats”)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.103, 0.81, 0.119], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skill Proficiencies:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Arcana and History"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.119, 0.818, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tool Proficiency:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Calligrapher’s Supplies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.136, 0.885, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose A or B: (A) Quarterstaff, Calligrapher’s Supplies, Book (history), Parchment (8 sheets), Robe, 8 GP; or (B) 50 GP"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.192, 0.596, 0.209], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Soldier"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.211, 0.878, 0.244], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Strength, Dexterity, Constitution "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Feat:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Savage Attacker (see “Feats”)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.244, 0.85, 0.261], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skill Proficiencies:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Athletics and Intimidation"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.261, 0.895, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tool Proficiency:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose one kind of Gaming Set (see “Equipment”)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.295, 0.895, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose A or B: (A) Spear, Shortbow, 20 Arrows, Gaming Set (same as above), Healer’s Kit, Quiver, Traveler’s Clothes, 14 GP; or (B) 50 GP"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.354, 0.782, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Character Species"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.379, 0.912, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you choose your character’s species, you determine whether your character is a human or a member of a fantastical species, such as dragonborn or gnome."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.44, 0.908, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The peoples of the multiverse hail from different worlds and include many kinds of sapient life forms. A player character’s species is the set of game traits that an adventurer gains from being one of those life forms."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.517, 0.893, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some species can trace their origin to a single world, plane of existence, or god, while other species first appeared in multiple realms at once. Whatever a species’ genesis, its members have spread across the multiverse and contribute to many different cultures."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.609, 0.9, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Members of most species live for about 80 years, with exceptions noted in the text about the species in “Character Origins.” Regardless of life span, members of all species reach physical maturity at about the same age. Your character can be any age "}, {"type": "text", "content": "that isn’t beyond their species’ normal life span.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.524, 0.709, 0.718, 0.728], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parts of a Species"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.523, 0.731, 0.81, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A species includes the following parts."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.524, 0.755, 0.662, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.521, 0.773, 0.9, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A character’s species determines the character’s creature type, which is described in “Rules Glossary.” Every species in “Character Origins” is Humanoid; playable non-Humanoid species appear in other books."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.523, 0.858, 0.568, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.522, 0.875, 0.912, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your character’s species determines the character’s size. Individuals within a species cover a wide range of heights, and some species include such diversity"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.033, 0.952, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "83"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 83, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.48, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "of size that you can choose whether your character is Small or Medium."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.164, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.107, 0.485, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your character’s species determines the character’s Speed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.145, 0.23, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.163, 0.49, 0.256], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each species gives a character special traits— unique characteristics based on the species’ physiology or magical nature. When you choose a species, your character gets all the special traits listed for it. Some traits involve making a choice from a handful of options."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.327, 0.282], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Species Descriptions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.287, 0.22, 0.305], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragonborn", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.306, 0.301, 0.322], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.323, 0.346, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 5–7 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.339, 0.215, 0.355], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.362, 0.451, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Dragonborn, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.377, 0.482, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Draconic Ancestry.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your lineage stems from a dragon progenitor. Choose the kind of dragon from the Draconic Ancestors table. Your choice affects your Breath Weapon and Damage Resistance traits as well as your appearance."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.105, 0.486, 0.284, 0.599], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.467, 0.273, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Draconic Ancestors"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.105, 0.486, 0.284, 0.599], "content": "<table><tr><td>Dragon</td><td>Damage Type</td></tr><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td></tr><tr><td>Copper Acid</td><td></td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.31, 0.486, 0.488, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.31, 0.486, 0.488, 0.598], "content": "<table><tr><td>Dragon</td><td>Damage Type</td></tr><tr><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.613, 0.49, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Breath Weapon.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you take the Attack action on your turn, you can replace one of your attacks with an exhalation of magical energy in either a 15-foot Cone or a 30-foot Line that is 5 feet wide (choose the shape each time). Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Constitution modifier and Proficiency Bonus). On a failed save, a creature takes 1d10 damage of the type determined by your Draconic Ancestry trait. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach character levels 5 (2d10), 11 (3d10), and 17 (4d10)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.813, 0.486, 0.859], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use this Breath Weapon a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.859, 0.481, 0.905], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to the damage type determined by your Draconic Ancestry trait."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.9, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.913, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Draconic Flight.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you reach character level 5, you can channel draconic magic to give yourself temporary flight. As a Bonus Action, you sprout spectral wings on your back that last for 10 minutes or until you retract the wings (no action required) or have the Incapacitated condition. During that time, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. Your wings appear to be made of the same energy as your Breath Weapon. Once you use this trait, you can’t use it again until you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.242, 0.59, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarf"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.261, 0.722, 0.277], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.278, 0.769, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 4–5 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.295, 0.636, 0.31], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.316, 0.829, 0.332], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Dwarf, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.332, 0.9, 0.362], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 120 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.363, 0.895, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarven Resilience.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to Poison damage. You also have Advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the Poisoned condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.424, 0.91, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarven Toughness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Hit Point maximum increases by 1, and it increases by 1 again whenever you gain a level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.47, 0.911, 0.546], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stonecunning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Bonus Action, you gain Tremorsense with a range of 60 feet for 10 minutes. You must be on a stone surface or touching a stone surface to use this Tremorsense. The stone can be natural or worked."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.546, 0.902, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use this Bonus Action a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.6, 0.555, 0.616], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elf"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.619, 0.722, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.635, 0.769, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 5–6 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.652, 0.636, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.674, 0.812, 0.69], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As an Elf, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.691, 0.9, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.721, 0.901, 0.782], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elven Lineage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are part of a lineage that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose a lineage from the Elven Lineages table. You gain the level 1 benefit of that lineage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.782, 0.905, 0.891], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you reach character levels 3 and 5, you learn a higher-level spell, as shown on the table. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.058, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "84"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 84, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.23, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elven Lineages"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.068, 0.91, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.068, 0.91, 0.208], "content": "<table><tr><td>Lineage</td><td>Level I</td><td>Level 3</td><td>Level 5</td></tr><tr><td>Drow</td><td>The range of your Darkvision increases to I20 feet. You also know the Dancing Lights cantrip.</td><td>Faerie Fire</td><td>Darkness</td></tr><tr><td>High Elf</td><td>You know the Prestidigitation cantrip. Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can replace that cantrip with a different cantrip from the Wizard spell list.</td><td>Detect Magic</td><td>Misty Step</td></tr><tr><td>Wood Elf</td><td>Your Speed increases to 35 feet. You also know the Druidcraft cantrip.</td><td>Longstrider</td><td>Pass without Trace</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.229, 0.482, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the lineage)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.275, 0.455, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fey Ancestry.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the Charmed condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.32, 0.479, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Keen Senses.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have proficiency in the Insight, Perception, or Survival skill."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.352, 0.486, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You don’t need to sleep, and magic can’t put you to sleep. You can finish a Long Rest in 4 hours if you spend those hours in a trancelike meditation, during which you retain consciousness."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.421, 0.176, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gnome"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.44, 0.301, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.456, 0.328, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Small (about 3–4 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.473, 0.214, 0.489], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.495, 0.412, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Gnome, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.51, 0.48, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.541, 0.485, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gnomish Cunning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.572, 0.485, 0.665], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gnomish Lineage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are part of a lineage that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose one of the following options; whichever one you choose, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the lineage):"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.67, 0.486, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Forest Gnome.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know the Minor Illusion cantrip. You also always have the Speak with Animals spell prepared. You can cast it without a spell slot a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also use any spell slots you have to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.777, 0.487, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rock Gnome.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know the Mending and Prestidigitation cantrips. In addition, you can spend 10 minutes casting Prestidigitation to create a Tiny clockwork device (AC 5, 1 HP), such as a toy, fire starter, or music box. When you create the device, you determine its function by choosing one effect from Prestidigitation; the device produces that"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.535, 0.228, 0.912, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "effect whenever you or another creature takes a Bonus Action to activate it with a touch. If the chosen effect has options within it, you choose one of those options for the device when you create it. For example, if you choose the spell’s ignite-extinguish effect, you determine whether the device ignites or extinguishes fire; the device doesn’t do both. You can have three such devices in existence at a time, and each falls apart 8 hours after its creation or when you dismantle it with a touch as a Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.405, 0.598, 0.422], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goliath"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.424, 0.722, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.44, 0.768, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 7–8 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.457, 0.636, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 35 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.479, 0.836, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Goliath, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.495, 0.912, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant Ancestry.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are descended from Giants. Choose one of the following benefits—a supernatural boon from your ancestry; you can use the chosen benefit a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.593, 0.911, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloud’s Jaunt (Cloud Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Bonus Action, you magically teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.525, 0.64, 0.902, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire’s Burn (Fire Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a target with an attack roll and deal damage to it, you can also deal 1d10 Fire damage to that target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.686, 0.901, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Frost’s Chill (Frost Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a target with an attack roll and deal damage to it, you can also deal 1d6 Cold damage to that target and reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.762, 0.892, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hill’s Tumble (Hill Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a Large or smaller creature with an attack roll and deal damage to it, you can give that target the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.823, 0.907, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stone’s Endurance (Stone Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you take damage, you can take a Reaction to roll 1d12. Add your Constitution modifier to the number rolled and reduce the damage by that total."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "85"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 85, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Storm’s Thunder (Storm Giant).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you take damage from a creature within 60 feet of you, you can take a Reaction to deal 1d8 Thunder damage to that creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.118, 0.488, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Form.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Starting at character level 5, you can change your size to Large as a Bonus Action if you’re in a big enough space. This transformation lasts for 10 minutes or until you end it (no action required). For that duration, you have Advantage on Strength checks, and your Speed increases by 10 feet. Once you use this trait, you can’t use it again until you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.241, 0.483, 0.304], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Powerful Build.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on any ability check you make to end the Grappled condition. You also count as one size larger when determining your carrying capacity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.31, 0.178, 0.328], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Halfling"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.33, 0.3, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.346, 0.326, 0.361], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Small (about 2–3 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.362, 0.214, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.384, 0.421, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Halfling, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.4, 0.482, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brave.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the Frightened condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.431, 0.478, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Halfling Nimbleness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can move through the space of any creature that is a size larger than you, but you can’t stop in the same space."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.477, 0.476, 0.522], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Luck.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, you can reroll the die, and you must use the new roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.523, 0.487, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Naturally Stealthy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take the Hide action even when you are obscured only by a creature that is at least one size larger than you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.577, 0.175, 0.593], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Human"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.595, 0.3, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.611, 0.489, 0.661], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 4–7 feet tall) or Small (about 2–4 feet tall), chosen when you select this species "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.668, 0.415, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Human, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.683, 0.47, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resourceful.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain Heroic Inspiration whenever you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.714, 0.471, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skillful.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.744, 0.47, 0.776], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Versatile.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain an Origin feat of your choice (see “Feats”). Skilled is recommended."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.566, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Orc"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.07, 0.722, 0.086], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.086, 0.768, 0.103], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 6–7 feet tall)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.103, 0.636, 0.119], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.125, 0.818, 0.14], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As an Orc, you have these special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.141, 0.906, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adrenaline Rush.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action. When you do so, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.202, 0.898, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use this trait a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Short or Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.248, 0.901, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 120 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.278, 0.911, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Relentless Endurance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead. Once you use this trait, you can’t do so again until you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.348, 0.598, 0.365], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tiefling"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.366, 0.722, 0.382], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Humanoid"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.383, 0.911, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Medium (about 4–7 feet tall) or Small (about 3–4 feet tall), chosen when you select this species "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.438, 0.898, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Tiefling, you have the following special traits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.454, 0.901, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.485, 0.907, 0.546], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fiendish Legacy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are the recipient of a legacy that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose a legacy from the Fiendish Legacies table. You gain the level 1 benefit of the chosen legacy."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.546, 0.905, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you reach character levels 3 and 5, you learn a higher-level spell, as shown on the table. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.653, 0.902, 0.7], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the legacy)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.7, 0.898, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Otherworldly Presence.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know the Thaumaturgy cantrip. When you cast it with this trait, the spell uses the same spellcasting ability you use for your Fiendish Legacy trait."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.104, 0.807, 0.909, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.79, 0.252, 0.806], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fiendish Legacies"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.104, 0.807, 0.909, 0.931], "content": "<table><tr><td>Legacy</td><td>Level I</td><td>Level 3</td><td>Level 5</td></tr><tr><td>Abyssal</td><td>You have Resistance to Poison damage. You also know the Poison Spray cantrip.</td><td>Ray of Sickness</td><td>Hold Person</td></tr><tr><td>Chthonic</td><td>You have Resistance to Necrotic damage. You also know the Chill Touch cantrip.</td><td>False Life</td><td>Ray of Enfeeblement</td></tr><tr><td>Infernal</td><td>You have Resistance to Fire damage. You also know the Fire Bolt cantrip.</td><td>Hellish Rebuke</td><td>Darkness</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "86"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 86, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.243, 0.051, 0.352, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feats"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.095, 0.352, 0.117], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feat Descriptions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.473, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The feats that follow are organized by category— Origin, General, Fighting Style, or Epic Boon—and alphabetized in each category."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.174, 0.263, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parts of a Feat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.197, 0.464, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The description of a feat contains the following parts, which are presented after the feat’s name."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.229, 0.486, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Category.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A feat is a member of a category, which is noted in the feat. If you’re instructed to choose a feat from a specific category, such as the Origin category, that category must appear under the feat’s name. If you’re instructed to choose a feat and no category is specified, you can choose from any category."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.336, 0.475, 0.412], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prerequisite.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " To take a feat, you must meet any prerequisite in its description unless a feature allows you to take the feat without the prerequisite. If a prerequisite includes a class, you must have at least 1 level in that class to take the feat."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.412, 0.475, 0.458], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Benefit.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The benefits of a feat are detailed after any prerequisites are listed. If you have a feat, you gain its benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.458, 0.479, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Repeatable.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A feat can be taken only once unless its description states otherwise in a “Repeatable” subsection."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.511, 0.239, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Origin Feats"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.537, 0.158, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alert", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.554, 0.189, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Origin Feat"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.574, 0.338, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.589, 0.469, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative Proficiency.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you roll Initiative, you can add your Proficiency Bonus to the roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.621, 0.487, 0.698], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative Swap.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Immediately after you roll Initiative, you can swap your Initiative with the Initiative of one willing ally in the same combat. You can’t make this swap if you or the ally has the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.705, 0.229, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Initiate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.723, 0.19, 0.738], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Origin Feat"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.742, 0.338, 0.757], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.758, 0.487, 0.834], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Two Cantrips.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You learn two cantrips of your choice from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this feat’s spells (choose when you select this feat)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.1, 0.834, 0.485, 0.928], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Spell.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose a level 1 spell from the same list you selected for this feat’s cantrips. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.91, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Change.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whenever you gain a new level, you can replace one of the spells you chose for this feat with a different spell of the same level from the chosen spell list."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.112, 0.904, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Repeatable.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take this feat more than once, but you must choose a different spell list each time."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.166, 0.677, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Savage Attacker"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.183, 0.612, 0.199], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Origin Feat"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.203, 0.887, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You’ve trained to deal particularly damaging strikes. Once per turn when you hit a target with a weapon, you can roll the weapon’s damage dice twice and use either roll against the target."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.272, 0.59, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skilled"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.29, 0.61, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Origin Feat"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.309, 0.884, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain proficiency in any combination of three skills or tools of your choice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.341, 0.874, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Repeatable.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take this feat more than once."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.378, 0.678, 0.397], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "General Feats"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.404, 0.775, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Improvement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.422, 0.785, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "General Feat (Prerequisite: Level 4+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.441, 0.905, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. This feat can’t increase an ability score above 20."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.488, 0.874, 0.519], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Repeatable.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take this feat more than once."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.526, 0.613, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grappler"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.543, 0.868, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "General Feat (Prerequisite: Level 4+, Strength or Dexterity 13+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.578, 0.76, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.594, 0.906, 0.625], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 20."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.625, 0.908, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Punch and Grab.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a creature with an Unarmed Strike as part of the Attack action on your turn, you can use both the Damage and the Grapple option. You can use this benefit only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.523, 0.686, 0.907, 0.717], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Advantage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on attack rolls against a creature Grappled by you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.522, 0.717, 0.912, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fast Wrestler.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You don’t have to spend extra movement to move a creature Grappled by you if the creature is your size or smaller."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.524, 0.77, 0.736, 0.79], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting Style Feats"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.524, 0.796, 0.606, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Archery", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.523, 0.812, 0.862, 0.845], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting Style Feat (Prerequisite: Fighting Style Feature)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.522, 0.848, 0.891, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with Ranged weapons."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.033, 0.952, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "87"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 87, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.182, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Defense"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.068, 0.441, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting Style Feat (Prerequisite: Fighting Style Feature)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.473, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you’re wearing Light, Medium, or Heavy armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.143, 0.319, 0.16], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Great Weapon Fighting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.16, 0.44, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting Style Feat (Prerequisite: Fighting Style Feature)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.195, 0.486, 0.274], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you roll damage for an attack you make with a Melee weapon that you are holding with two hands, you can treat any 1 or 2 on a damage die as a 3. The weapon must have the Two-Handed or Versatile property to gain this benefit."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.28, 0.307, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Two-Weapon Fighting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.297, 0.44, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting Style Feat (Prerequisite: Fighting Style Feature)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.333, 0.484, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make an extra attack as a result of using a weapon that has the Light property, you can add your ability modifier to the damage of that attack if you aren’t already adding it to the damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.402, 0.278, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feats"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.427, 0.338, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Combat Prowess"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.444, 0.386, 0.46], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.464, 0.338, 0.48], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.48, 0.482, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.51, 0.48, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Peerless Aim.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you miss with an attack roll, you can hit instead. Once you use this benefit, you can’t use it again until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.564, 0.358, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Dimensional Travel"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.582, 0.386, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.601, 0.338, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.617, 0.482, 0.647], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.648, 0.481, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blink Steps.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Immediately after you take the Attack action or the Magic action, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.103, 0.702, 0.224, 0.718], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Fate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.719, 0.386, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.739, 0.338, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.102, 0.755, 0.482, 0.785], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.101, 0.786, 0.484, 0.833], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Improve Fate.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you or another creature within 60 feet of you succeeds on or fails a D20 Test, you can roll 2d4 and apply the total rolled as a"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "bonus or penalty to the d20 roll. Once you use this benefit, you can’t use it again until you roll Initiative or finish a Short or Long Rest."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.105, 0.778, 0.12], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Irresistible Offense"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.122, 0.808, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.141, 0.761, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.157, 0.905, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase your Strength or Dexterity score by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.189, 0.895, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Overcome Defenses.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage you deal always ignores Resistance."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.234, 0.91, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Overwhelming Strike.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you roll a 20 on the d20 for an attack roll, you can deal extra damage to the target equal to the ability score increased by this feat. The extra damage’s type is the same as the attack’s type."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.318, 0.709, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Spell Recall"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.336, 0.894, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+, Spellcasting Feature)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.523, 0.371, 0.76, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.387, 0.91, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma score by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.433, 0.911, 0.48], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Free Casting.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whenever you cast a spell with a level 1–4 spell slot, roll 1d4. If the number you roll is the same as the slot’s level, the slot isn’t expended."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.486, 0.747, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of the Night Spirit"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.504, 0.807, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.524, 0.524, 0.76, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.54, 0.903, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.523, 0.571, 0.903, 0.646], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Merge with Shadows.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While within Dim Light or Darkness, you can give yourself the Invisible condition as a Bonus Action. The condition ends on you immediately after you take an action, a Bonus Action, or a Reaction."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.523, 0.647, 0.905, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shadowy Form.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While within Dim Light or Darkness, you have Resistance to all damage except Psychic and Radiant."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.524, 0.701, 0.692, 0.718], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boon of Truesight"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.524, 0.718, 0.808, 0.734], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Epic Boon Feat (Prerequisite: Level 19+)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.524, 0.738, 0.761, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.524, 0.754, 0.903, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score Increase.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one ability score of your choice by 1, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 47, "bbox": [0.524, 0.785, 0.902, 0.815], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Truesight.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Truesight with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 48, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "88"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 49, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 88, "blocks": [{"type": "doc_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.188, 0.05, 0.407, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment"}], "level": 1}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.095, 0.187, 0.116], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Coins"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.488, 0.242], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Characters often find coins on their adventures and can spend those coins in shops, inns, and other businesses. Coins come in different denominations based on the relative worth of their material. The Coin Values table lists coins and how much they’re worth relative to the Gold Piece, which is the game’s main coin. For example, 100 Copper Pieces are worth 1 Gold Piece."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.243, 0.468, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A coin weighs about a third of an ounce, so fifty coins weigh a pound."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.287, 0.206, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Coin Values"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.305, 0.489, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.305, 0.489, 0.419], "content": "<table><tr><td>Coin</td><td>Value in GP</td></tr><tr><td>Copper Piece (CP)</td><td>1/100</td></tr><tr><td>Silver Piece (SP)</td><td>1/10</td></tr><tr><td>Electrum Piece (EP)</td><td>1/2</td></tr><tr><td>Gold Piece (GP)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Platinum Piece (PP)</td><td>10</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.434, 0.237, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapons"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.458, 0.49, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Weapons table in this section shows the game’s main weapons. The table lists the cost and weight of each weapon, as well as the following details:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.511, 0.48, 0.573], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Category.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Every weapon falls into a category: Simple or Martial. Weapon proficiencies are usually tied to one of these categories. For example, you might have proficiency with Simple weapons."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.573, 0.477, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Melee or Ranged.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A weapon is classified as either Melee or Ranged. A Melee weapon is used to attack a target within 5 feet, whereas a Ranged weapon is used to attack at a greater distance."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.634, 0.49, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The table lists the amount of damage a weapon deals when an attacker hits with it as well as the type of that damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.68, 0.487, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Properties.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any properties a weapon has are listed in the Properties column. Each property is defined in the “Properties” section."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.726, 0.49, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mastery.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each weapon has a mastery property, which is defined in the “Mastery Properties” section. To use that property, you must have a feature that lets you use it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.117, 0.802, 0.287, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "S elling Equipment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.116, 0.821, 0.46, 0.885], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment fetches half its cost when sold. In contrast, trade goods and valuables—like gems and art objects—retain their full value in the marketplace. “Magic Items” has prices for magic items."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.743, 0.071], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon Proficiency"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.075, 0.908, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Anyone can wield a weapon, but you must have proficiency with it to add your Proficiency Bonus to an attack roll you make with it. A player character’s features can provide weapon proficiencies. A mon"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ster is proficient with any weapon in its stat block.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.159, 0.643, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Properties"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.182, 0.909, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Here are definitions of the properties in the Properties column of the Weapons table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.222, 0.644, 0.238], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ammunition"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.521, 0.24, 0.91, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use a weapon that has the Ammunition property to make a ranged attack only if you have ammunition to fire from it. The type of ammunition required is specified with the weapon’s range. Each attack expends one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). After a fight, you can spend 1 minute to recover half the ammunition (round down) you used in the fight; the rest is lost."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.401, 0.596, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Finesse"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.418, 0.907, 0.481], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When making an attack with a Finesse weapon, use your choice of your Strength or Dexterity modifier for the attack and damage rolls. You must use the same modifier for both rolls."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.487, 0.588, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heavy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.505, 0.907, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Disadvantage on attack rolls with a Heavy weapon if it’s a Melee weapon and your Strength score isn’t at least 13 or if it’s a Ranged weapon and your Dexterity score isn’t at least 13."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.574, 0.578, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Light"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.592, 0.912, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Attack action on your turn and attack with a Light weapon, you can make one extra attack as a Bonus Action later on the same turn. That extra attack must be made with a different Light weapon, and you don’t add your ability modifier to the extra attack’s damage unless that modifier is negative. For example, you can attack with a Shortsword in one hand and a Dagger in the other using the Attack action and a Bonus Action, but you don’t add your Strength or Dexterity modifier to the damage roll of the Bonus Action unless that modifier is negative."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "89"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 89, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.181, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Loading"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.47, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can fire only one piece of ammunition from a Loading weapon when you use an action, a Bonus Action, or a Reaction to fire it, regardless of the number of attacks you can normally make."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.138, 0.165, 0.156], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.1, 0.155, 0.489, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Range weapon has a range in parentheses after the Ammunition or Thrown property. The range lists two numbers. The first is the weapon’s normal range in feet, and the second is the weapon’s long range. When attacking a target beyond normal range, you have Disadvantage on the attack roll. You can’t attack a target beyond the long range."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.165, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reach"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.1, 0.287, 0.487, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Reach weapon adds 5 feet to your reach when you attack with it, as well as when determining your reach for Opportunity Attacks with it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.343, 0.181, 0.358], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thrown"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.1, 0.36, 0.484, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a weapon has the Thrown property, you can throw the weapon to make a ranged attack, and you can draw that weapon as part of the attack. If the weapon is a Melee weapon, use the same ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls that you use for a melee attack with that weapon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.46, 0.227, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Two-Handed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.478, 0.47, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Two-Handed weapon requires two hands when you attack with it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.516, 0.188, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Versatile"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.1, 0.533, 0.489, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Versatile weapon can be used with one or two hands. A damage value in parentheses appears with the property. The weapon deals that damage when used with two hands to make a melee attack."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.603, 0.314, 0.622], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mastery Properties"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.626, 0.481, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each weapon has a mastery property, which is usable only by a character who has a feature, such as Weapon Mastery, that unlocks the property for the character. The properties are defined below."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.116, 0.704, 0.306, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "I mprovised Weapons"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.115, 0.723, 0.477, 0.802], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you use an object—such as a table leg, frying pan, or bottle—as a makeshift weapon, see “Improvised Weapons” in “Rules Glossary.” Also see those rules if you wield a weapon in an unusual way, such as using a Ranged weapon to make a melee attack."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.593, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cleave"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.521, 0.068, 0.904, 0.193], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with a melee attack roll using this weapon, you can make a melee attack roll with the weapon against a second creature within 5 feet of the first that is also within your reach. On a hit, the second creature takes the weapon’s damage, but don’t add your ability modifier to that damage unless that modifier is negative. You can make this extra attack only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.199, 0.587, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Graze"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.521, 0.216, 0.9, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If your attack roll with this weapon misses a creature, you can deal damage to that creature equal to the ability modifier you used to make the attack roll. This damage is the same type dealt by the weapon, and the damage can be increased only by increasing the ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.316, 0.574, 0.333], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nick"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.521, 0.334, 0.907, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make the extra attack of the Light property, you can make it as part of the Attack action instead of as a Bonus Action. You can make this extra attack only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.403, 0.575, 0.42], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Push"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.521, 0.421, 0.908, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with this weapon, you can push the creature up to 10 feet straight away from yourself if it is Large or smaller."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.476, 0.564, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sap"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.492, 0.91, 0.541], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with this weapon, that creature has Disadvantage on its next attack roll before the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.546, 0.576, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slow"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.521, 0.564, 0.913, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. If the creature is hit more than once by weapons that have this property, the Speed reduction doesn’t exceed 10 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.649, 0.595, 0.667], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Topple"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.521, 0.666, 0.91, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with this weapon, you can force the creature to make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 plus the ability modifier used to make the attack roll and your Proficiency Bonus). On a failed save, the creature has the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.751, 0.567, 0.767], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vex"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.521, 0.769, 0.913, 0.833], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to the creature, you have Advantage on your next attack roll against that creature before the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.033, 0.952, 0.058, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "90"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.951, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 90, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.081, 0.036, 0.933, 0.94], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.081, 0.036, 0.933, 0.94], "content": "<table><tr><td>Name</td><td>Damage</td><td>Properties</td><td>Mastery</td><td>Weight</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"6\">Simple Melee Weapons</td></tr><tr><td>Club</td><td>Id4 Bludgeoning</td><td>Light</td><td>Slow</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>I SP</td></tr><tr><td>Dagger</td><td>Id4 Piercing</td><td>Finesse, Light, Thrown (Range 20/60)</td><td>Nick</td><td>I lb.</td><td>2 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Greatclub</td><td>Id8 Bludgeoning</td><td>Two-Handed</td><td>Push</td><td>10 lb.</td><td>2 SP</td></tr><tr><td>Handaxe</td><td>Id6 Slashing</td><td>Light, Thrown (Range 20/60)</td><td>Vex</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Javelin</td><td>Id6 Piercing</td><td>Thrown (Range 30/120)</td><td>Slow</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>5 SP</td></tr><tr><td>Light Hammer</td><td>Id4 Bludgeoning</td><td>Light, Thrown (Range 20/60)</td><td>Nick</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>2 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Mace</td><td>I