d>1/2 Ilb.</td><td>I GP</td></tr><tr><td>Bullets, Firearm</td><td>10</td><td>Pouch</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>3 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Bullets, Sling</td><td>20</td><td>Pouch</td><td>1/2 Ib.</td><td>4 CP</td></tr><tr><td>Needles</td><td>50</td><td>Pouch</td><td>I lb.</td><td>IGP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.194, 0.268, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Antitoxin (50 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.213, 0.484, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can drink a vial of Antitoxin to gain Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.267, 0.307, 0.284], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Focus (Varies)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.284, 0.482, 0.348], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Arcane Focus takes one of the forms in the Arcane Focuses table and is bejeweled or carved to channel arcane magic. A Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard can use such an item as a Spellcasting Focus."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.359, 0.238, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Focuses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.104, 0.377, 0.487, 0.491], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.104, 0.377, 0.487, 0.491], "content": "<table><tr><td>Focus                              Weight     Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Crystal                                 I lb.    10 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Orb                                     3 lb.    20 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Rod                                     2 lb.    10 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Staff (also a Quarterstaff)              4 lb.     5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Wand                                   I lb.    10 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.503, 0.258, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Backpack (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.52, 0.467, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Backpack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot. It can also serve as a saddlebag."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.559, 0.287, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ball Bearings (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.577, 0.484, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can spill Ball Bearings from their pouch. They spread to cover a level, 10-footsquare area within 10 feet of yourself. A creature that enters this area for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition. It takes 10 minutes to recover the Ball Bearings."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.691, 0.23, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Barrel (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.709, 0.472, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Barrel holds up to 40 gallons of liquid or up to 4 cubic feet of dry goods."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.748, 0.228, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Basket (4 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.766, 0.48, 0.783], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Basket holds up to 40 pounds within 2 cubic feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.789, 0.237, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bedroll (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.807, 0.486, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Bedroll sleeps one Small or Medium creature. While in a Bedroll, you automatically succeed on saving throws against extreme cold (see “Gameplay Toolbox”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.876, 0.206, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bell (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.894, 0.456, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When rung as a Utilize action, a Bell produces a sound that can be heard up to 60 feet away."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.658, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blanket (5 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.909, 0.116], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wrapped in a blanket, you have Advantage on saving throws against extreme cold (see “Gameplay Toolbox”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.121, 0.745, 0.14], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Block and Tackle (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.14, 0.884, 0.172], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Block and Tackle allows you to hoist up to four times the weight you can normally lift."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.178, 0.652, 0.196], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Book (25 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.196, 0.913, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Book contains fiction or nonfiction. If you consult an accurate nonfiction Book about its topic, you gain a +5 bonus to Intelligence (Arcana, History, Nature, or Religion) checks you make about that topic."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.265, 0.71, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bottle, Glass (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.283, 0.788, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Glass Bottle holds up to 11/2 pints."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.306, 0.656, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bucket (5 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.324, 0.887, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Bucket holds up to half a cubic foot of contents."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.347, 0.73, 0.365], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burglar’s Pack (16 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.365, 0.904, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Burglar’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Ball Bearings, Bell, 10 Candles, Crowbar, Hooded Lantern, 7 flasks of Oil, 5 days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, and Waterskin."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.434, 0.672, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Caltrops (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.521, 0.452, 0.913, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can spread Caltrops from their bag to cover a 5-foot-square area within 5 feet of yourself. A creature that enters this area for the first time on a turn must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 1 Piercing damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. It takes 10 minutes to recover the Caltrops."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.567, 0.656, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Candle (1 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.585, 0.911, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For 1 hour, a lit Candle sheds Bright Light in a 5-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 5 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.623, 0.782, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Case, Crossbow Bolt (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.641, 0.839, 0.658], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Crossbow Bolt Case holds up to 20 Bolts."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.664, 0.77, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Case, Map or Scroll (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.682, 0.901, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Map or Scroll Case holds up to 10 sheets of paper or 5 sheets of parchment."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.72, 0.647, 0.738], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chain (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.521, 0.739, 0.91, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can wrap a Chain around an unwilling creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition if you succeed on a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check. If the creature’s legs are bound, the creature has the Restrained condition until it escapes. Escaping the Chain requires the creature to make a successful DC 18 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check as an action. Bursting the Chain requires a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check as an action."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "96"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 96, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.225, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chest (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.433, 0.086], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Chest holds up to 12 cubic feet of contents."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.091, 0.302, 0.109], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Climber’s Kit (25 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.109, 0.476, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Climber’s Kit includes boot tips, gloves, pitons, and a harness. As a Utilize action, you can use the Climber’s Kit to anchor yourself; when you do, you can’t fall more than 25 feet from the anchor point, and you can’t move more than 25 feet from there without undoing the anchor as a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.209, 0.299, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clothes, Fine (15 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.227, 0.484, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fine Clothes are made of expensive fabrics and adorned with expertly crafted details. Some events and locations admit only people wearing these clothes."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.296, 0.34, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clothes, Traveler’s (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.314, 0.476, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traveler’s Clothes are resilient garments designed for travel in various environments."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.352, 0.351, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Component Pouch (25 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.37, 0.475, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Component Pouch is watertight and filled with compartments that hold all the free Material components of your spells."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.424, 0.255, 0.441], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Costume (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.442, 0.482, 0.49], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing a Costume, you have Advantage on any ability check you make to impersonate the person or type of person it represents."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.496, 0.253, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crowbar (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.513, 0.475, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Crowbar gives you Advantage on Strength checks where the Crowbar’s leverage can be applied."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.567, 0.327, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Diplomat’s Pack (39 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.585, 0.472, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Diplomat’s Pack contains the following items: Chest, Fine Clothes, Ink, 5 Ink Pens, Lamp, 2 Map or Scroll Cases, 4 flasks of Oil, 5 sheets of Paper, 5 sheets of Parchment, Perfume, and Tinderbox."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.654, 0.308, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Druidic Focus (Varies)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.672, 0.49, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Druidic Focus takes one of the forms in the Druidic Focuses table and is carved, tied with ribbon, or painted to channel primal magic. A Druid or Ranger can use such an object as a Spellcasting Focus."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.747, 0.24, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Druidic Focuses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.105, 0.765, 0.487, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.105, 0.765, 0.487, 0.84], "content": "<table><tr><td>Focus</td><td>Weight</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Sprig of mistletoe</td><td></td><td>IGP</td></tr><tr><td>Wooden staff (also a Quarterstaff)</td><td>4 lb.</td><td>5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Yew wand</td><td>I lb.</td><td>I0 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.852, 0.353, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dungeoneer’s Pack (12 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.87, 0.478, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Dungeoneer’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Caltrops, Crowbar, 2 flasks of Oil, 10"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.892, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, 10 Torches, and Waterskin."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.088, 0.77, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Entertainer’s Pack (40 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.107, 0.908, 0.17], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Entertainer’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Bedroll, Bell, Bullseye Lantern, 3 Costumes, Mirror, 8 flasks of Oil, 9 days of Rations, Tinderbox, and Waterskin."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.175, 0.744, 0.193], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Explorer’s Pack (10 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.901, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Explorer’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Bedroll, 2 flasks of Oil, 10 days of Rations, Rope, Tinderbox, 10 Torches, and Waterskin."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.246, 0.64, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flask (2 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.265, 0.719, 0.282], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Flask holds up to 1 pint."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.288, 0.738, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grappling Hook (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.307, 0.912, 0.385], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can throw the Grappling Hook at a railing, a ledge, or another catch within 50 feet of yourself, and the hook catches on if you succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. If you tied a Rope to the hook, you can then climb it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.39, 0.701, 0.407], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healer’s Kit (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.408, 0.902, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Healer’s Kit has ten uses. As a Utilize action, you can expend one of its uses to stabilize an Unconscious creature that has 0 Hit Points without needing to make a Wisdom (Medicine) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.477, 0.72, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Symbol (Varies)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.496, 0.902, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Holy Symbol takes one of the forms in the Holy Symbol table and is bejeweled or painted to channel divine magic. A Cleric or Paladin can use a Holy Symbol as a Spellcasting Focus."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.557, 0.903, 0.604], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The table indicates whether a Holy Symbol needs to be held, worn, or borne on fabric (such as a tabard or banner) or a Shield."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.615, 0.643, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Symbols"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.527, 0.634, 0.911, 0.71], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.527, 0.634, 0.911, 0.71], "content": "<table><tr><td>Symbol</td><td>Weight</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Amulet (worn or held)</td><td>I lb.</td><td>5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Emblem (borne on fabric or a Shield)</td><td></td><td>5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Reliquary (held)</td><td>2 lb.</td><td>5 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.523, 0.721, 0.712, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Water (25 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.521, 0.74, 0.905, 0.849], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with throwing a flask of Holy Water. Target one creature you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or take 2d8 Radiant damage if it is a Fiend or an Undead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.523, 0.854, 0.715, 0.872], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hunting Trap (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.522, 0.872, 0.907, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can set a Hunting Trap, which is a sawtooth steel ring that snaps shut when a creature steps on a pressure plate in the center."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.033, 0.952, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "97"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 97, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.251], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The trap is affixed by a heavy chain to an immobile object, such as a tree or a spike driven into the ground. A creature that steps on the plate must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 1d4 Piercing damage and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. Thereafter, until the creature breaks free of the trap, its movement is limited by the length of the chain (typically 3 feet). A creature can use its action to make a DC 13 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing itself or another creature within its reach on a success. Each failed check deals 1 Piercing damage to the trapped creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.257, 0.21, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ink (10 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.275, 0.443, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ink comes in a 1-ounce bottle, which provides enough ink to write about 500 pages."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.313, 0.239, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ink Pen (2 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.331, 0.444, 0.348], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using Ink, an Ink Pen is used to write or draw."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.354, 0.199, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Jug (2 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.373, 0.296, 0.389], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Jug holds up to 1 gallon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.395, 0.23, 0.412], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ladder (1 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.413, 0.476, 0.444], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Ladder is 10 feet tall. You must climb to move up or down it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.452, 0.218, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lamp (5 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.469, 0.488, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Lamp burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 15- foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.509, 0.336, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lantern, Bullseye (10 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.526, 0.474, 0.573], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Bullseye Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 60-foot Cone and Dim Light for an additional 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.58, 0.327, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lantern, Hooded (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.598, 0.483, 0.676], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Hooded Lantern burns Oil as fuel to cast Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. As a Bonus Action, you can lower the hood, reducing the light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius, or raise it again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.682, 0.225, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lock (10 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.7, 0.481, 0.748], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Lock comes with a key. Without the key, a creature can use Thieves’ Tools to pick this Lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.754, 0.342, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magnifying Glass (100 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.772, 0.485, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Magnifying Glass grants Advantage on any ability check made to appraise or inspect a highly detailed item. Lighting a fire with a Magnifying Glass requires light as bright as sunlight to focus, tinder to ignite, and about 5 minutes for the fire to ignite."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.856, 0.255, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Manacles (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.101, 0.874, 0.481, 0.936], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can use Manacles to bind an unwilling Small or Medium creature within 5 feet of yourself that has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition if you succeed on a DC 13"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.905, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check. While bound, a creature has Disadvantage on attack rolls, and the creature is Restrained if the Manacles are attached to a chain or hook that is fixed in place. Escaping the Manacles requires a successful DC 20 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check as an action. Bursting them requires a successful DC 25 Strength (Athletics) check as an action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.173, 0.912, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each set of Manacles comes with a key. Without the key, a creature can use Thieves’ Tools to pick the Manacles’ lock with a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.242, 0.632, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Map (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.26, 0.905, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you consult an accurate Map, you gain a +5 bonus to Wisdom (Survival) checks you make to find your way in the place represented on it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.313, 0.655, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mirror (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.331, 0.9, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A handheld steel Mirror is useful for personal cosmetics but also for peeking around corners and reflecting light as a signal."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.385, 0.628, 0.403], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Net (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.403, 0.904, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with throwing a Net. Target a creature you can see within 15 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or have the Restrained condition until it escapes. The target succeeds automatically if it is Huge or larger."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.526, 0.895, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To escape, the target or a creature within 5 feet of it must take an action to make a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing the Restrained creature on a success. Destroying the Net (AC 10; 5 HP; Immunity to Bludgeoning, Poison, and Psychic damage) also frees the target, ending the effect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.626, 0.616, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oil (1 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.643, 0.896, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can douse a creature, object, or space with Oil or use it as fuel, as detailed below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.674, 0.912, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dousing a Creature or an Object.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you take the Attack action, you can replace one of your attacks with throwing an Oil flask. Target one creature or object within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or be covered in oil. If the target takes Fire damage before the oil dries (after 1 minute), the target takes an extra 5 Fire damage from burning oil."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.812, 0.912, 0.937], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dousing a Space.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take the Utilize action to pour an Oil flask on level ground to cover a 5-foot-square area within 5 feet of yourself. If lit, the oil burns until the end of the turn 2 rounds from when the oil was lit (or 12 seconds) and deals 5 Fire damage to any creature that enters the area or ends its turn there. A creature can take this damage only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.057, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "98"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 98, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.491, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fuel.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Oil serves as fuel for Lamps and Lanterns. Once lit, a flask of Oil burns for 6 hours in a Lamp or Lantern. That duration doesn’t need to be consecutive; you can extinguish the burning Oil (as a Utilize action) and rekindle it again until it has burned for a total of 6 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.15, 0.221, 0.168], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Paper (2 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.168, 0.484, 0.199], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One sheet of Paper can hold about 250 handwritten words."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.206, 0.264, 0.224], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parchment (1 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.223, 0.471, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One sheet of Parchment can hold about 250 handwritten words."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.249, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Perfume (5 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.28, 0.487, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Perfume comes in a 4-ounce vial. For 1 hour after applying Perfume to yourself, you have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to influence an Indifferent Humanoid within 5 feet of yourself."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.35, 0.309, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison, Basic (100 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.1, 0.367, 0.486, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can use a vial of Basic Poison to coat one weapon or up to three pieces of ammunition. A creature that takes Piercing or Slashing damage from the poisoned weapon or ammunition takes an extra 1d4 Poison damage. Once applied, the poison retains potency for 1 minute or until its damage is dealt, whichever comes first."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.482, 0.21, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pole (5 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.5, 0.482, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Pole is 10 feet long. You can use it to touch something up to 10 feet away. If you must make a Strength (Athletics) check as part of a High or Long Jump, you can use the Pole to vault, giving yourself Advantage on the check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.584, 0.253, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pot, Iron (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.603, 0.342, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Iron Pot holds up to 1 gallon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.625, 0.338, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Healing (50 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.644, 0.484, 0.721], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion is a magic item. As a Bonus Action, you can drink it or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of yourself. The creature that drinks the magical red fluid in this vial regains 2d4 + 2 Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.728, 0.222, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pouch (5 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.745, 0.474, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Pouch holds up to 6 pounds within one-fifth of a cubic foot."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.784, 0.296, 0.801], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Priest’s Pack (33 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.802, 0.481, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Priest’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Blanket, Holy Water, Lamp, 7 days of Rations, Robe, and Tinderbox."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.856, 0.234, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Quiver (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.874, 0.342, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Quiver holds up to 20 Arrows."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.722, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ram, Portable (4 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.905, 0.132], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use a Portable Ram to break down doors. When doing so, you gain a +4 bonus to the Strength check. One other character can help you use the ram, giving you Advantage on this check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.657, 0.155], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rations (5 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.91, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rations consist of travel-ready food, including jerky, dried fruit, hardtack, and nuts. See “Malnutrition” in “Rules Glossary” for the risks of not eating."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.209, 0.641, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.227, 0.904, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Robe has vocational or ceremonial significance. Some events and locations admit only people wearing a Robe bearing certain colors or symbols."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.64, 0.298], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rope (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.298, 0.901, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can tie a knot with Rope if you succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check. The Rope can be burst with a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.36, 0.907, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can bind an unwilling creature with the Rope only if the creature has the Grappled, Incapacitated, or Restrained condition. If the creature’s legs are bound, the creature has the Restrained condition until it escapes. Escaping the Rope requires the creature to make a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check as an action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.475, 0.634, 0.492], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sack (1 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.492, 0.887, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Sack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.516, 0.732, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scholar’s Pack (40 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.534, 0.907, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Scholar’s Pack contains the following items: Backpack, Book, Ink, Ink Pen, Lamp, 10 flasks of Oil, 10 sheets of Parchment, and Tinderbox."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.587, 0.653, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shovel (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.606, 0.883, 0.652], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Working for 1 hour, you can use a Shovel to dig a hole that is 5 feet on each side in soil or similar material."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.659, 0.722, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Signal Whistle (5 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.677, 0.895, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When blown as a Utilize action, a Signal Whistle produces a sound that can be heard up to 600 feet away."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.523, 0.73, 0.783, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Scroll (Cantrip, 30 GP; Level 1, 50 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.761, 0.91, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Spell Scroll (Cantrip) or Spell Scroll (Level 1) is a magic item that bears the words of a cantrip or level 1 spell, respectively, determined by the scroll’s creator. If the spell is on your class’s spell list, you can read the scroll and cast the spell using its normal casting time and without providing any Material components."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.522, 0.869, 0.892, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell requires a saving throw or an attack roll, the spell save DC is 13, and the attack bonus is +5. The scroll disintegrates when the casting is completed."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.033, 0.953, 0.056, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "99"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 99, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.277, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spikes, Iron (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.488, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Iron Spikes come in bundles of ten. As a Utilize action, you can use a blunt object, such as a Light Hammer, to hammer a spike into wood, earth, or a similar material. You can do so to jam a door shut or to then tie a Rope or Chain to the Spike."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.153, 0.283, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spyglass (1,000 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.171, 0.487, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Objects viewed through a Spyglass are magnified to twice their size."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.209, 0.221, 0.227], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "String (1 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.227, 0.489, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "String is 10 feet long. You can tie a knot in it as a Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.265, 0.215, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tent (2 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.283, 0.483, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Tent sleeps up to two Small or Medium creatures."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.306, 0.262, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tinderbox (5 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.324, 0.474, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Tinderbox is a small container holding flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a Candle, Lamp, Lantern, or Torch—or anything else with exposed fuel—takes a Bonus Action. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.424, 0.224, 0.441], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Torch (1 CP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.1, 0.441, 0.47, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Torch burns for 1 hour, casting Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet. When you take the Attack action, you can attack with the Torch, using it as a Simple Melee weapon. On a hit, the target takes 1 Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.526, 0.205, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vial (1 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.544, 0.307, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Vial holds up to 4 ounces."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.567, 0.262, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Waterskin (2 SP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.585, 0.472, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Waterskin holds up to 4 pints. If you don’t drink sufficient water, you risk dehydration (see “Rules Glossary”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.641, 0.391, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mounts and Vehicles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.1, 0.667, 0.482, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A mount can help you move more quickly through the wilderness, but its primary purpose is to carry gear that would otherwise slow you down. The Mounts and Other Animals table shows each animal’s carrying capacity. See “Monsters” for the animals’ stat blocks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.766, 0.304, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mounts and Cargo"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.1, 0.79, 0.48, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An animal pulling a carriage, cart, chariot, sled, or wagon can move weight up to five times its base carrying capacity, including the weight of the vehicle. If multiple animals pull the same vehicle, add "}, {"type": "text", "content": "their carrying capacities together.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.874, 0.191, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Barding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.897, 0.466, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Barding is armor designed for a mount. Any type of armor on the Armor table in “Equipment” can"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.521, 0.049, 0.902, 0.083], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "be purchased as barding. The cost is four times the normal cost, and it weighs twice as much."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.088, 0.611, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saddles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.111, 0.893, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A saddle comes with a bit, a bridle, reins, and any other equipment needed to use the saddle. A Military Saddle gives Advantage on any ability check you make to remain mounted. An Exotic Saddle is required for riding an aquatic or a flying mount."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.527, 0.221, 0.901, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.202, 0.755, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mounts and Other Animals"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.527, 0.221, 0.901, 0.392], "content": "<table><tr><td>Item</td><td>Carrying Capacity Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Camel</td><td>50 GP 450 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Elephant</td><td>200 GP 1,320 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Horse, Draft</td><td>50 GP 540 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Horse, Riding</td><td>480 lb. 75 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Mastiff</td><td>195 lb. 25 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Mule</td><td>420 lb. 8 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Pony</td><td>225 lb. 30 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Warhorse</td><td>400 GP 540 lb.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.527, 0.427, 0.909, 0.658], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.409, 0.82, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tack, Harness, and Drawn Vehicles"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.527, 0.427, 0.909, 0.658], "content": "<table><tr><td>Weight Item</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Carriage</td><td>600 lb. 100 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Cart</td><td>200 lb. I5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Chariot</td><td>100 lb. 250 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Feed per day</td><td>5 CP 10 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Saddle</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Exotic</td><td>40 lb. 60 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Military</td><td>30 lb. 20 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Riding</td><td>25 lb. 10 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Sled</td><td>300 lb. 20 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Stabling per day</td><td>5 SP</td></tr><tr><td>Wagon</td><td>35 GP 400 lb.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.669, 0.684, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Vehicles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.692, 0.894, 0.742], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Airborne and Waterborne Vehicles table provides statistics for various types of large vehicles. The following notes apply."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.747, 0.587, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.521, 0.764, 0.912, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A ship sailing against a strong wind moves at half speed. In a dead calm (no wind), waterborne ships can’t move under sail and must be rowed. Keelboats and Rowboats are used on lakes and rivers. If going downstream, add the speed of the current (typically 3 miles per hour) to the speed of the vehicle. These vehicles can’t be rowed against any significant current, but they can be pulled upstream by draft animals on the shores. A Rowboat can be carried and weighs 100 pounds."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "100"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 100, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.104, 0.068, 0.91, 0.222], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.399, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Airborne and Waterborne Vehicles"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.104, 0.068, 0.91, 0.222], "content": "<table><tr><td>Ship</td><td>Speed</td><td>Crew</td><td>Passengers</td><td>Cargo (Tons)</td><td>AC</td><td>HP</td><td>Damage Threshold</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Airship</td><td>8 mph</td><td>10</td><td>20</td><td>I</td><td>13</td><td>300</td><td></td><td>40,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Galley</td><td>4 mph</td><td>80</td><td></td><td>150</td><td>15</td><td>500</td><td>20</td><td>30,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Keelboat</td><td>I mph</td><td>I</td><td>6</td><td>1/2</td><td>15</td><td>100</td><td>10</td><td>3,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Longship</td><td>3 mph</td><td>40</td><td>150</td><td>10</td><td>15</td><td>300</td><td>15</td><td>10,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Rowboat</td><td>1/½ mph</td><td>I</td><td>3</td><td></td><td>ⅡI</td><td>50</td><td></td><td>50 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Sailing Ship</td><td>2 mph</td><td>20</td><td>20</td><td>100</td><td>15</td><td>300</td><td>15</td><td>10,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Warship</td><td>2/½ mph</td><td>60</td><td>60</td><td>200</td><td>15</td><td>500</td><td>20</td><td>25,000 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.159, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crew"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.1, 0.267, 0.486, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A ship larger than a Keelboat or Rowboat needs a crew of skilled hirelings (see “Hirelings” later in “Equipment”) to function. The minimum number of skilled hirelings needed to crew a ship depends on the type of ship, as shown in the table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.353, 0.208, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Passengers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.37, 0.492, 0.479], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The table lists the number of Small and Medium passengers the ship can accommodate using hammocks. A ship outfitted with private accommodations can carry one-fifth as many passengers. A passenger usually pays 5 SP per day for a hammock, but prices can vary from ship to ship. A small private cabin usually costs 2 GP per day."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.485, 0.279, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Threshold"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.503, 0.488, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a vehicle has a damage threshold (see “Rules Glossary”), it’s noted in the table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.541, 0.212, 0.559], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ship Repair"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.559, 0.486, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Repairs to a damaged ship can be made while the vessel is berthed. Repairing 1 Hit Point of damage requires 1 day and costs 20 GP for materials and labor. If the repairs are made in a location where sup plies and skilled labor are abundant, such as a city shipyard, the repair time and cost are halved."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.662, 0.362, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lifestyle Expenses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.687, 0.485, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lifestyle expenses summarize the cost of living in a fantasy world. They cover lodging, food, equipment maintenance, and other necessities."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.733, 0.488, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the start of each week or month (GM’s choice), choose a lifestyle below—Wretched, Squalid, Poor, Modest, Comfortable, Wealthy, or Aristocratic—and pay the price to sustain that lifestyle."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.794, 0.49, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lifestyles have no inherent consequences, but the GM might take them into account when determining risks or how others perceive your character."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.847, 0.285, 0.867], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wretched (Free)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.871, 0.472, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You survive via chance and charity. You’re often exposed to natural dangers as a result of sleeping outside."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.25, 0.765, 0.271], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Squalid (1 SP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.274, 0.9, 0.323], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You spend the bare minimum for your necessities. You might be exposed to unhealthy conditions and opportunistic criminals."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.328, 0.742, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poor (2 SP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.352, 0.817, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You spend frugally for your necessities."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.374, 0.773, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Modest (1 GP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.399, 0.824, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You support yourself at an average level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.421, 0.83, 0.441], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Comfortable (2 GP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.446, 0.91, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You spend modestly for your necessities and enjoy a few luxuries."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.483, 0.783, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wealthy (4 GP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.507, 0.879, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You’re accustomed to the finer things in life and might have servants."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.546, 0.832, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aristocratic (10 GP per Day)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.57, 0.908, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You pay for the best and might have a staff that supports your lifestyle. Others notice your wealth and might encourage you to share it, either legally or otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.881, 0.666], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Food, Drink, and Lodging"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.667, 0.902, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Food, Drink, and Lodging table gives prices for food and a single night’s lodging. Prices for daily lodging and meals are included in your lifestyle’s expenses."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.742, 0.741, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Food, Drink, and Lodging"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.526, 0.76, 0.91, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.526, 0.76, 0.91, 0.912], "content": "<table><tr><td>Item</td><td>Cost Item</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Ale (mug) 4CP</td><td>Comfortable</td><td>8 SP</td></tr><tr><td>Bread (loaf)</td><td>2 CP</td><td>Wealthy 2 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Cheese (wedge)</td><td>ISP Aristocratic</td><td>4 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Inn Stay per Day</td><td>Meal</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Squalid</td><td>7CP Squalid</td><td>ICP</td></tr><tr><td>Poor</td><td>I SP Poor</td><td>2 CP</td></tr><tr><td>Modest</td><td>5 SP Modest</td><td>I SP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.06, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "101"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 101, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.105, 0.054, 0.487, 0.13], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.105, 0.054, 0.487, 0.13], "content": "<table><tr><td>Item</td><td>Cost</td><td>Item</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Comfortable</td><td>2 SP</td><td>Wine (bottle)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Wealthy</td><td>3 SP</td><td>Common</td><td>2 SP</td></tr><tr><td>Aristocratic</td><td>6 SP</td><td>Fine</td><td>10 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.144, 0.231, 0.168], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hirelings"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.169, 0.477, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skilled hirelings include anyone hired to perform a service that involves a proficiency (including weapon, tool, or skill): a mercenary, an artisan, a scribe, or the like. The pay shown on the Hirelings table is a minimum; some expert hirelings require more pay. Untrained hirelings are hired for work that requires no particular proficiencies; they include laborers and porters."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.306, 0.183, 0.322], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hirelings"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.324, 0.488, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.324, 0.488, 0.4], "content": "<table><tr><td>Service</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Skilled hireling</td><td>2 GP per day</td></tr><tr><td>Untrained hireling</td><td>2 SP per day</td></tr><tr><td>Messenger</td><td>2 CP per mile</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.271, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.438, 0.483, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most settlements contain individuals who are willing to cast spells in exchange for payment. If a spell has expensive components, add the cost of those components to the cost listed in the Spellcasting Services table. The higher the level of a desired spell, the harder it is to find someone to cast it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.544, 0.281, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting Services"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.562, 0.487, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.562, 0.487, 0.715], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell Level</td><td>Availability</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Village, town, or city</td><td>30 GP</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Village, town, or city</td><td>50 GP</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Village, town, or city</td><td>200 GP</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Town or city only</td><td>300 GP</td></tr><tr><td>4-5</td><td>Town or city only</td><td>2,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>6-8</td><td>City only</td><td>20,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>City only</td><td>100,000 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.729, 0.274, 0.753], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.754, 0.487, 0.833], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adventures hold the promise—but not a guarantee—of finding magic items. Hundreds of magic items are detailed in “Magic Items” later in this document. Here’s what you need to know about using magic items."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.839, 0.361, 0.859], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Identifying a Magic Item"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.863, 0.486, 0.911], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items are indistinguishable from their nonmagical counterparts, while others are conspicuously magical. Handling a magic item is enough to"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.897, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "give you a sense that it is extraordinary, but learning a magic item’s properties isn’t automatic."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.897, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Identify spell is the fastest way to reveal an item’s properties. Alternatively, you can focus on one magic item during a Short Rest while being in physical contact with the item. At the end of the rest, you learn its properties and how to use them (but not any curse the item might bear)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.173, 0.906, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes a magic item carries a clue to its prop erties. The command word to activate a ring might be etched inside the band, or a feathered design might hint that it’s a Ring of Feather Falling."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.234, 0.912, 0.374], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wearing or experimenting with an item can also offer hints about its properties. In the specific case of Potions, a little taste is enough to tell the taster what a potion does. Other items might require more experimentation. For example, if your character puts on a Ring of Swimming, the GM might say, “Your movement feels strangely fluid.” Perhaps you then dive into a river to see what happens. The GM would then say you swim unexpectedly well."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.38, 0.661, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attunement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.521, 0.403, 0.912, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items require a creature to form a bond—called Attunement—with them before the creature can use an item’s magical properties. Without becoming attuned to an item that requires Attunement, you gain only its nonmagical benefits unless its description states otherwise. For example, a magic Shield that requires Attunement provides the benefits of a normal Shield if you aren’t attuned to it, but none of its magical properties."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.55, 0.775, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attune during a Short Rest"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.521, 0.567, 0.913, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attuning to an item requires you to spend a Short Rest focused on only that item while being in physical contact with it (this can’t be the same Short Rest used to learn the item’s properties). This focus can take the form of weapon practice (for a Weapon), meditation (for a Wand), or some other appropriate activity. If the Short Rest is interrupted, the Attunement attempt fails. Otherwise, at the end of the Short Rest, you’re attuned to the magic item and can access its full magical capabilities."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.728, 0.781, 0.744], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No More Than Three Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.521, 0.746, 0.913, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can be attuned to no more than three magic items at a time. Any attempt to attune to a fourth item fails; you must end your Attunement to an item first. Additionally, you can’t attune to more than one copy of an item. For example, you can’t attune to more than one Ring of Protection at a time."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.846, 0.708, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ending Attunement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.863, 0.908, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your Attunement to an item ends if you no longer satisfy the prerequisites for Attunement, if the item has been more than 100 feet away for at least 24 hours, if you die, or if another creature attunes to"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "102"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 102, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.486, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "the item. You can also voluntarily end Attunement by spending another Short Rest focused on the item unless the item is cursed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.41, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wearing and Wielding Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.128, 0.49, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a magic item’s properties might mean wearing or wielding it. A magic item meant to be worn must be donned in the intended fashion: boots go on feet, gloves on hands, hats and helmets on a head, and rings on a finger. Magic armor must be donned, a Shield strapped to the arm, a cloak fastened about the shoulders. A weapon must be held."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.236, 0.488, 0.298], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In most cases, a magic item that’s meant to be worn can fit a creature regardless of size or build. Magic garments are made to be easily adjustable, or they magically adjust themselves to the wearer."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.304, 0.398, 0.321], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiple Items of the Same Kind"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.1, 0.322, 0.487, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can’t wear more than one of certain magic items. You can’t normally wear more than one pair of footwear, one pair of gloves or gauntlets, one pair of bracers, one suit of armor, one item of headwear, or one cloak. The GM might make exceptions."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.406, 0.222, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Paired Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.1, 0.423, 0.487, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Items that come in pairs—such as boots, bracers, gauntlets, and gloves—impart their benefits only if both items of the pair are worn. For example, a character wearing a Boot of Striding and Springing on one foot and a Boot of Elvenkind on the other foot gains no benefit from either."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.526, 0.481, 0.55], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crafting Nonmagical Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.552, 0.485, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To craft a nonmagical item, you need tools, raw materials, and time, each of which is detailed below. If you meet the requirements, you make the item, and you can use it or sell it at its normal price."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.621, 0.167, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tools"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.644, 0.487, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The “Tools” section of “Equipment” lists which tools are required to make certain items. The GM assigns required tools for items not listed there."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.691, 0.47, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You must use the required tool to make an item and have proficiency with that tool. Anyone who helps you must also have proficiency with it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.744, 0.258, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Raw Materials"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.1, 0.767, 0.488, 0.846], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To make an item, you need raw materials worth half its purchase cost (round down). For example, you need 750 GP of raw materials to make Plate Armor, which sells for 1,500 GP. The GM determines whether appropriate raw materials are available."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.852, 0.165, 0.871], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Time"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.875, 0.472, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To determine how many days (working 8 hours a day) it takes to make an item, divide its purchase cost in GP by 10 (round a fraction up to a day). For"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.892, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "example, you need 5 days to make a Heavy Cross-bow, which sells for 50 GP."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.909, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If an item requires multiple days, the days needn’t be consecutive."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.112, 0.901, 0.19], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Characters can combine their efforts to shorten the crafting time. Divide the time needed to create an item by the number of characters working on it. Normally, only one other character can assist you, but the GM might allow more assistants."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.199, 0.905, 0.223], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brewing Potions of Healing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.521, 0.224, 0.91, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A character who has proficiency with the Herbalism Kit can create a Potion of Healing. Doing so requires using that kit and 25 GP of raw material over the course of 1 day (8 hours of work)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.295, 0.818, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scribing Spell Scrolls"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.32, 0.908, 0.353], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spellcaster can transfer a spell to a scroll and create a Spell Scroll, using the rules below."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.359, 0.688, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Time and Cost"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.383, 0.911, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scribing a scroll takes an amount of time and money based on the level of the spell, as shown in the Spell Scroll Costs table. For each day of inscription, you must work for 8 hours. If a scroll requires multiple days, those days needn’t be consecutive."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.467, 0.821, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prerequisites for the Scribe"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.521, 0.49, 0.91, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To scribe a scroll, you must have proficiency in the Arcana skill or with Calligrapher’s Supplies and have the spell prepared on each day of the inscription. You must also have at hand any Material components required by the spell; if the spell consumes its Material components, they are consumed only when you complete the scroll. The scroll’s spell uses "}, {"type": "text", "content": "your spell save DC and spell attack bonus.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.621, 0.622, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrips"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.644, 0.89, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the scribed spell is a cantrip, the version on the scroll works as if the caster were your level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.689, 0.676, 0.705], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Scroll Costs"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.707, 0.91, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.707, 0.91, 0.917], "content": "<table><tr><td>Time Spell Level</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>I day Cantrip</td><td>I5 GP</td></tr><tr><td>I day 1</td><td>25 GP</td></tr><tr><td>3 days 2</td><td>100 GP</td></tr><tr><td>5 days 3</td><td>150 GP</td></tr><tr><td>10 days 4</td><td>1,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>25 days 5</td><td>1,500 GP</td></tr><tr><td>40 days 6</td><td>10,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>50 days 7</td><td>12,500 GP</td></tr><tr><td>60 days 8</td><td>15,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>120 days 9</td><td>50,000 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "103"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 103, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.236, 0.05, 0.356, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.094, 0.302, 0.119], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gaining Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.488, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Before you can cast a spell, you must have the spell prepared in your mind or have access to the spell from a magic item, such as a Spell Scroll. Your features specify which spells you have access to, if any; whether you always have certain spells prepared; and whether you can change the list of spells you have prepared."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.235, 0.279, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Preparing Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.258, 0.485, 0.323], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have a list of level 1+ spells you prepare, your spellcasting feature specifies when you can change the list and the number of spells you can change, as summarized in the Spell Preparation by Class t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "able", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.333, 0.325, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Preparation by Class"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.352, 0.487, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.352, 0.487, 0.537], "content": "<table><tr><td>Class</td><td>Change When You</td><td>Number of Spells</td></tr><tr><td>Bard</td><td>Gain a level</td><td>One</td></tr><tr><td>Cleric</td><td>Finish a Long Rest</td><td>Any</td></tr><tr><td>Druid</td><td>Finish a Long Rest</td><td>Any</td></tr><tr><td>Paladin</td><td>Finish a Long Rest</td><td>One</td></tr><tr><td>Ranger</td><td>Finish a Long Rest</td><td>One</td></tr><tr><td>Sorcerer</td><td>Gain a level</td><td>One</td></tr><tr><td>Warlock</td><td>Gain a level</td><td>One</td></tr><tr><td>Wizard</td><td>Finish a Long Rest</td><td>Any</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.545, 0.481, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most spellcasting monsters don’t change their lists of prepared spells, but the GM is free to alter t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "hem", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.583, 0.357, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Always-Prepared Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.607, 0.483, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Certain features might give you a spell that you always have prepared. If you also have a list of pre-pared spells that you can change, a spell that you always have prepared doesn’t count against the number of spells on that list."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.695, 0.3, 0.719], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.487, 0.783], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each spell description has a series of entries that provide the details needed to cast the spell. The following sections explain each of those entries, which follow a spell’s name."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.118, 0.794, 0.284, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting in Armor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.116, 0.814, 0.471, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You must have training with any armor you are wearing to cast spells while wearing it. You are otherwise too hampered by the armor for spellcasting."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.643, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Level"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.074, 0.897, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every spell has a level from 0 to 9, which is indicated in a spell’s description. A spell’s level is an indicator of how powerful it is. Cantrips—simple spells that can be cast almost by rote—are level 0. The rules for each spellcasting class say when its members gain access to spells of certain levels."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.174, 0.625, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Slots"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.907, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting is taxing, so a spellcaster can cast only a limited number of level 1+ spells before resting. Spell slots are the main way a spellcaster’s magical potential is represented. Each spellcasting class gives its members a limited number of spell slots of certain spell levels. For example, a level 3 Wizard has four level 1 spell slots and two level 2 slots."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.3, 0.909, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast a spell, you expend a slot of that spell’s level or higher, effectively “filling” a slot with the spell. Imagine a spell slot is a groove of a certain size—small for a level 1 slot and larger for a higher-level spell. A level 1 spell fits into a slot of any size, but a level 2 spell fits only into a slot that’s at least level 2. So when a level 3 Wizard casts Magic Missile, a level 1 spell, that Wizard spends one of four level 1 slots and has three remaining."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.438, 0.909, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Finishing a Long Rest restores any expended spell slots."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.476, 0.723, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting without Slots"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.495, 0.866, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "There are several ways to cast a spell without expending a spell slot:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.531, 0.87, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrips.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A cantrip is cast without a spell slot."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.548, 0.913, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rituals", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". Certain spells have the Ritual tag in the Casting Time entry. Such a spell can be cast following the normal rules for spellcasting, or it can be cast as a Ritual. The Ritual version of a spell takes 10 minutes longer to cast than normal, but it doesn’t expend a spell slot. To cast a spell as a Ritual, a spellcaster must have it prepared."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.655, 0.911, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Abilities.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some characters and monsters have special abilities that allow them to cast specific spells without a spell slot. This casting is usually limited in another way, such as being able to cast the spell a limited number of times per day."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.731, 0.895, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Items.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Spell Scrolls and some other magic items contain spells that can be cast without a spell slot. The description of such an item specifies how many times a spell can be cast from it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.8, 0.808, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.521, 0.818, 0.912, 0.911], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a spellcaster casts a spell using a slot that is of a higher level than the spell, the spell takes on the higher level for that casting. For instance, if a Wizard casts Magic Missile using a level 2 slot, that Magic Missile is level 2. Effectively, the spell expands to fill the slot it is put into."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "104"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 104, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.481, 0.098], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some spells, such as Magic Missile and Cure Wounds, have more powerful effects when cast at a higher level, as detailed in a spell’s description."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.103, 0.275, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "School of Magic"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.488, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each spell belongs to a school of magic. The schools are listed in the Schools of Magic table. These categories help describe spells but have no rules of their own, although some other rules refer to them."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.202, 0.246, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Schools of Magic"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.22, 0.487, 0.409], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.22, 0.487, 0.409], "content": "<table><tr><td>School</td><td>Typical Effects</td></tr><tr><td>Abjuration</td><td>Prevents or reverses harmful effects</td></tr><tr><td>Conjuration</td><td>Transports creatures or objects</td></tr><tr><td>Divination</td><td>Reveals information</td></tr><tr><td>Enchantment</td><td>Influences minds</td></tr><tr><td>Evocation</td><td>Channels energy to create effects that are often destructive</td></tr><tr><td>Illusion</td><td>Deceives the mind or senses</td></tr><tr><td>Necromancy</td><td>Manipulates life and death</td></tr><tr><td>Transmutation</td><td>Transforms creatures or objects</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.419, 0.277, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Class Spell Lists"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.1, 0.443, 0.466, 0.522], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a spell is on a class’s spell list, the class’s name appears in parentheses after the spell’s school of magic. Some features add a spell to a character’s spell list even if the character isn’t a member of a class in the parentheses."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.528, 0.25, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.551, 0.484, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most spells require the Magic action to cast, but some spells require a Bonus Action, a Reaction, or 1 minute or more. A spell’s Casting Time entry specifies which of those is required."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.621, 0.432, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Spell with a Spell Slot per Turn"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.64, 0.486, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a turn, you can expend only one spell slot to cast a spell. This rule means you can’t, for example, cast a spell with a spell slot using the Magic action and another one using a Bonus Action on the same turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.708, 0.432, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reaction and Bonus Action Triggers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.726, 0.487, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell that has a casting time of a Reaction is cast in response to a trigger that is defined in the spell’s Casting Time entry. Some spells that have a casting time of a Bonus Action are also cast in response to a trigger defined in the spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.81, 0.307, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Longer Casting Times"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.099, 0.828, 0.488, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Certain spells—including a spell cast as a Ritual—require more time to cast: minutes or even hours. While you cast a spell with a casting time of 1 minute or more, you must take the Magic action on each of your turns, and you must maintain Concentration (see “Rules Glossary”) while you do so. If"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.521, 0.05, 0.91, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "your Concentration is broken, the spell fails, but you don’t expend a spell slot. To cast the spell again, you must start over."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.104, 0.596, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.521, 0.127, 0.909, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell’s range indicates how far from the spellcaster the spell’s effect can originate, and the spell’s description specifies which part of the effect is limited by the range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.535, 0.189, 0.901, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A range usually takes one of the following forms:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.211, 0.83, 0.227], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Distance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The range is expressed in feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.227, 0.898, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Touch", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The spell’s effect originates on something, as defined by the spell, that the spellcaster must touch within their reach."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.273, 0.91, 0.304], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Self.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell is cast on the spellcaster or emanates from them, as specified in the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.309, 0.904, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a spell has movable effects, they aren’t restricted by its range unless the spell’s description says otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.364, 0.667, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.387, 0.908, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell’s components are physical requirements the spellcaster must meet to cast the spell. Each spell’s description indicates whether it requires Verbal (V), Somatic (S), or Material (M) components. If the spellcaster can’t provide one or more of a spell’s components, the spellcaster can’t cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.487, 0.625, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Verbal (V)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.505, 0.911, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Verbal component is the chanting of esoteric words that sound like nonsense to the uninitiated. The words must be uttered in a normal speaking voice. The words themselves aren’t the source of the spell’s power; rather, the particular combination of sounds, with specific pitch and resonance, sets the threads of magic in motion. Thus, a creature who is gagged or in an area of magical silence can’t cast a spell with a Verbal component."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.651, 0.634, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Somatic (S)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.669, 0.889, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Somatic component is a forceful gesticulation or an intricate set of gestures. A spellcaster must use at least one of their hands to perform these movements."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.737, 0.643, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Material (M)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.521, 0.755, 0.905, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Material component is a particular material used in a spell’s casting, as specified in parentheses in the Components entry. These materials aren’t consumed by the spell unless the spell’s description states otherwise. The spellcaster must have a hand free to access them, but it can be the same hand used to perform Somatic components, if any."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.863, 0.911, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a spell doesn’t consume its materials and doesn’t specify a cost for them, a spellcaster can use a Component Pouch (see “Equipment”) instead of providing the materials specified in the spell, or the"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "105"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 105, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.49, 0.144], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "spellcaster can substitute a Spellcasting Focus if the caster has a feature that allows that substitution. To use a Component Pouch, you must have a hand free to reach into it, and to use a Spellcasting Focus, you must hold it unless its description says otherwise (see “Equipment” for descriptions)."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.15, 0.205, 0.168], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.173, 0.492, 0.221], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell’s duration is the length of time the spell persists after it is cast. A duration typically takes one of the following forms:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.227, 0.49, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Concentration.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A duration that requires Concentration follows the Concentration rules (see “Rules Glossary”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.273, 0.481, 0.318], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instantaneous.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An instantaneous duration means the spell’s magic appears only for a moment and then disappears."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.319, 0.49, 0.442], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Time Span.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A duration that provides a time span specifies how long the spell lasts in rounds, minutes, hours, or the like. For example, a Duration entry might say “1 minute,” meaning the spell ends after 1 minute has passed. While a time-span spell that you cast is ongoing, you can dismiss it (no action required) if you don’t have the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.448, 0.181, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.1, 0.472, 0.482, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The effects of a spell are detailed after its duration entry. Those details present exactly what the spell does, which ignores mundane physical laws; any outcomes beyond those effects are under the GM’s purview. Whatever the effects, they typically deal with targets, saving throws, attack rolls, or all three, each of which is detailed below."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.588, 0.178, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Targets"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.606, 0.473, 0.667], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A typical spell requires the caster to pick one or more targets to be affected by the spell’s magic. A spell’s description says whether the spell targets creatures, objects, or something else."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.667, 0.482, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Clear Path to the Target.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " To target something with a spell, a caster must have a clear path to it, so it can’t be behind Total Cover."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.713, 0.477, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Targeting Yourself.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If a spell targets a creature of your choice, you can choose yourself unless the creature must be Hostile or specifically a creature other than you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.774, 0.481, 0.883], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Areas of Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some spells, such as Thunderwave, cover an area called an area of effect, which is defined in “Rules Glossary.” The area determines what the spell targets. The description of a spell specifies whether it has an area of effect, which is typically one of these shapes: Cone, Cube, Cylinder, Emanation, Line, or Sphere."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.902, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Awareness of Being Targeted.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Unless a spell has a perceptible effect, a creature doesn’t know it was targeted by the spell. An effect like lightning is obvious, but a more subtle effect, such as an attempt to read thoughts, goes unnoticed unless a spell’s description says otherwise."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.143, 0.907, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invalid Targets.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you cast a spell on someone or something that can’t be affected by it, nothing happens to that target, but if you used a spell slot to cast the spell, the slot is still expended."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.204, 0.907, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell normally has no effect on a target that succeeds on a saving throw, the invalid target appears to have succeeded on its saving throw, even though it didn’t attempt one (giving no hint that the creature is an invalid target). Otherwise, you perceive that the spell did nothing to the target."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.303, 0.662, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.321, 0.898, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Many spells specify that a target makes a saving throw to avoid some or all of a spell’s effects. The spell specifies the ability that the target uses for the save and what happens on a success or failure. Here’s how to calculate the DC for your spells:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.526, 0.406, 0.908, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell save DC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " = 8 + your spellcasting ability modifier + your Proficiency Bonus"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.445, 0.641, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Rolls"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.462, 0.906, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some spells require the caster to make an attack roll to determine whether the spell hits a target. Here’s how to calculate the attack modifier for your spells:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.545, 0.532, 0.89, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell attack modifier", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " = your spellcasting ability modifier + your Proficiency Bonus"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.571, 0.743, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combining Spell Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.588, 0.911, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The effects of different spells add together while their durations overlap. In contrast, the effects of the same spell cast multiple times don’t combine. Instead, the most potent effect—such as the highest bonus—from those castings applies while their durations overlap. The most recent effect applies if the castings are equally potent and their durations overlap. For example, if two Clerics cast Bless on the same target, that target gains the spell’s benefit only once; the target doesn’t receive two bonus dice. But if the durations of the spells overlap, the effect continues until the duration of the second Bless ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.538, 0.802, 0.809, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Identifying an Ongoing Spell"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.538, 0.821, 0.882, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can try to identify a non-instantaneous spell by its observable effects if its duration is ongoing. To identify it, you must take the Study action and succeed on a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "106"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 106, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.358, 0.076], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Descriptions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.078, 0.423, 0.175], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Acid Arrow", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Evocation (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (powdered rhubarb leaf) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.182, 0.485, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A shimmering green arrow streaks toward a target within range and bursts in a spray of acid. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 4d4 Acid damage and 2d4 Acid damage at the end of its next turn. On a miss, the arrow splashes the target with acid for half as much of the initial damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.289, 0.461, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage (both initial and later) increases by 1d4 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.344, 0.369, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Acid Splash", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.447, 0.488, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create an acidic bubble at a point within range, where it explodes in a 5-foot-radius Sphere. Each creature in that Sphere must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d6 Acid damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.509, 0.473, 0.556], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 when you reach levels 5 (2d6), 11 (3d6), and 17 (4d6)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.563, 0.141, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aid"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.58, 0.438, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.616, 0.407, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a strip of white cloth) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.682, 0.479, 0.728], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose up to three creatures within range. Each target’s Hit Point maximum and current Hit Points increase by 5 for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.728, 0.486, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target’s Hit Points increase by 5 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.768, 0.405, 0.864], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alarm", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Abjuration (Ranger, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bell and silver wire) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.871, 0.479, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You set an alarm against intrusion. Choose a door, a window, or an area within range that is no larger than a 20-foot Cube. Until the spell ends, an alarm"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.91, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "alerts you whenever a creature touches or enters the warded area. When you cast the spell, you can designate creatures that won’t set off the alarm. You also choose whether the alarm is audible or mental:"}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.118, 0.896, 0.164], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Audible Alarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The alarm produces the sound of a handbell for 10 seconds within 60 feet of the warded area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.165, 0.896, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mental Alarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are alerted by a mental ping if you are within 1 mile of the warded area. This ping awakens you if you’re asleep."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.219, 0.821, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alter Self", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.323, 0.907, 0.384], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You alter your physical form. Choose one of the following options. Its effects last for the duration, during which you can take a Magic action to replace the option you chose with a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.385, 0.905, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aquatic Adaptation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You sprout gills and grow webs between your fingers. You can breathe underwater and gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.431, 0.909, 0.614], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Change Appearance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You alter your appearance. You decide what you look like, including your height, weight, facial features, sound of your voice, hair length, coloration, and other distinguishing characteristics. You can make yourself appear as a member of another species, though none of your statistics change. You can’t appear as a creature of a different size, and your basic shape stays the same; if you’re bipedal, you can’t use this spell to become quadrupedal, for instance. For the duration, you can take a Magic action to change your appearance in this way again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.614, 0.902, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Natural Weapons.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You grow claws (Slashing), fangs (Piercing), horns (Piercing), or hooves (Bludgeoning). When you use your Unarmed Strike to deal damage with that new growth, it deals 1d6 damage of the type in parentheses instead of dealing the normal damage for your Unarmed Strike, and you use your spellcasting ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls rather than using Strength."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.76, 0.832, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animal Friendship", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.797, 0.801, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a morsel of food) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.864, 0.905, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Target a Beast that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. If you"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "107"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 107, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.483, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "or one of your allies deals damage to the target, the spells ends."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.488, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional Beast for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.12, 0.274, 0.137], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animal Messenger", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.137, 0.409, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.157, 0.379, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a morsel of food) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.224, 0.484, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Tiny Beast of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw, or it attempts to deliver a message for you (if the target’s Challenge Rating isn’t 0, it automatically succeeds). You specify a location you have visited and a recipient who matches a general description, such as “a person dressed in the uniform of the town guard” or “a red-haired dwarf wearing a pointed hat.” You also communicate a message of up to twenty-five words. The Beast travels for the duration toward the specified location, covering about 25 miles per 24 hours or 50 miles if the Beast can fly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.423, 0.489, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the Beast arrives, it delivers your message to the creature that you described, mimicking your communication. If the Beast doesn’t reach its destination before the spell ends, the message is lost, and the Beast returns to where you cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.5, 0.482, 0.546], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell’s duration increases by 48 hours for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.554, 0.241, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animal Shapes", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.571, 0.321, 0.587], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Transmutation (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.591, 0.256, 0.65], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.658, 0.484, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose any number of willing creatures that you can see within range. Each target shape-shifts into a Large or smaller Beast of your choice that has a Challenge Rating of 4 or lower. You can choose a different form for each target. On later turns, you can take a Magic action to transform the targets again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.75, 0.487, 0.888], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target’s game statistics are replaced by the chosen Beast’s statistics, but the target retains its creature type; Hit Points; Hit Point Dice; alignment; ability to communicate; and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The target’s actions are limited by the Beast form’s anatomy, and it can’t cast spells. The target’s equipment melds into the new form, and the target can’t use any of that equipment while in that form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.888, 0.475, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target gains a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the first form into"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.911, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "which it shape-shifts. These Temporary Hit Points vanish if any remain when the spell ends. The transformation lasts for the duration or until the target ends it as a Bonus Action."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.662, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animate Dead", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.785, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Necromancy (Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.156, 0.693, 0.172], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.172, 0.631, 0.187], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.187, 0.898, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of blood, a piece of flesh, and a pinch of bone dust) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.238, 0.901, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a pile of bones or a corpse of a Medium or Small Humanoid within range. The target becomes an Undead creature: a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Skeleton", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " if you chose bones or a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Zombie", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " if you chose a corpse (see “Monsters” for the stat blocks)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.316, 0.91, 0.514], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On each of your turns, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 60 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move on its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature takes the Dodge action and moves only to avoid harm. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.515, 0.907, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you’ve given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature again before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to four creatures you have animated with this spell rather than animating a new creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.638, 0.907, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You animate or reassert control over two additional Undead creatures for each spell slot level above 3. Each of the creatures must come from a different corpse or pile of bones."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.722, 0.684, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animate Objects", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.739, 0.862, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Transmutation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.76, 0.808, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.826, 0.912, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Objects animate at your command. Choose a number of nonmagical objects within range that aren’t being worn or carried, aren’t fixed to a surface, and aren’t Gargantuan. The maximum number of objects is equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; for this number, a Medium or smaller target counts as"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "108"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 108, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.486, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "one object, a Large target counts as two, and a Huge target counts as three."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.484, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each target animates, sprouts legs, and becomes a Construct that uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Animated Object", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block; this creature is under your control until the spell ends or until it is reduced to 0 Hit Points. Each creature you make with this spell is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count and takes its turn immediately after yours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.189, 0.487, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). If you issue no commands, the creature takes the Dodge action and moves only to avoid harm. When the creature drops to 0 Hit Points, it reverts to its object form, and any remaining damage carries over to that form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.342, 0.49, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The creature’s Slam damage increases by 1d4 (Medium or smaller), 1d6 (Large), or 1d12 (Huge) for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.415, 0.294, 0.435], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animated Object"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.44, 0.428, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Huge or Smaller Construct, Unaligned "}, {"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 15 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 (Medium or smaller), 20 (Large), 40 (Huge) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 ft."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.507, 0.487, 0.554], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.507, 0.487, 0.554], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 16 +3 +3</td><td>Dex 10 +0 +0</td><td>Con10 +0 +0</td></tr><tr><td>Int 3 -4 -4</td><td>Wis 3 -4 -4</td><td>Cha 1 -5 -5</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.564, 0.439, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immunities", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Poison, Psychic; Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Poisoned "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Senses", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Blindsight 30 ft.; Passive Perception 6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Understands the languages you know "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " None (XP 0; PB equals your Proficiency Bonus)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.649, 0.172, 0.665], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.67, 0.487, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slam.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. Hit: Force damage equal to 1d4 + 3 (Medium or smaller), 2d6 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Large), or 2d12 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Huge)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.754, 0.223, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Antilife Shell"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.771, 0.292, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Abjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.791, 0.371, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.858, 0.485, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An aura extends from you in a 10-foot Emanation for the duration. The aura prevents creatures other than Constructs and Undead from passing or reaching through it. An affected creature can cast spells"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.881, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "or make attacks with Ranged or Reach weapons through the barrier."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.081, 0.9, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you move so that an affected creature is forced to pass through the barrier, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.67, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Antimagic Field"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.772, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Abjuration (Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.157, 0.793, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (iron filings) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.224, 0.901, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An aura of antimagic surrounds you in 10-foot Emanation. No one can cast spells, take Magic actions, or create other magical effects inside the aura, and those things can’t target or otherwise affect anything inside it. Magical properties of magic items don’t work inside the aura or on anything inside it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.316, 0.899, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Areas of effect created by spells or other magic can’t extend into the aura, and no one can teleport into or out of it or use planar travel there. Portals close temporarily while in the aura."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.377, 0.907, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ongoing spells, except those cast by an Artifact or a deity, are suppressed in the area. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn’t function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.439, 0.905, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dispel Magic has no effect on the aura, and the auras created by different Antimagic Field spells don’t nullify each other."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.492, 0.711, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Antipathy/Sympathy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.51, 0.832, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.53, 0.679, 0.545], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.545, 0.632, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.559, 0.867, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a mix of vinegar and honey) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.597, 0.91, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As you cast the spell, choose whether it creates antipathy or sympathy, and target one creature or object that is Huge or smaller. Then specify a kind of creature, such as red dragons, goblins, or vampires. A creature of the chosen kind makes a Wisdom saving throw when it comes within 120 feet of the target. Your choice of antipathy or sympathy determines what happens to a creature when it fails that save:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.742, 0.902, 0.803], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Antipathy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The creature has the Frightened condition. The Frightened creature must use its movement on its turns to get as far away as possible from the target, moving by the safest route."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.803, 0.904, 0.911], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sympathy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The creature has the Charmed condition. The Charmed creature must use its movement on its turns to get as close as possible to the target, moving by the safest route. If the creature is within 5 feet of the target, the creature can’t willingly move away. If the target damages the Charmed creature, that creature can make a"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "109"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 109, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.115, 0.05, 0.455, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wisdom saving throw to end the effect, as described below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.489, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ending the Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the Frightened or Charmed creature ends its turn more than 120 feet away from the target, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is no longer affected by the target. A creature that successfully saves against this effect is immune to it for 1 minute, after which it can be affected again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.204, 0.212, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Eye", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.221, 0.302, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Divination (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.24, 0.371, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of bat fur) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.308, 0.483, 0.384], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create an Invisible, invulnerable eye within range that hovers for the duration. You mentally receive visual information from the eye, which can see in every direction. It also has Darkvision with a range of 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.384, 0.488, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can move the eye up to 30 feet in any direction. A solid barrier blocks the eye’s movement, but the eye can pass through an opening as small as 1 inch in diameter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.453, 0.228, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Hand", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.47, 0.364, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.49, 0.418, 0.55], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (an eggshell and a glove) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.558, 0.487, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a Large hand of shimmering magical energy in an unoccupied space that you can see within range. The hand lasts for the duration, and it moves at your command, mimicking the movements of your own hand."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.634, 0.481, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The hand is an object that has AC 20 and Hit Points equal to your Hit Point maximum. If it drops to 0 Hit Points, the spell ends. The hand doesn’t occupy its space."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.696, 0.48, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell and as a Bonus Action on your later turns, you can move the hand up to 60 feet and then cause one of the following effects:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.748, 0.474, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clenched Fist.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The hand strikes a target within 5 feet of it. Make a melee spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 5d8 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.795, 0.487, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Forceful Hand.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The hand attempts to push a Huge or smaller creature within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw, or the hand pushes the target up to 5 feet plus a number of feet equal to five times your spellcasting ability modifier. The hand moves with the target, remaining within 5 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.905, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grasping Hand.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The hand attempts to grapple a Huge or smaller creature within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw, or the target has the Grappled condition, with an escape DC equal to your spell save DC. While the hand grapples the target, you can take a Bonus Action to cause the hand to crush it, dealing Bludgeoning damage to the target equal to 4d6 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.189, 0.906, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interposing Hand.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The hand grants you Half Cover against attacks and other effects that originate from its space or that pass through it. In addition, its space counts as Difficult Terrain for your enemies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.271, 0.912, 0.334], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage of the Clenched Fist increases by 2d8 and the damage of the Grasping Hand increases by 2d6 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.341, 0.647, 0.358], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Lock", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.358, 0.727, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.377, 0.68, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.394, 0.626, 0.409], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.408, 0.892, 0.437], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (gold dust worth 25+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.437, 0.7, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.46, 0.908, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a closed door, window, gate, container, or hatch and magically lock it for the duration. This lock can’t be unlocked by any nonmagical means. You and any creatures you designate when you cast the spell can open and close the object despite the lock. You can also set a password that, when spoken within 5 feet of the object, unlocks it for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.575, 0.659, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcane Sword", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.593, 0.762, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Evocation (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.612, 0.68, 0.629], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.628, 0.632, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.85, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a miniature sword worth 250+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.672, 0.808, 0.687], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.694, 0.873, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a spectral sword that hovers within range. It lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.726, 0.902, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the sword appears, you make a melee spell attack against a target within 5 feet of the sword. On a hit, the target takes Force damage equal to 4d12 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.787, 0.91, 0.848], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On your later turns, you can take a Bonus Action to move the sword up to 30 feet to a spot you can see and repeat the attack against the same target or a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.856, 0.727, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcanist’s Magic Aura", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Illusion (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "110"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 110, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.405, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a small square of silk) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.087, 0.487, 0.195], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a touch, you place an illusion on a willing creature or an object that isn’t being worn or carried. A creature gains the Mask effect below, and an object gains the False Aura effect below. The effect lasts for the duration. If you cast the spell on the same target every day for 30 days, the illusion lasts until dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.195, 0.487, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mask (Creature).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose a creature type other than the target’s actual type. Spells and other magical effects treat the target as if it were a creature of the chosen type."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.1, 0.257, 0.49, 0.364], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "False Aura (Object).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You change the way the target appears to spells and magical effects that detect magical auras, such as Detect Magic. You can make a nonmagical object appear magical, make a magic item appear nonmagical, or change the object’s aura so that it appears to belong to a school of magic you choose."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.372, 0.263, 0.389], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Astral Projection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.389, 0.429, 0.406], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Necromancy (Cleric, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.409, 0.258, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.424, 0.209, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.439, 0.484, 0.483], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (for each of the spell’s targets, one jacinth worth 1,000+ GP and one silver bar worth 100+ GP, all of which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.483, 0.278, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.506, 0.488, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and up to eight willing creatures within range project your astral bodies into the Astral Plane (the spell ends instantly if you are already on that plane). Each target’s body is left behind in a state of suspended animation; it has the Unconscious condition, doesn’t need food or air, and doesn’t age."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.598, 0.49, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target’s astral form resembles its body in almost every way, replicating its game statistics and possessions. The principal difference is the addition of a silvery cord that trails from between the shoulder blades of the astral form. The cord fades from view after 1 foot. If the cord is cut—which happens only when an effect states that it does so—the target’s body and astral form both die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.481, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target’s astral form can travel through the Astral Plane. The moment an astral form leaves that plane, the target’s body and possessions travel along the silver cord, causing the target to re-enter its body on the new plane."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.797, 0.484, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any damage or other effects that apply to an astral form have no effect on the target’s body and vice versa. If a target’s body or astral form drops to 0 Hit Points, the spell ends for that target. The spell ends for all the targets if you take a Magic action to dismiss it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.899, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends for a target who isn’t dead, the target reappears in its body and exits the state of suspended animation."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.105, 0.597, 0.122], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Augury"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.121, 0.818, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Divination (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.141, 0.756, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.156, 0.608, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.171, 0.887, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (specially marked sticks, bones, cards, or other divinatory tokens worth 25+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.201, 0.698, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.223, 0.908, 0.286], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You receive an omen from an otherworldly entity about the results of a course of action that you plan to take within the next 30 minutes. The GM chooses the omen from the Omens table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.298, 0.59, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Omens"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.526, 0.316, 0.91, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.526, 0.316, 0.91, 0.41], "content": "<table><tr><td>Omen</td><td>For Results That Will Be</td></tr><tr><td>Weal</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Woe</td><td>Bad</td></tr><tr><td>Weal and woe</td><td>Good and bad</td></tr><tr><td>Indifference</td><td>Neither good nor bad</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.419, 0.91, 0.45], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell doesn’t account for circumstances, such as other spells, that might change the results."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.45, 0.904, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you cast the spell more than once before finishing a Long Rest, there is a cumulative 25 percent chance for each casting after the first that you get no answer."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.519, 0.638, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aura of Life"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.536, 0.773, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.556, 0.68, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.571, 0.609, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.586, 0.642, 0.601], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.6, 0.822, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.623, 0.912, 0.717], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An aura radiates from you in a 30-foot Emanation for the duration. While in the aura, you and your allies have Resistance to Necrotic damage, and your Hit Point maximums can’t be reduced. If an ally with 0 Hit Points starts its turn in the aura, that ally regains 1 Hit Point."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.724, 0.604, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Awaken"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.523, 0.741, 0.785, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Transmutation (Bard, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.76, 0.687, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.776, 0.627, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.79, 0.906, 0.821], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (an agate worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.82, 0.698, 0.835], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.842, 0.901, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You spend the casting time tracing magical pathways within a precious gemstone, and then touch the target. The target must be either a Beast or Plant creature with an Intelligence of 3 or less or a natural plant that isn’t a creature. The target gains"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.032, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "111"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 111, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.481, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "an Intelligence of 10 and the ability to speak one language you know. If the target is a natural plant, it becomes a Plant creature and gains the ability to move its limbs, roots, vines, creepers, and so forth, and it gains senses similar to a human’s. The GM chooses statistics appropriate for the awakened Plant, such as the statistics for the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Awakened Shrub", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " or "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Awakened Tree", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " in “Monsters.”"}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.173, 0.484, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The awakened target has the Charmed condition for 30 days or until you or your allies deal damage to it. When that condition ends, the awakened creature chooses its attitude toward you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.243, 0.154, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bane"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.26, 0.418, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric, Warlock) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of blood) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.347, 0.49, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Up to three creatures of your choice that you can see within range must each make a Charisma saving throw. Whenever a target that fails this save makes an attack roll or a saving throw before the spell ends, the target must subtract 1d4 from the attack roll or save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.439, 0.468, 0.485], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.492, 0.215, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Banishment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.51, 0.479, 0.541], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.545, 0.385, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pentacle) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.612, 0.483, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature that you can see within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be transported to a harmless demiplane for the duration. While there, the target has the Incapacitated condition. When the spell ends, the target reappears in the space it left or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.475, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target is an Aberration, a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend, the target doesn’t return if the spell lasts for 1 minute. The target is instead transported to a random location on a plane (GM’s choice) associated with its creature type."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.796, 0.468, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.85, 0.187, 0.867], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Barkskin"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.868, 0.379, 0.885], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.887, 0.303, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.794, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a handful of bark) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.087, 0.893, 0.15], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature. Until the spell ends, the target’s skin assumes a bark-like appearance, and the target has an Armor Class of 17 if its AC is lower than that."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.158, 0.809, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beacon of Hope", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Abjuration (Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.262, 0.908, 0.34], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose any number of creatures within range. For the duration, each target has Advantage on Wisdom saving throws and Death Saving Throws and regains the maximum number of Hit Points possible from any healing."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.346, 0.657, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Befuddlement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.364, 0.898, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.384, 0.842, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a key ring with no keys) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.451, 0.904, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You blast the mind of a creature that you can see within range. The target makes an Intelligence saving throw."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.497, 0.904, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, the target takes 10d12 Psychic damage and can’t cast spells or take the Magic action. At the end of every 30 days, the target repeats the save, ending the effect on a success. The effect can also be ended by the Greater Restoration, Heal, or Wish spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.589, 0.909, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.627, 0.827, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bestow Curse", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Necromancy (Bard, Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.665, 0.808, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.731, 0.905, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature, which must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become cursed for the duration. Until the curse ends, the target suffers one of the following effects of your choice:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.8, 0.896, 0.846], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Choose one ability. The target has Disadvantage on ability checks and saving throws made with that ability."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.846, 0.865, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The target has Disadvantage on attack rolls against you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.877, 0.907, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In combat, the target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw at the start of each of its turns or be forced to take the Dodge action on that turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "112"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 112, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.05, 0.468, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• If you deal damage to the target with an attack roll or a spell, the target takes an extra 1d8 Necrotic damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.487, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you cast this spell using a level 4 spell slot, you can maintain Concentration on it for up to 10 minutes. If you use a level 5+ spell slot, the spell doesn’t require Concentration, and the duration becomes 8 hours (level 5–6 slot) or 24 hours (level 7–8 slot). If you use a level 9 spell slot, the spell lasts until dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.387, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Black Tentacles", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Conjuration (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a tentacle) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.323, 0.48, 0.384], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Squirming, ebony tentacles fill a 20-foot square on ground that you can see within range. For the duration, these tentacles turn the ground in that area into Difficult Terrain."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.384, 0.489, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature in that area makes a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 3d6 Bludgeoning damage, and it has the Restrained condition until the spell ends. A creature also makes that save if it enters the area or ends it turn there. A creature makes that save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.476, 0.484, 0.523], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Restrained creature can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC, ending the condition on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.53, 0.4, 0.628], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blade Barrier", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Evocation (Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.634, 0.488, 0.742], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a wall of whirling blades made of magical energy. The wall appears within range and lasts for the duration. You make a straight wall up to 100 feet long, 20 feet high, and 5 feet thick, or a ringed wall up to 60 feet in diameter, 20 feet high, and 5 feet thick. The wall provides Three-Quarters Cover, and its space is Difficult Terrain."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.742, 0.483, 0.835], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature in the wall’s space makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 6d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature also makes that save if it enters the wall’s space or ends it turn there. A creature makes that save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.841, 0.37, 0.91], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bless", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Cleric, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.878, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a Holy Symbol worth 5+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.91, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You bless up to three creatures within range. Whenever a target makes an attack roll or a saving throw before the spell ends, the target adds 1d4 to the attack roll or save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.149, 0.89, 0.195], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.204, 0.856, 0.252], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blight", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Necromancy (Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.256, 0.696, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.323, 0.902, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that you can see within range makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 8d8 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A Plant creature automatically fails the save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.4, 0.908, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, target a nonmagical plant that isn’t a creature, such as a tree or shrub. It doesn’t make a save; it simply withers and dies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.446, 0.897, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.484, 0.702, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blindness/Deafness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.501, 0.909, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.589, 0.906, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature that you can see within range must succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or it has the Blinded or Deafened condition (your choice) for the duration. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.681, 0.89, 0.727], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.735, 0.821, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blink", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.839, 0.909, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Roll 1d6 at the end of each of your turns for the duration. On a roll of 4–6, you vanish from your current plane of existence and appear in the Ethereal Plane (the spell ends instantly if you are already on that plane). While on the Ethereal Plane, you can"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "113"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 113, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.479, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "perceive the plane you left, which is cast in shades of gray, but you can’t see anything there more than 60 feet away. You can affect and be affected only by other creatures on the Ethereal Plane, and creatures on the other plane can’t perceive you unless they have a special ability that lets them perceive things on the Ethereal Plane."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.482, 0.267], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You return to the other plane at the start of your next turn and when the spell ends if you are on the Ethereal Plane. You return to an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of the space you left. If no unoccupied space is available within that range, you appear in the nearest unoccupied space."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.273, 0.148, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blur"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.29, 0.345, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Illusion (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.31, 0.385, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.377, 0.472, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your body becomes blurred. For the duration, any creature has Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. An attacker is immune to this effect if it perceives you with Blindsight or Truesight."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.446, 0.241, 0.463], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burning Hands"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.464, 0.364, 0.48], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.484, 0.274, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.55, 0.487, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A thin sheet of flames shoots forth from you. Each creature in a 15-foot Cone makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.612, 0.471, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flammable objects in the Cone that aren’t being worn or carried start burning."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.643, 0.474, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.681, 0.233, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Call Lightning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.699, 0.3, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.719, 0.399, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.786, 0.478, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A storm cloud appears at a point within range that you can see above yourself. It takes the shape of a Cylinder that is 10 feet tall with a 60-foot radius."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.833, 0.49, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, choose a point you can see under the cloud. A lightning bolt shoots from the cloud to that point. Each creature within 5 feet of that point makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d10 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.91, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to call down lightning in that way again, targeting the same point or a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.904, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you’re outdoors in a storm when you cast this spell, the spell gives you control over that storm instead of creating a new one. Under such conditions, the spell’s damage increases by 1d10."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.158, 0.896, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.196, 0.668, 0.213], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Calm Emotions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.215, 0.808, 0.293], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.3, 0.909, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each Humanoid in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point you choose within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be affected by one of the following effects (choose for each creature):"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.369, 0.906, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature has Immunity to the Charmed and Frightened conditions until the spell ends. If the creature was already Charmed or Frightened, those conditions are suppressed for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.431, 0.912, 0.508], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature becomes Indifferent about creatures of your choice that it’s Hostile toward. This indifference ends if the target takes damage or witnesses its allies taking damage. When the spell ends, the creature’s attitude returns to normal."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.514, 0.672, 0.532], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chain Lightning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.532, 0.785, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.552, 0.796, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (three silver pins) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.619, 0.901, 0.711], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You launch a lightning bolt toward a target you can see within range. Three bolts then leap from that target to as many as three other targets of your choice, each of which must be within 30 feet of the first target. A target can be a creature or an object and can be targeted by only one of the bolts."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.711, 0.899, 0.757], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d8 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.757, 0.905, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " One additional bolt leaps from the first target to another target for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.811, 0.673, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Charm Monster", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.829, 0.902, 0.859], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.863, 0.679, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "114"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 114, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.491, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature you can see within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. It does so with Advantage if you or your allies are fighting it. On a failed save, the target has the Charmed condition until the spell ends or until you or your allies damage it. The Charmed creature is Friendly to you. When the spell ends, the target knows it was Charmed by you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.158, 0.469, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.211, 0.481, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Charm Person", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.331, 0.49, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Humanoid you can see within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. It does so with Advantage if you or your allies are fighting it. On a failed save, the target has the Charmed condition until the spell ends or until you or your allies damage it. The Charmed creature is Friendly to you. When the spell ends, the target knows it was Charmed by you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.439, 0.467, 0.485], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.492, 0.452, 0.527], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chill Touch", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Necromancy Cantrip (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.531, 0.295, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.598, 0.488, 0.66], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Channeling the chill of the grave, make a melee spell attack against a target within reach. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 Necrotic damage, and it can’t regain Hit Points until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.66, 0.482, 0.707], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 when you reach levels 5 (2d10), 11 (3d10), and 17 (4d10)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.714, 0.364, 0.748], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chromatic Orb", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.751, 0.438, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 50+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.818, 0.479, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hurl an orb of energy at a target within range. Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder for the type of orb you create, and then make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 3d8 damage of the chosen type."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.895, 0.468, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you roll the same number on two or more of the d8s, the orb leaps to a different target of your"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.91, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "choice within 30 feet of the target. Make an attack roll against the new target, and make a new damage roll. The orb can’t leap again unless you cast the spell with a level 2+ spell slot."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.112, 0.907, 0.19], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 1. The orb can leap a maximum number of times equal to the level of the slot expended, and a creature can be targeted only once by each casting of this spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.196, 0.668, 0.213], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ci l f D h rc e o eat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.202, 0.89, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (the powder of a crushed black pearl worth 500+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.316, 0.903, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Negative energy ripples out in a 60-foot-radius Sphere from a point you choose within range. Each creature in that area makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 8d8 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.392, 0.897, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 2d8 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.525, 0.431, 0.647, 0.447], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clairvoyance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.448, 0.878, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.468, 0.707, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.483, 0.624, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 mile"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.497, 0.898, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a focus worth 100+ GP, either a jeweled horn for hearing or a glass eye for seeing) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.55, 0.907, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create an Invisible sensor within range in a location familiar to you (a place you have visited or seen before) or in an obvious location that is unfamiliar to you (such as behind a door, around a corner, or in a grove of trees). The intangible, invulnerable sensor remains in place for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.642, 0.908, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, choose seeing or hearing. You can use the chosen sense through the sensor as if you were in its space. As a Bonus Action, you can switch between seeing and hearing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.703, 0.911, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that sees the sensor (such as a creature benefiting from See Invisibility or Truesight) sees a luminous orb about the size of your fist."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.757, 0.739, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clone", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 8 Necromancy (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.794, 0.68, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.525, 0.809, 0.625, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.824, 0.901, 0.897], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes, and a sealable vessel worth 2,000+ GP that is large enough to hold the creature being cloned) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "115"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 115, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.488, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature or at least 1 cubic inch of its flesh. An inert duplicate of that creature forms inside the vessel used in the spell’s casting and finishes growing after 120 days; you choose whether the finished clone is the same age as the creature or younger. The clone remains inert and endures i"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ndef", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "initely while its vessel remains undisturbed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.477, 0.281], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the original creature dies after the clone finishes forming, the creature’s soul transfers to the clone if the soul is free and willing to return. The clone is physically identical to the original and has the same personality, memories, and abilities, but none of the original’s equipment. The creature’s original remains, if any, become inert and can’t be revived, since the creature’s soul is elsewhere."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.288, 0.19, 0.304], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloudkill"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.306, 0.399, 0.385], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.393, 0.49, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of yellow-green fog centered on a point within range. The fog lasts for the duration or until strong wind (such as the one created by Gust of Wind) disperses it, ending the spell. Its area is Heavily Obscured."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.469, 0.484, 0.576], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature in the Sphere makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 5d8 Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature must also make this save when the Sphere moves into its space and when it enters the Sphere or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.577, 0.468, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Sphere moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.607, 0.474, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.646, 0.217, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Color Spray"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.663, 0.387, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.683, 0.423, 0.742], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of colorful sand) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.749, 0.488, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You launch a dazzling array of flashing, colorful light. Each creature in a 15-foot Cone originating from you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the Blinded condition until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.835, 0.412, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Command", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.696, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components: V Duration: Instantaneous"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.909, 0.151], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You speak a one-word command to a creature you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or follow the command on its next turn. Choose the command from these options:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.156, 0.912, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Approach.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target moves toward you by the shortest and most direct route, ending its turn if it moves within 5 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.203, 0.896, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Drop.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target drops whatever it is holding and then ends its turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.233, 0.905, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flee.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target spends its turn moving away from you by the fastest available means."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.264, 0.91, 0.293], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grovel.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target has the Prone condition and then ends its turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.295, 0.905, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Halt.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " On its turn, the target doesn’t move and takes no action or Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.331, 0.886, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can affect one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.386, 0.625, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Commune"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.403, 0.712, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Divination (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.423, 0.753, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (incense) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.49, 0.89, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You contact a deity or a divine proxy and ask up to three questions that can be answered with yes or no. You must ask your questions before the spell ends. You receive a correct answer for each question."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.567, 0.912, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divine beings aren’t necessarily omniscient, so you might receive “unclear” as an answer if a question pertains to information that lies beyond the deity’s knowledge. In a case where a one-word answer could be misleading or contrary to the deity’s interests, the GM might offer a short phrase as an answer instead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.674, 0.904, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you cast the spell more than once before finishing a Long Rest, there is a cumulative 25 percent chance for each casting after the first that you get no answer."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.743, 0.77, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Commune with Nature", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Divination (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.78, 0.756, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.848, 0.911, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You commune with nature spirits and gain knowledge of the surrounding area. In the outdoors, the spell gives you knowledge of the area within 3 miles of you. In caves and other natural underground settings, the radius is limited to 300 feet. The spell"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "116"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 116, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.486, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "doesn’t function where nature has been replaced by construction, such as in castles and s"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ettlements", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.081, 0.455, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose three of the following facts; you learn those facts as they pertain to the spell’s area:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.119, 0.307, 0.133], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Locations of settlements"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.134, 0.475, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Locations of portals to other planes of existence"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.15, 0.468, 0.195], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Location of one Challenge Rating 10+ creature (GM’s choice) that is a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, a Fiend, or an Undead"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.195, 0.452, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The most prevalent kind of plant, mineral, or Beast (you choose which to learn)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.226, 0.333, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Locations of bodies of water"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.247, 0.479, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For example, you could determine the location of a powerful monster in the area, the locations of bodies of water, and the locations of any towns."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.303, 0.325, 0.319], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Comprehend Languages"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.32, 0.475, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Divination (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.339, 0.321, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.354, 0.187, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.369, 0.421, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of soot and salt) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.406, 0.484, 0.514], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you understand the literal meaning of any language that you hear or see signed. You also understand any written language that you see, but you must be touching the surface on which the words are written. It takes about 1 minute to read one page of text. This spell doesn’t decode symbols or secret messages."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.521, 0.216, 0.538], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Compulsion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.539, 0.305, 0.555], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Enchantment (Bard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.559, 0.386, 0.618], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.626, 0.488, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.672, 0.484, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you can take a Bonus Action to designate a direction that is horizontal to you. Each Charmed target must use as much of its movement as possible to move in that direction on its next turn, taking the safest route. After moving in this way, a target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.787, 0.229, 0.803], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cone of Cold"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.804, 0.412, 0.821], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.825, 0.453, 0.885], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a small crystal or glass cone) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.101, 0.891, 0.452, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You unleash a blast of cold air. Each creature in a 60-foot Cone originating from you makes a"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.904, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Constitution saving throw, taking 8d8 Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature killed by this spell becomes a frozen statue until it thaws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.112, 0.897, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage in"}, {"type": "text", "content": "creases", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.622, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Confusion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.168, 0.898, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Enchantment (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.188, 0.68, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.203, 0.632, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.217, 0.793, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (three nut shells)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.233, 0.807, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.91, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature in a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point you choose within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw, or that target can’t take Bonus Actions or Reactions and must roll 1d10 at the start of each of its turns to determine its behavior for that turn, consulting the table below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.534, 0.352, 0.738, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d10 Behavior for the Turn", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.544, 0.371, 0.902, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target doesn’t take an action, and it uses all its movement to move. Roll 1d4 for the direction: 1, north; 2, east; 3, south; or 4, west."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.536, 0.423, 0.856, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2–6 The target doesn’t move or take actions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.534, 0.441, 0.885, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "7–8 The target doesn’t move, and it takes the Attack action to make one melee attack against a random creature within reach. If none are within reach, the target takes no action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.532, 0.509, 0.797, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "9–10 The target chooses its behavior."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.534, 0.895, 0.579], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the end of each of its turns, an affected target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.523, 0.58, 0.887, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Sphere’s radius increases by 5 feet for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.524, 0.634, 0.682, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Animals"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.651, 0.779, 0.668], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.524, 0.671, 0.68, 0.687], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.524, 0.686, 0.632, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.524, 0.701, 0.656, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.524, 0.715, 0.822, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.522, 0.738, 0.905, 0.815], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure nature spirits that appear as a Large pack of spectral, intangible animals in an unoccupied space you can see within range. The pack lasts for the duration, and you choose the spirits’ animal form, such as wolves, serpents, or birds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.522, 0.815, 0.91, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Advantage on Strength saving throws while you’re within 5 feet of the pack, and when you move on your turn, you can also move the pack up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 47, "bbox": [0.522, 0.876, 0.911, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever the pack moves within 10 feet of a creature you can see and whenever a creature you can see enters a space within 10 feet of the pack or ends"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 48, "bbox": [0.032, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "117"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 49, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 117, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.485, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "its turn there, you can force that creature to make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d10 Slashing damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.112, 0.475, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.15, 0.399, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Celestial", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 7 Conjuration (Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.255, 0.489, 0.332], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a spirit from the Upper Planes, which manifests as a pillar of light in a 10-foot-radius, 40-foot-high Cylinder centered on a point within range. For each creature you can see in the Cylinder, choose which of these lights shines on it:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.338, 0.487, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healing Light.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target regains Hit Points equal to 4d12 plus your spellcasting ability modifier. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Searing Light.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 6d12 Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.422, 0.49, 0.468], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, Bright Light fills the Cylinder, and when you move on your turn, you can also move the Cylinder up to 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.468, 0.479, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever the Cylinder moves into the space of a creature you can see and whenever a creature you can see enters the Cylinder or ends its turn there, you can bathe it in one of the lights. A creature can be affected by this spell only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.544, 0.478, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing and damage increase by 1d12 for each spell slot level above 7."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.598, 0.278, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.616, 0.358, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Conjuration (Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.636, 0.399, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.703, 0.481, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a Large, intangible spirit from the Elemental Planes that appears in an unoccupied space within range. Choose the spirit’s element, which determines its damage type: air (Lightning), earth (Thunder), fire (Fire), or water (Cold). The spirit lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.795, 0.488, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever a creature you can see enters the spirit’s space or starts its turn within 5 feet of the spirit, you can force that creature to make a Dexterity saving throw if the spirit has no creature Restrained. On failed save, the target takes 8d8 damage of the spirit’s type, and the target has the Restrained condition until the spell ends. At the start of each of its turns, the Restrained target repeats the save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.905, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, the target takes 4d8 damage of the spirit’s type. On a successful save, the target isn’t Restrained by the spirit."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.096, 0.896, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.136, 0.822, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Fey", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Conjuration (Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.24, 0.903, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a Medium spirit from the Feywild in an unoccupied space you can see within range. The spirit lasts for the duration, and it looks like a Fey creature of your choice. When the spirit appears, you can make one melee spell attack against a creature within 5 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes Psychic damage equal to 3d12 plus your spellcasting ability modifier, and the target has the Frightened condition until the start of your next turn, with both you and the spirit as the source of the fear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.409, 0.895, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action on your later turns, you can teleport the spirit to an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of the space it left and make the attack against a creature within 5 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.469, 0.895, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d12 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.508, 0.781, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Minor Elementals", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Conjuration (Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.546, 0.821, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.908, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure spirits from the Elemental Planes that flit around you in a 15-foot Emanation for the duration. Until the spell ends, any attack you make deals an extra 2d8 damage when you hit a creature in the Emanation. This damage is Acid, Cold, Fire, or Lightning (your choice when you make the attack)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.704, 0.898, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, the ground in the Emanation is Difficult Terrain for your enemies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.735, 0.896, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.773, 0.779, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjure Woodland Beings", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.811, 0.821, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.878, 0.897, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure nature spirits that flit around you in a 10-foot Emanation for the duration. Whenever the Emanation enters the space of a creature you can"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "118"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 118, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.489, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "see and whenever a creature you can see enters the Emanation or ends its turn there, you can force that creature to make a Wisdom saving throw. The creature takes 5d8 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.143, 0.488, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, you can take the Disengage action as a Bonus Action for the spell’s duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.173, 0.475, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.211, 0.298, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Contact Other Plane", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.229, 0.368, 0.246], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Divination (Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.248, 0.333, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.484, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You mentally contact a demigod, the spirit of a longdead sage, or some other knowledgeable entity from another plane. Contacting this otherworldly intelligence can break your mind. When you cast this spell, make a DC 15 Intelligence saving throw. On a successful save, you can ask the entity up to five questions. You must ask your questions before the spell ends. The GM answers each question with one word, such as “yes,” “no,” “maybe,” “never,” “irrelevant,” or “unclear” (if the entity doesn’t know the answer to the question). If a one-word answer would be misleading, the GM might instead offer a short phrase as an answer."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.488, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, you take 6d6 Psychic damage and have the Incapacitated condition until you finish a Long Rest. A Greater Restoration spell cast on you ends this effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.585, 0.202, 0.601], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Contagion", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.602, 0.351, 0.618], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Necromancy (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.622, 0.257, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 7 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.689, 0.485, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your touch inflicts a magical contagion. The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 11d8 Necrotic damage and have the Poisoned condition. Also, choose one ability when you cast the spell. While Poisoned, the target has Disadvantage on saving throws made with the chosen ability."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.781, 0.485, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target must repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns until it gets three successes or failures. If the target succeeds on three of these saves, the spell ends on the target. If the target fails three of the saves, the spell lasts for 7 days on it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.857, 0.487, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever the Poisoned target receives an effect that would end the Poisoned condition, the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or the Poisoned condition doesn’t end on it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.882, 0.163], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Contingency", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Abjuration (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a gem-encrusted statuette of yourself worth 1,500+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.169, 0.904, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a spell of level 5 or lower that you can cast, that has a casting time of an action, and that can target you. You cast that spell—called the contingent spell—as part of casting Contingency, expending spell slots for both, but the contingent spell doesn’t come into effect. Instead, it takes effect when a certain trigger occurs. You describe that trigger when you cast the two spells. For example, a Contingency cast with Water Breathing might stip ulate that Water Breathing comes into effect when you are engulfed in water or a similar liquid."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.339, 0.902, 0.385], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The contingent spell takes effect immediately after the trigger occurs for the first time, whether or not you want it to, and then Contingency ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.385, 0.909, 0.478], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The contingent spell takes effect only on you, even if it can normally target others. You can use only one Contingency spell at a time. If you cast this spell again, the effect of another Contingency spell on you ends. Also, Contingency ends on you if its material component is ever not on your person."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.484, 0.678, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Continual Flame", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.502, 0.814, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.521, 0.679, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.537, 0.625, 0.552], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.551, 0.893, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (ruby dust worth 50+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.581, 0.7, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.603, 0.91, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A flame springs from an object that you touch. The effect casts Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet. It looks like a regular flame, but it creates no heat and consumes no fuel. The flame can be covered or hidden but not smothered or quenched."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.703, 0.665, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Control Water", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.72, 0.848, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.74, 0.679, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.756, 0.639, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.771, 0.875, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a mixture of water and dust) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.808, 0.906, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you control any water inside an area you choose that is a Cube up to 100 feet on a side, using one of the following effects. As a Magic action on your later turns, you can repeat the same effect or choose a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.884, 0.912, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flood.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause the water level of all standing water in the area to rise by as much as 20 feet. If you"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.06, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "119"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 119, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.486, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "choose an area in a large body of water, you instead create a 20-foot tall wave that travels from one side of the area to the other and then crashes. Any Huge or smaller vehicles in the wave’s path are carried with it to the other side. Any Huge or smaller vehicles struck by the wave have a 25 percent chance of capsizing."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.475, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The water level remains elevated until the spell ends or you choose a different effect. If this effect produced a wave, the wave repeats on the start of your next turn while the flood effect lasts."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.489, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Part Water.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You part water in the area and create a trench. The trench extends across the spell’s area, and the separated water forms a wall to either side. The trench remains until the spell ends or you choose a different effect. The water then slowly fills in the trench over the course of the next round until the normal water level is restored."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.488, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Redirect Flow.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause flowing water in the area to move in a direction you choose, even if the water has to flow over obstacles, up walls, or in other unlikely directions. The water in the area moves as you direct it, but once it moves beyond the spell’s area, it resumes its flow based on the terrain. The water continues to move in the direction you chose until the spell ends or you choose a different effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.464, 0.484, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whirlpool.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause a whirlpool to form in the center of the area, which must be at least 50 feet square and 25 feet deep. The whirlpool lasts until you choose a different effect or the spell ends. The whirlpool is 5 feet wide at the base, up to 50 feet wide at the top, and 25 feet tall. Any creature in the water and within 25 feet of the whirlpool is pulled 10 feet toward it. When a creature enters the whirlpool for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there, it makes a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 2d8 Bludgeoning damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage. A creature can swim away from the whirlpool only if it first takes an action to pull away and succeeds on a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.717, 0.266, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Control Weather"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.734, 0.427, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.754, 0.287, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.77, 0.187, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.784, 0.373, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (burning incense)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.799, 0.378, 0.814], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.822, 0.475, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You take control of the weather within 5 miles of you for the duration. You must be outdoors to cast this spell, and it ends early if you go indoors."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.869, 0.472, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, you change the current weather conditions, which are determined by the GM. You can change precipitation, temperature, and wind. It takes 1d4 × 10 minutes for the new"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.895, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "conditions to take effect. Once they do so, you can change the conditions again. When the spell ends, the weather gradually returns to normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.912, 0.16], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you change the weather conditions, find a current condition on the following tables and change its stage by one, up or down. When changing the wind, you can change its direction."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.171, 0.637, 0.187], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Precipitation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.526, 0.19, 0.91, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.526, 0.19, 0.91, 0.303], "content": "<table><tr><td>Stage</td><td>Condition</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Clear</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Light clouds</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Overcast or ground fog</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Rain, hail, or snow</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Torrential rain, driving hail, or blizzard</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.325, 0.905, 0.459], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.325, 0.905, 0.459], "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Temperature</td><td colspan=\"2\">Wind</td></tr><tr><td>Stage</td><td>Condition</td><td>Stage</td><td>Condition</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Heat wave</td><td>I</td><td>Calm</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Hot</td><td>2</td><td>Moderate wind</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Warm</td><td>3</td><td>Strong wind</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Cool</td><td>4</td><td>Gale</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Cold</td><td>5</td><td>Storm</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.486, 0.647, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Counterspell"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.503, 0.857, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Abjuration (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.523, 0.906, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reaction, which you take when you see a creature within 60 feet of yourself casting a spell with Verbal, Somatic, or Material components"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.567, 0.632, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.583, 0.64, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.598, 0.696, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.619, 0.913, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to interrupt a creature in the process of casting a spell. The creature makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the spell dissipates with no effect, and the action, Bonus Action, or Reaction used to cast it is wasted. If that spell was cast with a spell slot, the slot isn’t expended."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.72, 0.747, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create Food and Water"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.737, 0.781, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Conjuration (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.757, 0.68, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.772, 0.632, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.786, 0.657, 0.801], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.801, 0.697, 0.816], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.521, 0.823, 0.911, 0.932], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create 45 pounds of food and 30 gallons of fresh water on the ground or in containers within range—both useful in fending off the hazards of malnutrition and dehydration. The food is bland but nourishing and looks like a food of your choice, and the water is clean. The food spoils after 24 hours if uneaten."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "120"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 120, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.428, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create or Destroy Water", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a mix of water and sand) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.154, 0.311, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You do one of the following:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.177, 0.489, 0.239], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create Water.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create up to 10 gallons of clean water within range in an open container. Alternatively, the water falls as rain in a 30-foot Cube within range, extinguishing exposed flames there."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.239, 0.485, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Destroy Water.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You destroy up to 10 gallons of water in an open container within range. Alternatively, you destroy fog in a 30-foot Cube within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.307, 0.487, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create or destroy 10 additional gallons of water, or the size of the Cube increases by 5 feet, for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.376, 0.247, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Create Undead"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.393, 0.429, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Necromancy (Cleric, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.272, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.209, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.443, 0.467, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (one 150+ GP black onyx stone for each corpse)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.473, 0.275, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.495, 0.491, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can cast this spell only at night. Choose up to three corpses of Medium or Small Humanoids within range. Each one becomes a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghoul", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " under your control (see “Monsters” for its stat block)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.557, 0.487, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action on each of your turns, you can mentally command any creature you animated with this spell if the creature is within 120 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to them). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move on its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a particular place. If you issue no commands, the creature takes the Dodge action and moves only to avoid harm. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow the order until its task is complete."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.741, 0.484, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you’ve given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to three creatures you have animated with this spell rather than animating new ones."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.863, 0.481, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you use a level 7 spell slot, you can animate or reassert control over four "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghouls", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". If you use a level 8 spell slot, you can animate or reassert control over five "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghouls", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.908, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "or two "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghasts", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " or "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Wights", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". If you use a level 9 spell slot, you can animate or reassert control over six "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghouls", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", three "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ghasts", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " or "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Wights", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", or two "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mummies", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". See “Monsters” for these stat blocks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.611, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.768, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Illusion (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.156, 0.694, 0.172], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.171, 0.632, 0.187], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.186, 0.771, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a paintbrush)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.201, 0.651, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Special"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.223, 0.904, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You pull wisps of shadow material from the Shadowfell to create an object within range. It is either an object of vegetable matter (soft goods, rope, wood, and the like) or mineral matter (stone, crystal, metal, and the like). The object must be no larger than a 5-foot Cube, and the object must be of a form and material that you have seen."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.331, 0.911, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell’s duration depends on the object’s material, as shown in the Materials table. If the object is composed of multiple materials, use the shortest duration. Using any object created by this spell as another spell’s Material component causes the other spell to fail."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.436, 0.607, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Materials"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.526, 0.455, 0.909, 0.568], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.526, 0.455, 0.909, 0.568], "content": "<table><tr><td>Material</td><td>Duration</td></tr><tr><td>Vegetable matter</td><td>24 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Stone or crystal</td><td>12 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Precious metals</td><td>I hour</td></tr><tr><td>Gems</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Adamantine or mithral</td><td>I minute</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.577, 0.884, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Cube increases by 5 feet for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.525, 0.616, 0.655, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cure Wounds"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.633, 0.86, 0.665], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.669, 0.697, 0.728], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.735, 0.907, 0.798], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature you touch regains a number of Hit Points equal to 2d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 2d8 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.805, 0.662, 0.822], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dancing Lights"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.822, 0.819, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Illusion Cantrip (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of phosphorus) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "121"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 121, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create up to four torch-size lights within range, making them appear as torches, lanterns, or glowing orbs that hover for the duration. Alternatively, you combine the four lights into one glowing Medium form that is vaguely humanlike. Whichever form you choose, each light sheds Dim Light in a 10- foot radius."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.483, 0.221], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can move the lights up to 60 feet to a space within range. A light must be within 20 feet of another light created by this spell, and a light vanishes if it exceeds the spell’s range."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.227, 0.193, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.246, 0.428, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (bat fur and a piece of coal) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.331, 0.485, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, magical Darkness spreads from a point within range and fills a 15-foot-radius Sphere. Darkvision can’t see through it, and nonmagical light can’t illuminate it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.393, 0.488, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, you cast the spell on an object that isn’t being worn or carried, causing the Darkness to fill a 15-foot Emanation originating from that object. Covering that object with something opaque, such as a bowl or helm, blocks the Darkness."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.469, 0.48, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If any of this spell’s area overlaps with an area of Bright Light or Dim Light created by a spell of level 2 or lower, that other spell is dispelled."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.524, 0.206, 0.539], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.54, 0.441, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.576, 0.36, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a dried carrot) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.643, 0.47, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, a willing creature you touch has Darkvision with a range of 150 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.681, 0.184, 0.698], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Daylight"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.7, 0.447, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Sorcerer)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.735, 0.256, 0.793], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.801, 0.477, 0.862], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, sunlight spreads from a point within range and fills a 60-foot-radius Sphere. The sunlight’s area is Bright Light and sheds Dim Light for an additional 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.863, 0.477, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, you cast the spell on an object that isn’t being worn or carried, causing the sunlight to fill a 60-foot Emanation originating from that"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.91, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "object. Covering that object with something opaque, such as a bowl or helm, blocks the sunlight."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.081, 0.902, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If any of this spell’s area overlaps with an area of Darkness created by a spell of level 3 or lower, that other spell is dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.135, 0.773, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Death Ward", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.24, 0.907, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature and grant it a measure of protection from death. The first time the target would drop to 0 Hit Points before the spell ends, the target instead drops to 1 Hit Point, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.301, 0.903, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell is still in effect when the target is subjected to an effect that would kill it instantly without dealing damage, that effect is negated against the target, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.37, 0.725, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Delayed Blast Fireball"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.388, 0.785, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.408, 0.879, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a ball of bat guano and sulfur) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.474, 0.91, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A beam of yellow light flashes from you, then condenses at a chosen point within range as a glowing bead for the duration. When the spell ends, the bead explodes, and each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on that point makes a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes Fire damage equal to the total accumulated damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.597, 0.901, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell’s base damage is 12d6, and the damage increases by 1d6 whenever your turn ends and the spell hasn’t ended."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.643, 0.91, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a creature touches the glowing bead before the spell ends, that creature makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the spell ends, causing the bead to explode. On a successful save, the creature can throw the bead up to 40 feet. If the thrown bead enters a creature’s space or collides with a solid object, the spell ends, and the bead explodes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.75, 0.91, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the bead explodes, flammable objects in the explosion that aren’t being worn or carried start burning."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.796, 0.91, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The base damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 7."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.835, 0.864, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Demiplane", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 8 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.872, 0.679, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "122"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 122, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.489, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a shadowy Medium door on a flat solid surface that you can see within range. This door can be opened and closed, and it leads to a demiplane that is an empty room 30 feet in each dimension, made of wood or stone (your choice)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.478, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, the door vanishes, and any objects inside the demiplane remain there. Any creatures inside also remain unless they opt to be shunted through the door as it vanishes, landing with the Prone condition in the unoccupied spaces closest to the door’s former space."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.22, 0.489, 0.327], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each time you cast this spell, you can create a new demiplane or connect the shadowy door to a demiplane you created with a previous casting of this spell. Additionally, if you know the nature and contents of a demiplane created by a casting of this spell by another creature, you can connect the shadowy door to that demiplane instead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.335, 0.349, 0.368], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect Evil and Good", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Divination (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.371, 0.399, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.439, 0.483, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you sense the location of any Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey, Fiend, or Undead within 30 feet of yourself. You also sense whether the Hallow spell is active there and, if so, where."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.5, 0.456, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell is blocked by 1 foot of stone, dirt, or wood; 1 inch of metal; or a thin sheet of lead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.539, 0.436, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect Magic", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.591, 0.4, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.658, 0.484, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you sense the presence of magical effects within 30 feet of yourself. If you sense such effects, you can take the Magic action to see a faint aura around any visible creature or object in the area that bears the magic, and if an effect was created by a spell, you learn the spell’s school of magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.75, 0.456, 0.782], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell is blocked by 1 foot of stone, dirt, or wood; 1 inch of metal; or a thin sheet of lead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.789, 0.454, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect Poison and Disease", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Divination (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.827, 0.4, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a yew leaf) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.893, 0.478, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you sense the location of poisons, poisonous or venomous creatures, and magical"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.903, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "contagions within 30 feet of yourself. You sense the kind of poison, creature, or contagion in each case."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.525, 0.081, 0.892, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell is blocked by 1 foot of stone, dirt, or wood; 1 inch of metal; or a thin sheet of lead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.832, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect Thoughts", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Divination (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (1 Copper Piece) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.224, 0.91, 0.269], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You activate one of the effects below. Until the spell ends, you can activate either effect as a Magic action on your later turns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.27, 0.889, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sense Thoughts.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You sense the presence of thoughts within 30 feet of yourself that belong to creatures that know languages or are telepathic. You don’t read the thoughts, but you know that a thinking creature is present."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.347, 0.875, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell is blocked by 1 foot of stone, dirt, or wood; 1 inch of metal; or a thin sheet of lead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.377, 0.905, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read Thoughts.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Target one creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself or one creature within 30 feet of yourself that you detected with the Sense Thoughts option. You learn what is most on the target’s mind right now. If the target doesn’t know any languages and isn’t telepathic, you learn nothing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.47, 0.91, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action on your next turn, you can try to probe deeper into the target’s mind. If you probe deeper, the target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, you discern the target’s reasoning, emotions, and something that looms large in its mind (such as a worry, love, or hate). On a successful save, the spell ends. Either way, the target knows that you are probing into its mind, and until you shift your attention away from the target’s mind, the target can take an action on its turn to make an Intelligence (Arcana) check against your spell save DC, ending the spell on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.662, 0.907, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dimension Door", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Conjuration (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 500 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.766, 0.906, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You teleport to a location within range. You arrive at exactly the spot desired. It can be a place you can see, one you can visualize, or one you can describe by stating distance and direction, such as “200 feet straight downward” or “300 feet upward to the northwest at a 45-degree angle.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.858, 0.912, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can also teleport one willing creature. The creature must be within 5 feet of you when you teleport, and it teleports to a space within 5 feet of your destination space."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "123"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 123, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.486, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you, the other creature, or both would arrive in a space occupied by a creature or completely filled by one or more objects, you and any creature traveling with you each take 4d6 Force damage, and the teleportation fails."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.135, 0.224, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disguise Self"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.153, 0.387, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.172, 0.256, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.239, 0.485, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You make yourself—including your clothing, armor, weapons, and other belongings on your person— look different until the spell ends. You can seem 1 foot shorter or taller and can appear heavier or lighter. You must adopt a form that has the same basic arrangement of limbs as you have. Otherwise, the extent of the illusion is up to you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.347, 0.477, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The changes wrought by this spell fail to hold up to physical inspection. For example, if you use this spell to add a hat to your outfit, objects pass through the hat, and anyone who touches it would feel nothing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.423, 0.49, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To discern that you are disguised, a creature must take the Study action to inspect your appearance and succeed on an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.493, 0.219, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disintegrate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.51, 0.398, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.53, 0.406, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a lodestone and dust) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.597, 0.476, 0.658], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You launch a green ray at a target you can see within range. The target can be a creature, a non-magical object, or a creation of magical force, such as the wall created by Wall of Force."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.658, 0.479, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature targeted by this spell makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 10d6 + 40 Force damage. If this damage reduces it to 0 Hit Points, it and everything nonmagical it is wearing and carrying are disintegrated into gray dust. The target can be revived only by a True Resurrection or a Wish spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.766, 0.476, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell automatically disintegrates a Large or smaller nonmagical object or a creation of magical force. If such a target is Huge or larger, this spell disintegrates a 10-foot-Cube portion of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.827, 0.474, 0.858], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 3d6 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.865, 0.351, 0.899], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dispel Evil and Good", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.903, 0.256, 0.933], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.855, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (powdered silver and iron) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.087, 0.907, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, and Undead have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. You can end the spell early by using either of the following special functions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.15, 0.91, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Break Enchantment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you touch a creature that is possessed by or has the Charmed or Frightened condition from one or more creatures of the types above. The target is no longer possessed, Charmed, or Frightened by such creatures."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.226, 0.905, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dismissal.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you target one creature you can see within 5 feet of you that has one of the creature types above. The target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be sent back to its home plane if it isn’t there already. If they aren’t on their home plane, Undead are sent to the Shadowfell, and Fey are sent to the Feywild."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.341, 0.644, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dispel Magic"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.359, 0.859, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.394, 0.696, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.461, 0.905, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose one creature, object, or magical effect within range. Any ongoing spell of level 3 or lower on the target ends. For each ongoing spell of level 4 or higher on the target, make an ability check using your spellcasting ability (DC 10 plus that spell’s level). On a successful check, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.553, 0.89, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You automatically end a spell on the target if the spell’s level is equal to or less than the level of the spell slot you use."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.622, 0.712, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dissonant Whispers", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.64, 0.727, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Enchantment (Bard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.66, 0.696, 0.719], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.726, 0.906, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature of your choice that you can see within range hears a discordant melody in its mind. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 3d6 Psychic damage and must immediately use its Reaction, if available, to move as far away from you as it can, using the safest route. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.849, 0.897, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "124"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 124, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.202, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divination"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.068, 0.395, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Divination (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.088, 0.32, 0.103], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.103, 0.187, 0.118], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.118, 0.484, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (incense worth 25+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.148, 0.275, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.17, 0.486, 0.277], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell puts you in contact with a god or a god’s servants. You ask one question about a specific goal, event, or activity to occur within 7 days. The GM offers a truthful reply, which might be a short phrase or cryptic rhyme. The spell doesn’t account for circumstances that might change the answer, such as the casting of other spells."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.277, 0.482, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you cast the spell more than once before finishing a Long Rest, there is a cumulative 25 percent chance for each casting after the first that you get no answer."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.346, 0.223, 0.362], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divine Favor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.364, 0.333, 0.38], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Transmutation (Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.384, 0.302, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.399, 0.186, 0.413], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.413, 0.237, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.241, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.451, 0.488, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, your attacks with weapons deal an extra 1d4 Radiant damage on a hit."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.103, 0.489, 0.224, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divine Smite"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.103, 0.507, 0.299, 0.523], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.527, 0.475, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action, which you take immediately after hitting a target with a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.103, 0.571, 0.187, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.103, 0.586, 0.214, 0.601], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.601, 0.274, 0.616], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.623, 0.485, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target takes an extra 2d8 Radiant damage from the attack. The damage increases by 1d8 if the target is a Fiend or an Undead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.669, 0.474, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.103, 0.708, 0.225, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divine Word"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.102, 0.726, 0.285, 0.742], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Evocation (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.102, 0.745, 0.302, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.103, 0.76, 0.21, 0.775], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.103, 0.775, 0.221, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.79, 0.275, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.101, 0.812, 0.478, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You utter a word imbued with power from the Upper Planes. Each creature of your choice in range makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, a target that has 50 Hit Points or fewer suffers an effect based on its current Hit Points, as shown in the Divine Word Effects table. Regardless of its Hit Points, a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.91, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "target that fails its save is forced back to its plane of origin (if it isn’t there already) and can’t return to the current plane for 24 hours by any means short of a Wish spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.124, 0.698, 0.141], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divine Word Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.525, 0.143, 0.91, 0.286], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.525, 0.143, 0.91, 0.286], "content": "<table><tr><td>Hit Points</td><td>Effect</td></tr><tr><td>0-20</td><td>The target dies.</td></tr><tr><td>21-30</td><td>The target has the Blinded, Deafened, and Stunned conditions for I hour.</td></tr><tr><td>31-40</td><td>The target has the Blinded and Deafened conditions for 10 minutes.</td></tr><tr><td>41-50</td><td>The target has the Deafened condition for I minute.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.296, 0.676, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dominate Beast"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.313, 0.855, 0.33], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Enchantment (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.333, 0.68, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.349, 0.632, 0.364], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.363, 0.656, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.378, 0.807, 0.393], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.4, 0.898, 0.492], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Beast you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. The target has Advantage on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.522, 0.492, 0.908, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a telepathic link with the Charmed target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as “Attack that creature,” “Move over there,” or “Fetch that object.” The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn’t receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.524, 0.631, 0.888, 0.661], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can command the target to take a Reaction but must take your own Reaction to do so."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.523, 0.661, 0.903, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 5 (up to 10 minutes), 6 (up to 1 hour), or 7+ (up to 8 hours)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.524, 0.715, 0.701, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dominate Monster"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.524, 0.732, 0.855, 0.748], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock,"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.525, 0.748, 0.588, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.524, 0.767, 0.679, 0.783], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 47, "bbox": [0.525, 0.783, 0.632, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 48, "bbox": [0.524, 0.797, 0.656, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 49, "bbox": [0.524, 0.812, 0.793, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 50, "bbox": [0.522, 0.835, 0.908, 0.928], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. The target has Advantage on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 51, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "125"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 52, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 125, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a telepathic link with the Charmed target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as “Attack that creature,” “Move over there,” or “Fetch that object.” The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn’t receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.189, 0.467, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can command the target to take a Reaction but must take your own Reaction to do so."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.479, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration can last longer with a level 9 spell slot (up to 8 hours)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.273, 0.265, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dominate Person"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.291, 0.43, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.31, 0.387, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.377, 0.487, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Humanoid you can see within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. The target has Advantage on the save if you or your allies are fighting it. Whenever the target takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.469, 0.487, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a telepathic link with the Charmed target while the two of you are on the same plane of existence. On your turn, you can use this link to issue commands to the target (no action required), such as “Attack that creature,” “Move over there,” or “Fetch that object.” The target does its best to obey on its turn. If it completes an order and doesn’t receive further direction from you, it acts and moves as it likes, focusing on protecting itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.607, 0.467, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can command the target to take a Reaction but must take your own Reaction to do so."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.638, 0.481, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 6 (up to 10 minutes), 7 (up to 1 hour), or 8+ (up to 8 hours)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.691, 0.255, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragon’s Breath"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.709, 0.398, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.73, 0.387, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a hot pepper) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.796, 0.488, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch one willing creature, and choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison. Until the spell ends, the target can take a Magic action to exhale a 15-foot Cone. Each creature in that area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 3d6 damage of the chosen type on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.895, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.525, 0.089, 0.593, 0.105], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dream"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.107, 0.807, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Illusion (Bard, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Special "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a handful of sand) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.904, 0.27], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You target a creature you know on the same plane of existence. You or a willing creature you touch enters a trance state to act as a dream messenger. While in the trance, the messenger is Incapacitated and has a Speed of 0."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.27, 0.909, 0.393], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target is asleep, the messenger appears in the target’s dreams and can converse with the target as long as it remains asleep, through the spell’s duration. The messenger can also shape the dream’s environment, creating landscapes, objects, and other images. The messenger can emerge from the trance at any time, ending the spell. The target recalls the dream perfectly upon waking."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.393, 0.903, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target is awake when you cast the spell, the messenger knows it and can either end the trance (and the spell) or wait for the target to sleep, at which point the messenger enters its dreams."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.455, 0.907, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can make the messenger terrifying to the target. If you do so, the messenger can deliver a message of no more than ten words, and then the target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target gains no benefit from its rest, and it takes 3d6 Psychic damage when it wakes up."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.554, 0.625, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Druidcraft"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.571, 0.747, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Transmutation Cantrip (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.591, 0.696, 0.65], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.658, 0.901, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whispering to the spirits of nature, you create one of the following effects within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.689, 0.91, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weather Sensor.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a Tiny, harmless sensory effect that predicts what the weather will be at your location for the next 24 hours. The effect might manifest as a golden orb for clear skies, a cloud for rain, falling snowflakes for snow, and so on. This effect persists for 1 round."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.781, 0.885, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bloom.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You instantly make a flower blossom, a seed pod open, or a leaf bud bloom."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.812, 0.904, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sensory Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a harmless sensory effect, such as falling leaves, spectral dancing fairies, a gentle breeze, the sound of an animal, or the faint odor of skunk. The effect must fit in a 5-foot Cube."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.873, 0.897, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Play.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You light or snuff out a candle, a torch, or a campfire."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "126"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 126, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.212, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "E th k ar qua e"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.058, 0.435, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 500 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a fractured rock) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.487, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a point on the ground that you can see within range. For the duration, an intense tremor rips through the ground in a 100-foot-radius circle centered on that point. The ground there is Difficult Terrain."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.232, 0.485, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast this spell and at the end of each of your turns for the duration, each creature on the ground in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature has the Prone condition, and its Concentration is broken."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.116, 0.309, 0.388, 0.323], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can also cause the effects below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.324, 0.488, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fissures.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A total of 1d6 fissures open in the spell’s area at the end of the turn you cast it. You choose the fissures’ locations, which can’t be under structures. Each fissure is 1d10 × 10 feet deep and 10 feet wide, and it extends from one edge of the spell’s area to another edge. A creature in the same space as a fissure must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or fall in. A creature that successfully saves moves with the fissure’s edge as it opens."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.462, 0.488, 0.538], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Structures.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The tremor deals 50 Bludgeoning damage to any structure in contact with the ground in the area when you cast the spell and at the end of each of your turns until the spell ends. If a structure drops to 0 Hit Points, it collapses."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.539, 0.492, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature within a distance from a collapsing structure equal to half the structure’s height makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 12d6 Bludgeoning damage, has the Prone condition, and is buried in the rubble, requiring a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check as an action to escape. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.669, 0.23, 0.685], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eldritch Blast"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.686, 0.309, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Evocation Cantrip (Warlock)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.706, 0.274, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.773, 0.484, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hurl a beam of crackling energy. Make a ranged spell attack against one creature or object in range. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.82, 0.49, 0.897], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell creates two beams at level 5, three beams at level 11, and four beams at level 17. You can direct the beams at the same target or at different ones. Make a separate attack roll for each beam."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.055, 0.873, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elementalism", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Transmutation Cantrip (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.155, 0.905, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You exert control over the elements, creating one of the following effects within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.186, 0.904, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beckon Air.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a breeze strong enough to ripple cloth, stir dust, rustle leaves, and close open doors and shutters, all in a 5-foot Cube. Doors and shutters being held open by someone or something aren’t affected."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.263, 0.908, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beckon Earth.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a thin shroud of dust or sand that covers surfaces in a 5-foot-square area, or you cause a single word to appear in your handwriting in a patch of dirt or sand."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.324, 0.911, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beckon Fire.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a thin cloud of harmless embers and colored, scented smoke in a 5-foot Cube. You choose the color and scent, and the embers can light candles, torches, or lamps in that area. The smoke’s scent lingers for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.401, 0.912, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beckon Water.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a spray of cool mist that lightly dampens creatures and objects in a 5-foot Cube. Alternatively, you create 1 cup of clean water either in an open container or on a surface, and the water evaporates in 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.477, 0.91, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sculpt Element.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause dirt, sand, fire, smoke, mist, or water that can fit in a 1-foot Cube to assume a crude shape (such as that of a creature) for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.531, 0.67, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "E h Abili n ance ty"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.537, 0.888, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (fur or a feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.651, 0.911, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature and choose Strength, Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma. For the duration, the target has Advantage on ability checks using the chosen ability."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.712, 0.899, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 2. You can choose a different ability for each target."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.781, 0.67, 0.798], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Enlarge/Reduce"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.797, 0.908, 0.878], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of powdered iron) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.886, 0.903, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, the spell enlarges or reduces a creature or an object you can see within range (see"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "127"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 127, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.48, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "the chosen effect below). A targeted object must be neither worn nor carried. If the target is an unwilling creature, it can make a Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the spell has no effect."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.113, 0.485, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Everything that a targeted creature is wearing and carrying changes size with it. Any item it drops returns to normal size at once. A thrown weapon or piece of ammunition returns to normal size immediately after it hits or misses a target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.189, 0.474, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Enlarge.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target’s size increases by one category—from Medium to Large, for example. The target also has Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target’s attacks with its enlarged weapons or Unarmed Strikes deal an extra 1d4 damage on a hit."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.28, 0.482, 0.389], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reduce.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target’s size decreases by one c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ate", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "gory—from Medium to Small, for example. The target also has Disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The target’s attacks with its reduced weapons or Unarmed Strikes deal 1d4 less damage on a hit (this can’t reduce the damage below 1)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.395, 0.255, 0.412], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ensnaring Strike", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.31, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.432, 0.469, 0.507], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action, which you take immediately after hitting a creature with a weapon "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.481, 0.606], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As you hit the target, grasping vines appear on it, and it makes a Strength saving throw. A Large or larger creature has Advantage on this save. On a failed save, the target has the Restrained condition until the spell ends. On a successful save, the vines shrivel away, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.607, 0.488, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While Restrained, the target takes 1d6 Piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. The target or a creature within reach of it can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.683, 0.475, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.722, 0.187, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Entangle", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.739, 0.358, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.76, 0.385, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.826, 0.487, 0.887], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grasping plants sprout from the ground in a 20-foot square within range. For the duration, these plants turn the ground in the area into Difficult Terrain. They disappear when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.888, 0.473, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature (other than you) in the area when you cast the spell must succeed on a Strength"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "saving throw or have the Restrained condition until the spell ends. A Restrained creature can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success, it frees itself from the grasping plants and is no longer Restrained by them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.602, 0.166], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Enthrall", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.168, 0.792, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Warlock)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.188, 0.807, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.91, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You weave a distracting string of words, causing creatures of your choice that you can see within range to make a Wisdom saving throw. Any creature you or your companions are fighting automatically succeeds on this save. On a failed save, a target has a −10 penalty to Wisdom (Perception) checks and Passive Perception until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.37, 0.645, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Etherealness", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.388, 0.891, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Conjuration (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.423, 0.698, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Up to 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.49, 0.907, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You step into the border regions of the Ethereal Plane, where it overlaps with your current plane. You remain in the Border Ethereal for the duration. During this time, you can move in any direction. If you move up or down, every foot of movement costs an extra foot. You can perceive the plane you left, which looks gray, and you can’t see anything there more than 60 feet away."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.612, 0.903, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While on the Ethereal Plane, you can affect and be affected only by creatures, objects, and effects on that plane. Creatures that aren’t on the Ethereal Plane can’t perceive or interact with you unless a feature gives them the ability to do so."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.689, 0.911, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, you return to the plane you left in the spot that corresponds to your space in the Border Ethereal. If you appear in an occupied space, you are shunted to the nearest unoccupied space and take Force damage equal to twice the number of feet you are moved."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.781, 0.891, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell ends instantly if you cast it while you are on the Ethereal Plane or a plane that doesn’t border it, such as one of the Outer Planes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.827, 0.91, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target up to three willing creatures (including yourself) for each spell slot level above 7. The creatures must be within 10 feet of you when you cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "128"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 128, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.467, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Expeditious Retreat", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.154, 0.469, 0.187], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You take the Dash action, and until the spell ends, you can take that action again as a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.194, 0.175, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "E bit ye e"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.2, 0.489, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Necromancy (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.298, 0.482, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, your eyes become an inky void. One creature of your choice within 60 feet of you that you can see must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be affected by one of the following effects of your choice for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.375, 0.486, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On each of your turns until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to target another creature but can’t target a creature again if it has succeeded on a save against this casting of the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.436, 0.485, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Asleep.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target has the Unconscious condition. It wakes up if it takes any damage or if another creature takes an action to shake it awake."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.482, 0.485, 0.573], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Panicked.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target has the Frightened condition. On each of its turns, the Frightened target must take the Dash action and move away from you by the safest and shortest route available. If the target moves to a space at least 60 feet away from you where it can’t see you, this effect ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.115, 0.574, 0.478, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sickened.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target has the Poisoned condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.598, 0.193, 0.613], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fabricate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.615, 0.333, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Transmutation (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.634, 0.284, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.702, 0.489, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You convert raw materials into products of the same material. For example, you can fabricate a wooden bridge from a clump of trees, a rope from a patch of hemp, or clothes from flax or wool."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.764, 0.49, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose raw materials that you can see within range. You can fabricate a Large or smaller object (contained within a 10-foot Cube or eight connected 5-foot Cubes) given a sufficient quantity of material. If you’re working with metal, stone, or another mineral substance, however, the fabricated object can be no larger than Medium (contained within a 5-foot Cube). The quality of any fabricated objects is based on the quality of the raw materials."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures and magic items can’t be created by this spell. You also can’t use it to create items that require a high degree of skill—such as weapons and armor—unless you have proficiency with the type of Artisan’s Tools used to craft such objects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.135, 0.808, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Faerie Fire", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Evocation (Bard, Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.239, 0.905, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Objects in a 20-foot Cube within range are outlined in blue, green, or violet light (your choice). Each creature in the Cube is also outlined if it fails a Dexterity saving throw. For the duration, objects and affected creatures shed Dim Light in a 10-foot radius and can’t benefit from the Invisible condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.331, 0.907, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack rolls against an affected creature or object have Advantage if the attacker can see it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.37, 0.789, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Faithful Hound", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Conjuration (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a silver whistle) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.474, 0.904, 0.536], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a phantom watchdog in an unoccupied space that you can see within range. The hound remains for the duration or until the two of you are more than 300 feet apart from each other."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.536, 0.905, 0.628], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No one but you can see the hound, and it is intangible and invulnerable. When a Small or larger creature comes within 30 feet of it without first speaking the password that you specify when you cast this spell, the hound starts barking loudly. The hound has Truesight with a range of 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.628, 0.909, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the start of each of your turns, the hound attempts to bite one enemy within 5 feet of it. That enemy must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 4d8 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.689, 0.91, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On your later turns, you can take a Magic action to move the hound up to 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.727, 0.805, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "False Life", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of alcohol) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.831, 0.815, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain 2d4 + 4 Temporary Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.847, 0.903, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain 5 additional Temporary Hit Points for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "129"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 129, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.15, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "F ear"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.056, 0.454, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a white feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.49, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature in a 30-foot Cone must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or drop whatever it is holding and have the Frightened condition for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.201, 0.482, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Frightened creature takes the Dash action and moves away from you by the safest route on each of its turns unless there is nowhere to move. If the creature ends its turn in a space where it doesn’t have line of sight to you, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the spell ends on that creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.316, 0.216, 0.332], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feather Fall"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.333, 0.441, 0.35], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Transmutation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.354, 0.478, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reaction, which you take when you or a creature you can see within 60 feet of you falls "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.398, 0.466, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (a small feather or piece of down) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.435, 0.489, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose up to five falling creatures within range. A falling creature’s rate of descent slows to 60 feet per round until the spell ends. If a creature lands before the spell ends, the creature takes no damage from the fall, and the spell ends for that creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.52, 0.225, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find Familiar", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.537, 0.313, 0.554], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.557, 0.319, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.572, 0.208, 0.587], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.587, 0.47, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (burning incense worth 10+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.639, 0.488, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the service of a familiar, a spirit that takes an animal form you choose: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bat, Cat, Frog, Hawk, Lizard, Octopus, Owl, Rat, Raven, Spider, Weasel,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " or another Beast that has a Challenge Rating of 0. Appearing in an unoccupied space within range, the familiar has the statistics of the chosen form (see “Monsters”), though it is a Celestial, Fey, or Fiend (your choice) instead of a Beast. Your familiar acts independently of you, but it obeys your commands."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.777, 0.487, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathic Connection.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While your familiar is within 100 feet of you, you can communicate with it telepathically. Additionally, as a Bonus Action, you can see through the familiar’s eyes and hear what it hears until the start of your next turn, gaining the benefits of any special senses it has."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.869, 0.475, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Finally, when you cast a spell with a range of touch, your familiar can deliver the touch. Your familiar must be within 100 feet of you, and it must"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.896, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "take a Reaction to deliver the touch when you cast the spell."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.898, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combat.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The familiar is an ally to you and your allies. It rolls its own Initiative and acts on its own turn. A familiar can’t attack, but it can take other actions as normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.142, 0.911, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disappearance of the Familiar.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When the familiar drops to 0 Hit Points, it disappears. It reappears after you cast this spell again. As a Magic action, you can temporarily dismiss the familiar to a pocket dimension. Alternatively, you can dismiss it forever. As a Magic action while it is temporarily dismissed, you can cause it to reappear in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you. Whenever the familiar drops to 0 Hit Points or disappears into the pocket dimension, it leaves behind in its space anything it was wearing or carrying."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.311, 0.901, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Familiar Only.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t have more than one familiar at a time. If you cast this spell while you have a familiar, you instead cause it to adopt a new eligible form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.38, 0.626, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find Steed", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.398, 0.733, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Conjuration (Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.417, 0.679, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.432, 0.63, 0.447], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.447, 0.65, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.463, 0.696, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.485, 0.907, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You summon an otherworldly being that appears as a loyal steed in an unoccupied space of your choice within range. This creature uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Otherworldly Steed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block. If you already have a steed from this spell, the steed is replaced by the new one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.561, 0.894, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The steed resembles a Large, rideable animal of your choice, such as a horse, a camel, a dire wolf, or an elk. Whenever you cast the spell, choose the steed’s creature type—Celestial, Fey, or Fiend— which determines certain traits in the stat block."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.638, 0.901, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combat.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The steed is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your Initiative count, and it functions as a controlled mount while you ride it (as defined in the rules on mounted combat). If you have the Incapacitated condition, the steed takes its turn immediately after yours and acts independently, focusing on protecting you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.745, 0.907, 0.837], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disappearance of the Steed.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The steed disappears if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if you die. When it disappears, it leaves behind anything it was wearing or carrying. If you cast this spell again, you decide whether you summon the steed that disappeared or a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.837, 0.876, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "130"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 130, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.051, 0.324, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Otherworldly Steed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.075, 0.473, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Celestial, Fey, or Fiend (Your Choice), Neutral "}, {"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 + 1 per spell level "}, {"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 5 + 10 per spell level (the steed has a number of Hit Dice [d10s] equal to the spell’s level) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 ft., Fly 60 ft. (requires level 4+ spell)"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.159, 0.487, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.159, 0.487, 0.205], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 18 +4 +4</td><td>Dex 12 +1 +1</td><td>Con14 +2 +2</td></tr><tr><td>Int 6 -2 -2</td><td>Wis 12 +1 +1</td><td>Cha 8 -1 -1</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.214, 0.295, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses Passive Perception 11"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.23, 0.438, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Telepathy 1 mile (works only with you) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " None (XP 0; PB equals your Proficiency Bonus)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.269, 0.156, 0.285], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.29, 0.489, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Life Bond.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you regain Hit Points from a level 1+ spell, the steed regains the same number of Hit Points if you’re within 5 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.344, 0.172, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.366, 0.481, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Otherworldly Slam.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. Hit: 1d8 plus the spell’s level of Radiant (Celestial), Psychic (Fey), or Necrotic (Fiend) damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.435, 0.228, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.456, 0.487, 0.534], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fell Glare (Fiend Only; Recharges after a Long Rest).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Wisdom Saving Throw: DC equals your spell save DC, one creature within 60 feet the steed can see. Failure: The target has the Frightened condition until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.538, 0.485, 0.587], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fey Step (Fey Only; Recharges after a Long Rest).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The steed teleports, along with its rider, to an unoccupied space of your choice up to 60 feet away from itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.59, 0.488, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healing Touch (Celestial Only; Recharges after a Long Rest).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " One creature within 5 feet of the steed regains a number of Hit Points equal to 2d8 plus the spell’s level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.643, 0.229, 0.66], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find the Path"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.661, 0.379, 0.678], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.68, 0.273, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.696, 0.187, 0.711], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.71, 0.483, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a set of divination tools—such as cards or runes—worth 100+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 day"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.763, 0.487, 0.855], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You magically sense the most direct physical route to a location you name. You must be familiar with the location, and the spell fails if you name a destination on another plane of existence, a moving destination (such as a mobile fortress), or an unspecific destination (such as “a green dragon’s lair”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.855, 0.487, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, as long as you are on the same plane of existence as the destination, you know how far it is and in what direction it lies. Whenever you"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.91, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "face a choice of paths along the way there, you know which path is the most direct."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.088, 0.625, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find Traps"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.107, 0.817, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Divination (Cleric, Druid, Ranger) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.91, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You sense any trap within range that is within line of sight. A trap, for the purpose of this spell, includes any object or mechanism that was created to cause damage or other danger. Thus, the spell would sense the Alarm or Glyph of Warding spell or a mechanical pit trap, but it wouldn’t reveal a natural weakness in the floor, an unstable ceiling, or a hidden sinkhole."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.316, 0.908, 0.364], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell reveals that a trap is present but not its location. You do learn the general nature of the danger posed by a trap you sense."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.37, 0.67, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Finger of Death"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.387, 0.869, 0.405], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.407, 0.679, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.525, 0.422, 0.631, 0.437], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.525, 0.437, 0.657, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.452, 0.696, 0.466], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.474, 0.907, 0.55], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You unleash negative energy toward a creature you can see within range. The target makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 7d8 + 30 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.55, 0.908, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Humanoid killed by this spell rises at the start of your next turn as a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Zombie", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (see “Monsters”) that follows your verbal orders."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.604, 0.598, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fireball"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.622, 0.785, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.68, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.657, 0.638, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.671, 0.879, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a ball of bat guano and sulfur) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.709, 0.907, 0.816], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A bright streak flashes from you to a point you choose within range and then blossoms with a low roar into a fiery explosion. Each creature in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on that point makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 8d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.523, 0.817, 0.892, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flammable objects in the area that aren’t being worn or carried start burning."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.847, 0.896, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "131"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 131, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.188, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Bolt"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.068, 0.368, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.492, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hurl a mote of fire at a creature or an object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 Fire damage. A flammable object hit by this spell starts burning if it isn’t being worn or carried."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.232, 0.482, 0.279], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 when you reach levels 5 (2d10), 11 (3d10), and 17 (4d10)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.285, 0.204, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.303, 0.411, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.323, 0.257, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.338, 0.186, 0.353], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.353, 0.47, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of phosphorus or a firefly) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.389, 0.473, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wispy flames wreathe your body for the duration, shedding Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 10 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.436, 0.479, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The flames provide you with a warm shield or a chill shield, as you choose. The warm shield grants you Resistance to Cold damage, and the chill shield grants you Resistance to Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.498, 0.49, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, whenever a creature within 5 feet of you hits you with a melee attack roll, the shield erupts with flame. The attacker takes 2d8 Fire damage from a warm shield or 2d8 Cold damage from a chill shield."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.582, 0.206, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Storm"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.599, 0.399, 0.616], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.619, 0.273, 0.679], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.686, 0.484, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A storm of fire appears within range. The area of the storm consists of up to ten 10-foot Cubes, which you arrange as you like. Each Cube must be contiguous with at least one other Cube. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 7d10 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.794, 0.467, 0.825], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flammable objects in the area that aren’t being worn or carried start burning."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.103, 0.832, 0.218, 0.848], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flame Blade"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.85, 0.353, 0.866], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.87, 0.399, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a sumac leaf) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You evoke a fiery blade in your free hand. The blade is similar in size and shape to a scimitar, and it lasts for the duration. If you let go of the blade, it disappears, but you can evoke it again as a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.113, 0.899, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can make a melee spell attack with the fiery blade. On a hit, the target takes Fire damage equal to 3d6 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.899, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The flaming blade sheds Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 10 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.204, 0.897, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.242, 0.644, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flame Strike"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.26, 0.707, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Evocation (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.795, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of sulfur) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.347, 0.907, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A vertical column of brilliant fire roars down from above. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius, 40-foothigh Cylinder centered on a point within range makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 5d6 Fire damage and 5d6 Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.439, 0.905, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Fire damage and the Radiant damage increase by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.492, 0.847, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flaming Sphere", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Conjuration (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.53, 0.807, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a ball of wax) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.597, 0.91, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a 5-foot-diameter sphere of fire in an unoccupied space on the ground within range. It lasts for the duration. Any creature that ends its turn within 5 feet of the sphere makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d6 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.689, 0.904, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can move the sphere up to 30 feet, rolling it along the ground. If you move the sphere into a creature’s space, that creature makes the save against the sphere, and the sphere stops moving for the turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.766, 0.904, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you move the sphere, you can direct it over barriers up to 5 feet tall and jump it across pits up to 10 feet wide. Flammable objects that aren’t being worn or carried start burning if touched by the sphere, and it sheds Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.857, 0.896, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "132"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 132, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.447, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flesh to Stone", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Transmutation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a cockatrice feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.483, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to turn one creature that you can see within range into stone. The target makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it has the Restrained condition for the duration. On a successful save, its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn. Constructs automatically succeed on the save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.247, 0.48, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Restrained target makes another Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns. If it successfully saves against this spell three times, the spell ends. If it fails its saves three times, it is turned to stone and has the Petrified condition for the duration. The successes and failures needn’t be consecutive; keep track of both until the target collects three of a kind."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.37, 0.477, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you maintain your Concentration on this spell for the entire possible duration, the target is Petrified until the condition is ended by Greater Restoration or similar magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.439, 0.227, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Floating Disk", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.457, 0.313, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.476, 0.389, 0.536], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of mercury) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.543, 0.488, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell creates a circular, horizontal plane of force, 3 feet in diameter and 1 inch thick, that floats 3 feet above the ground in an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within range. The disk remains for the duration and can hold up to 500 pounds. If more weight is placed on it, the spell ends, and everything on the disk falls to the ground."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.651, 0.488, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The disk is immobile while you are within 20 feet of it. If you move more than 20 feet away from it, the disk follows you so that it remains within 20 feet of you. It can move across uneven terrain, up or down stairs, slopes and the like, but it can’t cross an elevation change of 10 feet or more. For example, the disk can’t move across a 10-foot-deep pit, nor could it leave such a pit if it was created at the bottom."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.773, 0.49, 0.82], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you move more than 100 feet from the disk (typically because it can’t move around an obstacle to follow you), the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.828, 0.466, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fly", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.906, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature. For the duration, the target gains a Fly Speed of 60 feet and can hover. When the spell ends, the target falls if it is still aloft unless it can stop the fall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.112, 0.89, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.166, 0.902, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fog Cloud", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.269, 0.898, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of fog centered on a point within range. The Sphere is Heavily Obscured. It lasts for the duration or until a strong wind (such as one created by Gust of Wind) disperses it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.347, 0.906, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The fog’s radius increases by 20 feet for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.385, 0.642, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Forbiddance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.402, 0.713, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Abjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.422, 0.873, 0.483], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (ruby dust worth 1,000+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 day"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.49, 0.912, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a ward against magical travel that protects up to 40,000 square feet of floor space to a height of 30 feet above the floor. For the duration, creatures can’t teleport into the area or use portals, such as those created by the Gate spell, to enter the area. The spell proofs the area against planar travel, and therefore prevents creatures from accessing the area by way of the Astral Plane, the Ethereal Plane, the Feywild, the Shadowfell, or the Plane Shift spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.643, 0.901, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, the spell damages types of creatures that you choose when you cast it. Choose one or more of the following: Aberrations, Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, and Undead. When a creature of a chosen type enters the spell’s area for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there, the creature takes 5d10 Radiant or Necrotic damage (your choice when you cast this spell)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.766, 0.901, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can designate a password when you cast the spell. A creature that speaks the password as it enters the area takes no damage from the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.811, 0.906, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell’s area can’t overlap with the area of another Forbiddance spell. If you cast Forbiddance every day for 30 days in the same location, the spell lasts until it is dispelled, and the Material components are consumed on the last casting."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "133"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 133, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.053, 0.453, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Forcecage", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 7 Evocation (Bard, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 100 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (ruby dust worth 1,500+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.17, 0.489, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An immobile, Invisible, Cube-shaped prison composed of magical force springs into existence around an area you choose within range. The prison can be a cage or a solid box, as you choose."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.232, 0.488, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A prison in the shape of a cage can be up to 20 feet on a side and is made from 1/2-inch diameter bars spaced 1/2 inch apart. A prison in the shape of a box can be up to 10 feet on a side, creating a solid barrier that prevents any matter from passing through it and blocking any spells cast into or out from the area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.339, 0.485, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, any creature that is completely inside the cage’s area is trapped. Creatures only partially within the area, or those too large to fit inside it, are pushed away from the center of the area until they are completely outside it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.416, 0.478, 0.552], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature inside the cage can’t leave it by non-magical means. If the creature tries to use teleportation or interplanar travel to leave, it must first make a Charisma saving throw. On a successful save, the creature can use that magic to exit the cage. On a failed save, the creature doesn’t exit the cage and wastes the spell or effect. The cage also extends into the Ethereal Plane, blocking ethereal travel."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.116, 0.553, 0.442, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell can’t be dispelled by Dispel Magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.578, 0.458, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Foresight", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 9 Divination (Bard, Druid, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a hummingbird feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.68, 0.482, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature and bestow a limited ability to see into the immediate future. For the du ration, the target has Advantage on D20 Tests, and other creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against it. The spell ends early if you cast it again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.766, 0.314, 0.782], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Freedom of Movement", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.783, 0.438, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.803, 0.365, 0.862], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a leather strap) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.869, 0.462, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature. For the duration, the target’s movement is unaffected by Difficult Terrain, and spells and other magical effects can"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.908, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "neither reduce the target’s Speed nor cause the target to have the Paralyzed or Restrained conditions. The target also has a Swim Speed equal to its Speed."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.097, 0.908, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, the target can spend 5 feet of movement to automatically escape from nonmagical restraints, such as manacles or a creature imposing the Grappled condition on it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.158, 0.89, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.211, 0.675, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Freezing Sphere"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.229, 0.786, 0.245], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.249, 0.862, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a miniature crystal sphere) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.316, 0.904, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A frigid globe streaks from you to a point of your choice within range, where it explodes in a 60-foot-radius Sphere. Each creature in that area makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 10d6 Cold damage on failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.408, 0.905, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the globe strikes a body of water, it freezes the water to a depth of 6 inches over an area 30 feet square. This ice lasts for 1 minute. Creatures that were swimming on the surface of frozen water are trapped in the ice and have the Restrained condition. A trapped creature can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to break free."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.531, 0.909, 0.684], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can refrain from firing the globe after completing the spell’s casting. If you do so, a globe about the size of a sling bullet, cool to the touch, appears in your hand. At any time, you or a creature you give the globe to can throw the globe (to a range of 40 feet) or hurl it with a sling (to the sling’s normal range). It shatters on impact, with the same effect as a normal casting of the spell. You can also set the globe down without shattering it. After 1 minute, if the globe hasn’t already shattered, it explodes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.684, 0.897, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.723, 0.661, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gaseous Form"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.74, 0.885, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.76, 0.793, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of gauze) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.827, 0.907, 0.905], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A willing creature you touch shape-shifts, along with everything it’s wearing and carrying, into a misty cloud for the duration. The spell ends on the target if it drops to 0 Hit Points or if it takes a Magic action to end the spell on itself."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "134"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 134, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.489, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While in this form, the target’s only method of movement is a Fly Speed of 10 feet, and it can hover. The target can enter and occupy the space of another creature. The target has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage; it has Immunity to the Prone condition; and it has Advantage on Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution saving throws. The target can pass through narrow open-ings, but it treats liquids as though they were solid surfaces."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.204, 0.468, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target can’t talk or manipulate objects, and any objects it was carrying or holding can’t be dropped, used, or otherwise interacted with. Finally, the target can’t attack or cast spells."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.265, 0.467, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.319, 0.153, 0.334], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.337, 0.488, 0.352], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Conjuration (Cleric, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.356, 0.257, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.371, 0.208, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.385, 0.459, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 5,000+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.423, 0.482, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a portal linking an unoccupied space you can see within range to a precise location on a different plane of existence. The portal is a circular opening, which you can make 5 to 20 feet in diameter. You can orient the portal in any direction you choose. The portal lasts for the duration, and the portal’s destination is visible through it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.531, 0.487, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The portal has a front and a back on each plane where it appears. Travel through the portal is possible only by moving through its front. Anything that does so is instantly transported to the other plane, appearing in the unoccupied space nearest to the portal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.623, 0.488, 0.668], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deities and other planar rulers can prevent portals created by this spell from opening in their presence or anywhere within their domains."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.669, 0.487, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast this spell, you can speak the name of a specific creature (a pseudonym, title, or nickname doesn’t work). If that creature is on a plane other than the one you are on, the portal opens next to the named creature and transports it to the nearest unoccupied space on your side of the portal. You gain no special power over the creature, and it is free to act as the GM deems appropriate. It might leave, attack you, or help you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.815, 0.155, 0.83], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Geas", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.831, 0.456, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.867, 0.27, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.9, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You give a verbal command to a creature that you can see within range, ordering it to carry out some service or refrain from an action or a course of activity as you decide. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. The target automatically succeeds if it can’t understand your command."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.158, 0.898, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While Charmed, the creature takes 5d10 Psychic damage if it acts in a manner directly counter to your command. It takes this damage no more than once each day."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.219, 0.879, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can issue any command you choose, short of an activity that would result in certain death. Should you issue a suicidal command, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.904, 0.31], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Remove Curse, Greater Restoration, or Wish spell ends this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.311, 0.904, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you use a level 7 or 8 spell slot, the duration is 365 days. If you use a level 9 spell slot, the spell lasts until it is ended by one of the spells mentioned above."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.381, 0.663, 0.397], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gentle Repose"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.398, 0.844, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Necromancy (Cleric, Paladin, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.417, 0.742, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.432, 0.625, 0.447], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.447, 0.902, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (2 Copper Pieces, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.477, 0.653, 0.491], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.499, 0.898, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a corpse or other remains. For the dura tion, the target is protected from decay and can’t become Undead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.546, 0.909, 0.608], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell also effectively extends the time limit on raising the target from the dead, since days spent under the influence of this spell don’t count against the time limit of spells such as Raise Dead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.615, 0.641, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant Insect", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.632, 0.722, 0.648], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.652, 0.821, 0.711], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.719, 0.912, 0.826], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You summon a giant centipede, spider, or wasp (chosen when you cast the spell). It manifests in an unoccupied space you can see within range and uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Insect", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block. The form you choose determines certain details in its stat block. The creature disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.826, 0.912, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, the creature shares your Initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you). If you don’t issue any, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "135"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 135, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.453, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.104, 0.092, 0.239, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant Insect"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.115, 0.259, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Beast, Unaligned"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.136, 0.264, 0.151], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 11 + the spell’s level"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.152, 0.419, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 + 10 for each spell level above 4 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 40 ft., Climb 40 ft., Fly 40 ft. (Wasp only)"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.184, 0.485, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.184, 0.485, 0.231], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 17 +3 +3</td><td>Dex 13 +1 +1</td><td>Con15 +2 +2</td></tr><tr><td>Int 4 -3 -3</td><td>Wis 14 +2 +2</td><td>Cha 3 -4 -4</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.24, 0.438, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Darkvision 60 ft.; Passive Perception 12 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Understands the languages you know "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " None (XP 0; PB equals your Proficiency Bonus)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.295, 0.156, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.47, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spider Climb.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The insect can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.371, 0.172, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.392, 0.455, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The insect makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell’s level (round down)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.429, 0.488, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison Jab.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 10 ft. Hit: 1d6 + 3 plus the spell’s level Piercing damage plus 1d4 Poison damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.48, 0.485, 0.558], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Web Bolt (Spider Only).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Ranged Attack Roll: Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, range 60 ft. Hit: 1d10 + 3 plus the spell’s level Bludgeoning damage, and the target’s Speed is reduced to 0 until the start of the insect’s next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.565, 0.228, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.586, 0.488, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Venomous Spew (Centipede Only).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Constitution Saving Throw: Your spell save DC, one creature the insect can see within 10 feet. Failure: The target has the Poisoned condition until the start of the insect’s next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.104, 0.655, 0.185, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Glibness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.672, 0.37, 0.688], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Enchantment (Bard, Warlock)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.692, 0.256, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.758, 0.487, 0.837], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, when you make a Charisma check, you can replace the number you roll with a 15. Additionally, no matter what you say, magic that would determine if you are telling the truth indicates that you are being truthful."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.843, 0.37, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Globe of Invulnerability", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Abjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.807, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a glass bead) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.897, 0.133], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An immobile, shimmering barrier appears in a 10- foot Emanation around you and remains for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.134, 0.906, 0.225], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any spell of level 5 or lower cast from outside the barrier can’t affect anything within it. Such a spell can target creatures and objects within the barrier, but the spell has no effect on them. Similarly, the area within the barrier is excluded from areas of effect created by such spells."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.226, 0.912, 0.273], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The barrier blocks spells of 1 level higher for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.69, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Glyph of Warding", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.297, 0.814, 0.314], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.317, 0.679, 0.332], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.525, 0.332, 0.625, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.347, 0.898, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (powdered diamond worth 200+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.376, 0.784, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled or triggered"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.399, 0.899, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You inscribe a glyph that later unleashes a magical effect. You inscribe it either on a surface (such as a table or a section of floor) or within an object that can be closed (such as a book or chest) to conceal the glyph. The glyph can cover an area no larger than 10 feet in diameter. If the surface or object is moved more than 10 feet from where you cast this spell, the glyph is broken, and the spell ends without being triggered."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.537, 0.906, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The glyph is nearly imperceptible and requires a successful Wisdom (Perception) check against your spell save DC to notice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.583, 0.905, 0.629], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you inscribe the glyph, you set its trigger and choose whether it’s an explosive rune or a spell glyph, as explained below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.629, 0.908, 0.752], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Set the Trigger.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You decide what triggers the glyph when you cast the spell. For glyphs inscribed on a surface, common triggers include touching or stepping on the glyph, removing another object covering it, or approaching within a certain distance of it. For glyphs inscribed within an object, common triggers include opening that object or seeing the glyph. Once a glyph is triggered, this spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.523, 0.752, 0.911, 0.829], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can refine the trigger so that only creatures of certain types activate it (for example, the glyph could be set to affect Aberrations). You can also set conditions for creatures that don’t trigger the glyph, such as those who say a certain password."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.828, 0.911, 0.907], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Explosive Rune.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When triggered, the glyph erupts with magical energy in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on the glyph. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 5d8 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "136"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 136, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.473, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "choice when you create the glyph) on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.479, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Glyph.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can store a prepared spell of level 3 or lower in the glyph by casting it as part of creating the glyph. The spell must target a single creature or an area. The spell being stored has no immediate effect when cast in this way."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.49, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the glyph is triggered, the stored spell takes effect. If the spell has a target, it targets the creature that triggered the glyph. If the spell affects an area, the area is centered on that creature. If the spell summons Hostile creatures or creates harmful objects or traps, they appear as close as possible to the intruder and attack it. If the spell requires Concentration, it lasts until the end of its full duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.28, 0.49, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage of an explosive rune increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 3. If you create a spell glyph, you can store any spell of up to the same level as the spell slot you use for the Glyph of Warding."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.365, 0.209, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goodberry"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.383, 0.358, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.402, 0.258, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.417, 0.187, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.431, 0.395, 0.447], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a sprig of mistletoe)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.446, 0.241, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.469, 0.472, 0.546], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ten berries appear in your hand and are infused with magic for the duration. A creature can take a Bonus Action to eat one berry. Eating a berry restores 1 Hit Point, and the berry provides enough nourishment to sustain a creature for one day."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.115, 0.546, 0.468, 0.562], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Uneaten berries disappear when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.569, 0.174, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grease"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.587, 0.378, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.606, 0.258, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.622, 0.21, 0.636], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.636, 0.447, 0.666], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of pork rind or butter) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.673, 0.467, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nonflammable grease covers the ground in a 10- foot square centered on a point within range and turns it into Difficult Terrain for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.486, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the grease appears, each creature standing in its area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition. A creature that enters the area or ends its turn there must also succeed on that save or fall Prone."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.804, 0.276, 0.821], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Greater Invisibility", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.822, 0.388, 0.838], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.841, 0.387, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature you touch has the Invisible condition until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.713, 0.105], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Greater Restoration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.107, 0.861, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.141, 0.679, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.157, 0.625, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.171, 0.887, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (diamond dust worth 100+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.223, 0.895, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature and magically remove one of the following effects from it:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.261, 0.684, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 1 Exhaustion level"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.276, 0.808, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The Charmed or Petrified condition"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.292, 0.885, 0.322], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• A curse, including the target’s Attunement to a cursed magic item"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.322, 0.904, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Any reduction to one of the target’s ability scores"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.338, 0.903, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Any reduction to the target’s Hit Point maximum"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.361, 0.687, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Guardian of Faith"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.378, 0.721, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Conjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.398, 0.68, 0.413], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.413, 0.632, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.428, 0.644, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.524, 0.443, 0.655, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.522, 0.465, 0.905, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Large spectral guardian appears and hovers for the duration in an unoccupied space that you can see within range. The guardian occupies that space and is invulnerable, and it appears in a form appropriate for your deity or pantheon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.522, 0.542, 0.909, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any enemy that moves to a space within 10 feet of the guardian for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 20 Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. The guardian vanishes when it has dealt a total of 60 damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.7, 0.658], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Guards and Wards", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.524, 0.659, 0.768, 0.676], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Abjuration (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.524, 0.679, 0.681, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 45, "bbox": [0.524, 0.694, 0.626, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 46, "bbox": [0.523, 0.708, 0.864, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a silver rod worth 10+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 47, "bbox": [0.522, 0.746, 0.904, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a ward that protects up to 2,500 square feet of floor space. The warded area can be up to 20 feet tall, and you shape it as one 50-foot square, one hundred 5-foot squares that are contiguous, or twenty-five 10-foot squares that are contiguous."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 48, "bbox": [0.522, 0.823, 0.912, 0.901], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast this spell, you can specify individuals that are unaffected by the spell’s effects. You can also specify a password that, when spoken aloud within 5 feet of the warded area, makes the speaker immune to its effects."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 49, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "137"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 50, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 137, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.488, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell creates the effects below within the warded area. Dispel Magic has no effect on Guards and Wards itself, but each of the following effects can be dispelled. If all four are dispelled, Guards and Wards ends. If you cast the spell every day for 365 days on the same area, the spell thereafter lasts until all its effects are dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.485, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Corridors.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Fog fills all the warded corridors, making them Heavily Obscured. In addition, at each intersection or branching passage offering a choice of direction, there is a 50 percent chance that a creature other than you believes it is going in the opposite direction from the one it chooses."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.487, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Doors.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " All doors in the warded area are magically locked, as if sealed by the Arcane Lock spell. In addition, you can cover up to ten doors with an illusion to make them appear as plain sections of wall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.311, 0.487, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stairs.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Webs fill all stairs in the warded area from top to bottom, as in the Web spell. These strands regrow in 10 minutes if they are destroyed while Guards and Wards lasts."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.372, 0.488, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Other Spell Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Place one of the following magical effects within the warded area:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.41, 0.475, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Dancing Lights in four corridors, with a simple program that the lights repeat as long as Guards and Wards lasts"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.456, 0.339, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Magic Mouth in two locations"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.471, 0.485, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Stinking Cloud in two locations (the vapors return within 10 minutes if dispersed while Guards and Wards lasts)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.517, 0.465, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Gust of Wind in one corridor or room (the wind blows continuously while the spell lasts)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.549, 0.467, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Suggestion in one 5-foot square; any creature that enters that square receives the suggestion mentally"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.601, 0.193, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Guidance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.619, 0.341, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divination Cantrip (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.64, 0.385, 0.698], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.706, 0.489, 0.753], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature and choose a skill. Until the spell ends, the creature adds 1d4 to any ability check using the chosen skill."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.103, 0.76, 0.222, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Guiding Bolt"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.778, 0.285, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.797, 0.257, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 round"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.865, 0.474, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hurl a bolt of light toward a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, it takes 4d6 Radiant damage, and the"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.887, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "next attack roll made against it before the end of your next turn has Advantage."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.081, 0.895, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.12, 0.893, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gust of Wind", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Evocation (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a legume seed) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.224, 0.908, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Line of strong wind 60 feet long and 10 feet wide blasts from you in a direction you choose for the duration. Each creature in the Line must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed 15 feet away from you in a direction following the Line. A creature that ends its turn in the Line must make the same save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.331, 0.891, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature in the Line must spend 2 feet of movement for every 1 foot it moves when moving closer to you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.377, 0.898, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The gust disperses gas or vapor, and it extinguishes candles and similar unprotected flames in the area. It causes protected flames, such as those of lanterns, to dance wildly and has a 50 percent chance to extinguish them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.455, 0.898, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action on your later turns, you can change the direction in which the Line blasts from you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.508, 0.594, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hallow"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.526, 0.712, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Abjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.545, 0.693, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.525, 0.56, 0.625, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.575, 0.901, 0.619], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (incense worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.627, 0.908, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a point and infuse an area around it with holy or unholy power. The area can have a radius up to 60 feet, and the spell fails if the radius includes an area already under the effect of Hallow. The affected area has the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.704, 0.907, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hallowed Ward.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose any of these creature types: Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey, Fiend, or Undead. Creatures of the chosen types can’t willingly enter the area, and any creature that is possessed by or that has the Charmed or Frightened condition from such creatures isn’t possessed, Charmed, or Frightened by them while in the area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.811, 0.898, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Extra Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You bind an extra effect to the area from the list below:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.525, 0.848, 0.896, 0.879], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Courage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose can’t gain the Frightened condition while in the area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.525, 0.88, 0.901, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Darkness fills the area. Normal light, as well as magical light created by spells of a level lower than this spell, can’t illuminate the area."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "138"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 138, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.472, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Daylight.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bright light fills the area. Magical Darkness created by spells of a level lower than this spell can’t extinguish the light."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.097, 0.462, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Peaceful Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Dead bodies interred in the area can’t be turned into Undead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.127, 0.488, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Extradimensional Interference.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose can’t enter or exit the area using teleportation or interplanar travel."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.173, 0.469, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fear.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose have the Frightened condition while in the area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.205, 0.49, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose have Resistance to one damage type of your choice while in the area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.46, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Silence.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " No sound can emanate from within the area, and no sound can reach into it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.281, 0.482, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tongues.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose can communicate with any other creature in the area even if they don’t share a common language."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.326, 0.473, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vulnerability.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Creatures of any types you choose have Vulnerability to one damage type of your choice while in the area."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.38, 0.302, 0.397], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hallucinatory Terrain"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.398, 0.435, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Illusion (Bard, Druid, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.417, 0.352, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a mushroom) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.485, 0.492, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You make natural terrain in a 150-foot Cube in range look, sound, and smell like another sort of natural terrain. Thus, open fields or a road can be made to resemble a swamp, hill, crevasse, or some other difficult or impassable terrain. A pond can be made to seem like a grassy meadow, a precipice like a gentle slope, or a rock-strewn gully like a wide and smooth road. Manufactured structures, equipment, and creatures within the area aren’t changed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.623, 0.487, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The tactile characteristics of the terrain are unchanged, so creatures entering the area are likely to notice the illusion. If the difference isn’t obvious by touch, a creature examining the illusion can take the Study action to make an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC to disbelieve it. If a creature discerns that the terrain is illusory, the creature sees a vague image superimposed on the real terrain."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.769, 0.161, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Harm"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.786, 0.304, 0.802], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Necromancy (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.806, 0.275, 0.865], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.873, 0.468, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You unleash virulent magic on a creature you can see within range. The target makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, it takes 14d6"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.898, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Necrotic damage, and its Hit Point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the Necrotic damage it took. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage only. This spell can’t reduce a target’s Hit Point maximum below 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.135, 0.585, 0.151], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Haste"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.152, 0.821, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.173, 0.853, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a shaving of licorice root) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.239, 0.907, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a willing creature that you can see within range. Until the spell ends, the target’s Speed is doubled, it gains a +2 bonus to Armor Class, it has Advantage on Dexterity saving throws, and it gains an additional action on each of its turns. That action can be used to take only the Attack (one attack only), Dash, Disengage, Hide, or Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.347, 0.91, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, the target is Incapacitated and has a Speed of 0 until the end of its next turn, as a wave of lethargy washes over it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.4, 0.573, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heal"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.418, 0.761, 0.434], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Abjuration (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.438, 0.696, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.505, 0.898, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a creature that you can see within range. Positive energy washes through the target, restoring 70 Hit Points. This spell also ends the Blinded, Deafened, and Poisoned conditions on the target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.566, 0.893, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 10 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.605, 0.658, 0.622], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healing Word"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.623, 0.803, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.725, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.709, 0.888, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature of your choice that you can see within range regains Hit Points equal to 2d4 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.755, 0.892, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 2d4 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.794, 0.632, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heat Metal"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.811, 0.786, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.831, 0.865, 0.892], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of iron and a flame) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "139"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 139, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a manufactured metal object, such as a metal weapon or a suit of Heavy or Medium metal armor, that you can see within range. You cause the object to glow red-hot. Any creature in physical contact with the object takes 2d8 Fire damage when you cast the spell. Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action on each of your later turns to deal this damage again if the object is within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.174, 0.48, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a creature is holding or wearing the object and takes the damage from it, the creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or drop the object if it can. If it doesn’t drop the object, it has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.265, 0.475, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.303, 0.243, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hellish Rebuke"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.321, 0.305, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Warlock)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.34, 0.482, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reaction, which you take in response to taking damage from a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.437, 0.485, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature that damaged you is momentarily surrounded by green flames. It makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 2d10 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.499, 0.475, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.537, 0.235, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heroes’ Feast"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.555, 0.389, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Conjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.574, 0.286, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.589, 0.187, 0.604], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.603, 0.457, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a gem-encrusted bowl worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.656, 0.48, 0.748], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a feast that appears on a surface in an unoccupied 10-foot Cube next to you. The feast takes 1 hour to consume and disappears at the end of that time, and the beneficial effects don’t set in until this hour is over. Up to twelve creatures can partake of the feast."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.749, 0.482, 0.841], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that partakes gains several benefits, which last for 24 hours. The creature has Resistance to Poison damage, and it has Immunity to the Frightened and Poisoned conditions. Its Hit Point maximum also increases by 2d10, and it gains the same number of Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.848, 0.365, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heroism", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.808, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.904, 0.164], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A willing creature you touch is imbued with bravery. Until the spell ends, the creature is immune to the Frightened condition and gains Temporary Hit Points equal to your spellcasting ability modifier at the start of each of its turns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.165, 0.89, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.219, 0.868, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hex", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Enchantment (Warlock) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (the petrified eye of a newt) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.324, 0.909, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You place a curse on a creature that you can see within range. Until the spell ends, you deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage to the target whenever you hit it with an attack roll. Also, choose one ability when you cast the spell. The target has Disadvantage on ability checks made with the chosen ability."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.415, 0.905, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target drops to 0 Hit Points before this spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action on a later turn to curse a new creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.461, 0.904, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 2 (up to 4 hours), 3–4 (up to 8 hours), or 5+ (24 hours)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.515, 0.692, 0.532], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hideous Laughter", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.532, 0.851, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.552, 0.819, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a tart and a feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.619, 0.903, 0.711], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature of your choice that you can see within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, it has the Prone and Incapacitated conditions for the duration. During that time, it laughs uncontrollably if it’s capable of laughter, and it can’t end the Prone condition on itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.712, 0.896, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the end of each of its turns and each time it takes damage, it makes another Wisdom saving throw. The target has Advantage on the save if the save is triggered by damage. On a successful save, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.788, 0.889, 0.834], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.842, 0.855, 0.891], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hold Monster", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.895, 0.679, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "140"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 140, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.418, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a straight piece of iron) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.486, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition for the duration. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.165, 0.468, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.218, 0.221, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hold Person"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.236, 0.462, 0.268], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.418, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a straight piece of iron) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.338, 0.485, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a Humanoid that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition for the duration. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.415, 0.468, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional Humanoid for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.469, 0.203, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Aura", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.486, 0.292, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Abjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.506, 0.258, 0.521], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.521, 0.187, 0.536], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.535, 0.461, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a reliquary worth 1,000+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.573, 0.488, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you emit an aura in a 30-foot Emanation. While in the aura, creatures of your choice have Advantage on all saving throws, and other creatures have Disadvantage on attack rolls against them. In addition, when a Fiend or an Undead hits an affected creature with a melee attack roll, the attacker must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the Blinded condition until the end of its next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.719, 0.24, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hunter’s Mark", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.737, 0.301, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Divination (Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.757, 0.372, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.1, 0.823, 0.488, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You magically mark one creature you can see within range as your quarry. Until the spell ends, you deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target whenever you hit it with an attack roll. You also have Advantage on any Wisdom (Perception or Survival) check you make to find it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.908, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target drops to 0 Hit Points before this spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to move the mark to a new creature you can see within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.904, 0.144], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 3–4 (up to 8 hours) or 5+ (up to 24 hours)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.687, 0.168], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hypnotic Pattern"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.167, 0.875, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.188, 0.808, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (a pinch of confetti) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.91, 0.362], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a twisting pattern of colors in a 30-foot Cube within range. The pattern appears for a moment and vanishes. Each creature in the area who can see the pattern must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration. While Charmed, the creature has the Incapacitated condition and a Speed of 0."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.362, 0.898, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell ends for an affected creature if it takes any damage or if someone else uses an action to shake the creature out of its stupor."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.416, 0.61, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ice Knife"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.431, 0.89, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (a drop of water or a piece of ice) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.52, 0.904, 0.628], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a shard of ice and fling it at one creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d10 Piercing damage. Hit or miss, the shard then explodes. The target and each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 2d6 Cold damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.628, 0.908, 0.66], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Cold damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.666, 0.619, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ice Storm"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.683, 0.834, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.703, 0.746, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a mitten) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.77, 0.898, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hail falls in a 20-foot-radius, 40-foot-high Cylinder centered on a point within range. Each creature in the Cylinder makes a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 2d10 Bludgeoning damage and 4d6 Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.863, 0.901, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hailstones turn ground in the Cylinder into Difficult Terrain until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "141"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 141, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.485, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Bludgeoning damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.105, 0.177, 0.121], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Identify", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.121, 0.344, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Divination (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.142, 0.422, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pearl worth 100+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.209, 0.49, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch an object throughout the spell’s casting. If the object is a magic item or some other magical object, you learn its properties and how to use them, whether it requires Attunement, and how many charges it has, if any. You learn whether any ongoing spells are affecting the item and what they are. If the item was created by a spell, you learn that spell’s name."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.331, 0.474, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you instead touch a creature throughout the casting, you learn which ongoing spells, if any, are currently affecting it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.385, 0.235, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Illusory Script"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.402, 0.387, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Illusion (Bard, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.423, 0.334, 0.437], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.438, 0.204, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.452, 0.472, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (ink worth 10+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.482, 0.231, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.505, 0.487, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You write on parchment, paper, or another suitable material and imbue it with an illusion that lasts for the duration. To you and any creatures you designate when you cast the spell, the writing appears normal, seems to be written in your hand, and conveys whatever meaning you intended when you wrote the text. To all others, the writing appears as if it were written in an unknown or magical script that is unintelligible. Alternatively, the illusion can alter the meaning, handwriting, and language of the text, though the language must be one you know."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.673, 0.484, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell is dispelled, the original script and the illusion both disappear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.703, 0.484, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that has Truesight can read the hidden message."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.743, 0.236, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imprisonment", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.76, 0.37, 0.776], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Abjuration (Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.779, 0.272, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.103, 0.794, 0.209, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.809, 0.467, 0.838], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a statuette of the target worth 5,000+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.103, 0.838, 0.277, 0.854], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.861, 0.483, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a magical restraint to hold a creature that you can see within range. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the target is unaffected, and it is immune to this"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.905, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "spell for the next 24 hours. On a failed save, the target is imprisoned. While imprisoned, the target doesn’t need to breathe, eat, or drink, and it doesn’t age. Divination spells can’t locate or perceive the imprisoned target, and the target can’t teleport."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.127, 0.9, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, the target is also affected by one of the following effects of your choice:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.165, 0.907, 0.225], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burial.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target is entombed beneath the earth in a hollow globe of magical force that is just large enough to contain the target. Nothing can pass into or out of the globe."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.525, 0.226, 0.901, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chaining.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Chains firmly rooted in the ground hold the target in place. The target has the Restrained condition and can’t be moved by any means."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.525, 0.272, 0.892, 0.333], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hedged Prison.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target is trapped in a demiplane that is warded against teleportation and planar travel. The demiplane is your choice of a labyrinth, a cage, a tower, or the like."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.333, 0.905, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Minimus Containment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target becomes 1 inch tall and is trapped inside an indestructible gemstone or a similar object. Light can pass through the gemstone (allowing the target to see out and other creatures to see in), but nothing else can pass through by any means."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.425, 0.905, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slumber.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target has the Unconscious condition and can’t be awoken."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.463, 0.905, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ending the Spell.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you cast the spell, specify a trigger that will end it. The trigger can be as simple or as elaborate as you choose, but the GM must agree that it has a high likelihood of happening within the next decade. The trigger must be an observable action, such as someone making a particular offering at the temple of your god, saving your true love, or defeating a specific monster."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.586, 0.893, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Dispel Magic spell can end the spell only if it is cast with a level 9 spell slot, targeting either the prison or the component used to create it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.639, 0.684, 0.656], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incendiary Cloud", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.657, 0.846, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Conjuration (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.676, 0.679, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.691, 0.638, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.525, 0.706, 0.656, 0.721], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.721, 0.807, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.743, 0.906, 0.82], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A swirling cloud of embers and smoke fills a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range. The cloud’s area is Heavily Obscured. It lasts for the duration or until a strong wind (like that created by Gust of Wind) disperses it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.821, 0.91, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the cloud appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d8 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature must also make this save when the Sphere moves into its space and when it enters the Sphere or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.031, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "142"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 142, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.485, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The cloud moves 10 feet away from you in a direction you choose at the start of each of your turns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.304, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inflict Wounds", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Necromancy (Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.193, 0.49, 0.239], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature you touch makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 2d10 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.24, 0.475, 0.271], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.279, 0.412, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Insect Plague", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Conjuration (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a locust) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.382, 0.468, 0.444], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Swarming locusts fill a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point you choose within range. The Sphere remains for the duration, and its area is Lightly Obscured and Difficult Terrain."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.444, 0.481, 0.551], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the swarm appears, each creature in it makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 4d10 Piercing damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature also makes this save when it enters the spell’s area for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.551, 0.475, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.59, 0.313, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instant Summons", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.627, 0.472, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a sapphire worth 1,000+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.694, 0.487, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch the sapphire used in the casting and an object weighing 10 pounds or less whose longest dimension is 6 feet or less. The spell leaves an Invisible mark on that object and invisibly inscribes the object’s name on the sapphire. Each time you cast this spell, you must use a different sapphire."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.786, 0.476, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thereafter, you can take a Magic action to speak the object’s name and crush the sapphire. The object instantly appears in your hand regardless of physical or planar distances, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.847, 0.481, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If another creature is holding or carrying the object, crushing the sapphire doesn’t transport it, but instead you learn who that creature is and where that creature is currently located."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.808, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Irresistible Dance", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Enchantment (Bard, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.905, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature that you can see within range must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the target dances comically until the end of its next turn, during which it must spend all its movement to dance in place."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.232, 0.904, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, the target has the Charmed condition for the duration. While Charmed, the target dances comically, must use all its movement to dance in place, and has Disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws and attack rolls, and other creatures have Advantage on attack rolls against it. On each of its turns, the target can take an action to collect itself and repeat the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.379, 0.875, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invisibility", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (an eyelash in gum arabic) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.482, 0.907, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature you touch has the Invisible condition until the spell ends. The spell ends early immediately after the target makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.543, 0.888, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.599, 0.862, 0.646], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Jump", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.65, 0.842, 0.71], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a grasshopper’s hind leg) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.717, 0.911, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature. Once on each of its turns until the spell ends, that creature can jump up to 30 feet by spending 10 feet of movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.763, 0.89, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.818, 0.864, 0.914], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Knock", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Transmutation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "143"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 143, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose an object that you can see within range. The object can be a door, a box, a chest, a set of manacles, a padlock, or another object that contains a mundane or magical means that prevents access."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.113, 0.483, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target that is held shut by a mundane lock or that is stuck or barred becomes unlocked, unstuck, or unbarred. If the object has multiple locks, only one of them is unlocked."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.173, 0.487, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target is held shut by Arcane Lock, that spell is suppressed for 10 minutes, during which time the target can be opened and closed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.219, 0.48, 0.251], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, a loud knock, audible up to 300 feet away, emanates from the target."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.258, 0.222, 0.274], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Legend Lore"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.275, 0.392, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.295, 0.286, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.31, 0.187, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.325, 0.467, 0.368], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (incense worth 250+ GP, which the spell consumes, and four ivory strips worth 50+ GP each)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.369, 0.275, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.391, 0.482, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Name or describe a famous person, place, or object. The spell brings to your mind a brief summary of the significant lore about that famous thing, as described by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.453, 0.487, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The lore might consist of important details, amusing revelations, or even secret lore that has never been widely known. The more information you already know about the thing, the more precise and detailed the information you receive is. That information is accurate but might be couched in figurative language or poetry, as determined by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.56, 0.484, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the famous thing you chose isn’t actually famous, you hear sad musical notes played on a trombone, and the spell fails."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.614, 0.278, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lesser Restoration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.631, 0.438, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.667, 0.302, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.733, 0.465, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature and end one condition on it: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, or Poisoned."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.773, 0.399, 0.806], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Levitate", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.81, 0.4, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a metal spring) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.876, 0.484, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One creature or loose object of your choice that you can see within range rises vertically up to 20 feet and remains suspended there for the duration. The"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.892, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "spell can levitate an object that weighs up to 500 pounds. An unwilling creature that succeeds on a Constitution saving throw is unaffected."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.912, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target can move only by pushing or pulling against a fixed object or surface within reach (such as a wall or a ceiling), which allows it to move as if it were climbing. You can change the target’s altitude by up to 20 feet in either direction on your turn. If you are the target, you can move up or down as part of your move. Otherwise, you can take a Magic action to move the target, which must remain within the spell’s range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.234, 0.912, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, the target floats gently to the ground if it is still aloft."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.273, 0.578, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Light"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.291, 0.879, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Evocation Cantrip (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.31, 0.892, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (a firefly or phosphorescent moss) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.377, 0.909, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch one Large or smaller object that isn’t being worn or carried by someone else. Until the spell ends, the object sheds Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet. The light can be colored as you like."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.454, 0.912, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Covering the object with something opaque blocks the light. The spell ends if you cast it again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.492, 0.657, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning Bolt"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.51, 0.786, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.53, 0.679, 0.545], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.545, 0.609, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.56, 0.875, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of fur and a crystal rod) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.597, 0.901, 0.688], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A stroke of lightning forming a 100-foot-long, 5-foot-wide Line blasts out from you in a direction you choose. Each creature in the Line makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 8d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.689, 0.896, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.728, 0.812, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Locate Animals or Plants", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Divination (Bard, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.765, 0.842, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (fur from a bloodhound) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.832, 0.905, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Describe or name a specific kind of Beast, Plant creature, or nonmagical plant. You learn the direction and distance to the closest creature or plant of that kind within 5 miles, if any are present."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "144"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 144, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.435, 0.163], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Locate Creature", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (fur from a bloodhound) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.171, 0.481, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Describe or name a creature that is familiar to you. You sense the direction to the creature’s location if that creature is within 1,000 feet of you. If the creature is moving, you know the direction of its movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.247, 0.478, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell can locate a specific creature known to you or the nearest creature of a specific kind (such as a human or a unicorn) if you have seen such a creature up close—within 30 feet—at least once. If the creature you described or named is in a different form, such as under the effects of a Flesh to Stone or Polymorph spell, this spell doesn’t locate the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.37, 0.476, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell can’t locate a creature if any thickness of lead blocks a direct path between you and the creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.423, 0.238, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Locate Object"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.441, 0.436, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.477, 0.399, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a forked twig) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.543, 0.49, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Describe or name an object that is familiar to you. You sense the direction to the object’s location if that object is within 1,000 feet of you. If the object is in motion, you know the direction of its movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.605, 0.49, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell can locate a specific object known to you if you have seen it up close—within 30 feet—at least once. Alternatively, the spell can locate the nearest object of a particular kind, such as a certain kind of apparel, jewelry, furniture, tool, or weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.682, 0.469, 0.728], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell can’t locate an object if any thickness of lead blocks a direct path between you and the object."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.735, 0.213, 0.752], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Longstrider"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.753, 0.478, 0.769], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Transmutation (Bard, Druid, Ranger, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.773, 0.361, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of dirt) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.839, 0.475, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature. The target’s Speed increases by 10 feet until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.871, 0.468, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.052, 0.848, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mage Armor", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Abjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of cured leather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.907, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature who isn’t wearing armor. Until the spell ends, the target’s base AC becomes 13 plus its Dexterity modifier. The spell ends early if the target dons armor."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.224, 0.633, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mage Hand"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.24, 0.91, 0.321], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjuration Cantrip (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.329, 0.892, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spectral, floating hand appears at a point you choose within range. The hand lasts for the duration. The hand vanishes if it is ever more than 30 feet away from you or if you cast this spell again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.39, 0.898, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, you can use the hand to manipulate an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or retrieve an item from an open container, or pour the contents out of a vial."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.452, 0.908, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action on your later turns, you can control the hand thus again. As part of that action, you can move the hand up to 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.497, 0.883, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The hand can’t attack, activate magic items, or carry more than 10 pounds."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.536, 0.642, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Circle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.554, 0.897, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.573, 0.693, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.525, 0.589, 0.632, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.603, 0.892, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (salt and powdered silver worth 100+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.632, 0.648, 0.647], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.655, 0.911, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a 10-foot-radius, 20-foot-tall Cylinder of magical energy centered on a point on the ground that you can see within range. Glowing runes appear wherever the Cylinder intersects with the floor or other surface."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.731, 0.91, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose one or more of the following types of creatures: Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, or Undead. The circle affects a creature of the chosen type in the following ways:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.8, 0.902, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The creature can’t willingly enter the Cylinder by nonmagical means. If the creature tries to use teleportation or interplanar travel to do so, it must first succeed on a Charisma saving throw."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.525, 0.862, 0.885, 0.893], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The creature has Disadvantage on attack rolls against targets within the Cylinder."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "145"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 145, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.05, 0.473, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Targets within the Cylinder can’t be possessed by or gain the Charmed or Frightened condition from the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.487, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each time you cast this spell, you can cause its magic to operate in the reverse direction, preventing a creature of the specified type from leaving the Cylinder and protecting targets outside it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.165, 0.481, 0.196], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The duration increases by 1 hour for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.203, 0.192, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Jar", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.221, 0.318, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Necromancy (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.24, 0.272, 0.256], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.256, 0.187, 0.27], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.27, 0.487, 0.299], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a gem, crystal, or reliquary worth 500+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.299, 0.278, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.322, 0.483, 0.475], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your body falls into a catatonic state as your soul leaves it and enters the container you used for the spell’s Material component. While your soul inhabits the container, you are aware of your surroundings as if you were in the container’s space. You can’t move or take Reactions. The only action you can take is to project your soul up to 100 feet out of the container, either returning to your living body (and ending the spell) or attempting to possess a Humanoid’s body."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.476, 0.486, 0.614], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can attempt to possess any Humanoid within 100 feet of you that you can see (creatures warded by a Protection from Evil and Good or Magic Circle spell can’t be possessed). The target makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, your soul enters the target’s body, and the target’s soul becomes trapped in the container. On a successful save, the target resists your efforts to possess it, and you can’t attempt to possess it again for 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.614, 0.487, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once you possess a creature’s body, you control it. Your Hit Points, Hit Point Dice, Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Speed, and senses are replaced by the creature’s. You otherwise keep your game statistics."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.675, 0.487, 0.721], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Meanwhile, the possessed creature’s soul can perceive from the container using its own senses, but it can’t move and it is Incapacitated."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.721, 0.485, 0.843], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While possessing a body, you can take a Magic action to return from the host body to the container if it is within 100 feet of you, returning the host creature’s soul to its body. If the host body dies while you’re in it, the creature dies, and you make a Charisma saving throw against your own spellcasting DC. On a success, you return to the container if it is within 100 feet of you. Otherwise, you die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.1, 0.843, 0.489, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the container is destroyed or the spell ends, your soul returns to your body. If your body is more than 100 feet away from you or if your body is dead, you die. If another creature’s soul is in the container when it is destroyed, the creature’s soul returns to"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.91, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "its body if the body is alive and within 100 feet. Otherwise, that creature dies."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.536, 0.081, 0.894, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, the container is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.104, 0.648, 0.121], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Missile"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.122, 0.785, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.141, 0.696, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.208, 0.91, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create three glowing darts of magical force. Each dart strikes a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4 + 1 Force damage to its target. The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.301, 0.907, 0.332], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell creates one more dart for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.339, 0.648, 0.356], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Mouth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.357, 0.744, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Illusion (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.376, 0.755, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.391, 0.632, 0.406], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.406, 0.892, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (jade dust worth 10+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.458, 0.908, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You implant a message within an object in range—a message that is uttered when a trigger condition is met. Choose an object that you can see and that isn’t being worn or carried by another creature. Then speak the message, which must be 25 words or fewer, though it can be delivered over as long as 10 minutes. Finally, determine the circumstance that will trigger the spell to deliver your message."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.581, 0.905, 0.734], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When that trigger occurs, a magical mouth appears on the object and recites the message in your voice and at the same volume you spoke. If the object you chose has a mouth or something that looks like a mouth (for example, the mouth of a statue), the magical mouth appears there, so the words appear to come from the object’s mouth. When you cast this spell, you can have the spell end after it delivers its message, or it can remain and repeat its message whenever the trigger occurs."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.735, 0.907, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The trigger can be as general or as detailed as you like, though it must be based on visual or audible conditions that occur within 30 feet of the object. For example, you could instruct the mouth to speak when any creature moves within 30 feet of the object or when a silver bell rings within 30 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.834, 0.876, 0.883], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Weapon", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Transmutation (Paladin, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.886, 0.724, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "146"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 146, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.234, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.482, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a nonmagical weapon. Until the spell ends, that weapon becomes a magic weapon with a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls. The spell ends early if you cast it again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.149, 0.476, 0.196], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The bonus increases to +2 with a level 3–5 spell slot. The bonus increases to +3 with a level 6+ spell slot."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.205, 0.48, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magnificent Mansion", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 7 Conjuration (Bard, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 300 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a miniature door worth 15+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.308, 0.49, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a shimmering door in range that lasts for the duration. The door leads to an extradimensional dwelling and is 5 feet wide and 10 feet tall. You and any creature you designate when you cast the spell can enter the extradimensional dwelling as long as the door remains open. You can open or close it (no action required) if you are within 30 feet of it. While closed, the door is imperceptible."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.431, 0.478, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beyond the door is a magnificent foyer with numerous chambers beyond. The dwelling’s atmosphere is clean, fresh, and warm."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.477, 0.49, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can create any floor plan you like for the dwelling, but it can’t exceed 50 contiguous 10-foot Cubes. The place is furnished and decorated as you choose. It contains sufficient food to serve a ninecourse banquet for up to 100 people. Furnishings and other objects created by this spell dissipate into smoke if removed from it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.583, 0.488, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A staff of 100 near-transparent servants attends all who enter. You determine the appearance of these servants and their attire. They are invulnerable and obey your commands. Each servant can perform tasks that a human could perform, but they can’t attack or take any action that would directly harm another creature. Thus the servants can fetch things, clean, mend, fold clothes, light fires, serve food, pour wine, and so on. The servants can’t leave the dwelling."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.737, 0.485, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, any creatures or objects left inside the extradimensional space are expelled into the unoccupied spaces nearest to the entrance."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.791, 0.221, 0.808], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Major Image"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.808, 0.453, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.828, 0.399, 0.888], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of fleece) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.896, 0.461, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create the image of an object, a creature, or some other visible phenomenon that is no larger"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.901, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "than a 20-foot Cube. The image appears at a spot that you can see within range and lasts for the duration. It seems real, including sounds, smells, and temperature appropriate to the thing depicted, but it can’t deal damage or cause conditions."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.128, 0.908, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you are within range of the illusion, you can take a Magic action to cause the image to move to any other spot within range. As the image changes location, you can alter its appearance so that its movements appear natural for the image. For example, if you create an image of a creature and move it, you can alter the image so that it appears to be walking. Similarly, you can cause the illusion to make different sounds at different times, even making it carry on a conversation, for example."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.28, 0.907, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Physical interaction with the image reveals it to be an illusion, for things can pass through it. A creature that takes a Study action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the image, and its other sensory qualities become faint to the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.418, 0.902, 0.465], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell lasts until dispelled, without requiring Concentration, if cast with a level 4+ spell slot."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.472, 0.705, 0.488], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mass Cure Wounds", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.49, 0.802, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.509, 0.697, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.577, 0.892, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A wave of healing energy washes out from a point you can see within range. Choose up to six creatures in a 30-foot-radius Sphere centered on that point. Each target regains Hit Points equal to 5d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.653, 0.892, 0.685], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.691, 0.623, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mass Heal", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.709, 0.713, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Abjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.729, 0.697, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.796, 0.911, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A flood of healing energy flows from you into creatures around you. You restore up to 700 Hit Points, divided as you choose among any number of creatures that you can see within range. Creatures healed by this spell also have the Blinded, Deafened, and Poisoned conditions removed from them."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "147"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 147, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.333, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mass Healing Word", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.473, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Up to six creatures of your choice that you can see within range regain Hit Points equal to 2d4 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.201, 0.47, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 1d4 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.24, 0.43, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mass Suggestion", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (a snake’s tongue) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.344, 0.486, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You suggest a course of activity—described in no more than 25 words—to twelve or fewer creatures you can see within range that can hear and understand you. The suggestion must sound achievable and not involve anything that would obviously deal damage to any of the targets or their allies. For example, you could say, “Walk to the village down that road, and help the villagers there harvest crops until sunset.” Or you could say, “Now is not the time for violence. Drop your weapons, and dance! Stop in an hour.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.513, 0.487, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration or until you or your allies deal damage to the target. Each Charmed target pursues the suggestion to the best of its ability. The suggested activity can continue for the entire duration, but if the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends for a target upon completing it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.635, 0.474, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The duration is longer with a spell slot of level 7 (10 days), 8 (30 days), or 9 (366 days)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.69, 0.156, 0.705], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Maze"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.707, 0.312, 0.723], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.727, 0.398, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.794, 0.486, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You banish a creature that you can see within range into a labyrinthine demiplane. The target remains there for the duration or until it escapes the maze."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.84, 0.482, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target can take a Study action to try to escape. When it does so, it makes a DC 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. If it succeeds, it escapes, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.905, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the spell ends, the target reappears in the space it left or, if that space is occupied, in the nearest unoccupied space."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.105, 0.847, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Meld into Stone", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Ranger) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.209, 0.911, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You step into a stone object or surface large enough to fully contain your body, merging yourself and your equipment with the stone for the duration. You must touch the stone to do so. Nothing of your presence remains visible or otherwise detectable by nonmagical senses."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.301, 0.911, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While merged with the stone, you can’t see what occurs outside it, and any Wisdom (Perception) checks you make to hear sounds outside it are made with Disadvantage. You remain aware of the passage of time and can cast spells on yourself while merged in the stone. You can use 5 feet of movement to leave the stone where you entered it, which ends the spell. You otherwise can’t move."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.423, 0.91, 0.562], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Minor physical damage to the stone doesn’t harm you, but its partial destruction or a change in its shape (to the extent that you no longer fit within it) expels you and deals 6d6 Force damage to you. The stone’s complete destruction (or transmutation into a different substance) expels you and deals 50 Force damage to you. If expelled, you move into an unoccupied space closest to where you first entered and have the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.57, 0.608, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mending"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.587, 0.899, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Transmutation Cantrip (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.622, 0.793, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (two lodestones) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.688, 0.91, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell repairs a single break or tear in an object you touch, such as a broken chain link, two halves of a broken key, a torn cloak, or a leaking wineskin. As long as the break or tear is no larger than 1 foot in any dimension, you mend it, leaving no trace of the former damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.781, 0.9, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell can physically repair a magic item, but it can’t restore magic to such an object."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.82, 0.852, 0.868], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Message", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Transmutation Cantrip (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.872, 0.765, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (a copper wire) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 round"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "148"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 148, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.485, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You point toward a creature within range and whisper a message. The target (and only the target) hears the message and can reply in a whisper that only you can hear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.112, 0.484, 0.175], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can cast this spell through solid objects if you are familiar with the target and know it is beyond the barrier. Magical silence; 1 foot of stone, metal, or wood; or a thin sheet of lead blocks the spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.181, 0.244, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Meteor Swarm"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.198, 0.364, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.218, 0.274, 0.277], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 mile "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.285, 0.488, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blazing orbs of fire plummet to the ground at four different points you can see within range. Each creature in a 40-foot-radius Sphere centered on each of those points makes a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 20d6 Fire damage and 20d6 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature in the area of more than one fiery Sphere is affected only once."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.423, 0.478, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A nonmagical object that isn’t being worn or carried also takes the damage if it’s in the spell’s area, and the object starts burning if it’s flammable."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.477, 0.21, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mind Blank", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.495, 0.345, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Abjuration (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.514, 0.256, 0.574], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.582, 0.485, 0.705], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch has Immunity to Psychic damage and the Charmed condition. The target is also unaffected by anything that would sense its emotions or alignment, read its thoughts, or magically detect its location, and no spell—not even Wish—can gather information about the target, observe it remotely, or control its mind."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.712, 0.207, 0.729], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mind Spike", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.729, 0.432, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Divination (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.749, 0.372, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.817, 0.481, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You drive a spike of psionic energy into the mind of one creature you can see within range. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw, taking 3d8 Psychic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. On a failed save, you also always know the target’s location until the spell ends, but only while the two of you are on the same plane"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.905, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "of existence. While you have this knowledge, the target can’t become hidden from you, and if it has the Invisible condition, it gains no benefit from that condition against you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.112, 0.896, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.654, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Minor Illusion", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.168, 0.879, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Illusion Cantrip (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.188, 0.762, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (a bit of fleece) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.907, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a sound or an image of an object within range that lasts for the duration. See the descriptions below for the effects of each. The illusion ends if you cast this spell again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.316, 0.905, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a creature takes a Study action to examine the sound or image, the creature can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the illusion becomes faint to the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.408, 0.91, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sound.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you create a sound, its volume can range from a whisper to a scream. It can be your voice, someone else’s voice, a lion’s roar, a beating of drums, or any other sound you choose. The sound continues unabated throughout the duration, or you can make discrete sounds at different times before the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.515, 0.91, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Image.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you create an image of an object—such as a chair, muddy footprints, or a small chest—it must be no larger than a 5-foot Cube. The image can’t create sound, light, smell, or any other sensory effect. Physical interaction with the image reveals it to be an illusion, since things can pass through it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.616, 0.663, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mirage Arcane"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.633, 0.79, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Illusion (Bard, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.652, 0.707, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Sight "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 days"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.72, 0.91, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You make terrain in an area up to 1 mile square look, sound, smell, and even feel like some other sort of terrain. Open fields or a road could be made to resemble a swamp, hill, crevasse, or some other rough or impassable terrain. A pond can be made to seem like a grassy meadow, a precipice like a gentle slope, or a rock-strewn gully like a wide and smooth road."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.842, 0.912, 0.888], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Similarly, you can alter the appearance of structures or add them where none are present. The spell doesn’t disguise, conceal, or add creatures."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.888, 0.893, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The illusion includes audible, visual, tactile, and olfactory elements, so it can turn clear ground"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.031, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "149"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 149, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.465, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "into Difficult Terrain (or vice versa) or otherwise impede movement through the area. Any piece of the illusory terrain (such as a rock or stick) that is removed from the spell’s area disappears immediately."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.487, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures with Truesight can see through the illusion to the terrain’s true form; however, all other elements of the illusion remain, so while the creature is aware of the illusion’s presence, the creature can still physically interact with the illusion."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.212, 0.228, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mirror Image", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.229, 0.453, 0.245], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.249, 0.255, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.487, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Three illusory duplicates of yourself appear in your space. Until the spell ends, the duplicates move with you and mimic your actions, shifting position so it’s impossible to track which image is real."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.377, 0.48, 0.485], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each time a creature hits you with an attack roll during the spell’s duration, roll a d6 for each of your remaining duplicates. If any of the d6s rolls a 3 or higher, one of the duplicates is hit instead of you, and the duplicate is destroyed. The duplicates otherwise ignore all other damage and effects. The spell ends when all three duplicates are destroyed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.485, 0.478, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature is unaffected by this spell if it has the Blinded condition, Blindsight, or Truesight."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.523, 0.178, 0.539], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mislead", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.54, 0.387, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Illusion (Bard, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.56, 0.373, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.628, 0.484, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the Invisible condition at the same time that an illusory double of you appears where you are standing. The double lasts for the duration, but the invisibility ends immediately after you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.704, 0.485, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can move the illusory double up to twice your Speed and make it gesture, speak, and behave in whatever way you choose. It is intangible and invulnerable."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.766, 0.482, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can see through its eyes and hear through its ears as if you were located where it is."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.805, 0.442, 0.838], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Misty Step", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.841, 0.302, 0.901], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.902, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Briefly surrounded by silvery mist, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.787, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Modify Memory", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Enchantment (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.127, 0.807, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.194, 0.912, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to reshape another creature’s memories. One creature that you can see within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. If you are fighting the creature, it has Advantage on the save. On a failed save, the target has the Charmed condition for the duration. While Charmed in this way, the target also has the Incapacitated condition and is unaware of its surroundings, though it can hear you. If it takes any damage or is targeted by another spell, this spell ends, and no memories are modified."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.347, 0.907, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While this charm lasts, you can affect the target’s memory of an event that it experienced within the last 24 hours and that lasted no more than 10 minutes. You can permanently eliminate all memory of the event, allow the target to recall the event with perfect clarity, change its memory of the event’s details, or create a memory of some other event."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.454, 0.908, 0.576], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You must speak to the target to describe how its memories are affected, and it must be able to understand your language for the modified memories to take root. Its mind fills in any gaps in the details of your description. If the spell ends before you finish describing the modified memories, the creature’s memory isn’t altered. Otherwise, the modified memories take hold when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.577, 0.907, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A modified memory doesn’t necessarily affect how a creature behaves, particularly if the memory contradicts the creature’s natural inclinations, alignment, or beliefs. An illogical modified memory, such as a false memory of how much the creature enjoyed swimming in acid, is dismissed as a bad dream. The GM might deem a modified memory too nonsensical to affect a creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.699, 0.899, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Remove Curse or Greater Restoration spell cast on the target restores the creature’s true memory."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.73, 0.904, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can alter the target’s memories of an event that took place up to 7 days ago (level 6 spell slot), 30 days ago (level 7 spell slot), 365 days ago (level 8 spell slot), or any time in the creature’s past (level 9 spell slot)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.815, 0.632, 0.83], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Moonbeam", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.832, 0.709, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.851, 0.806, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a moonseed leaf) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "150"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 150, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A silvery beam of pale light shines down in a 5-foot-radius, 40-foot-high Cylinder centered on a point within range. Until the spell ends, Dim Light fills the Cylinder, and you can take a Magic action on later turns to move the Cylinder up to 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.488, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the Cylinder appears, each creature in it makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d10 Radiant damage, and if the creature is shape-shifted (as a result of the Polymorph spell, for example), it reverts to its true form and can’t shape-shift until it leaves the Cylinder. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. A creature also makes this save when the spell’s area moves into its space and when it enters the spell’s area or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.296, 0.476, 0.327], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.334, 0.215, 0.35], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Move Earth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.351, 0.448, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Transmutation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a miniature shovel) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 2 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.439, 0.485, 0.668], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose an area of terrain no larger than 40 feet on a side within range. You can reshape dirt, sand, or clay in the area in any manner you choose for the duration. You can raise or lower the area’s elevation, create or fill in a trench, erect or flatten a wall, or form a pillar. The extent of any such changes can’t exceed half the area’s largest dimension. For example, if you affect a 40-foot square, you can create a pillar up to 20 feet high, raise or lower the square’s elevation by up to 20 feet, dig a trench up to 20 feet deep, and so on. It takes 10 minutes for these changes to complete. Because the terrain’s transformation occurs slowly, creatures in the area can’t usually be trapped or injured by the ground’s movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.669, 0.483, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the end of every 10 minutes you spend concentrating on the spell, you can choose a new area of terrain to affect within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.715, 0.483, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell can’t manipulate natural stone or stone construction. Rocks and structures shift to accommodate the new terrain. If the way you shape the terrain would make a structure unstable, it might collapse."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.791, 0.476, 0.838], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Similarly, this spell doesn’t directly affect plant growth. The moved earth carries any plants along with it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.845, 0.402, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nondetection", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Abjuration (Bard, Ranger, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.882, 0.257, 0.913], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.89, 0.095], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of diamond dust worth 25+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.103, 0.896, 0.196], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you hide a target that you touch from Divination spells. The target can be a willing creature, or it can be a place or an object no larger than 10 feet in any dimension. The target can’t be targeted by any Divination spell or perceived through magical scrying sensors."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.203, 0.607, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Passwall"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.22, 0.756, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Transmutation (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.24, 0.848, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of sesame seeds) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.308, 0.91, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A passage appears at a point that you can see on a wooden, plaster, or stone surface (such as a wall, ceiling, or floor) within range and lasts for the duration. You choose the opening’s dimensions: up to 5 feet wide, 8 feet tall, and 20 feet deep. The passage creates no instability in a structure surrounding it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.4, 0.909, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the opening disappears, any creatures or objects still in the passage created by the spell are safely ejected to an unoccupied space nearest to the surface on which you cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.469, 0.702, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pass without Trace", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.486, 0.772, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.506, 0.881, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (ashes from burned mistletoe) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.572, 0.899, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You radiate a concealing aura in a 30-foot Emanation for the duration. While in the aura, you and each creature you choose have a +10 bonus to Dexterity (Stealth) checks and leave no tracks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.642, 0.81, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Phantasmal Force", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.68, 0.808, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of fleece) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.746, 0.899, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to craft an illusion in the mind of a creature you can see within range. The target makes an Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, you create a phantasmal object, creature, or other phenomenon that is no larger than a 10-foot Cube and that is perceivable only to the target for the duration. The phantasm includes sound, temperature, and other stimuli."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.869, 0.912, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target can take a Study action to examine the phantasm with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If the check succeeds,"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "151"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 151, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.48, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "the target realizes that the phantasm is an illusion, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.488, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While affected by the spell, the target treats the phantasm as if it were real and rationalizes any illogical outcomes from interacting with it. For example, if the target steps through a phantasmal bridge and survives the fall, it believes the bridge exists and something else caused it to fall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.173, 0.487, 0.282], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An affected target can even take damage from the illusion if the phantasm represents a dangerous creature or hazard. On each of your turns, such a phantasm can deal 2d8 Psychic damage to the target if it is in the phantasm’s area or within 5 feet of the phantasm. The target perceives the damage as a type appropriate to the illusion."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.288, 0.386, 0.385], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Phantasmal Killer", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 4 Illusion (Bard, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.393, 0.484, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You tap into the nightmares of a creature you can see within range and create an illusion of its deep est fears, visible only to that creature. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 4d10 Psychic damage and has Disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls for the duration. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.481, 0.576], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, the target makes a Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a failed save, it takes the Psychic damage again. On a successful save, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.577, 0.474, 0.608], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d10 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.615, 0.247, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Phantom Steed", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.633, 0.281, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Illusion (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.652, 0.333, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.487, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Large, quasi-real, horselike creature appears on the ground in an unoccupied space of your choice within range. You decide the creature’s appearance, and it is equipped with a saddle, bit, and bridle. Any of the equipment created by the spell vanishes in a puff of smoke if it is carried more than 10 feet away from the steed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.827, 0.487, 0.935], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you or a creature you choose can ride the steed. The steed uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Riding Horse", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block (see “Monsters”), except it has a Speed of 100 feet and can travel 13 miles in an hour. When the spell ends, the steed gradually fades, giving the rider 1 minute to dismount. The spell ends early if the steed takes any damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.72, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Planar Ally", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Conjuration (Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.154, 0.912, 0.293], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You beseech an otherworldly entity for aid. The being must be known to you: a god, a demon prince, or some other being of cosmic power. That entity sends a Celestial, an Elemental, or a Fiend loyal to it to aid you, making the creature appear in an unoccupied space within range. If you know a specific creature’s name, you can speak that name when you cast this spell to request that creature, though you might get a different creature anyway (GM’s choice)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.294, 0.907, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the creature appears, it is under no compulsion to behave a particular way. You can ask it to perform a service in exchange for payment, but it isn’t obliged to do so. The requested task could range from simple (fly us across the chasm, or help us fight a battle) to complex (spy on our enemies, or protect us during our foray into the dungeon). You must be able to communicate with the creature to bargain for its services."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.431, 0.899, 0.523], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Payment can take a variety of forms. A Celestial might require a sizable donation of gold or magic items to an allied temple, while a Fiend might demand a living sacrifice or a gift of treasure. Some creatures might exchange their service for a quest undertaken by you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.523, 0.911, 0.707], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A task that can be measured in minutes requires a payment worth 100 GP per minute. A task measured in hours requires 1,000 GP per hour. And a task measured in days (up to 10 days) requires 10,000 GP per day. The GM can adjust these payments based on the circumstances under which you cast the spell. If the task is aligned with the creature’s ethos, the payment might be halved or even waived. Nonhazardous tasks typically require only half the suggested payment, while especially dangerous tasks might require a greater gift. Creatures rarely accept tasks that seem suicidal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.707, 0.91, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After the creature completes the task, or when the agreed-upon duration of service expires, the creature returns to its home plane after reporting back to you if possible. If you are unable to agree on a price for the creature’s service, the creature immediately returns to its home plane."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.807, 0.659, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Planar Binding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.824, 0.865, 0.855], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.525, 0.859, 0.679, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.875, 0.632, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.889, 0.897, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a jewel worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.525, 0.919, 0.663, 0.933], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "152"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 152, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.48, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to bind a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend to your service. The creature must be within range for the entire casting of the spell. (Typically, the creature is first summoned into the center of the inverted version of the Magic Circle spell to trap it while this spell is cast.) At the completion of the casting, the target must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or be bound to serve you for the duration. If the creature was summoned or created by another spell, that spell’s duration is extended to match the duration of this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.484, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A bound creature must follow your commands to the best of its ability. You might command the creature to accompany you on an adventure, to guard a location, or to deliver a message. If the creature is Hostile, it strives to twist your commands to achieve its own objectives. If the creature carries out your commands completely before the spell ends, it travels to you to report this fact if you are on the same plane of existence. If you are on a different plane, it returns to the place where you bound it and remains there until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.388, 0.481, 0.435], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The duration increases with a spell slot of level 6 (10 days), 7 (30 days), 8 (180 days), and 9 (366 days)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.441, 0.206, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plane Shift", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.459, 0.474, 0.49], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Conjuration (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.494, 0.256, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.509, 0.203, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.523, 0.475, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a forked, metal rod worth 250+ GP and attuned to a plane of existence)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.554, 0.275, 0.568], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.576, 0.49, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and up to eight willing creatures who link hands in a circle are transported to a different plane of existence. You can specify a target destination in general terms, such as a specific city on the Elemental Plane of Fire or palace on the second level of the Nine Hells, and you appear in or near that destination, as determined by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.683, 0.49, 0.776], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, if you know the sigil sequence of a teleportation circle on another plane of existence, this spell can take you to that circle. If the teleportation circle is too small to hold all the creatures you transported, they appear in the closest unoccupied spaces next to the circle."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.783, 0.231, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plant Growth", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.8, 0.42, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Bard, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.82, 0.375, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action (Overgrowth) or 8 hours (Enrichment) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.902, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell channels vitality into plants. The casting time you use determines whether the spell has the Overgrowth or the Enrichment effect below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.909, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Overgrowth.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose a point within range. All normal plants in a 100-foot-radius Sphere centered on that point become thick and overgrown. A creature moving through that area must spend 4 feet of movement for every 1 foot it moves. You can exclude one or more areas of any size within the spell’s area from being affected."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.204, 0.91, 0.281], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Enrichment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " All plants in a half-mile radius centered on a point within range become enriched for 365 days. The plants yield twice the normal amount of food when harvested. They can benefit from only one Plant Growth per year."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.288, 0.646, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison Spray", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.306, 0.859, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Necromancy Cantrip (Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.341, 0.696, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.408, 0.901, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You spray toxic mist at a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d12 Poison damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.454, 0.902, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d12 when you reach levels 5 (2d12), 11 (3d12), and 17 (4d12)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.507, 0.629, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Polymorph", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.525, 0.908, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Transmutation (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.545, 0.679, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.56, 0.631, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.575, 0.821, 0.605], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a caterpillar cocoon) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.906, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You attempt to transform a creature that you can see within range into a Beast. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or shape-shift into a Beast form for the duration. That form can be any Beast you choose that has a Challenge Rating equal to or less than the target’s (or the target’s level if it doesn’t have a Challenge Rating). The target’s game statistics are replaced by the stat block of the chosen Beast, but the target retains its alignment, personality, creature type, Hit Points, and Hit Point Dice. See the “Animals” section of “Monsters” for a sample of Beast stat blocks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.796, 0.908, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target gains a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the Beast form. These Temporary Hit Points vanish if any remain when the spell ends. The spell ends early on the target if it has no Temporary Hit Points left."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.873, 0.91, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target is limited in the actions it can perform by the anatomy of its new form, and it can’t speak or cast spells."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "153"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 153, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.483, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target’s gear melds into the new form. The creature can’t use or otherwise benefit from any of that equipment. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Power Word Heal", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 9 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.209, 0.482, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A wave of healing energy washes over one creature you can see within range. The target regains all its Hit Points. If the creature has the Charmed, Frightened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, or Stunned condition, the condition ends. If the creature has the Prone condition, it can use its Reaction to stand up."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.308, 0.26, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Power Word Kill"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.321, 0.435, 0.42], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.428, 0.475, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You compel one creature you can see within range to die. If the target has 100 Hit Points or fewer, it dies. Otherwise, it takes 12d12 Psychic damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.482, 0.27, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Power Word Stun"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.499, 0.434, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.602, 0.482, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You overwhelm the mind of one creature you can see within range. If the target has 150 Hit Points or fewer, it has the Stunned condition. Otherwise, its Speed is 0 until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.663, 0.488, 0.71], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Stunned target makes a Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the condition on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.717, 0.265, 0.734], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prayer of Healing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.735, 0.351, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.755, 0.284, 0.814], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.822, 0.472, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Up to five creatures of your choice who remain within range for the spell’s entire casting gain the benefits of a Short Rest and also regain 2d8 Hit Points. A creature can’t be affected by this spell again until that creature finishes a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.892, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The healing increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.872, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prestidigitation", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Transmutation Cantrip (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.209, 0.902, 0.27], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a magical effect within range. Choose the effect from the options below. If you cast this spell multiple times, you can have up to three of its non-instantaneous effects active at a time."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.271, 0.908, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sensory Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create an instantaneous, harmless sensory effect, such as a shower of sparks, a puff of wind, faint musical notes, or an odd odor."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.316, 0.906, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Play.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You instantaneously light or snuff out a candle, a torch, or a small campfire."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.347, 0.908, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clean or Soil.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You instantaneously clean or soil an object no larger than 1 cubic foot."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.525, 0.377, 0.901, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Minor Sensation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You chill, warm, or flavor up to 1 cubic foot of nonliving material for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.409, 0.901, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Mark.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You make a color, a small mark, or a symbol appear on an object or a surface for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.439, 0.899, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Minor Creation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create a nonmagical trinket or an illusory image that can fit in your hand. It lasts until the end of your next turn. A trinket can deal no damage and has no monetary worth."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.508, 0.67, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prismatic Spray"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.52, 0.828, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Evocation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.611, 0.905, 0.69], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eight rays of light flash from you in a 60-foot Cone. Each creature in the Cone makes a Dexterity saving throw. For each target, roll 1d8 to determine which color ray affects it, consulting the Prismatic Rays table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.702, 0.65, 0.718], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prismatic Rays"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.53, 0.722, 0.91, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.53, 0.722, 0.91, 0.88], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id8 Ray</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Red. Failed Save: 12d6 Fire damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Orange. Failed Save: 12d6 Acid damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Yellow. Failed Save: I2d6 Lightning damage. Suc- cessful Save: Half as much damage.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Green. Failed Save: I2d6 Poison damage. Success- ful Save: Half as much damage.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "154"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 154, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.112, 0.056, 0.18, 0.071], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d8 Ray", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.116, 0.074, 0.465, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "5 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Blue.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: 12d6 Cold damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.116, 0.11, 0.479, 0.253], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Indigo.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: The target has the Restrained condition and makes a Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns. If it successfully saves three times, the condition ends. If it fails three times, it has the Petrified condition until it is freed by an effect like the Greater Restoration spell. The successes and failures needn’t be consecutive; keep track of both until the target collects three of a kind."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.116, 0.257, 0.481, 0.353], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "7 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Violet.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: The target has the Blinded condition and makes a Wisdom saving throw at the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the condition ends. On a failed save, the condition ends, and the creature teleports to another plane of existence (GM’s choice)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.117, 0.356, 0.458, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "8 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Special.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target is struck by two rays. Roll twice, rerolling any 8."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.4, 0.239, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prismatic Wall", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.418, 0.345, 0.434], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Abjuration (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.438, 0.257, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.453, 0.209, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.468, 0.235, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.483, 0.254, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.505, 0.485, 0.628], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A shimmering, multicolored plane of light forms a vertical opaque wall—up to 90 feet long, 30 feet high, and 1 inch thick—centered on a point within range. Alternatively, you shape the wall into a globe up to 30 feet in diameter centered on a point within range. The wall lasts for the duration. If you position the wall in a space occupied by a creature, the spell ends instantly without effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.628, 0.489, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall sheds Bright Light within 100 feet and Dim Light for an additional 100 feet. You and creatures you designate when you cast the spell can pass through and be near the wall without harm. If another creature that can see the wall moves within 20 feet of it or starts its turn there, the creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the Blinded condition for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.75, 0.485, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall consists of seven layers, each with a different color. When a creature reaches into or passes through the wall, it does so one layer at a time through all the layers. Each layer forces the creature to make a Dexterity saving throw or be affected by that layer’s properties as described in the Prismatic Layers table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.857, 0.487, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall, which has AC 10, can be destroyed one layer at a time, in order from red to violet, by means"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.91, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "specific to each layer. If a layer is destroyed, it is gone for the duration. Antimagic Field has no effect on the wall, and Dispel Magic can affect only the violet layer."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.125, 0.666, 0.141], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prismatic Layers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.535, 0.144, 0.648, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Order Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.547, 0.162, 0.904, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Red. Failed Save: 12d6 Fire damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage. Additional Effects: Nonmagical ranged attacks can’t pass through this layer, which is destroyed if it takes at least 25 Cold damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.55, 0.246, 0.898, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Orange.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: 12d6 Acid damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage. Additional Effects: Magical ranged attacks can’t pass through this layer, which is destroyed by a strong wind (such as the one created by Gust of Wind)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.551, 0.345, 0.902, 0.409], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "3 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Yellow.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: 12d6 Lightning damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage. Additional Effects: The layer is destroyed if it takes at least 60 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.551, 0.413, 0.898, 0.492], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "4 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Green.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: 12d6 Poison damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage. Additional Effects: A Passwall spell, or another spell of equal or greater level that can open a portal on a solid surface, destroys this layer."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.551, 0.496, 0.903, 0.559], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "5 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Blue.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: 12d6 Cold damage. Successful Save: Half as much damage. Additional Effects: The layer is destroyed if it takes at least 25 Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.55, 0.563, 0.904, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Indigo.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: The target has the Restrained condition and makes a Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns. If it successfully saves three times, the condition ends. If it fails three times, it has the Petrified condition until it is freed by an effect like the Greater Restoration spell. The successes and failures needn’t be consecutive; keep track of both until the target collects three of a kind. Additional Effects: Spells can’t be cast through this layer, which is destroyed by Bright Light shed by the Daylight spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.548, 0.757, 0.904, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "7 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Violet.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Failed Save: The target has the Blinded condition and makes a Wisdom saving throw at the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the condition ends. On a failed save, the condition ends, and the creature teleports to another plane of existence (GM’s choice). Additional Effects: This layer is destroyed by Dispel Magic."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "155"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 155, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.255, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Private Sanctum"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.068, 0.395, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Abjuration (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a thin sheet of lead) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.477, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You make an area within range magically secure. The area is a Cube that can be as small as 5 feet to as large as 100 feet on each side. The spell lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.217, 0.478, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, you decide what sort of security the spell provides, choosing any of the following properties:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.269, 0.476, 0.299], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Sound can’t pass through the barrier at the edge of the warded area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.3, 0.481, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The barrier of the warded area appears dark and foggy, preventing vision (including Darkvision) through it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.346, 0.487, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Sensors created by Divination spells can’t appear inside the protected area or pass through the barrier at its perimeter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.392, 0.484, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Creatures in the area can’t be targeted by Divination spells."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.423, 0.462, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Nothing can teleport into or out of the warded area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.453, 0.479, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Planar travel is blocked within the warded area. Casting this spell on the same spot every day for 365 days makes the spell last until dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.507, 0.483, 0.552], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can increase the size of the Cube by 100 feet for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.56, 0.242, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Produce Flame", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.577, 0.304, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conjuration Cantrip (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.597, 0.302, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.664, 0.488, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A flickering flame appears in your hand and remains there for the duration. While there, the flame emits no heat and ignites nothing, and it sheds Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet. The spell ends if you cast it again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.742, 0.487, 0.802], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to hurl fire at a creature or an object within 60 feet of you. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.802, 0.473, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.857, 0.295, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Programmed Illusion", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.874, 0.321, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Illusion (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.894, 0.257, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.85, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (jade dust worth 25+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.91, 0.21], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create an illusion of an object, a creature, or some other visible phenomenon within range that activates when a specific trigger occurs. The illusion is imperceptible until then. It must be no larger than a 30-foot Cube, and you decide when you cast the spell how the illusion behaves and what sounds it makes. This scripted performance can last up to 5 minutes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.211, 0.908, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the trigger you specify occurs, the illusion springs into existence and performs in the manner you described. Once the illusion finishes performing, it disappears and remains dormant for 10 minutes, after which the illusion can be activated again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.288, 0.91, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The trigger can be as general or as detailed as you like, though it must be based on visual or audible phenomena that occur within 30 feet of the area. For example, you could create an illusion of yourself to appear and warn off others who attempt to open a trapped door."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.38, 0.911, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Physical interaction with the image reveals it to be illusory, since things can pass through it. A creature that takes the Study action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the image, and any noise it makes sounds hollow to the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.525, 0.655, 0.542], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Project Image", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.543, 0.743, 0.559], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Illusion (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.562, 0.679, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.577, 0.647, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 500 miles"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.592, 0.876, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a statuette of yourself worth 5+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.621, 0.784, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 day"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.644, 0.906, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create an illusory copy of yourself that lasts for the duration. The copy can appear at any location within range that you have seen before, regardless of intervening obstacles. The illusion looks and sounds like you, but it is intangible. If the illusion takes any damage, it disappears, and the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.737, 0.91, 0.813], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can see through the illusion’s eyes and hear through its ears as if you were in its space. As a Magic action, you can move it up to 60 feet and make it gesture, speak, and behave in whatever way you choose. It mimics your mannerisms perfectly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.813, 0.912, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Physical interaction with the image reveals it to be illusory, since things can pass through it. A creature that takes the Study action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "156"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 156, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.481, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "image, and any noise it makes sounds hollow to the creature."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.461, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protection from Energy", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Abjuration (Cleric, Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.208, 0.485, 0.256], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, the willing creature you touch has Resistance to one damage type of your choice: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.482, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protection from Evil and Good", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Abjuration (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a flask of Holy Water worth 25+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.397, 0.487, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch is protected against creatures that are Aberrations, Celestials, Elementals, Fey, Fiends, or Undead. The protection grants several benefits. Creatures of those types have Disadvantage on attack rolls against the target. The target also can’t be possessed by or gain the Charmed or Frightened conditions from them. If the target is already possessed, Charmed, or Frightened by such a creature, the target has Advantage on any new saving throw against the relevant effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.574, 0.457, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protection from Poison", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Abjuration (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.678, 0.479, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature and end the Poisoned condition on it. For the duration, the target has Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition, and it has Resistance to Poison damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.747, 0.428, 0.844], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Purify Food and Drink", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.851, 0.468, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You remove poison and rot from nonmagical food and drink in a 5-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.909, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Raise Dead", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Necromancy (Bard, Cleric, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 500+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.523, 0.169, 0.901, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a touch, you revive a dead creature if it has been dead no longer than 10 days and it wasn’t Undead when it died."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.216, 0.903, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature returns to life with 1 Hit Point. This spell also neutralizes any poisons that affected the creature at the time of death."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.262, 0.904, 0.323], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell closes all mortal wounds, but it doesn’t restore missing body parts. If the creature is lacking body parts or organs integral for its survival— its head, for instance—the spell automatically fails."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.323, 0.902, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Coming back from the dead is an ordeal. The target takes a −4 penalty to D20 Tests. Every time the target finishes a Long Rest, the penalty is reduced by 1 until it becomes 0."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.393, 0.807, 0.49], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ray of Enfeeblement", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Necromancy (Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.497, 0.91, 0.573], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A beam of enervating energy shoots from you toward a creature within range. The target must make a Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, the target has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.574, 0.901, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage on Strength-based D20 Tests for the duration. During that time, it also subtracts 1d8 from all its damage rolls. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.658, 0.79, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ray of Frost", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.762, 0.895, 0.839], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A frigid beam of blue-white light streaks toward a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, it takes 1d8 Cold damage, and its Speed is reduced by 10 feet until the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.839, 0.895, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "157"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 157, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.212, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regenerate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.068, 0.41, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Transmutation (Bard, Cleric, Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a prayer wheel) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.478, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature you touch regains 4d8 + 15 Hit Points. For the duration, the target regains 1 Hit Point at the start of each of its turns, and any severed body parts regrow after 2 minutes."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.224, 0.245, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ray of Sickness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.242, 0.382, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.262, 0.274, 0.321], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.329, 0.485, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You shoot a greenish ray at a creature within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.39, 0.478, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.216, 0.445], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reincarnate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.446, 0.305, 0.463], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Necromancy (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.466, 0.257, 0.481], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.481, 0.203, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.496, 0.484, 0.527], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (rare oils worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.526, 0.275, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.547, 0.478, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a dead Humanoid or a piece of one. If the creature has been dead no longer than 10 days, the spell forms a new body for it and calls the soul to enter that body. Roll 1d10 and consult the table below to determine the body’s species, or the GM chooses another playable species."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.104, 0.65, 0.488, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.104, 0.65, 0.488, 0.764], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI0</td><td>Species</td><td>IdI0</td><td>Species</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Roll again.</td><td>6</td><td>Goliath</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Dragonborn</td><td>7</td><td>Halfling</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Dwarf</td><td>8</td><td>Human</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Elf</td><td>9</td><td>Orc</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Gnome</td><td>10</td><td>Tiefling</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.774, 0.488, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The reincarnated creature makes any choices that a species’ description offers, and the creature recalls its former life. It retains the capabilities it had in its original form, except it loses the traits of its previous species and gains the traits of its new one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.86, 0.477, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Remove Curse", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.696, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.892, 0.166], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At your touch, all curses affecting one creature or object end. If the object is a cursed magic item, its curse remains, but the spell breaks its owner’s Attunement to the object so it can be removed or discarded."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.676, 0.19], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resilient Sphere"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.19, 0.727, 0.207], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Abjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.21, 0.807, 0.27], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a glass sphere) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.277, 0.902, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A shimmering sphere encloses a Large or smaller creature or object within range. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or be enclosed for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.339, 0.912, 0.46], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nothing—not physical objects, energy, or other spell effects—can pass through the barrier, in or out, though a creature in the sphere can breathe there. The sphere is immune to all damage, and a creature or object inside can’t be damaged by attacks or effects originating from outside, nor can a creature inside the sphere damage anything outside it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.461, 0.905, 0.554], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The sphere is weightless and just large enough to contain the creature or object inside. An enclosed creature can take an action to push against the sphere’s walls and thus roll the sphere at up to half the creature’s Speed. Similarly, the globe can be picked up and moved by other creatures."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.553, 0.909, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Disintegrate spell targeting the globe destroys it without harming anything inside."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.592, 0.625, 0.608], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.609, 0.765, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Abjuration Cantrip (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.629, 0.807, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.696, 0.906, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a willing creature and choose a damage type: Acid, Bludgeoning, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, Piercing, Poison, Radiant, Slashing, or Thunder. When the creature takes damage of the chosen type before the spell ends, the creature reduces the total damage taken by 1d4. A creature can benefit from this spell only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.811, 0.647, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resurrection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.829, 0.768, 0.846], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Necromancy (Bard, Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.849, 0.878, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "158"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 158, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.48, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a touch, you revive a dead creature that has been dead for no more than a century, didn’t die of old age, and wasn’t Undead when it died."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.486, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature returns to life with all its Hit Points. This spell also neutralizes any poisons that affected the creature at the time of death. This spell closes all mortal wounds and restores any missing body parts."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.173, 0.478, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Coming back from the dead is an ordeal. The target takes a −4 penalty to D20 Tests. Every time the target finishes a Long Rest, the penalty is reduced by 1 until it becomes 0."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.234, 0.47, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting this spell to revive a creature that has been dead for 365 days or longer taxes you. Until you finish a Long Rest, you can’t cast spells again, and you have Disadvantage on D20 Tests."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.303, 0.253, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reverse Gravity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.32, 0.446, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Transmutation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.341, 0.447, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 100 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a lodestone and iron filings) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.408, 0.49, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell reverses gravity in a 50-foot-radius, 100- foot high Cylinder centered on a point within range. All creatures and objects in that area that aren’t anchored to the ground fall upward and reach the top of the Cylinder. A creature can make a Dexterity saving throw to grab a fixed object it can reach, thus avoiding the fall upward."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.484, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a ceiling or an anchored object is encountered in this upward fall, creatures and objects strike it just as they would during a downward fall. If an affected creature or object reaches the Cylinder’s top without striking anything, it hovers there for the duration. When the spell ends, affected objects and creatures fall downward."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.631, 0.179, 0.647], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Revivify"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.648, 0.468, 0.664], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Necromancy (Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.668, 0.257, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.683, 0.204, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.697, 0.486, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a diamond worth 300+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.749, 0.487, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature that has died within the last minute. That creature revives with 1 Hit Point. This spell can’t revive a creature that has died of old age, nor does it restore any missing body parts."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.819, 0.208, 0.836], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rope Trick"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.836, 0.334, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.856, 0.388, 0.915], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a segment of rope) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.902, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a rope. One end of it hovers upward until the rope hangs perpendicular to the ground or the rope reaches a ceiling. At the rope’s upper end, an Invisible 3-foot-by-5-foot portal opens to an extradimensional space that lasts until the spell ends. That space can be reached by climbing the rope, which can be pulled into or dropped out of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.158, 0.905, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The space can hold up to eight Medium or smaller creatures. Attacks, spells, and other effects can’t pass into or out of the space, but creatures inside it can see through the portal. Anything inside the space drops out when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.242, 0.652, 0.259], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sacred Flame"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.26, 0.712, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Evocation Cantrip (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.696, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.347, 0.91, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 Radiant damage. The target gains no benefit from Half Cover or Three-Quarters Cover for this save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.423, 0.895, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.477, 0.622, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sanctuary", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.495, 0.713, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Abjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.514, 0.724, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.53, 0.632, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.544, 0.886, 0.574], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a shard of glass from a mirror) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.582, 0.907, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You ward a creature within range. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack roll or a damaging spell must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or either choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn’t protect the warded creature from areas of effect. The spell ends if the warded creature makes an attack roll, casts a spell, or deals damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.712, 0.787, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scorching Ray", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.749, 0.697, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.817, 0.895, 0.878], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hurl three fiery rays. You can hurl them at one target within range or at several. Make a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.523, 0.878, 0.891, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create one additional ray for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "159"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 159, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.176, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scrying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.068, 0.442, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.103, 0.285, 0.119], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.118, 0.187, 0.133], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.132, 0.485, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a focus worth 1,000+ GP, such as a crystal ball, mirror, or water-filled font) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.185, 0.482, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can see and hear a creature you choose that is on the same plane of existence as you. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw, which is modified (see the tables below) by how well you know the target and the sort of physical connection you have to it. The target doesn’t know what it is making the save against, only that it feels uneasy."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.297, 0.487, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.104, 0.297, 0.487, 0.372], "content": "<table><tr><td>Your Knowledge of the Target Is ..</td><td>Save Modifier</td></tr><tr><td>Secondhand (heard of the target)</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>Firsthand (met the target)</td><td>+0</td></tr><tr><td>Extensive (know the target well)</td><td>-5</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.105, 0.385, 0.486, 0.46], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.105, 0.385, 0.486, 0.46], "content": "<table><tr><td>You Have the Targets&#x27;s .</td><td>Save Modifier</td></tr><tr><td>Picture or other likeness</td><td>-2</td></tr><tr><td>Garment or other possession</td><td>-4</td></tr><tr><td>Body part, lock of hair, or bit of nail</td><td>-10</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.469, 0.483, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a successful save, the target isn’t affected, and you can’t use this spell on it again for 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.5, 0.485, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, the spell creates an Invisible, intangible sensor within 10 feet of the target. You can see and hear through the sensor as if you were there. The sensor moves with the target, remaining within 10 feet of it for the duration. If something can see the sensor, it appears as a luminous orb about the size of your fist."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.607, 0.481, 0.654], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instead of targeting a creature, you can target a location you have seen. When you do so, the sensor appears at that location and doesn’t move."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.661, 0.233, 0.678], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Searing Smite"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.678, 0.299, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.697, 0.476, 0.742], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action, which you take immediately after hitting a target with a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.742, 0.187, 0.757], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.757, 0.214, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.772, 0.24, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.794, 0.489, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As you hit the target, it takes an extra 1d6 Fire damage from the attack. At the start of each of its turns until the spell ends, the target takes 1d6 Fire damage and then makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the spell continues. On a successful save, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.886, 0.472, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " All the damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.648, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Secret Chest"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.068, 0.735, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.087, 0.68, 0.103], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.103, 0.625, 0.118], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.118, 0.909, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a chest, 3 feet by 2 feet by 2 feet, constructed from rare materials worth 5,000+ GP, and a Tiny replica of the chest made from the same materials worth 50+ GP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.176, 0.699, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.199, 0.905, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You hide a chest and all its contents on the Ethereal Plane. You must touch the chest and the miniature replica that serve as Material components for the spell. The chest can contain up to 12 cubic feet of nonliving material (3 feet by 2 feet by 2 feet)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.276, 0.908, 0.368], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While the chest remains on the Ethereal Plane, you can take a Magic action and touch the replica to recall the chest. It appears in an unoccupied space on the ground within 5 feet of you. You can send the chest back to the Ethereal Plane by taking a Magic action to touch the chest and the replica."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.368, 0.908, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After 60 days, there is a cumulative 5 percent chance at the end of each day that the spell ends. The spell also ends if you cast this spell again or if the Tiny replica chest is destroyed. If the spell ends and the larger chest is on the Ethereal Plane, the chest remains there for you or someone else to find."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.467, 0.659, 0.485], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "See Invisibility"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.485, 0.832, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Divination (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.505, 0.679, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.52, 0.609, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.534, 0.782, 0.55], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of talc)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.549, 0.65, 0.564], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.571, 0.907, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you see creatures and objects that have the Invisible condition as if they were visible, and you can see into the Ethereal Plane. Creatures and objects there appear ghostly."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.641, 0.608, 0.659], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Seeming"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.658, 0.809, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.678, 0.68, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.525, 0.693, 0.632, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.524, 0.708, 0.656, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.724, 0.655, 0.738], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.522, 0.746, 0.905, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You give an illusory appearance to each creature of your choice that you can see within range. An unwilling target can make a Charisma saving throw, and if it succeeds, it is unaffected by this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.522, 0.807, 0.905, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can give the same appearance or different ones to the targets. The spell can change the appearance of the targets’ bodies and equipment. You can make each creature seem 1 foot shorter or taller and appear heavier or lighter. A target’s new appearance must have the same basic arrangement of limbs as the target, but the extent of the illusion"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "160"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 160, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.435, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "is otherwise up to you. The spell lasts for the duration."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.481, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The changes wrought by this spell fail to hold up to physical inspection. For example, if you use this spell to add a hat to a creature’s outfit, objects pass through the hat."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.143, 0.483, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that takes the Study action to examine a target can make an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If it succeeds, it becomes aware that the target is disguised."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.211, 0.18, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sending"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.229, 0.391, 0.245], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.249, 0.361, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Unlimited "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a copper wire) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.48, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You send a short message of 25 words or fewer to a creature you have met or a creature described to you by someone who has met it. The target hears the message in its mind, recognizes you as the sender if it knows you, and can answer in a like manner immediately. The spell enables targets to understand the meaning of your message."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.423, 0.487, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can send the message across any distance and even to other planes of existence, but if the target is on a different plane than you, there is a 5 percent chance that the message doesn’t arrive. You know if the delivery fails."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.5, 0.49, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Upon receiving your message, a creature can block your ability to reach it again with this spell for 8 hours. If you try to send another message during that time, you learn that you are blocked, and the spell fails."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.585, 0.199, 0.601], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sequester"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.602, 0.333, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Transmutation (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.621, 0.257, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.637, 0.203, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.65, 0.448, 0.666], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (gem dust worth 5,000+ GP,"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.112, 0.667, 0.295, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.68, 0.278, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.703, 0.488, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a touch, you magically sequester an object or a willing creature. For the duration, the target has the Invisible condition and can’t be targeted by Divination spells, detected by magic, or viewed remotely with magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.781, 0.489, 0.826], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the target is a creature, it enters a state of suspended animation; it has the Unconscious condition, doesn’t age, and doesn’t need food, water, or air."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.827, 0.483, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can set a condition for the spell to end early. The condition can be anything you choose, but it must occur or be visible within 1 mile of the target. Examples include “after 1,000 years” or “when the tarrasque awakens.” This spell also ends if the target takes any damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.647, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shapechange"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.802, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Transmutation (Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.088, 0.895, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a jade circlet worth 1,500+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.907, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You shape-shift into another creature for the duration or until you take a Magic action to shape-shift into a different eligible form. The new form must be of a creature that has a Challenge Rating no higher than your level or Challenge Rating. You must have seen the sort of creature before, and it can’t be a Construct or an Undead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.263, 0.908, 0.339], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast the spell, you gain a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the first form into which you shape-shift. These Temporary Hit Points vanish if any remain when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.339, 0.91, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your game statistics are replaced by the stat block of the chosen form, but you retain your creature type; alignment; personality; Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; Hit Points; Hit Point Dice; proficiencies; and ability to communicate. If you have the Spellcasting feature, you retain it too."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.431, 0.91, 0.478], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Upon shape-shifting, you determine whether your equipment drops to the ground or changes in size and shape to fit the new form while you’re in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.485, 0.599, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shatter"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.503, 0.827, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a chip of mica) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.589, 0.903, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A loud noise erupts from a point of your choice within range. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered there makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 3d8 Thunder damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A Construct has Disadvantage on the save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.682, 0.898, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A nonmagical object that isn’t being worn or carried also takes the damage if it’s in the spell’s area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.712, 0.896, 0.744], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage inc"}, {"type": "text", "content": "reases", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.75, 0.585, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.768, 0.792, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Abjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.788, 0.894, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reaction, which you take when you are hit by an attack roll or targeted by the Magic Missile spell"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.525, 0.832, 0.608, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.525, 0.847, 0.656, 0.862], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.863, 0.657, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 round"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.884, 0.901, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An imperceptible barrier of magical force protects you. Until the start of your next turn, you have a +5"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "161"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 161, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.083], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and you take no damage from Magic Missile."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.088, 0.4, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shield of Faith", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a prayer scroll) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.193, 0.487, 0.24], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A shimmering field surrounds a creature of your choice within range, granting it a +2 bonus to AC for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.247, 0.33, 0.344], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shillelagh", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Transmutation Cantrip (Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (mistletoe) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.352, 0.485, 0.474], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Club or Quarterstaff you are holding is imbued with nature’s power. For the duration, you can use your spellcasting ability instead of Strength for the attack and damage rolls of melee attacks using that weapon, and the weapon’s damage die becomes a d8. If the attack deals damage, it can be Force damage or the weapon’s normal damage type (your choice)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.474, 0.489, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell ends early if you cast it again or if you let go of the weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.505, 0.481, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage die changes when you reach levels 5 (d10), 11 (d12), and 17 (2d6)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.543, 0.333, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shining Smite", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Transmutation (Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.58, 0.474, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action, which you take immediately after hitting a creature with a Melee weapon or an Unarmed Strike "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.677, 0.488, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target hit by the strike takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage from the attack. Until the spell ends, the target sheds Bright Light in a 5-foot radius, attack rolls against it have Advantage, and it can’t benefit from the Invisible condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.754, 0.475, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.793, 0.368, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shocking Grasp", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.83, 0.274, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.897, 0.474, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning springs from you to a creature that you try to touch. Make a melee spell attack against the"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.909, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "target. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 Lightning damage, and it can’t make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.096, 0.895, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.15, 0.822, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Silence", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 2 Illusion (Bard, Cleric, Ranger) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.255, 0.911, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, no sound can be created within or pass through a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point you choose within range. Any creature or object entirely inside the Sphere has Immunity to Thunder damage, and creatures have the Deafened condition while entirely inside it. Casting a spell that includes a Verbal component is impossible there."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.385, 0.821, 0.483], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Silent Image", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Illusion (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of fleece) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.49, 0.897, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create the image of an object, a creature, or some other visible phenomenon that is no larger than a 15-foot Cube. The image appears at a spot within range and lasts for the duration. The image is purely visual; it isn’t accompanied by sound, smell, or other sensory effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.583, 0.89, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can cause the image to move to any spot within range. As the image changes location, you can alter its appearance so that its movements appear natural for the image. For example, if you create an image of a creature and move it, you can alter the image so that it appears to be walking."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.689, 0.912, 0.813], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Physical interaction with the image reveals it to be an illusion, since things can pass through it. A creature that takes a Study action to examine the image can determine that it is an illusion with a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If a creature discerns the illusion for what it is, the creature can see through the image."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.819, 0.638, 0.836], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Simulacrum"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.837, 0.702, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Illusion (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.857, 0.693, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 12 hours "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.886, 0.91, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (powdered ruby worth 1,500+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "162"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 162, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a simulacrum of one Beast or Humanoid that is within 10 feet of you for the entire casting of the spell. You finish the casting by touching both the creature and a pile of ice or snow that is the same size as that creature, and the pile turns into the simulacrum, which is a creature. It uses the game statistics of the original creature at the time of casting, except it is a Construct, its Hit Point maximum is half as much, and it can’t cast this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.189, 0.485, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The simulacrum is Friendly to you and creatures you designate. It obeys your commands and acts on your turn in combat. The simulacrum can’t gain levels, and it can’t take Short or Long Rests."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.479, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the simulacrum takes damage, the only way to restore its Hit Points is to repair it as you take a Long Rest, during which you expend components worth 100 GP per Hit Point restored. The simulacrum must stay within 5 feet of you for the repair."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.49, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The simulacrum lasts until it drops to 0 Hit Points, at which point it reverts to snow and melts away. If you cast this spell again, any simulacrum you created with this spell is instantly destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.396, 0.158, 0.413], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sleep"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.43, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.433, 0.257, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.448, 0.209, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.462, 0.463, 0.492], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pinch of sand or rose petals) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.5, 0.49, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature of your choice in a 5-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Incapacitated condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it must repeat the save. If the target fails the second save, the target has the Unconscious condition for the duration. The spell ends on a target if it takes damage or someone within 5 feet of it takes an action to shake it out of the spell’s effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.639, 0.471, 0.685], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures that don’t sleep, such as elves, or that have Immunity to the Exhaustion condition a"}, {"type": "text", "content": "uto", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "matically succeed on saves against this spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.691, 0.216, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sleet Storm"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.709, 0.425, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Conjuration (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.729, 0.406, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a miniature umbrella) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.795, 0.481, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, sleet falls in a 40-foot-tall, 20-foot-radius Cylinder centered on a point you choose within range. The area is Heavily Obscured, and exposed flames in the area are doused."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.858, 0.478, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ground in the Cylinder is Difficult Terrain. When a creature enters the Cylinder for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition and lose Concentration."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.575, 0.105], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slow"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.107, 0.863, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of molasses) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.895, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You alter time around up to six creatures of your choice in a 40-foot Cube within range. Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be affected by this spell for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.905, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An affected target’s Speed is halved, it takes a −2 penalty to AC and Dexterity saving throws, and it can’t take Reactions. On its turns, it can take either an action or a Bonus Action, not both, and it can make only one attack if it takes the Attack action. If it casts a spell with a Somatic component, there is a 25 percent chance the spell fails as a result of the target making the spell’s gestures too slowly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.377, 0.888, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An affected target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.431, 0.678, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sorcerous Burst", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.449, 0.732, 0.465], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Evocation Cantrip (Sorcerer)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.469, 0.697, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Component:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.536, 0.912, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You cast sorcerous energy at one creature or object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 damage of a type you choose: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, Psychic, or Thunder."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.912, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you roll an 8 on a d8 for this spell, you can roll another d8, and add it to the damage. When you cast this spell, the maximum number of these d8s you can add to the spell’s damage equals your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.689, 0.895, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.743, 0.778, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spare the Dying", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Necromancy Cantrip (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.78, 0.696, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 15 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.847, 0.912, 0.878], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose a creature within range that has 0 Hit Points and isn’t dead. The creature becomes Stable."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.879, 0.889, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The range doubles when you reach levels 5 (30 feet), 11 (60 feet), and 17 (120 feet)."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "163"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 163, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.455, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speak with Animals", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 1 Divination (Bard, Druid, Ranger, Warlock) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.481, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, you can comprehend and verbally communicate with Beasts, and you can use any of the Influence action’s skill options with them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.201, 0.483, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most Beasts have little to say about topics that don’t pertain to survival or companionship, but at minimum, a Beast can give you information about nearby locations and monsters, including whatever it has perceived within the past day."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.286, 0.407, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speak with Dead", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Necromancy (Bard, Cleric, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (burning incense) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.389, 0.482, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You grant the semblance of life to a corpse of your choice within range, allowing it to answer questions you pose. The corpse must have a mouth, and this spell fails if the deceased creature was Undead when it died. The spell also fails if the corpse was the target of this spell within the past 10 days."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.482, 0.49, 0.652], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can ask the corpse up to five questions. The corpse knows only what it knew in life, including the languages it knew. Answers are usually brief, cryptic, or repetitive, and the corpse is under no compulsion to offer a truthful answer if you are antagonistic toward it or it recognizes you as an enemy. This spell doesn’t return the creature’s soul to its body, only its animating spirit. Thus, the corpse can’t learn new information, doesn’t comprehend anything that has happened since it died, and can’t speculate about future events."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.659, 0.268, 0.676], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speak with Plants"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.676, 0.42, 0.693], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Bard, Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.696, 0.256, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.763, 0.491, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You imbue plants in an immobile 30-foot Emanation with limited sentience and animation, giving them the ability to communicate with you and follow your simple commands. You can question plants about events in the spell’s area within the past day, gaining information about creatures that have passed, weather, and other circumstances."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.87, 0.49, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can also turn Difficult Terrain caused by plant growth (such as thickets and undergrowth) into ordinary terrain that lasts for the duration. Or you"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.905, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "can turn ordinary terrain where plants are present into Difficult Terrain that lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.081, 0.891, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell doesn’t enable plants to uproot themselves and move about, but they can move their branches, tendrils, and stalks for you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.127, 0.899, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a Plant creature is in the area, you can communicate with it as if you shared a common language."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.166, 0.648, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spider Climb"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.183, 0.893, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of bitumen and a spider) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.269, 0.901, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch gains the ability to move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings, while leaving its hands free. The target also gains a Climb Speed equal to its Speed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.347, 0.89, 0.393], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can target one additional creature for each spell slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.4, 0.655, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spike Growth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.418, 0.8, 0.434], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.438, 0.821, 0.498], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (seven thorns) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.505, 0.91, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The ground in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range sprouts hard spikes and thorns. The area becomes Difficult Terrain for the duration. When a creature moves into or within the area, it takes 2d4 Piercing damage for every 5 feet it travels."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.597, 0.905, 0.69], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The transformation of the ground is camouflaged to look natural. Any creature that can’t see the area when the spell is cast must take a Search action and succeed on a Wisdom (Perception or Survival) check against your spell save DC to recognize the terrain as hazardous before entering it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.697, 0.678, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spirit Guardians"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.714, 0.721, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Conjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.735, 0.821, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a prayer scroll) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.8, 0.9, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protective spirits flit around you in a 15-foot Emanation for the duration. If you are good or neutral, their spectral form appears angelic or fey (your choice). If you are evil, they appear fiendish."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.863, 0.91, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you cast this spell, you can designate creatures to be unaffected by it. Any other creature’s Speed is halved in the Emanation, and whenever the Emanation enters a creature’s space and whenever"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "164"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 164, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.489, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "a creature enters the Emanation or ends its turn there, the creature must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 3d8 Radiant damage (if you are good or neutral) or 3d8 Necrotic damage (if you are evil). On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.158, 0.475, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.196, 0.267, 0.214], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spiritual Weapon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.214, 0.286, 0.23], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Evocation (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.234, 0.386, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bonus Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.301, 0.49, 0.409], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a floating, spectral force that resembles a weapon of your choice and lasts for the duration. The force appears within range in a space of your choice, and you can immediately make one melee spell attack against one creature within 5 feet of the force. On a hit, the target takes Force damage equal to 1d8 plus your spellcasting ability modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.409, 0.472, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action on your later turns, you can move the force up to 20 feet and repeat the attack against a creature within 5 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.454, 0.474, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for every slot level above 2."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.493, 0.333, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Starry Wisp", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Evocation Cantrip (Bard, Druid) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.597, 0.49, 0.688], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You launch a mote of light at one creature or object within range. Make a ranged spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d8 Radiant damage, and until the end of your next turn, it emits Dim Light in a 10-foot radius and can’t benefit from the Invisible condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.689, 0.474, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 when you reach levels 5 (2d8), 11 (3d8), and 17 (4d8)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.743, 0.419, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stinking Cloud", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Conjuration (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.78, 0.387, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a rotten egg) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.846, 0.476, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of yellow, nauseating gas centered on a point within range. The cloud is Heavily Obscured. The cloud lingers in the air for the duration or until a strong wind (such as the one created by Gust of Wind) disperses it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature that starts its turn in the Sphere must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition until the end of the current turn. While Poisoned in this way, the creature can’t take an action or a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.135, 0.644, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stone Shape"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.153, 0.848, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.172, 0.745, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (soft clay) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.239, 0.913, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a stone object of Medium size or smaller or a section of stone no more than 5 feet in any dimension and form it into any shape you like. For example, you could shape a large rock into a weapon, statue, or coffer, or you could make a small passage through a wall that is 5 feet thick. You could also shape a stone door or its frame to seal the door shut. The object you create can have up to two hinges and a latch, but finer mechanical detail isn’t possible."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.385, 0.618, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stoneskin"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.402, 0.863, 0.434], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.438, 0.679, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.453, 0.626, 0.468], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.468, 0.886, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (diamond dust worth 100+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.519, 0.904, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, one willing creature you touch has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.573, 0.722, 0.608], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Storm of Vengeance", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 9 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.611, 0.807, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 mile "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.678, 0.912, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A churning storm cloud forms for the duration, centered on a point within range and spreading to a radius of 300 feet. Each creature under the cloud when it appears must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 2d6 Thunder damage and have the Deafened condition for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.77, 0.902, 0.801], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the start of each of your later turns, the storm produces different effects, as detailed below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.8, 0.907, 0.831], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Turn 2.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Acidic rain falls. Each creature and object under the cloud takes 4d6 Acid damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.831, 0.887, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Turn 3.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You call six bolts of lightning from the cloud to strike six different creatures or objects beneath it. Each target makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "165"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 165, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.478, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Turn 4.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Hailstones rain down. Each creature under the cloud takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.487, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Turns 5–10.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Gusts and freezing rain assail the area under the cloud. Each creature there takes 1d6 Cold damage. Until the spell ends, the area is Difficult Terrain and Heavily Obscured, ranged attacks with weapons are impossible there, and strong wind blows through the area."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.181, 0.206, 0.199], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Suggestion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.198, 0.434, 0.23], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.233, 0.258, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.249, 0.209, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.378, 0.293], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (a drop of honey) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.301, 0.485, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You suggest a course of activity—described in no more than 25 words—to one creature you can see within range that can hear and understand you. The suggestion must sound achievable and not involve anything that would obviously deal damage to the target or its allies. For example, you could say, “Fetch the key to the cult’s treasure vault, and give the key to me.” Or you could say, “Stop fighting, leave this library peacefully, and don’t return.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.439, 0.482, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for the duration or until you or your allies deal damage to the target. The Charmed target pursues the suggestion to the best of its ability. The suggested activity can continue for the entire duration, but if the suggested activity can be completed in a shorter time, the spell ends for the target upon completing it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.569, 0.262, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Summon Dragon", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.587, 0.313, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Conjuration (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.606, 0.258, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.622, 0.21, 0.636], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.636, 0.456, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (an object with the image of a dragon engraved on it worth 500+ GP) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.688, 0.483, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You call forth a Dragon spirit. It manifests in an unoccupied space that you can see within range and uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Draconic Spirit", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block. The creature disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.765, 0.49, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, the creature shares your Initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you). If you don’t issue any, it takes the Dodge action and uses its movement to avoid danger."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.857, 0.455, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use the spell slot’s level for the spell’s level in the stat block."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.525, 0.051, 0.693, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Draconic Spirit"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.075, 0.788, 0.141], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Dragon, Neutral "}, {"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 14 + the spell’s level "}, {"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 50 + 10 for each spell level above 5 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 ft., Fly 60 ft., Swim 30 ft."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.525, 0.143, 0.91, 0.19], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.525, 0.143, 0.91, 0.19], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 19 +4 +4</td><td>Dex 14 +2 +2</td><td>Con17 +3 +3</td></tr><tr><td>Int 10 +0 +0</td><td>Wis 14 +2 +2</td><td>Cha 14 +2 +2</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.199, 0.833, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistances", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Immunities", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Charmed, Frightened, Poisoned "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Senses", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Blindsight 30 ft., Darkvision 60 ft.; Passive Perception 12"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.26, 0.912, 0.292], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Draconic, understands the languages you know "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " None (XP 0; PB equals your Proficiency Bonus)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.3, 0.578, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.32, 0.895, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shared Resistances.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you summon the spirit, choose one of its Resistances. You have Resistance to the chosen damage type until the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.375, 0.595, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.395, 0.91, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spirit makes a number of Rend attacks equal to half the spell’s level (round down), and it uses Breath Weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.448, 0.912, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rend.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 10 feet. Hit: 1d6 + 4 + the spell’s level Piercing damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.5, 0.903, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Breath Weapon.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Dexterity Saving Throw: DC equals your spell save DC, each creature in a 30-foot Cone. Failure: 2d6 damage of a type this spirit has Resistance to (your choice when you cast the spell). Success: Half damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.583, 0.614, 0.6], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sunbeam"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.6, 0.88, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.621, 0.808, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a magnifying glass) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.688, 0.912, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You launch a sunbeam in a 5-foot-wide, 60-foot-long Line. Each creature in the Line makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 6d8 Radiant damage and has the Blinded condition until the start of your next turn. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.78, 0.91, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can take a Magic action to create a new Line of radiance."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.811, 0.904, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, a mote of brilliant radiance shines above you. It sheds Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. This light is sunlight."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "166"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 166, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.19, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sunburst"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.068, 0.459, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Evocation (Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of sunstone) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.155, 0.482, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brilliant sunlight flashes in a 60-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point you choose within range. Each creature in the Sphere makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 12d6 Radiant damage and has the Blinded condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.472, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature Blinded by this spell makes another Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.309, 0.465, 0.34], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell dispels Darkness in its area that was created by any spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.348, 0.175, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Symbol"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.365, 0.439, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Abjuration (Bard, Cleric, Druid, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.385, 0.272, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.4, 0.203, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.488, 0.459], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (powdered diamond worth 1,000+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until dispelled or triggered"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.466, 0.488, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You inscribe a harmful glyph either on a surface (such as a section of floor or wall) or within an object that can be closed (such as a book or chest). The glyph can cover an area no larger than 10 feet in diameter. If you choose an object, it must remain in place; if it is moved more than 10 feet from where you cast this spell, the glyph is broken, and the spell ends without being triggered."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.589, 0.485, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The glyph is nearly imperceptible and requires a successful Wisdom (Perception) check against your spell save DC to notice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.635, 0.475, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you inscribe the glyph, you set its trigger and choose which effect the symbol bears: Death, Discord, Fear, Pain, Sleep, or Stunning. Each one is explained below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.696, 0.487, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Set the Trigger.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You decide what triggers the glyph when you cast the spell. For glyphs inscribed on a surface, common triggers include touching or stepping on the glyph, removing another object covering it, or approaching within a certain distance of it. For glyphs inscribed within an object, common triggers include opening that object or seeing the glyph."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.819, 0.489, 0.896], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can refine the trigger so that only creatures of certain types activate it (for example, the glyph could be set to affect Aberrations). You can also set conditions for creatures that don’t trigger the glyph, such as those who say a certain password."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.896, 0.429, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once triggered, the glyph glows, filling a 60-foot-radius Sphere with Dim Light for 10"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.912, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "minutes, after which time the spell ends. Each creature in the Sphere when the glyph activates is targeted by its effect, as is a creature that enters the Sphere for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. A creature is targeted only once per turn."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.128, 0.894, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Death.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 10d10 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.174, 0.903, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Discord.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target argues with other creatures for 1 minute. During this time, it is incapable of meaningful communication and has Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.25, 0.896, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fear.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition for 1 minute. While Frightened, the target must move at least 30 feet away from the glyph on each of its turns, if able."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.326, 0.902, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pain.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or have the Incapacitated condition for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.372, 0.91, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sleep.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Unconscious condition for 10 minutes. A creature awakens if it takes damage or if someone takes an action to shake it awake."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.434, 0.904, 0.48], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stunning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the Stunned condition for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.525, 0.487, 0.628, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telekinesis"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.505, 0.819, 0.521], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.525, 0.679, 0.539], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.54, 0.632, 0.554], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.554, 0.656, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.569, 0.821, 0.584], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.593, 0.909, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the ability to move or manipulate creatures or objects by thought. When you cast the spell and as a Magic action on your later turns before the spell ends, you can exert your will on one creature or object that you can see within range, causing the appropriate effect below. You can affect the same target round after round or choose a new one at any time. If you switch targets, the prior target is no longer affected by the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.73, 0.91, 0.852], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can try to move a Huge or smaller creature. The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw, or you move it up to 30 feet in any direction within the spell’s range. Until the end of your next turn, the creature has the Restrained condition, and if you lift it into the air, it is suspended there. It falls at the end of your next turn unless you use this option on it again and it fails the save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.853, 0.904, 0.915], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can try to move a Huge or smaller object. If the object isn’t being worn or carried, you automatically move it up to 30 feet in any direction within the spell’s range."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "167"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 167, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.488, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the object is worn or carried by a creature, that creature must succeed on a Strength saving throw, or you pull the object away and move it up to 30 feet in any direction within the spell’s range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.112, 0.483, 0.144], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can exert fine control on objects with your telekinetic grip, such as manipulating a simple tool,"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.15, 0.255, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathic Bond"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.168, 0.344, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Divination (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.187, 0.32, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.203, 0.209, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.217, 0.327, 0.233], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (two eggs)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.233, 0.227, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.254, 0.487, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You forge a telepathic link among up to eight willing creatures of your choice within range, psychically linking each creature to all the others for the duration. Creatures that can’t communicate in any languages aren’t affected by this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.331, 0.489, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, the targets can communicate telepathically through the bond whether or not they share a language. The communication is possible over any distance, though it can’t extend to other planes of existence."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.416, 0.188, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Teleport"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.433, 0.419, 0.45], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 7 Conjuration (Bard, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.453, 0.258, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.469, 0.21, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.483, 0.221, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.498, 0.274, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.52, 0.489, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell instantly transports you and up to eight willing creatures that you can see within range, or a single object that you can see within range, to a destination you select. If you target an object, it must be Large or smaller, and it can’t be held or carried by an unwilling creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.612, 0.482, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The destination you choose must be known to you, and it must be on the same plane of existence as you. Your familiarity with the destination determines whether you arrive there successfully. The GM rolls 1d100 and consults the Teleportation Outcome table and the explanations after it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.103, 0.717, 0.305, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Teleportation Outcome"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.104, 0.736, 0.486, 0.898], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.104, 0.736, 0.486, 0.898], "content": "<table><tr><td>Familiarity</td><td>Mishap</td><td>Similar Area</td><td>Off Target</td><td>On Target</td></tr><tr><td>Permanent circle</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>01-00</td></tr><tr><td>Linked object</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>01-00</td></tr><tr><td>Very familiar</td><td>01-05</td><td>06-13</td><td>14-24</td><td>25-00</td></tr><tr><td>Seen casually</td><td>01-33</td><td>34-43</td><td>44-53</td><td>54-00</td></tr><tr><td>Viewed once or described</td><td>01-43</td><td>44-53</td><td>54-73</td><td>74-00</td></tr><tr><td>False destination</td><td>01-50</td><td>51-00</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.895, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Familiarity.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Here are the meanings of the terms in the table’s Familiarity column:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.088, 0.91, 0.119], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• “Permanent circle” means a permanent teleportation circle whose sigil sequence you know."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.119, 0.912, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• “Linked object” means you possess an object taken from the desired destination within the last six months, such as a book from a wizard’s library."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.525, 0.165, 0.901, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• “Very familiar” is a place you have visited often, a place you have carefully studied, or a place you can see when you cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.211, 0.909, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• “Seen casually” is a place you have seen more than once but with which you aren’t very familiar."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.241, 0.893, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• “Viewed once or described” is a place you have seen once, possibly using magic, or a place you know through someone else’s description, perhaps from a map."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.303, 0.91, 0.365], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“False destination” is a place that doesn’t exist. Perhaps you tried to scry an enemy’s sanctum but instead viewed an illusion, or you are attempting to teleport to a location that no longer exists."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.37, 0.91, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mishap.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The spell’s unpredictable magic results in a difficult journey. Each teleporting creature (or the target object) takes 3d10 Force damage, and the GM rerolls on the table to see where you wind up (multiple mishaps can occur, dealing damage each time)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.448, 0.911, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Similar Area.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You and your group (or the target object) appear in a different area that’s visually or thematically similar to the target area. You appear in the closest similar place. If you are heading for your home laboratory, for example, you might appear in another person’s laboratory in the same city."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.54, 0.907, 0.616], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Off Target.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You and your group (or the target object) appear 2d12 miles away from the destination in a random direction. Roll 1d8 for the direction: 1, east; 2, southeast; 3, south; 4, southwest; 5, west; 6, northwest; 7, north; or 8, northeast."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.616, 0.901, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On Target.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You and your group (or the target object) appear where you intended."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.654, 0.713, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Teleportation Circle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.672, 0.905, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Conjuration (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.691, 0.693, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.707, 0.631, 0.721], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.72, 0.9, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (rare inks worth 50+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.751, 0.657, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 round"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.773, 0.91, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As you cast the spell, you draw a 5-foot-radius circle on the ground inscribed with sigils that link your location to a permanent teleportation circle of your choice whose sigil sequence you know and that is on the same plane of existence as you. A shimmering portal opens within the circle you drew and remains open until the end of your next turn. Any creature that enters the portal instantly appears within 5 feet of the destination circle or in the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "168"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 168, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Many major temples, guildhalls, and other important places have permanent teleportation circles. Each circle includes a unique sigil sequence—a string of runes arranged in a particular pattern."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.112, 0.486, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you first gain the ability to cast this spell, you learn the sigil sequences for two destinations on the Material Plane, determined by the GM. You might learn additional sigil sequences during your adventures. You can commit a new sigil sequence to memory after studying it for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.205, 0.479, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can create a permanent teleportation circle by casting this spell in the same location every day for 365 days."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.258, 0.324, 0.292], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thaumaturgy", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Transmutation Cantrip (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.295, 0.284, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.362, 0.49, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You manifest a minor wonder within range. You create one of the effects below within range. If you cast this spell multiple times, you can have up to three of its 1-minute effects active at a time."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.423, 0.462, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Altered Eyes.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You alter the appearance of your eyes for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.454, 0.478, 0.514], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Booming Voice.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your voice booms up to three times as loud as normal for 1 minute. For the duration, you have Advantage on Charisma (Intimidation) checks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.515, 0.465, 0.546], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Play.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause flames to flicker, brighten, dim, or change color for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.546, 0.484, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invisible Hand.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You instantaneously cause an unlocked door or window to fly open or slam shut."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.577, 0.49, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Phantom Sound.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create an instantaneous sound that originates from a point of your choice within range, such as a rumble of thunder, the cry of a raven, or ominous whispers."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.638, 0.448, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tremors.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You cause harmless tremors in the ground for 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.677, 0.232, 0.692], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thunderwave", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.694, 0.452, 0.71], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Evocation (Bard, Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.714, 0.274, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.781, 0.487, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You unleash a wave of thunderous energy. Each creature in a 15-foot Cube originating from you makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 Thunder damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.873, 0.479, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, unsecured objects that are entirely within the Cube are pushed 10 feet away from you, and a thunderous boom is audible within 300 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.895, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.09, 0.821, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Time Stop", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 9 Transmutation (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.193, 0.9, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You briefly stop the flow of time for everyone but yourself. No time passes for other creatures, while you take 1d4 + 1 turns in a row, during which you can use actions and move as normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.912, 0.348], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell ends if one of the actions you use during this period, or any effects that you create during it, affects a creature other than you or an object being worn or carried by someone other than you. In addi tion, the spell ends if you move to a place more than 1,000 feet from the location where you cast it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.354, 0.612, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tiny Hut", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.371, 0.762, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Evocation (Bard, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.392, 0.782, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a crystal bead) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.459, 0.908, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A 10-foot Emanation springs into existence around you and remains stationary for the duration. The spell fails when you cast it if the Emanation isn’t big enough to fully encapsulate all creatures in its area."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.521, 0.908, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures and objects within the Emanation when you cast the spell can move through it freely. All other creatures and objects are barred from passing through it. Spells of level 3 or lower can’t be cast through it, and the effects of such spells can’t extend into it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.907, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The atmosphere inside the Emanation is comfortable and dry, regardless of the weather outside. Until the spell ends, you can command the interior to have Dim Light or Darkness (no action required). The Emanation is opaque from the outside and of any color you choose, but it’s transparent from the inside."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.704, 0.906, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell ends early if you leave the Emanation or if you cast it again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.743, 0.606, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tongues"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.76, 0.882, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.796, 0.805, 0.855], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, M (a miniature ziggurat) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.862, 0.904, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell grants the creature you touch the ability to understand any spoken or signed language that it hears or sees. Moreover, when the target commu nicates by speaking or signing, any creature that"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.031, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "169"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 169, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "knows at least one language can understand it if that creature can hear the speech or see the signing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.3, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Transport via Plants", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.126, 0.256, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.193, 0.488, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell creates a magical link between a Large or larger inanimate plant within range and another plant, at any distance, on the same plane of existence. You must have seen or touched the destination plant at least once before. For the duration, any creature can step into the target plant and exit from the destination plant by using 5 feet of m"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ovement", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.308, 0.21, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tree Stride", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.326, 0.358, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Conjuration (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.346, 0.385, 0.406], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.413, 0.489, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the ability to enter a tree and move from inside it to inside another tree of the same kind within 500 feet. Both trees must be living and at least the same size as you. You must use 5 feet of movement to enter a tree. You instantly know the location of all other trees of the same kind within 500 feet and, as part of the move used to enter the tree, can either pass into one of those trees or step out of the tree you’re in. You appear in a spot of your choice within 5 feet of the destination tree, using another 5 feet of movement. If you have no movement left, you appear within 5 feet of the tree you entered."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.612, 0.476, 0.659], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can use this transportation ability only once on each of your turns. You must end each turn outside a tree."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.666, 0.255, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "True Polymorph", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.683, 0.44, 0.7], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Transmutation (Bard, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.703, 0.258, 0.718], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.719, 0.21, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.732, 0.464, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of mercury, a dollop of gum arabic, and a wisp of smoke) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.1, 0.785, 0.488, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose one creature or nonmagical object that you can see within range. The creature shape-shifts into a different creature or a nonmagical object, or the object shape-shifts into a creature (the object must be neither worn nor carried). The transformation lasts for the duration or until the target dies or is destroyed, but if you maintain Concentration on this spell for the full duration, the spell lasts until dispelled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.908, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An unwilling creature can make a Wisdom saving throw, and if it succeeds, it isn’t affected by this spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.081, 0.909, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature into Creature.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you turn a creature into another kind of creature, the new form can be any kind you choose that has a Challenge Rating equal to or less than the target’s Challenge Rating or level. The target’s game statistics are replaced by the stat block of the new form, but it retains its Hit Points, Hit Point Dice, alignment, and personality."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.189, 0.891, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target gains a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the new form. These Temporary Hit Points vanish if any remain when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.25, 0.91, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target is limited in the actions it can perform by the anatomy of its new form, and it can’t speak or cast spells."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.296, 0.904, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target’s gear melds into the new form. The creature can’t use or otherwise benefit from any of that equipment."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.342, 0.908, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object into Creature.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can turn an object into any kind of creature, as long as the creature’s size is no larger than the object’s size and the creature has a Challenge Rating of 9 or lower. The creature is Friendly to you and your allies. In combat, it takes its turns immediately after yours, and it obeys your commands."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.449, 0.904, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell lasts more than an hour, you no longer control the creature. It might remain Friendly to you, depending on how you have treated it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.496, 0.905, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature into Object.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you turn a creature into an object, it transforms along with whatever it is wearing and carrying into that form, as long as the object’s size is no larger than the creature’s size. The creature’s statistics become those of the object, and the creature has no memory of time spent in this form after the spell ends and it returns to normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.611, 0.695, 0.627], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "True Resurrection", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.628, 0.773, 0.644], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Necromancy (Cleric, Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.647, 0.679, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.662, 0.625, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.677, 0.881, 0.707], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (diamonds worth 25,000+ GP, which the spell consumes)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.707, 0.698, 0.721], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.729, 0.899, 0.79], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch a creature that has been dead for no longer than 200 years and that died for any reason except old age. The creature is revived with all its Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.79, 0.91, 0.882], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell closes all wounds, neutralizes any poison, cures all magical contagions, and lifts any curses affecting the creature when it died. The spell replaces damaged or missing organs and limbs. If the creature was Undead, it is restored to its non-Undead form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.882, 0.897, 0.914], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell can provide a new body if the original no longer exists, in which case you must speak the"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "170"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 170, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.48, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "creature’s name. The creature then appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 10 feet of you."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.216, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "True Seeing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.107, 0.461, 0.137], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Divination (Bard, Cleric, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.141, 0.257, 0.156], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.157, 0.203, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.171, 0.466, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (mushroom powder worth 25+ GP, which the spell consumes) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.223, 0.485, 0.255], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For the duration, the willing creature you touch has Truesight with a range of 120 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.262, 0.21, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "True Strike"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.279, 0.479, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Divination Cantrip (Bard, Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.299, 0.257, 0.314], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.314, 0.186, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.329, 0.489, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " S, M (a weapon with which you have proficiency and that is worth 1+ CP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.359, 0.275, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.381, 0.482, 0.488], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Guided by a flash of magical insight, you make one attack with the weapon used in the spell’s casting. The attack uses your spellcasting ability for the attack and damage rolls instead of using Strength or Dexterity. If the attack deals damage, it can be Radiant damage or the weapon’s normal damage type (your choice)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.488, 0.49, 0.551], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whether you deal Radiant damage or the weapon’s normal damage type, the attack deals extra Radiant damage when you reach levels 5 (1d6), 11 (2d6), and 17 (3d6)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.103, 0.558, 0.185, 0.574], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tsunami", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.575, 0.299, 0.591], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 8 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.595, 0.385, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 mile "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 6 rounds"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.662, 0.484, 0.723], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A wall of water springs into existence at a point you choose within range. You can make the wall up to 300 feet long, 300 feet high, and 50 feet thick. The wall lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.723, 0.475, 0.785], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the wall appears, each creature in its area makes a Strength saving throw, taking 6d10 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.101, 0.785, 0.484, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the start of each of your turns after the wall appears, the wall, along with any creatures in it, moves 50 feet away from you. Any Huge or smaller creature inside the wall or whose space the wall enters when it moves must succeed on a Strength saving throw or take 5d10 Bludgeoning damage. A creature can take this damage only once per round. At the end of the turn, the wall’s height is reduced by 50 feet, and the damage the wall deals on later"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.908, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "r"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ounds", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " is reduced by 1d10. When the wall reaches 0 feet in height, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.904, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature caught in the wall can move by swimming. Because of the wave’s force, though, the creature must succeed on a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC to move at all. If it fails the check, it can’t move. A creature that moves out of the wall falls to the ground."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.181, 0.675, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unseen Servant"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.198, 0.84, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 1 Conjuration (Bard, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.218, 0.865, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of string and of wood) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.285, 0.906, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell creates an Invisible, mindless, shapeless, Medium force that performs simple tasks at your command until the spell ends. The servant springs into existence in an unoccupied space on the ground within range. It has AC 10, 1 Hit Point, and a Strength of 2, and it can’t attack. If it drops to 0 Hit Points, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.393, 0.912, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once on each of your turns as a Bonus Action, you can mentally command the servant to move up to 15 feet and interact with an object. The servant can perform simple tasks that a human could do, such as fetching things, cleaning, mending, folding clothes, lighting fires, serving food, and pouring drinks. Once you give the command, the servant performs the task to the best of its ability until it completes the task, then waits for your next command."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.531, 0.912, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you command the servant to perform a task that would move it more than 60 feet away from you, the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.584, 0.671, 0.601], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vampiric Touch", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.601, 0.869, 0.618], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Necromancy (Sorcerer, Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.621, 0.679, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.636, 0.608, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.651, 0.656, 0.666], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.666, 0.807, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.688, 0.909, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The touch of your shadow-wreathed hand can siphon life force from others to heal your wounds. Make a melee spell attack against one creature within reach. On a hit, the target takes 3d6 Necrotic damage, and you regain Hit Points equal to half the amount of Necrotic damage dealt."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.781, 0.911, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Until the spell ends, you can make the attack again on each of your turns as a Magic action, targeting the same creature or a different one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.827, 0.896, 0.858], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 3."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.524, 0.865, 0.732, 0.933], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vicious Mockery", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Enchantment Cantrip (Bard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "171"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 171, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.274, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.49, 0.179], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You unleash a string of insults laced with subtle enchantments at one creature you can see or hear within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d6 Psychic damage and have Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.18, 0.473, 0.227], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip Upgrade.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d6 when you reach levels 5 (2d6), 11 (3d6), and 17 (4d6)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.234, 0.249, 0.251], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vitriolic Sphere", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.251, 0.364, 0.268], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Evocation (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.357, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a drop of bile) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.338, 0.488, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You point at a location within range, and a glowing, 1-foot-diameter ball of acid streaks there and explodes in a 20-foot-radius Sphere. Each creature in that area makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 10d4 Acid damage and another 5d4 Acid damage at the end of its next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half the initial damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.461, 0.479, 0.507], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The initial damage increases by 2d4 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.514, 0.214, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wall of Fire", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.532, 0.411, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 4 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.552, 0.393, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of charcoal) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.619, 0.479, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a wall of fire on a solid surface within range. You can make the wall up to 60 feet long, 20 feet high, and 1 foot thick, or a ringed wall up to 20 feet in diameter, 20 feet high, and 1 foot thick. The wall is opaque and lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.697, 0.479, 0.757], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the wall appears, each creature in its area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 5d8 Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.757, 0.49, 0.864], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One side of the wall, selected by you when you cast this spell, deals 5d8 Fire damage to each creature that ends its turn within 10 feet of that side or inside the wall. A creature takes the same damage when it enters the wall for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. The other side of the wall deals no damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.864, 0.475, 0.897], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 4."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.822, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wall of Force", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 5 Evocation (Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a shard of glass) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.909, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Invisible wall of force springs into existence at a point you choose within range. The wall appears in any orientation you choose, as a horizontal or vertical barrier or at an angle. It can be free floating or resting on a solid surface. You can form it into a hemispherical dome or a globe with a radius of up to 10 feet, or you can shape a flat surface made up of ten 10-foot-by-10-foot panels. Each panel must be contiguous with another panel. In any form, the wall is 1/4 inch thick and lasts for the duration. If the wall cuts through a creature’s space when it appears, the creature is pushed to one side of the wall (you choose which side)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.355, 0.899, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nothing can physically pass through the wall. It is immune to all damage and can’t be dispelled by Dispel Magic. A Disintegrate spell destroys the wall instantly, however. The wall also extends into the Ethereal Plane and blocks ethereal travel through the wall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.454, 0.628, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wall of Ice", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.472, 0.721, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Evocation (Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.491, 0.679, 0.507], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.506, 0.638, 0.521], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.521, 0.821, 0.551], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of quartz) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.559, 0.911, 0.665], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a wall of ice on a solid surface within range. You can form it into a hemispherical dome or a globe with a radius of up to 10 feet, or you can shape a flat surface made up of ten 10-foot-square panels. Each panel must be contiguous with another panel. In any form, the wall is 1 foot thick and lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.666, 0.908, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the wall cuts through a creature’s space when it appears, the creature is pushed to one side of the wall (you choose which side) and makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 10d6 Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.743, 0.91, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall is an object that can be damaged and thus breached. It has AC 12 and 30 Hit Points per 10-foot section, and it has Immunity to Cold, Poison, and Psychic damage and Vulnerability to Fire damage. Reducing a 10-foot section of wall to 0 Hit Points destroys it and leaves behind a sheet of frigid air in the space the wall occupied."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.85, 0.901, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature moving through the sheet of frigid air for the first time on a turn makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 5d6 Cold damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "172"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 172, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.488, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The damage the wall deals when it appears increases by 2d6 and the damage from passing through the sheet of frigid air increases by 1d6 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.12, 0.232, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wall of Stone", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.137, 0.412, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 5 Evocation (Druid, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.157, 0.402, 0.217], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a cube of granite) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.224, 0.487, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A nonmagical wall of solid stone springs into existence at a point you choose within range. The wall is 6 inches thick and is composed of ten 10-foot-by-10-foot panels. Each panel must be contiguous with another panel. Alternatively, you can create 10-footby-20-foot panels that are only 3 inches thick."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.487, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the wall cuts through a creature’s space when it appears, the creature is pushed to one side of the wall (you choose which side). If a creature would be surrounded on all sides by the wall (or the wall and another solid surface), that creature can make a Dexterity saving throw. On a success, it can use its Reaction to move up to its Speed so that it is no longer enclosed by the wall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.439, 0.488, 0.531], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall can have any shape you desire, though it can’t occupy the same space as a creature or object. The wall doesn’t need to be vertical or rest on a firm foundation. It must, however, merge with and be solidly supported by existing stone. Thus, you can use this spell to bridge a chasm or create a ramp."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.531, 0.484, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you create a span greater than 20 feet in length, you must halve the size of each panel to create supports. You can crudely shape the wall to create battlements and the like."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.592, 0.482, 0.684], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The wall is an object made of stone that can be damaged and thus breached. Each panel has AC 15 and 30 Hit Points per inch of thickness, and it has Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. Reducing a panel to 0 Hit Points destroys it and might cause connected panels to collapse at the GM’s discretion."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.684, 0.476, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you maintain your Concentration on this spell for its full duration, the wall becomes permanent and can’t be dispelled. Otherwise, the wall disappears when the spell ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.754, 0.3, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wall of Thorns", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 6 Conjuration (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.79, 0.399, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a handful of thorns) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.857, 0.49, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a wall of tangled brush bristling with needle-sharp thorns. The wall appears within range on a solid surface and lasts for the duration. You choose to make the wall up to 60 feet long, 10 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.895, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "high, and 5 feet thick or a circle that has a 20-foot diameter and is up to 20 feet high and 5 feet thick. The wall blocks line of sight."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.905, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the wall appears, each creature in its area makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 7d8 Piercing damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.158, 0.907, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature can move through the wall, albeit slowly and painfully. For every 1 foot a creature moves through the wall, it must spend 4 feet of movement. Furthermore, the first time a creature e"}, {"type": "text", "content": "nters", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " a space in the wall on a turn or ends its turn there, the creature makes a Dexterity saving throw, taking 7d8 Slashing damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature makes this save only once per turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.296, 0.884, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Both types of damage increase by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 6."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.349, 0.661, 0.366], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Warding Bond"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.367, 0.773, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Abjuration (Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.387, 0.679, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.525, 0.402, 0.625, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Touch"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.417, 0.9, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a pair of platinum rings worth 50+ GP each, which you and the target must wear for the duration)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.461, 0.648, 0.475], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.483, 0.901, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You touch another creature that is willing and create a mystic connection between you and the target until the spell ends. While the target is within 60 feet of you, it gains a +1 bonus to AC and saving throws, and it has Resistance to all damage. Also, each time it takes damage, you take the same amount of damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.59, 0.91, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The spell ends if you drop to 0 Hit Points or if you and the target become separated by more than 60 feet. It also ends if the spell is cast again on either of the connected creatures."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.66, 0.682, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Water Breathing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.677, 0.863, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Transmutation (Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.713, 0.773, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a short reed) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 24 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.779, 0.907, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell grants up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range the ability to breathe underwater until the spell ends. Affected creatures also retain their normal mode of respiration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.848, 0.913, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Water Walk", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 3 Transmutation (Cleric, Druid, Ranger, Sorcerer) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action or Ritual "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "173"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 173, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.367, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a piece of cork) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.489, 0.18], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This spell grants the ability to move across any liquid surface—such as water, acid, mud, snow, quicksand, or lava—as if it were harmless solid ground (creatures crossing molten lava can still take damage from the heat). Up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range gain this ability for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.18, 0.488, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An affected target must take a Bonus Action to pass from the liquid’s surface into the liquid itself and vice versa, but if the target falls into the liquid, the target passes through the surface into the liquid below."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.264, 0.153, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Web"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.282, 0.378, 0.299], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.302, 0.387, 0.361], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a bit of spiderweb) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 hour"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.369, 0.489, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You conjure a mass of sticky webbing at a point within range. The webs fill a 20-foot Cube there for the duration. The webs are Difficult Terrain, and the area within them is Lightly Obscured."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.431, 0.473, 0.522], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the webs aren’t anchored between two solid masses (such as walls or trees) or layered across a floor, wall, or ceiling, the web collapses on itself, and the spell ends at the start of your next turn. Webs layered over a flat surface have a depth of 5 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.523, 0.484, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first time a creature enters the webs on a turn or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the Restrained condition while in the webs or until it breaks free."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.584, 0.482, 0.644], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature Restrained by the webs can take an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. If it succeeds, it is no longer Restrained."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.645, 0.484, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The webs are flammable. Any 5-foot Cube of webs exposed to fire burns away in 1 round, dealing 2d4 Fire damage to any creature that starts its turn in the fire."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.714, 0.166, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weird", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.732, 0.345, 0.748], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 9 Illusion (Warlock, Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.752, 0.386, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.818, 0.49, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You try to create illusory terrors in others’ minds. Each creature of your choice in a 30-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target takes 10d10 Psychic damage and has the Frightened condition for the duration. On a successful save, a target takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.904, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Frightened target makes a Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a failed save, it takes 5d10 Psychic damage. On a successful save, the spell ends on that target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.119, 0.634, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wind Walk", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.744, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Transmutation (Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.157, 0.744, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 1 minute "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 30 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a candle) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 8 hours"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.224, 0.907, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and up to ten willing creatures of your choice within range assume gaseous forms for the duration, appearing as wisps of cloud. While in this cloud form, a target has a Fly Speed of 300 feet and can hover; it has Immunity to the Prone condition; and it has Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage. The only actions a target can take in this form are the Dash action or a Magic action to begin reverting to its normal form. Reverting takes 1 minute, during which the target has the Stunned condition. Until the spell ends, the target can revert to cloud form, which also requires a Magic action followed by a 1-minute transformation."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.423, 0.912, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a target is in cloud form and flying when the effect ends, the target descends 60 feet per round for 1 minute until it lands, which it does safely. If it can’t land after 1 minute, it falls the remaining distance."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.492, 0.628, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wind Wall", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.51, 0.766, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 3 Evocation (Druid, Ranger)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.53, 0.812, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 120 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S, M (a fan and a feather) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Concentration, up to 1 minute"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.597, 0.907, 0.689], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A wall of strong wind rises from the ground at a point you choose within range. You can make the wall up to 50 feet long, 15 feet high, and 1 foot thick. You can shape the wall in any way you choose so long as it makes one continuous path along the ground. The wall lasts for the duration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.689, 0.896, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the wall appears, each creature in its area makes a Strength saving throw, taking 4d8 Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.75, 0.907, 0.905], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The strong wind keeps fog, smoke, and other gases at bay. Small or smaller flying creatures or objects can’t pass through the wall. Loose, lightweight materials brought into the wall fly upward. Arrows, bolts, and other ordinary projectiles launched at targets behind the wall are deflected upward and miss automatically. Boulders hurled by Giants or siege engines, and similar projectiles, are unaffected. Creatures in gaseous form can’t pass through it."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "174"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 174, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.378, 0.148], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wish", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Level 9 Conjuration (Sorcerer, Wizard) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Self "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.155, 0.473, 0.186], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wish is the mightiest spell a mortal can cast. By simply speaking aloud, you can alter reality itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.186, 0.488, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The basic use of this spell is to duplicate any other spell of level 8 or lower. If you use it this way, you don’t need to meet any requirements to cast that spell, including costly components. The spell simply takes effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.263, 0.481, 0.294], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, you can create one of the following effects of your choice:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.3, 0.486, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object Creation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You create one object of up to 25,000 GP in value that isn’t a magic item. The object can be no more than 300 feet in any dimension, and it appears in an unoccupied space that you can see on the ground."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.377, 0.488, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instant Health.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You allow yourself and up to twenty creatures that you can see to regain all Hit Points, and you end all effects on them listed in the Greater Restoration spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.439, 0.48, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You grant up to ten creatures that you can see Resistance to one damage type that you choose. This Resistance is permanent."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.484, 0.481, 0.529], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Immunity.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You grant up to ten creatures you can see immunity to a single spell or other magical effect for 8 hours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.53, 0.488, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sudden Learning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You replace one of your feats with another feat for which you are eligible. You lose all the benefits of the old feat and gain the benefits of the new one. You can’t replace a feat that is a pre-requisite for any of your other feats or features."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.607, 0.49, 0.729], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Roll Redo.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You undo a single recent event by forcing a reroll of any die roll made within the last round (including your last turn). Reality reshapes itself to accommodate the new result. For example, a Wish spell could undo an ally’s failed saving throw or a foe’s Critical Hit. You can force the reroll to be made with Advantage or Disadvantage, and you choose whether to use the reroll or the original roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.73, 0.488, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reshape Reality.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You may wish for something not included in any of the other effects. To do so, state your wish to the GM as precisely as possible. The GM has great latitude in ruling what occurs in such an instance; the greater the wish, the greater the likelihood that something goes wrong. This spell might simply fail, the effect you desire might be achieved only in part, or you might suffer an unforeseen consequence as a result of how you worded the wish. For example, wishing that a villain were dead might propel you forward in time to a period when that villain is no longer alive, effectively removing you from the game."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.535, 0.05, 0.91, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Similarly, wishing for a Legendary magic item or an Artifact might instantly transport you to the presence of the item’s current owner. If your wish is granted and its effects have consequences for a whole community, region, or world, you are likely to attract powerful foes. If your wish would affect a god, the god’s divine servants might instantly intervene to prevent it or to encourage you to craft the wish in a particular way. If your wish would undo the multiverse itself, your wish fails."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.211, 0.913, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The stress of casting Wish to produce any effect other than duplicating another spell weakens you. After enduring that stress, each time you cast a spell until you finish a Long Rest, you take 1d10 Necrotic damage per level of that spell. This damage can’t be reduced or prevented in any way. In addition, your Strength score becomes 3 for 2d4 days. For each of those days that you spend resting and doing nothing more than light activity, your remaining recovery time decreases by 2 days. Finally, there is a 33 percent chance that you are unable to cast Wish ever again if you suffer this stress."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.402, 0.665, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Word of Recall", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.42, 0.72, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 6 Conjuration (Cleric)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.44, 0.696, 0.499], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 5 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.507, 0.908, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and up to five willing creatures within 5 feet of you instantly teleport to a previously designated sanctuary. You and any creatures that teleport with you appear in the nearest unoccupied space to the spot you designated when you prepared your sanctuary (see below). If you cast this spell without first preparing a sanctuary, the spell has no effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.615, 0.91, 0.646], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You must designate a location, such as a temple, as a sanctuary by casting this spell there."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.652, 0.656, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Zone of Truth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.67, 0.832, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Level 2 Enchantment (Bard, Cleric, Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.69, 0.678, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Time:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Action "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Range:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 feet "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Components:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " V, S "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 minutes"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.757, 0.911, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You create a magical zone that guards against deception in a 15-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point within range. Until the spell ends, a creature that enters the spell’s area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, a creature can’t speak a deliberate lie while in the radius. You know whether a creature succeeds or fails on this save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.88, 0.905, 0.942], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An affected creature is aware of the spell and can avoid answering questions to which it would normally respond with a lie. Such a creature can be evasive yet must be truthful."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "175"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 175, "blocks": [{"type": "doc_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.148, 0.05, 0.446, 0.083], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rules Glossary"}], "level": 1}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.094, 0.411, 0.118], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Glossary Conventions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.436, 0.137], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The glossary uses the following conventions:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.142, 0.49, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tags in Brackets.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some entries have a tag in brackets after the entry’s name, as in “Attack [Action].” A tag—Action, Area of Effect, Attitude, Condition, or Hazard—indicates that a rule is part of a family of rules. The tags also have glossary entries."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.219, 0.487, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“You.”", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The game’s rules—in this glossary and elsewhere—often talk about something happening to you in the game world. That “you” refers to the creature or object that the rule applies to in a particular moment of play. For example, the “you” in the Prone condition is a creature that currently has that condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.326, 0.49, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“See Also.”", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some glossary entries include a See also section that points to other entries in the glossary, to other parts of this document, or both."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.372, 0.485, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No Obsolete Terms.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The glossary contains definitions of current rules terms only. If you’re looking for a term from an earlier version of the fifth edition rules, consult the index."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.433, 0.482, 0.466], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Abbreviations.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The abbreviations listed below appear in this glossary and elsewhere in the rules."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.482, 0.294, 0.858], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.482, 0.294, 0.858], "content": "<table><tr><td>AC</td><td>Armor Class</td></tr><tr><td>C</td><td>Concentration</td></tr><tr><td>CE</td><td>Chaotic Evil</td></tr><tr><td>CG</td><td>Chaotic Good</td></tr><tr><td>Cha.</td><td>Charisma</td></tr><tr><td>CN</td><td>Chaotic Neutral</td></tr><tr><td>Con.</td><td>Constitution</td></tr><tr><td>CP</td><td>Copper Piece(s)</td></tr><tr><td>CR</td><td>Challenge Rating</td></tr><tr><td>DC</td><td>Difficulty Class</td></tr><tr><td>Dex.</td><td>Dexterity</td></tr><tr><td>EP</td><td>Electrum Piece(s)</td></tr><tr><td>GM</td><td>Game Master</td></tr><tr><td>GP</td><td>Gold Piece(s)</td></tr><tr><td>HP</td><td>Hit Point(s)</td></tr><tr><td>Int.</td><td>Intelligence</td></tr><tr><td>LE</td><td>Lawful Evil</td></tr><tr><td>LG</td><td>Lawful Good</td></tr><tr><td>LN</td><td>Lawful Neutral</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.301, 0.481, 0.489, 0.843], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.301, 0.481, 0.489, 0.843], "content": "<table><tr><td>M</td><td>Material component</td></tr><tr><td>N</td><td>Neutral</td></tr><tr><td>NE</td><td>Neutral Evil</td></tr><tr><td>NG</td><td>Neutral Good</td></tr><tr><td>NPC</td><td>Nonplayer character</td></tr><tr><td>PB</td><td>Proficiency Bonus</td></tr><tr><td>PP</td><td>Platinum Piece(s)</td></tr><tr><td>R</td><td>Ritual</td></tr><tr><td>S</td><td>Somatic component</td></tr><tr><td>SP</td><td>Silver Piece(s)</td></tr><tr><td>Str.</td><td>Strength</td></tr><tr><td>V</td><td>Verbal component</td></tr><tr><td>Wis.</td><td>Wisdom</td></tr><tr><td>XP</td><td>Experience Point(s)</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.763, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rules Definitions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.523, 0.076, 0.799, 0.093], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Here are definitions of various rules."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.099, 0.653, 0.116], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Check"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.117, 0.91, 0.18], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An ability check is a D20 Test that represents using one of the six abilities—or a specific skill associated with an ability—to overcome a challenge. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests” and “Proficiency”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.187, 0.767, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Score and Modifier"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.521, 0.204, 0.911, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature has six ability scores—Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma—each of which has a corresponding modifier. Add the modifier when you make a D20 Test with the corresponding ability or when a rule asks you to do so. See also “Playing the Game” (“The Six Abilities”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.32, 0.592, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Action"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.521, 0.337, 0.912, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On your turn, you can take one action. Choose which action to take from those below or from the special actions provided by your features. See also “Playing the Game” (“Actions”). These actions are defined elsewhere in this glossary:"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.421, 0.872, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.421, 0.872, 0.473], "content": "<table><tr><td>Attack</td><td>Dodge</td><td>Influence</td><td>Search</td></tr><tr><td>Dash</td><td>Help</td><td>Magic</td><td>Study</td></tr><tr><td>Disengage</td><td>Hide</td><td>Ready</td><td>Utilize</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.479, 0.626, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Advantage"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.521, 0.496, 0.901, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Advantage on a D20 Test, roll two d20s, and use the higher roll. A roll can’t be affected by more than one Advantage, and Advantage and Disadvantage on the same roll cancel each other. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.581, 0.627, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adventure"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.598, 0.862, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An adventure is a series of encounters. A story emerges through playing them. See also “Encounter.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.652, 0.624, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alignment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.669, 0.91, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature’s alignment broadly describes its ethical attitudes and ideals. Alignment is a combination of two factors: one identifies morality (good, evil, or neutral), and the other describes attitudes toward order (lawful, chaotic, or neutral). These factors allow for nine possible combinations, such as Lawful Good and Neutral Evil. See also “Character Creation” (“Create Your Character”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.801, 0.567, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ally"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.818, 0.913, 0.882], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature is your ally if it is a member of your adventuring party, your friend, on your side in combat, or a creature that the rules or the GM designates as your ally."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "176"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.951, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 176, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.235, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Area of Effect"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.068, 0.479, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The descriptions of many spells and other features specify that they have an area of effect, which typically has one of six shapes. These shapes are defined elsewhere in this glossary: Cone Cylinder Line Cube Emanation Sphere"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.177, 0.485, 0.299], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An area of effect has a point of origin, a location from which the effect’s energy erupts. The rules for each shape specify how to position its point of origin. If all straight lines extending from the point of origin to a location in the area of effect are blocked, that location isn’t included in the area of effect. To block a line, an obstruction must provide Total Cover. See also “Cover.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.299, 0.482, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the creator of an area of effect places it at an unseen point and an obstruction—such as a wall— is between the creator and that point, the point of origin comes into being on the near side of the obstruction."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.384, 0.223, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor Class"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.401, 0.478, 0.447], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Armor Class (AC) is the target number for an attack roll. AC represents how difficult it is to hit a target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.447, 0.489, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your base AC calculation is 10 plus your Dexterity modifier. If a rule gives you another base AC calculation, you choose which calculation to use; you can’t use more than one. See also “Attack Roll.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.517, 0.249, 0.534], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor Training"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.1, 0.535, 0.488, 0.659], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor training allows you to use armor of a certain category without the following drawbacks. If you wear Light, Medium, or Heavy armor and lack training with it, you have Disadvantage on any D20 Test that involves Strength or Dexterity, and you can’t cast spells. If you use a Shield and lack training with it, you don’t gain its AC bonus. See also “Disadvantage” and “Equipment” (“Armor”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.665, 0.248, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.683, 0.485, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Attack action, you can make one attack roll with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.714, 0.489, 0.836], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipping and Unequipping Weapons.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can either equip or unequip one weapon when you make an attack as part of this action. You do so either before or after the attack. If you equip a weapon before an attack, you don’t need to use it for that attack. Equipping a weapon includes drawing it from a sheath or picking it up. Unequipping a weapon includes sheathing, stowing, or dropping it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.836, 0.489, 0.914], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Moving between Attacks.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you move on your turn and have a feature, such as Extra Attack, that gives you more than one attack as part of the Attack action, you can use some or all of that movement to move between those attacks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.633, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Roll"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.901, 0.116], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An attack roll is a D20 Test that represents making an attack with a weapon, an Unarmed Strike, or a spell. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.122, 0.608, 0.139], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attitude"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.14, 0.901, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster has a starting attitude toward a player character: Friendly, Hostile, or Indifferent. See also “Friendly,” “Hostile,” “Indifferent,” and “Influence.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.194, 0.642, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attunement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.212, 0.893, 0.305], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items require a creature to form a bond—called Attunement—with them before the creature can use an item’s magical properties. A creature can have Attunement with no more than three magic items at a time. See also “Equipment” (“Magic Items”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.311, 0.707, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blinded [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.329, 0.896, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Blinded condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.36, 0.905, 0.391], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Can’t See.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t see and automatically fail any ability check that requires sight."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.391, 0.912, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage, and your attack rolls have Disadvantage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.429, 0.619, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blindsight"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.447, 0.908, 0.541], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Blindsight, you can see within a specific range without relying on physical sight. Within that range, you can see anything that isn’t behind Total Cover even if you have the Blinded condition or are in Darkness. Moreover, in that range, you can see something that has the Invisible condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.547, 0.612, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bloodied"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.564, 0.91, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature is Bloodied while it has half its Hit Points or fewer remaining."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.603, 0.652, 0.619], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Action"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.62, 0.908, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Bonus Action is a special action that you can take on the same turn that you take an action. You can’t take more than one Bonus Action on a turn, and you have a Bonus Action to take only if a rule explicitly says so. See also “Playing the Game” (“Actions”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.705, 0.686, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Breaking Objects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.723, 0.901, 0.785], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Objects can be harmed by attacks and by some spells, using the rules below. If an object is exceedingly fragile, the GM may allow a creature to break it automatically with the Attack or Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.785, 0.893, 0.816], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor Class.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Object Armor Class table suggests ACs for various substances."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "177"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 177, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.104, 0.069, 0.49, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.275, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object Armor Class"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.104, 0.069, 0.49, 0.162], "content": "<table><tr><td>AC</td><td>Substance</td><td>AC</td><td>Substance</td></tr><tr><td>ⅡI</td><td>Cloth, paper, rope</td><td>19</td><td>Iron, steel</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Crystal, glass, ice</td><td>21</td><td>Mithral</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>Wood</td><td>23</td><td>Adamantine</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td colspan=\"3\">Stone</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.171, 0.49, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Points.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An object is destroyed when it has 0 Hit Points. The Object Hit Points table suggests Hit Points for fragile and resilient objects that are Large or smaller. To track Hit Points for a Huge or Gargantuan object, divide it into Large or smaller sections, and track each section’s Hit Points separately. The GM determines whether destroying part of an object causes the whole thing to collapse."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.308, 0.253, 0.323], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object Hit Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.326, 0.487, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.326, 0.487, 0.421], "content": "<table><tr><td>Size Fragile</td><td>Resilient</td></tr><tr><td>2 (1d4) Tiny (bottle, lock)</td><td>5 (2d4)</td></tr><tr><td>3 (Id6) Small (chest, lute)</td><td>10 (3d6)</td></tr><tr><td>4 (1d8) Medium (barrel, chandelier)</td><td>18 (4d8)</td></tr><tr><td>Large (cart, dining table)</td><td>5 (IdI0) 27 (5d10)</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.429, 0.484, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Types and Objects.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Objects have Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. The GM might decide that some damage types are more or less effective against an object. For example, Bludgeoning damage works well for smashing things but not for cutting. Paper or cloth objects might have Vulnerability to Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.537, 0.477, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Threshold.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Big objects, such as castle walls, often have extra resilience represented by a damage threshold. See also “Damage Threshold.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.583, 0.474, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No Ability Scores.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An object lacks ability scores unless a rule assigns scores to the object. Without ability scores, an object can’t make ability checks, and it fails all saving throws."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.652, 0.216, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bright Light"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.669, 0.474, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bright Light is normal illumination. See also “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.708, 0.266, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burning [Hazard]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.1, 0.726, 0.485, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A burning creature or object takes 1d4 Fire damage at the start of each of its turns. As an action, you can extinguish fire on yourself by giving yourself the Prone condition and rolling on the ground. The fire also goes out if it is doused, submerged, or suffocated."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.826, 0.238, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burrow Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.843, 0.488, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that has a Burrow Speed can use that speed to move through sand, earth, mud, or ice. The creature can’t burrow through solid rock unless the creature has a trait that allows it to do so. See also “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.621, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Campaign"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.069, 0.859, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A campaign is a series of adventures. See also “Adventure.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.107, 0.6, 0.124], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cantrip"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.124, 0.891, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A cantrip is a level 0 spell, which is cast without a spell slot. See also “Spells.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.163, 0.694, 0.181], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Carrying Capacity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.181, 0.909, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your size and Strength score determine the maximum weight in pounds that you can carry, as shown in the Carrying Capacity table. The table also shows the maximum weight you can drag, lift, or push."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.242, 0.895, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While dragging, lifting, or pushing weight in exc"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ess", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " of the maximum weight you can carry, your Speed can be no more than 5 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.301, 0.681, 0.318], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Carrying Capacity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.526, 0.32, 0.91, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.526, 0.32, 0.91, 0.433], "content": "<table><tr><td>Creature Size</td><td>Carry</td><td>Drag/Lift/Push</td></tr><tr><td>Tiny</td><td>Str. × 7.5 lb.</td><td>Str.×15 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Small/Medium</td><td>Str. × 15 lb.</td><td>Str. × 30 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Large</td><td>Str. × 30 lb.</td><td>Str.× 60 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Huge</td><td>Str. × 60 lb.</td><td>Str. ×120 lb.</td></tr><tr><td>Gargantuan</td><td>Str.×120 lb.</td><td>Str.× 240 lb.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.45, 0.682, 0.468], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Challenge Rating"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.468, 0.913, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Challenge Rating (CR) summarizes the threat a monster poses to a group of four player characters. Compare a monster’s CR to the characters’ level. If the CR is higher, the monster is likely a danger. If the CR is lower, the monster likely poses little threat. But circumstances and the number of player characters can significantly alter how threatening a monster is in actual play. “Gameplay Toolbox” (“Combat Encounters”) provides guidance to the GM on using CR while planning potential combat encounters. See also “Stat Block.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.645, 0.68, 0.661], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Character Sheet"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.662, 0.894, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A character sheet is a paper or digital record that you use to track your character’s information. See also “Character Creation.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.715, 0.722, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Charmed [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.734, 0.905, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Charmed condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.764, 0.91, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Can’t Harm the Charmer.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t attack the charmer or target the charmer with damaging abilities or magical effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.81, 0.91, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Social Advantage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The charmer has Advantage on any ability check to interact with you socially."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.849, 0.612, 0.867], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Climbing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.867, 0.907, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you’re climbing, each foot of movement costs 1 extra foot (2 extra feet in Difficult Terrain). You "}, {"type": "text", "content": "ignore", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " this extra cost if you have a Climb Speed and use it to climb."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "178"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.951, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 178, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.481, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At the GM’s option, climbing a slippery surface or one with few handholds might require a successful DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.104, 0.224, 0.121], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Climb Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.121, 0.49, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Climb Speed can be used in place of Speed to traverse a vertical surface without expending the extra movement normally associated with climbing. See also “Climbing” and “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.192, 0.24, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Concentration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.1, 0.209, 0.488, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some spells and other effects require Concentration to remain active, as specified in their descriptions. If the effect’s creator loses Concentration, the effect ends. If the effect has a maximum duration, the effect’s description specifies how long the creator can concentrate on it: up to 1 minute, 1 hour, or some other duration. The creator can end Concentration at any time (no action required). The following factors break Concentration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.347, 0.476, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Another Concentration Effect.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You lose Concentration on an effect the moment you start casting a spell that requires Concentration or activate another effect that requires Concentration."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.408, 0.485, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you take damage, you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw to maintain Concentration. The DC equals 10 or half the damage taken (round down), whichever number is higher, up to a maximum DC of 30."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.485, 0.481, 0.517], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incapacitated or Dead.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration ends if you have the Incapacitated condition or you die."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.523, 0.199, 0.539], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Condition"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.541, 0.475, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A condition is a temporary game state. The definition of a condition says how it affects its recipient, and various rules define how to end a condition. This glossary defines these conditions:"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.609, 0.459, 0.693], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.609, 0.459, 0.693], "content": "<table><tr><td>Blinded</td><td>Grappled Incapacitated</td><td>Poisoned Prone</td></tr><tr><td>Charmed</td><td></td><td>Restrained</td></tr><tr><td>Deafened</td><td>Invisible</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Exhaustion</td><td>Paralyzed</td><td>Stunned</td></tr><tr><td>Frightened</td><td>Petrified</td><td>Unconscious</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.699, 0.466, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A condition doesn’t stack with itself; a recipient either has a condition or doesn’t. The Exhaustion condition is an exception to that rule."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.753, 0.3, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cone [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.771, 0.489, 0.893], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cone is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin in a direction its creator chooses. A Cone’s width at any point along its length is equal to that point’s distance from the point of origin. For example, a Cone is 15 feet wide at a point along its length that is 15 feet from the point of origin. The effect that creates a Cone specifies its maximum length."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.893, 0.475, 0.925], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cone’s point of origin isn’t included in the area of effect unless its creator decides otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.587, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cover"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.521, 0.069, 0.912, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cover provides a degree of protection to a target behind it. There are three degrees of cover, each of which provides a different benefit to a target: Half Cover (+2 bonus to AC and Dexterity saving throws), Three-Quarters Cover (+5 bonus to AC and Dexterity saving throws), and Total Cover (can’t be targeted directly). If behind more than one degree of cover, a target benefits only from the most protective degree. See also “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.214, 0.612, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crawling"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.232, 0.905, 0.279], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you’re crawling, each foot of movement costs 1 extra foot (2 extra feet in Difficult Terrain). See also “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.286, 0.613, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.303, 0.899, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any being in the game, including a player’s character, is a creature. See also “Creature Type.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.343, 0.662, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.521, 0.36, 0.91, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every creature, including every player character, has a tag in the rules that identifies the type of creature it is. Most player characters are of the Humanoid type. These are the game’s creature types:"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.428, 0.877, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.428, 0.877, 0.512], "content": "<table><tr><td>Aberration</td><td>Elemental</td><td>Monstrosity</td></tr><tr><td>Beast</td><td>Fey</td><td>Ooze</td></tr><tr><td>Celestial</td><td>Fiend</td><td>Plant</td></tr><tr><td>Construct</td><td>Giant</td><td>Undead</td></tr><tr><td>Dragon</td><td>Humanoid</td><td></td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.518, 0.896, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The types don’t have rules themselves, but some rules in the game affect creatures of certain types in different ways."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.571, 0.633, 0.588], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Critical Hit"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.589, 0.91, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you roll a 20 on the d20 for an attack roll, you score a Critical Hit, and the attack hits regardless of any modifiers or the target’s AC. A Critical Hit lets you roll extra dice for the attack’s damage against the target. Roll all of the attack’s damage dice twice and add them together. Then add any relevant modifiers. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.72, 0.722, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cube [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.738, 0.91, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cube is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin located anywhere on a face of the Cube. The effect that creates a Cube specifies its size, which is the length of each side."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.8, 0.898, 0.831], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cube’s point of origin isn’t included in the area of effect unless its creator decides otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.838, 0.594, 0.854], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.521, 0.856, 0.904, 0.933], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some game effects curse a creature or an object. The effect that confers a curse defines what the curse does. Curses can be removed by the Remove Curse and Greater Restoration spells or other magic that explicitly ends curses."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "179"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 179, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.328, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cylinder [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.487, 0.145], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cylinder is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin located at the center of the circular top or bottom of the Cylinder. The effect that creates a Cylinder specifies the radius of the Cylinder’s base and the Cylinder’s height."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.145, 0.485, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Cylinder’s point of origin is included in the area of effect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.183, 0.192, 0.2], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "D20 Test"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.1, 0.201, 0.487, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "D20 Tests encompass the three main d20 rolls of the game: ability checks, attack rolls, and saving throws. If something in the game affects D20 Tests, it affects all three of these rolls. The GM determines whether a D20 Test is warranted in a given circumstance. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.302, 0.183, 0.319], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.319, 0.48, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage represents harm that causes a creature or an object to lose Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.358, 0.224, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Roll"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.375, 0.489, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A damage roll is a die roll, adjusted by any applicable modifiers, that deals damage to a target. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.429, 0.28, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Threshold"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.447, 0.48, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature or an object that has a damage threshold has Immunity to all damage unless it takes an amount of damage from a single attack or effect equal to or greater than its damage threshold, in which case it takes that entire instance of damage. Any damage that fails to meet or exceed the damage threshold is superficial and doesn’t reduce Hit Points. For example, if an object has a damage threshold of 10, the object takes no damage if 9 damage is dealt to it, since that damage fails to exceed the threshold. If the same object is dealt 11 damage, it takes all of that damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.639, 0.241, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Types"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.657, 0.481, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks and other harmful effects deal different types of damage. Damage types have no rules of their own, but other rules, such as Resistance, rely on the types. The Damage Types table offers examples to help a GM assign a type to a new effect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.746, 0.23, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Types"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.764, 0.489, 0.898], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.764, 0.489, 0.898], "content": "<table><tr><td>Type</td><td>Examples</td></tr><tr><td>Acid</td><td>Corrosive liquids, digestive enzymes</td></tr><tr><td>Bludgeoning</td><td>Blunt objects, constriction, falling</td></tr><tr><td>Cold</td><td>Freezing water, icy blasts</td></tr><tr><td>Fire</td><td>Flames, unbearable heat</td></tr><tr><td>Force</td><td>Pure magical energy</td></tr><tr><td>Lightning</td><td>Electricity</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.527, 0.055, 0.91, 0.207], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.527, 0.055, 0.91, 0.207], "content": "<table><tr><td>Type</td><td>Examples</td></tr><tr><td>Necrotic</td><td>Life-draining energy</td></tr><tr><td>Piercing</td><td>Fangs, puncturing objects</td></tr><tr><td>Poison</td><td>Toxic gas, venom</td></tr><tr><td>Psychic</td><td>Mind-rending energy</td></tr><tr><td>Radiant</td><td>Holy energy, searing radiation</td></tr><tr><td>Slashing</td><td>Claws, cutting objects</td></tr><tr><td>Thunder</td><td>Concussive sound</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.219, 0.615, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.236, 0.881, 0.284], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An area of Darkness is Heavily Obscured. See also “Heavily Obscured” and “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.291, 0.629, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.308, 0.898, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Darkvision, you can see in Dim Light within a specified range as if it were Bright Light and in Darkness within that range as if it were Dim Light. You discern colors in that Darkness only as shades of gray. See also “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.408, 0.656, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dash [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.426, 0.913, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Dash action, you gain extra movement for the current turn. The increase equals your Speed after applying any modifiers. With a Speed of 30 feet, for example, you can move up to 60 feet on your turn if you Dash. If your Speed of 30 feet is reduced to 15 feet, you can move up to 30 feet this turn if you Dash."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.533, 0.908, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have a special speed, such as a Fly Speed or Swim Speed, you can use that speed instead of your Speed when you take this action. You choose which speed to use each time you take it. See also “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.602, 0.58, 0.618], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dead"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.62, 0.906, 0.728], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A dead creature has no Hit Points and can’t regain them unless it is first revived by magic such as the Raise Dead or Revivify spell. When such a spell is cast, the spirit knows who is casting it and can refuse. The spirit of a dead creature has left the body and departed for the Outer Planes, and reviving the creature requires calling the spirit back."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.521, 0.727, 0.912, 0.868], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the creature returns to life, the revival effect determines the creature’s current Hit Points. Unless otherwise stated, the creature returns to life with any conditions, magical contagions, or curses that were affecting it at death if the durations of those effects are still ongoing. If the creature died with any Exhaustion levels, it returns with 1 fewer level. If the creature had Attunement to one or more magic items, it is no longer attuned to them."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "180"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 180, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.303, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deafened [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.484, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Deafened condition, you experience the following effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.099, 0.476, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Can’t Hear.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t hear and automatically fail any ability check that requires hearing."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.138, 0.292, 0.155], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Death Saving Throw"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.156, 0.478, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A player character must make a Death Saving Throw (also called a Death Save) if they start their turn with 0 Hit Points. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.225, 0.308, 0.242], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dehydration [Hazard]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.243, 0.481, 0.366], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature requires an amount of water per day based on its size, as shown in the Water Needs per Day table. A creature that drinks less than half the required water for a day gains 1 Exhaustion level at the day’s end. Exhaustion caused by dehydration can’t be removed until the creature drinks the full amount of water required for a day. See also “Exhaustion.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.378, 0.29, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Water Needs per Day"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.397, 0.488, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.397, 0.488, 0.472], "content": "<table><tr><td>Size</td><td>Water</td><td>Size</td><td>Water</td></tr><tr><td>Tiny</td><td>1/4 gallon</td><td>Large</td><td>4 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Small</td><td>I gallon</td><td>Huge</td><td>16 gallons</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>I gallon</td><td>Gargantuan</td><td>64 gallons</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.484, 0.252, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Difficult Terrain"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.501, 0.49, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a space is Difficult Terrain, every foot of movement in that space costs 1 extra foot. For example, moving 5 feet through Difficult Terrain costs 10 feet of movement. Difficult Terrain isn’t cumulative; either a space is Difficult Terrain or it isn’t."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.578, 0.47, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A space is Difficult Terrain if the space contains any of the following or something similar:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.617, 0.372, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• A creature that isn’t Tiny or your ally"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.634, 0.461, 0.666], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Furniture that is sized for creatures of your size or larger"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.667, 0.401, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Heavy snow, ice, rubble, or undergrowth"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.104, 0.684, 0.413, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Liquid that’s between shin- and waist-deep"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.104, 0.7, 0.44, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• A narrow opening sized for a creature one size smaller than you"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.103, 0.733, 0.333, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• A slope of 20 degrees or more"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.756, 0.244, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Difficulty Class"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.774, 0.488, 0.821], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Difficulty Class (DC) is the target number for an ability check or a saving throw. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.828, 0.199, 0.845], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dim Light"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.845, 0.456, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An area with Dim Light is Lightly Obscured. See also “Lightly Obscured” and “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.651, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disadvantage"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.521, 0.069, 0.913, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Disadvantage on a D20 Test, roll two d20s and use the lower roll. A roll can’t be affected by more than one Disadvantage, and Advantage and Disadvantage on the same roll cancel each other. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.153, 0.701, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Disengage [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.171, 0.907, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you take the Disengage action, your movement doesn’t provoke Opportunity Attacks for the rest of the current turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.225, 0.668, 0.242], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dodge [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.242, 0.912, 0.319], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you take the Dodge action, you gain the following benefits: until the start of your next turn, any attack roll made against you has Disadvantage if you can see the attacker, and you make Dexterity saving throws with Advantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.319, 0.891, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You lose these benefits if you have the Incapacitated condition or if your Speed is 0."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.358, 0.77, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Emanation [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.376, 0.91, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Emanation is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a creature or an object in all directions. The effect that creates an Emanation specifies the distance it extends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.437, 0.901, 0.482], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Emanation moves with the creature or object that is its origin unless it is an instantaneous or a stationary effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.482, 0.896, 0.529], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Emanation’s origin (creature or object) isn’t included in the area of effect unless its creator decides otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.537, 0.624, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Encounter"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.554, 0.904, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An encounter is a scene in an adventure that is part of at least one of the game’s three pillars: social interaction, exploration, or combat. See also “Playing the Game” (“Social Interaction,” “Exploration,” and “Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.639, 0.592, 0.656], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Enemy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.657, 0.895, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature is your enemy if it fights against you in combat, actively works to harm you, or is designated as your enemy by the rules or GM."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.71, 0.738, 0.727], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Exhaustion [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.523, 0.728, 0.865, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Exhaustion condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.759, 0.899, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Exhaustion Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This condition is cumulative. Each time you receive it, you gain 1 Exhaustion level. You die if your Exhaustion level is 6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.522, 0.805, 0.907, 0.835], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "D20 Tests Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you make a D20 Test, the roll is reduced by 2 times your Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.522, 0.836, 0.904, 0.866], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed Reduced.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is reduced by a number of feet equal to 5 times your Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.522, 0.866, 0.908, 0.914], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Removing Exhaustion Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Finishing a Long Rest removes 1 of your Exhaustion levels. When your Exhaustion level reaches 0, the condition ends."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.06, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "181"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 181, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.271, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Experience Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.475, 0.161], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As they overcome challenges and complete adventures, characters earn Experience Points (XP), which are awarded by the Game Master. When a character’s XP total crosses certain thresholds, the character’s level increases. See also “Level Advancement.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.169, 0.196, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Expertise"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.186, 0.49, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Expertise is a feature that enhances your use of a skill proficiency. When you make an ability check with a skill proficiency in which you have Expertise, your Proficiency Bonus is doubled for that check unless the bonus is doubled by another feature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.263, 0.472, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you gain Expertise, you gain it in one skill in which you have proficiency. You can’t have Exper tise in the same skill proficiency more than once."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.115, 0.309, 0.44, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "See also “Playing the Game” (“Proficiency”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.332, 0.253, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Falling [Hazard]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.35, 0.481, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that falls takes 1d6 Bludgeoning damage at the end of the fall for every 10 feet it fell, to a maximum of 20d6. When the creature lands, it has the Prone condition unless it avoids taking any damage from the fall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.426, 0.488, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that falls into water or another liquid can use its Reaction to make a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check to hit the surface head or feet first. On a successful check, any damage resulting from the fall is halved."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.511, 0.162, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.528, 0.489, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A variety of effects allow a creature to fly. While flying, you fall if you have the Incapacitated or Prone condition or your Fly Speed is reduced to 0. You can stay aloft in those circumstances if you can hover. See also “Falling” and “Fly Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.613, 0.196, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fly Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.63, 0.482, 0.679], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Fly Speed can be used to travel through the air. While you have a Fly Speed, you can stay aloft until you land, fall, or die. See also “Flying” and “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.685, 0.277, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Friendly [Attitude]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.703, 0.47, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Friendly creature views you favorably. You have Advantage on an ability check to influence a Friendly creature. See also “Influence.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.756, 0.314, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Frightened [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.774, 0.485, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Frightened condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.805, 0.466, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Checks and Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls while the source of fear is within line of sight."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.851, 0.49, 0.881], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Can’t Approach.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t willingly move closer to the source of fear."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.723, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grappled [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.904, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Grappled condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.535, 0.099, 0.86, 0.114], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed 0.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is 0 and can’t increase."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.116, 0.912, 0.145], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on attack rolls against any target other than the grappler."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.145, 0.912, 0.207], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Movable.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The grappler can drag or carry you when it moves, but every foot of movement costs it 1 extra foot unless you are Tiny or two or more sizes smaller than it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.215, 0.62, 0.232], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grappling"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.233, 0.901, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature can grapple another creature. Characters typically grapple by using an Unarmed Strike. Many monsters have special attacks that allow them to quickly grapple prey. However a grapple is initiated, it follows these rules. See also “Unarmed Strike” and “Grappled.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.325, 0.878, 0.355], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grappled Condition.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Successfully grappling a c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "reature", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " gives it the Grappled condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.355, 0.912, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One Grapple per Hand.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature must have a hand free to grapple another creature. Some stat blocks and game effects allow a creature to grapple using a tentacle, a maw, or another body part. Whatever part a grappler uses, it can grapple only one creature at a time with that part, and the grappler can’t use that part to target another creature unless it ends the grapple."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.478, 0.907, 0.618], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ending a Grapple.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Grappled creature can use its action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against the grapple’s escape DC, ending the condition on itself on a success. The condition also ends if the grappler has the Incapacitated condition or if the distance between the Grappled target and the grappler exceeds the grapple’s range. In addition, the grappler can release the target at any time (no action required)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.623, 0.599, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hazard"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.64, 0.905, 0.688], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A hazard is an environmental danger. See also “Burning,” “Dehydration,” “Falling,” “Malnutrition,” and “Suffocation.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.695, 0.6, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.712, 0.905, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Healing is how you regain Hit Points. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.751, 0.69, 0.768], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heavily Obscured"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.769, 0.897, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have the Blinded condition while trying to see something in a Heavily Obscured space. See also “Blinded,” “Darkness,” and “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.838, 0.652, 0.856], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Help [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.856, 0.887, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Help action, you do one of the following."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.522, 0.887, 0.893, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assist an Ability Check.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose one of your skill or tool proficiencies and one ally who is near"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "182"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 182, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.488, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "enough for you to assist verbally or physically when they make an ability check. That ally has Advantage on the next ability check they make with the chosen skill or tool. This benefit expires if the ally doesn’t use it before the start of your next turn. The GM has final say on whether your assistance is possible."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.143, 0.489, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assist an Attack Roll.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You momentarily distract an enemy within 5 feet of you, giving Advantage to the next attack roll by one of your allies against that enemy. This benefit expires at the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.227, 0.272, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heroic Inspiration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.244, 0.478, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you (a player character) have Heroic Inspiration, you can expend it to reroll any die immediately after rolling it, and you must use the new roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.291, 0.481, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you gain Heroic Inspiration but already have it, it’s lost unless you give it to a player character who lacks it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.344, 0.231, 0.361], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hide [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.1, 0.362, 0.485, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With the Hide action, you try to hide yourself. To do so, you must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity (Stealth) check while you’re Heavily Obscured or behind Three-Quarters Cover or Total Cover, and you must be out of any enemy’s line of sight; if you can see a creature, you can discern whether it can see you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.454, 0.488, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a successful check, you have the Invisible condition while hidden. Make note of your check’s total, which is the DC for a creature to find you with a Wisdom (Perception) check."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.485, 0.579], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You stop being hidden immediately after any of the following occurs: you make a sound louder than a whisper, an enemy finds you, you make an attack roll, or you cast a spell with a Verbal c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "omponent", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.585, 0.203, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "High Jump"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.602, 0.482, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make a High Jump, you leap into the air a number of feet equal to 3 plus your Strength modifier (minimum of 0 feet) if you move at least 10 feet on foot immediately before the jump. When you make a standing High Jump, you can jump only half that distance. Either way, each foot of the jump costs a foot of movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.709, 0.485, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can extend your arms half your height above yourself during the jump. Thus, you can reach a dis tance equal to the height of the jump plus 1½ times your height."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.779, 0.237, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Point Dice"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.796, 0.487, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Point Dice, or Hit Dice for short, help determine a player character’s Hit Point maximum, as explained in “Character Creation.” Most monsters also have Hit Dice. A creature can spend Hit Dice during a Short Rest to regain Hit Points. See also “Short Rest.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.621, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.521, 0.068, 0.899, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Points (HP) are a measure of how difficult it is to kill or destroy a creature or an object. Damage reduces Hit Points, and healing restores them. You can’t have more Hit Points than your Hit Point maximum, and you can’t have less than 0. See also “Breaking Objects” and “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.183, 0.69, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hostile [Attitude]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.201, 0.909, 0.248], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Hostile creature views you unfavorably. You have Disadvantage on an ability check to influence a Hostile creature. See also “Influence.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.588, 0.271], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hover"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.521, 0.273, 0.9, 0.35], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some creatures can hover, as noted in their stat blocks, and some spells and other effects grant the ability to hover. Hovering while flying prevents you from falling in certain circumstances. See also “Flying.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.357, 0.604, 0.374], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Illusions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.375, 0.905, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells and other effects sometimes create magical illusions. Such an effect defines what the illusion does and which senses or mental faculties it deceives."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.422, 0.902, 0.545], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If an illusion manifests in space, the illusion is insubstantial and weightless, yet it seems to be affected by the environment as if the illusion were real unless the effect that created it specifies otherwise. For example, a visual illusion of a creature casts shadows and reflections, and wind appears to affect the illusory creature. Similarly, an audible illusion echoes in an echoey space."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.552, 0.618, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immunity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.57, 0.897, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Immunity to a damage type or a condition, it doesn’t affect you in any way."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.609, 0.721, 0.625], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Improvised Weapons"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.626, 0.912, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An improvised weapon is an object wielded as a makeshift weapon, such as broken glass, a table leg, or a frying pan. A Simple or Martial weapon also counts as an improvised weapon if it’s wielded in a way contrary to its design; if you use a Ranged weapon to make a melee attack or throw a Melee weapon that lacks the Thrown property, the weapon counts as an improvised weapon. An improvised weapon follows the rules below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.764, 0.901, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Proficiency.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Don’t add your Proficiency Bonus to attack rolls with an improvised weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.795, 0.912, 0.825], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " On a hit, the weapon deals 1d4 damage of a type the GM thinks is appropriate for the object."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.826, 0.9, 0.856], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Range.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you throw the weapon, it has a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.856, 0.906, 0.933], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon Equivalents.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If an improvised weapon resembles a Simple or Martial weapon, the GM may say it functions as that weapon and uses that weapon’s rules. For example, the GM could treat a table leg as a Club."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "183"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 183, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.337, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incapacitated [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.484, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Incapacitated condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.099, 0.481, 0.129], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inactive.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t take any action, Bonus Action, or Reaction."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.114, 0.13, 0.479, 0.16], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No Concentration.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Concentration is broken. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speechless.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t speak."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.16, 0.474, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Surprised.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you’re Incapacitated when you roll Initiative, you have Disadvantage on the roll."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.199, 0.298, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Indifferent [Attitude]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.217, 0.486, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Indifferent creature has no desire to help or hinder you. Indifferent is the default attitude of a monster. See also “Influence.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.269, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Influence [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.289, 0.489, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "With the Influence action, you urge a monster to do something. Describe or roleplay how you’re communicating with the monster. Are you trying to deceive, intimidate, amuse, or gently persuade? The GM then determines whether the monster feels willing, unwilling, or hesitant due to your interaction; this determination establishes whether an ability check is necessary, as explained below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.411, 0.478, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Willing.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If your urging aligns with the monster’s desires, no ability check is necessary; the monster fulfills your request in a way it prefers."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.457, 0.488, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unwilling.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If your urging is repugnant to the monster or counter to its alignment, no ability check is necessary; it doesn’t comply."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.503, 0.487, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hesitant.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you urge the monster to do something that it is hesitant to do, you must make an ability check, which is affected by the monster’s attitude: Indifferent, Friendly, or Hostile, each of which is defined in this glossary. The Influence Checks table suggests which ability check to make based on how you’re interacting with the monster. The GM chooses the check, which has a default DC equal to 15 or the monster’s Intelligence score, whichever is higher. On a successful check, the monster does as urged. On a failed check, you must wait 24 hours (or a duration set by the GM) before urging it in the same way again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.715, 0.249, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Influence Checks"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.104, 0.734, 0.489, 0.896], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.104, 0.734, 0.489, 0.896], "content": "<table><tr><td>Ability Check</td><td>Interaction</td></tr><tr><td>Charisma (Deception)</td><td>Deceiving a monster that understands you</td></tr><tr><td>Charisma (Intimidation)</td><td>Intimidating a monster</td></tr><tr><td>Charisma (Performance)</td><td>Amusing a monster</td></tr><tr><td>Charisma (Persuasion)</td><td>Persuading a monster that understands you</td></tr><tr><td>Wisdom (Animal Handling)</td><td>Gently coaxing a Beast or Monstrosity</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.609, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.521, 0.069, 0.911, 0.114], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative determines the order of turns during combat. The combat rules in “Playing the Game” explain how to roll Initiative."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.521, 0.115, 0.9, 0.224], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes a GM might have combatants use their Initiative scores instead of rolling Initiative. Your Initiative score equals 10 plus your Dexterity modifier. If you have Advantage on Initiative rolls, increase your Initiative score by 5. If you have Disadvantage on those rolls, decrease that score by 5. See also “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.23, 0.712, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invisible [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.247, 0.899, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Invisible condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.278, 0.898, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Surprise.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you’re Invisible when you roll Initiative, you have Advantage on the roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.309, 0.907, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Concealed.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You aren’t affected by any effect that requires its target to be seen unless the effect’s creator can somehow see you. Any equipment you are wearing or carrying is also concealed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.371, 0.897, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Disadvantage, and your attack rolls have Advantage. If a creature can somehow see you, you don’t gain this benefit against that creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.44, 0.604, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Jumping"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.521, 0.457, 0.905, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you jump, you make either a Long Jump (horizontal) or a High Jump (vertical). See also “Long Jump” and “High Jump.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.511, 0.759, 0.527], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Knocking Out a Creature"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.528, 0.9, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you would reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points with a melee attack, you can instead reduce the creature to 1 Hit Point. The creature then has the Unconscious condition and starts a Short Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.59, 0.909, 0.652], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature remains Unconscious until it regains any Hit Points or until someone uses an action to administer first aid to it, which requires a successful DC 10 Wisdom (Medicine) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.659, 0.685, 0.676], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightly Obscured"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.677, 0.9, 0.74], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to see something in a Lightly Obscured space. See also “Dim Light” and “Playing the Game” (“Exploration”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.746, 0.713, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Line [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.764, 0.908, 0.825], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Line is an area of effect that extends from a point of origin in a straight path along its length and covers an area defined by its width. The effect that creates a Line specifies its length and width."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.825, 0.91, 0.857], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Line’s point of origin isn’t included in the area of effect unless its creator decides otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.864, 0.627, 0.881], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Long Jump"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.881, 0.903, 0.914], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make a Long Jump, you leap horizontally a number of feet up to your Strength score if you"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "184"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 184, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.486, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "move at least 10 feet immediately before the jump. When you make a standing Long Jump, you can leap only half that distance. Either way, each foot you jump costs a foot of movement."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.112, 0.484, 0.157], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you land in Difficult Terrain, you must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check or have the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.158, 0.49, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This Long Jump rule assumes that the height of the jump doesn’t matter, such as a jump across a stream or chasm. At your GM’s option, you must succeed on a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check to clear a low obstacle (no taller than a quarter of the jump’s distance), such as a hedge or low wall. Otherwise, you hit the obstacle."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.273, 0.2, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Long Rest"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.291, 0.482, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Long Rest is a period of extended downtime—at least 8 hours—available to any creature. During a Long Rest, you sleep for at least 6 hours and perform no more than 2 hours of light activity, such as reading, talking, eating, or standing watch."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.367, 0.486, 0.413], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "During sleep, you have the Unconscious condition. After you finish a Long Rest, you must wait at least 16 hours before starting another one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.414, 0.478, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Benefits of the Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " To start a Long Rest, you must have at least 1 Hit Point. When you finish the rest, you gain the following benefits:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.465, 0.481, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regain All HP.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You regain all lost Hit Points and all spent Hit Point Dice. If your Hit Point maximum was reduced, it returns to normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.512, 0.45, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores Restored.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If any of your ability scores were reduced, they return to normal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.543, 0.473, 0.573], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Exhaustion Reduced.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you have the Exhaustion condition, its level decreases by 1."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.573, 0.483, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Feature.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some features are recharged by a Long Rest. If you have such a feature, it recharges in the way specified in its description."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.626, 0.48, 0.658], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interrupting the Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Long Rest is stopped by the following interruptions:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.663, 0.251, 0.679], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Rolling Initiative"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.68, 0.381, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Casting a spell other than a cantrip"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.103, 0.695, 0.269, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Taking any damage"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.71, 0.445, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 1 hour of walking or other physical exertion"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.732, 0.487, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you rested at least 1 hour before the interruption, you gain the benefits of a Short Rest. See also “Short Rest.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.778, 0.482, 0.825], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can resume a Long Rest immediately after an interruption. If you do so, the rest requires 1 additional hour per interruption to finish."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.832, 0.239, 0.849], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.85, 0.481, 0.911], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Magic action, you cast a spell that has a casting time of an action or use a feature or magic item that requires a Magic action to be activated."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.908, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you cast a spell that has a casting time of 1 minute or longer, you must take the Magic action on each turn of that casting, and you must maintain Concentration while you do so. If your Concentration is broken, the spell fails, but you don’t expend a spell slot. See also “Concentration.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.656, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magical Effect"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.168, 0.912, 0.2], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An effect is magical if it is created by a spell, a magic item, or a phenomenon that a rule labels as magical."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.206, 0.729, 0.223], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Malnutrition [Hazard]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.224, 0.912, 0.362], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature needs an amount of food per day based on its size, as shown in the Food Needs per Day table. A creature that eats but consumes less than half the required food for a day must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level at the day’s end. A creature that eats nothing for 5 days automatically gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of the fifth day as well as an additional level at the end of each subsequent day without food."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.362, 0.886, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Exhaustion caused by malnutrition can’t be removed until the creature eats the full amount of food required for a day. See also “Exhaustion.”"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.526, 0.44, 0.911, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.422, 0.7, 0.437], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Food Needs per Day"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.526, 0.44, 0.911, 0.515], "content": "<table><tr><td>Size</td><td>Food</td><td>Size</td><td>Food</td></tr><tr><td>Tiny</td><td>1/4 pound</td><td>Large</td><td>4 pounds</td></tr><tr><td>Small</td><td>I pound</td><td>Huge</td><td>16 pounds</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>I pound</td><td>Gargantuan</td><td>64 pounds</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.527, 0.607, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monster"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.544, 0.912, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster is a creature controlled by the GM, even if the creature is benevolent. See also “Creature” and “NPC.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.599, 0.722, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nonplayer Character"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.616, 0.904, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A nonplayer character (NPC) is a monster that has a personal name and a distinct personality. See also “Monster.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.67, 0.594, 0.687], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Object"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.688, 0.896, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An object is a nonliving, distinct thing. Composite things, like buildings, comprise more than one object. See also “Breaking Objects.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.742, 0.674, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Occupied Space"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.759, 0.876, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A space is occupied if a creature is in it or if it is completely filled by objects."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.798, 0.719, 0.815], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Opportunity Attacks"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.521, 0.816, 0.907, 0.941], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can make an Opportunity Attack when a creature that you can see leaves your reach using its action, its Bonus Action, its Reaction, or one of its speeds. To make the Opportunity Attack, take a Reaction to make one melee attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike against the provoking creature. The attack occurs right before the creature leaves your reach. See also “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "185"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 185, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.305, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Paralyzed [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.488, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Paralyzed condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.099, 0.434, 0.129], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incapacitated.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.115, 0.13, 0.439, 0.145], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed 0.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is 0 and can’t increase."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.145, 0.469, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You automatically fail Strength and Dexterity saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.176, 0.467, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.206, 0.485, 0.252], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Automatic Critical Hits.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any attack roll that hits you is a Critical Hit if the attacker is within 5 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.261, 0.275, 0.277], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Passive Perception"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.278, 0.471, 0.355], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Passive Perception is a score that reflects a creature’s general awareness of its surroundings. The GM uses this score when determining whether a creature notices something without consciously making a Wisdom (Perception) check."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.355, 0.488, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature’s Passive Perception equals 10 plus the creature’s Wisdom (Perception) check bonus. If the creature has Advantage on such checks, increase the score by 5. If the creature has Disadvantage on them, decrease the score by 5. For example, a level 1 character with a Wisdom of 15 and proficiency in Perception has a Passive Perception of 14 (10 + 2 + 2). If that character has Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks, the score becomes 19."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.501, 0.182, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Per Day"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.518, 0.481, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a rule says you can use something a certain number of times per day, that means you must finish a Long Rest to use it again after you run out of uses."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.572, 0.295, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Petrified [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.589, 0.48, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Petrified condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.621, 0.481, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Turned to Inanimate Substance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You are transformed, along with any nonmagical objects you are wearing and carrying, into a solid inanimate substance (usually stone). Your weight increases by a factor of ten, and you cease aging."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.697, 0.433, 0.727], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incapacitated.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.114, 0.728, 0.439, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed 0.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is 0 and can’t increase."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.743, 0.466, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.774, 0.469, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You automatically fail Strength and Dexterity saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.805, 0.433, 0.835], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resist Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to all damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.101, 0.835, 0.478, 0.866], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison Immunity.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Immunity to the Poisoned condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.874, 0.262, 0.891], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Player Character"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.101, 0.891, 0.459, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A player character is a character controlled by a player. See also “Character Creation.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.72, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poisoned [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.904, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Poisoned condition, you experience the following effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.099, 0.885, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Checks and Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.138, 0.626, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Possession"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.897, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some effects cause a creature to be possessed by another creature or entity. A possessing effect defines how the possession operates. Possession can be prevented by the Protection from Evil and Good spell and ended by the Dispel Evil and Good spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.24, 0.63, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Proficiency"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.521, 0.257, 0.908, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have proficiency with something, you can add your Proficiency Bonus to any D20 Test you make using that thing. A creature might have proficiency in a skill or saving throw or with a weapon or tool. See also “Playing the Game” (“Proficiency”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.342, 0.693, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prone [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.36, 0.909, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Prone condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.391, 0.909, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Restricted Movement.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your only movement options are to crawl or to spend an amount of movement equal to half your Speed (round down) to right yourself and thereby end the condition. If your Speed is 0, you can’t right yourself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.468, 0.905, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on attack rolls. An attack roll against you has Advantage if the attacker is within 5 feet of you. Otherwise, that attack roll has Disadvantage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.537, 0.585, 0.553], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reach"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.554, 0.889, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature has a reach of 5 feet unless a rule says otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.593, 0.61, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reaction"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.521, 0.611, 0.905, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Reaction is a special action taken in response to a trigger defined in the Reaction’s description. You can take a Reaction on another creature’s turn, and if you take it on your turn, you can do so even if you also take an action, a Bonus Action, or both. Once you take a Reaction, you can’t take another one until the start of your next turn. The Opportunity Attack is a Reaction available to all creatures. See also “Opportunity Attacks” and “Playing the Game” (“Actions”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.523, 0.771, 0.665, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ready [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.522, 0.789, 0.906, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You take the Ready action to wait for a particular circumstance before you act. To do so, you take this action on your turn, which lets you act by taking a Reaction before the start of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.521, 0.851, 0.896, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "First, you decide what perceivable circumstance will trigger your Reaction. Then, you choose the action you will take in response to that trigger, or you choose to move up to your Speed in response to it. Examples include “If the cultist steps on the"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "186"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 186, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.485, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "trapdoor, I’ll pull the lever that opens it,” and “If the zombie steps next to me, I move away.”"}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.485, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the trigger occurs, you can either take your Reaction right after the trigger finishes or ignore the trigger."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.487, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you Ready a spell, you cast it as normal (expending any resources used to cast it) but hold its energy, which you release with your Reaction when the trigger occurs. To be readied, a spell must have a casting time of an action, and holding on to the spell’s magic requires Concentration, which you can maintain up to the start of your next turn. If your Concentration is broken, the spell dissipates without taking effect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.273, 0.204, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.29, 0.482, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Resistance to a damage type, damage of that type is halved against you (round down). Resistance is applied only once to an instance of damage. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.375, 0.313, 0.393], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Restrained [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.393, 0.484, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Restrained condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.115, 0.423, 0.438, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed 0.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is 0 and can’t increase."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.44, 0.489, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage, and your attack rolls have Disadvantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.469, 0.481, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.508, 0.163, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ritual"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.1, 0.525, 0.481, 0.619], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have a spell prepared that has the Ritual tag, you can cast that spell as a Ritual. The Ritual version of a spell takes 10 minutes longer to cast than normal. It also doesn’t expend a spell slot, which means the ritual version of a spell can’t be cast at a higher level. See also “Spells.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.626, 0.227, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Round Down"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.643, 0.469, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you divide or multiply a number in the game, round down if you end up with a fraction, even if the fraction is one-half or greater. Some rules make an exception and tell you to round up."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.713, 0.15, 0.729], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Save"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.73, 0.464, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Save is another name for a saving throw. See also “Saving Throw.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.769, 0.232, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throw"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.1, 0.787, 0.483, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A saving throw—also called a save—represents an attempt to avoid or resist a threat. You normally make a saving throw only when a rule requires you to do so, but you can decide to fail the save without rolling. The result of a save is detailed in the effect that allowed it. If a target is forced to make a save and lacks the ability score used by it, the target automatically fails. See also “Playing the Game” (“D20 Tests”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.67, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.521, 0.069, 0.901, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Search action, you make a Wisdom check to discern something that isn’t obvious. The Search table suggests which skills are applicable when you take this action, depending on what you’re trying to detect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.158, 0.587, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.177, 0.91, 0.27], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.177, 0.91, 0.27], "content": "<table><tr><td>Skill</td><td>Thing to Detect</td></tr><tr><td>Insight</td><td>Creature&#x27;s state of mind</td></tr><tr><td>Medicine</td><td>Creature&#x27;s ailment or cause of death</td></tr><tr><td>Perception</td><td>Concealed creature or object</td></tr><tr><td>Survival</td><td>Tracks or food</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.283, 0.661, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shape-Shifting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.521, 0.301, 0.905, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If an effect, such as Wild Shape or the Polymorph spell, lets you shape-shift, its description specifies what happens to you. Unless that description says otherwise, any ongoing effects on you—conditions, spells, curses, and the like—carry over from one form to the other. You revert to your true form if you die."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.416, 0.628, 0.432], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Short Rest"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.433, 0.91, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Short Rest is a 1-hour period of downtime, during which a creature does nothing more strenuous than reading, talking, eating, or standing watch. To start a Short Rest, you must have at least 1 Hit Point."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.495, 0.912, 0.527], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Benefits of the Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you finish the rest, you gain the following benefits:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.532, 0.906, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spend Hit Point Dice.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can spend one or more of your Hit Point Dice to regain Hit Points. For each Hit Point Die you spend in this way, roll the die and add your Constitution modifier to it. You regain Hit Points equal to the total (minimum of 1 Hit Point). You can decide to spend an additional Hit Point Die after each roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.64, 0.907, 0.687], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Feature.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some features are recharged by a Short Rest. If you have such a feature, it recharges in the way specified in its description."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.692, 0.905, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Interrupting the Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Short Rest is stopped by the following interruptions:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.73, 0.672, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Rolling Initiative"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.746, 0.804, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Casting a spell other than a cantrip"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.762, 0.691, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Taking any damage"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.783, 0.867, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An interrupted Short Rest confers no benefits."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.806, 0.716, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Simultaneous Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.521, 0.824, 0.904, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If two or more things happen at the same time on a turn, the person at the game table—player or GM— whose turn it is decides the order in which those things happen. For example, if two effects occur at the start of a player character’s turn, the player decides which of the effects happens first."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "187"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 187, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.146, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.489, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature or an object belongs to a size category: Tiny, Small, Medium, Large, Huge, or Gargantuan. A creature’s size determines how much space the creature occupies in combat. An object’s size affects its Hit Points. See also “Breaking Objects” and “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.168, 0.147, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skill"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.1, 0.186, 0.488, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A skill is an area of specialization associated with an ability check. If you have proficiency in a skill, you can add your Proficiency Bonus when you make an ability check associated with that skill. See a"}, {"type": "text", "content": "lso", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " “Playing the Game” (“Proficiency”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.165, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.288, 0.487, 0.35], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature has a Speed, which is the distance in feet the creature can cover when it moves on its turn. See also “Climbing,” “Crawling,” “Flying,” “Jumping,” “Swimming” and “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.35, 0.489, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Speeds.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some creatures have special speeds, such as a Burrow Speed, Climb Speed, Fly Speed, or Swim Speed, each of which is defined in this glossary. If you have more than one speed, choose which one to use when you move; you can switch between the speeds during your move. Whenever you switch, subtract the distance already moved from the new speed. The result determines how much farther you can move. If the result is 0 or less, you can’t use the new speed during the current move. For example, if you have a Speed of 30 and a Fly Speed of 40, you could fly 10 feet, walk 10 feet, and leap into the air to fly 20 feet more."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.549, 0.49, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Changes to Your Speeds.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If an effect increases or decreases your Speed for a time, any special speed you have increases or decreases by an equal amount for the same duration. For example, if your Speed is reduced to 0 and you have a Climb Speed, your Climb Speed is also reduced to 0. Similarly, if your Speed is halved and you have a Fly Speed, your Fly Speed is also halved."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.68, 0.153, 0.696], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.697, 0.475, 0.729], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell is a magical effect that has the characteristics described in “Spells.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.736, 0.219, 0.752], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Attack"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.753, 0.49, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A spell attack is an attack roll made as part of a spell or another magical effect. See also “Spells” (“Casting Spells”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.807, 0.272, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting Focus"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.825, 0.484, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Spellcasting Focus is an object that certain creatures can use in place of a spell’s Material components if those materials aren’t consumed by the spell and don’t have a cost specified. Some classes allow its members to use certain types of Spellcasting Focuses. See also “Spells” (“Casting Spells”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.051, 0.738, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sphere [Area of Effect]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.906, 0.13], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Sphere is an area of effect that extends in straight lines from a point of origin outward in all directions. The effect that creates a Sphere specifies the distance it extends as the radius of the Sphere."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.13, 0.858, 0.161], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Sphere’s point of origin is included in the Sphere’s area of effect."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.168, 0.588, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stable"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.186, 0.883, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature is Stable if it has 0 Hit Points but isn’t required to make Death Saving Throws. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.24, 0.624, 0.256], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stat Block"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.257, 0.908, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A stat block contains the game statistics of a monster. Each stat block includes the following information presented after the monster’s name."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.304, 0.879, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A monster is Tiny, Small, Medium, Large, Huge, or Gargantuan. See also “Size.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.335, 0.904, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This entry notes the family of beings a monster belongs to, along with any descriptive tags. See also “Creature Type.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.381, 0.901, 0.426], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alignment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An alignment is suggested for the monster, with the GM determining its actual alignment. See also “Alignment.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.427, 0.908, 0.564], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "AC, Initiative, and HP.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These entries give the monster’s Armor Class, Initiative, and Hit Points, which are detailed in “Playing the Game.” In parentheses after the Hit Points, the monster’s Hit Point Dice are provided, along with the contribution of its Constitution, if any, to its Hit Points. Following the Initiative modifier is an Initiative score. Some creatures that are created by magic lack Hit Dice and Initiative information."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.564, 0.88, 0.625], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Here the monster’s Speed is provided, along with any special speeds. See also “Burrow Speed,” “Climb Speed,” “Fly Speed,” and “Swim Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.626, 0.902, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A table provides the monster’s ability scores, modifiers, and saving throw modifiers, all of which are detailed in “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.672, 0.879, 0.717], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skills.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This entry lists the monster’s skill proficiencies, if any. See also “Playing the Game” (“Proficiency”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.717, 0.91, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistances and Vulnerabilities.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These entries list the monster’s Resistances and Vulnerabilities, if any. See also “Resistance” and “Vulnerability.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.764, 0.893, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immunities.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This section lists the monster’s damage and condition Immunities, if any. See also “Immunity.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.81, 0.897, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gear.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster has any equipment that can be given away or retrieved, it’s listed in this entry."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.84, 0.899, 0.886], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This entry lists the monster’s special senses, such as Darkvision, and its Passive Perception. See also “Passive Perception.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.886, 0.882, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Languages.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This entry lists any languages the monster knows."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "188"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 188, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.485, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "CR.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Challenge Rating summarizes the threat a monster poses and is detailed in “Monsters.” The Experience Points characters receive for defeating a monster and its Proficiency Bonus follow. Some creatures that are created by magic have no CR. See also “Challenge Rating” and “Experience Points.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.143, 0.474, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The monster’s traits, if any, are features that are active at all times or in certain situations."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.174, 0.475, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The monster can take these actions in addition to those detailed in this glossary. See also “Playing the Game” (“Actions”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.219, 0.472, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster has Bonus Action options, they are listed in this section."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.473, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reactions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster can take special Reactions, those are listed in this section."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.28, 0.485, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Notation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The entry for a monster’s attack starts by identifying whether the attack is a melee or a ranged attack and then provides the attack roll’s bonus, its reach or range, and what happens on a hit. An attack is against one target unless its entry says otherwise."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.372, 0.488, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throw Effect Notation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If an effect forces a saving throw, the effect’s entry starts by identifying the kind of saving throw required and then provides the save’s DC, a description of which creatures must make the save, and what happens on a failed or a successful save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.464, 0.485, 0.558], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Notation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A stat block usually provides both a static number and a die expression for each instance of damage. For example, an attack might deal 4 (1d4 + 2) damage on a hit. The GM determines whether you use the static number or the die expression in parentheses; you don’t use both."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.564, 0.238, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Study [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.582, 0.484, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take the Study action, you make an Intelligence check to study your memory, a book, a clue, or another source of knowledge and call to mind an important piece of information about it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.643, 0.48, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Areas of Knowledge table suggests which skills are applicable to various areas of knowledge."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.527, 0.069, 0.91, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.696, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Areas of Knowledge"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.527, 0.069, 0.91, 0.343], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Skill</td><td>Areas</td></tr><tr><td>Arcana</td><td>Spells, magic items, eldritch symbols, magical traditions, planes of existence, and certain creatures (Aberrations, Constructs, Elementals, Fey, and Monstrosities)</td></tr><tr><td>History</td><td>Historic events and people, ancient civilizations, wars, and certain creatures (Giants and Humanoids)</td></tr><tr><td>Investigation Nature</td><td>Traps, ciphers, riddles, and gadgetry Terrain, flora, weather, and certain creatures (Beasts, Dragons, Oozes, and Plants)</td></tr><tr><td>Religion</td><td>Deities, religious hierarchies and rites, holy symbols, cults, and certain crea-tures (Celestials, Fiends, and Undead)</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.359, 0.713, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stunned [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.377, 0.898, 0.407], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Stunned condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.407, 0.854, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incapacitated.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.438, 0.89, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You automatically fail Strength and Dexterity saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.469, 0.887, 0.5], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.507, 0.718, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Suffocation [Hazard]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.525, 0.907, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature can hold its breath for a number of minutes equal to 1 plus its Constitution modifier (minimum of 30 seconds) before suffocation begins. When a creature runs out of breath or is choking, it gains 1 Exhaustion level at the end of each of its turns. When a creature can breathe again, it removes all levels of Exhaustion it gained from suffocating."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.656, 0.606, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Surprise"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.673, 0.899, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a creature is caught unawares by the start of combat, that creature is surprised, which causes it to have Disadvantage on its Initiative roll. See also “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.743, 0.624, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Swimming"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.76, 0.903, 0.854], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you’re swimming, each foot of movement costs 1 extra foot (2 extra feet in Difficult Terrain). You ignore this extra cost if you have a Swim Speed and use it to swim. At the GM’s option, moving any distance in rough water might require a successful DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.86, 0.64, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Swim Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.878, 0.909, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Swim Speed can be used to swim without expending the extra movement normally associated with swimming. See also “Swimming” and “Speed.”"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "189"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 189, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.169, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Target"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.483, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target is the creature or object targeted by an attack roll, forced to make a saving throw by an effect, or selected to receive the effects of a spell or another phenomenon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.138, 0.197, 0.155], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.156, 0.489, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathy is a magical ability that allows a creature to communicate mentally with another creature within a specified range. Unless a rule states otherwise, the contacted creature doesn’t need to share a language with the telepath to understand this communication, but the contacted creature must be able to understand at least one language or be telepathic itself to understand."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.279, 0.49, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A telepath doesn’t need to see a contacted creature, and the telepath can start or end the telepathic contact at any time (no action required). Telepathic contact can’t be initiated and is immediately broken if either the telepath or the other creature has the Incapacitated condition. Telepathic contact is also broken if the contacted creature is no longer within the telepathy’s range or if the telepath contacts a different creature within range."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.417, 0.478, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature without telepathy can receive telepathic messages but can’t initiate a telepathic conversation. Once a telepathic conversation starts, the non-telepath can communicate mentally to the telepath until the telepathic connection ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.501, 0.233, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Teleportation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.1, 0.518, 0.479, 0.625], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Teleportation is a special kind of magical transportation. If you teleport, you disappear and reappear elsewhere instantly, without moving through the intervening space. This transportation doesn’t expend movement unless a rule tells you otherwise, and teleportation never provokes Opportunity Attacks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.626, 0.476, 0.703], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you teleport, all the equipment you’re wearing and carrying teleports with you. If you’re touching another creature when you teleport, that creature doesn’t teleport with you unless the teleportation effect says otherwise."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.703, 0.482, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the destination space of your teleportation is occupied by another creature or blocked by a solid obstacle, you instead appear in the nearest unoccupied space of your choice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.763, 0.479, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The description of a teleportation effect tells you if you must see the teleportation’s destination."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.802, 0.304, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Temporary Hit Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.82, 0.487, 0.868], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Temporary Hit Points are granted by certain effects and act as a buffer against losing real Hit Points. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and H"}, {"type": "text", "content": "ealing", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.649, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tremorsense"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.521, 0.069, 0.905, 0.161], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature with Tremorsense can pinpoint the location of creatures and moving objects within a specific range, provided that the creature with Tremorsense and anything it is detecting are both in contact with the same surface (such as the ground, a wall, or a ceiling) or the same liquid."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.161, 0.897, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tremorsense can’t detect creatures or objects in the air, and it doesn’t count as a form of sight."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.2, 0.616, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Truesight"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.217, 0.888, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Truesight, your vision is enhanced within a specified range. Within that range, your vision pierces through the following:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.269, 0.865, 0.3], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can see in normal and magical Darkness."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.3, 0.912, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Invisibility.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You see creatures and objects that have the Invisible condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.331, 0.904, 0.377], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Visual Illusions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Visual illusions appear transparent to you, and you automatically succeed on saving throws against them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.377, 0.908, 0.423], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Transformations.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You discern the true form of any creature or object you see that has been transformed by magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.423, 0.883, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ethereal Plane.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You see into the Ethereal Plane."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.446, 0.675, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unarmed Strike"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.464, 0.907, 0.555], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instead of using a weapon to make a melee attack, you can use a punch, kick, headbutt, or similar forceful blow. In game terms, this is an Unarmed Strike—a melee attack that involves you using your body to damage, grapple, or shove a target within 5 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.556, 0.895, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you use your Unarmed Strike, choose one of the following options for its effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.587, 0.899, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You make an attack roll against the target. Your bonus to the roll equals your Strength modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. On a hit, the target takes Bludgeoning damage equal to 1 plus your Strength modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.663, 0.912, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Grapple.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target must succeed on a Strength or Dexterity saving throw (it chooses which), or it has the Grappled condition. The DC for the saving throw and any escape attempts equals 8 plus your Strength modifier and Proficiency Bonus. This grapple is possible only if the target is no more than one size larger than you and if you have a hand free to grab it. See also “Grappling.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.521, 0.786, 0.913, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shove.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The target must succeed on a Strength or Dexterity saving throw (it chooses which), or you either push it 5 feet away or cause it to have the Prone condition. The DC for the saving throw equals 8 plus your Strength modifier and Proficiency Bonus. This shove is possible only if the target is no more than one size larger than you."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "190"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 190, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.329, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unconscious [Condition]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.475, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you have the Unconscious condition, you experience the following effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.099, 0.474, 0.145], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inert.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have the Incapacitated and Prone conditions, and you drop whatever you’re holding. When this condition ends, you remain Prone."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.116, 0.145, 0.438, 0.16], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed 0.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Speed is 0 and can’t increase."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.161, 0.465, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attacks Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Attack rolls against you have Advantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.191, 0.468, 0.222], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throws Affected.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You automatically fail Strength and Dexterity saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.222, 0.484, 0.267], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Automatic Critical Hits.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any attack roll that hits you is a Critical Hit if the attacker is within 5 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.116, 0.268, 0.476, 0.284], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unaware.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You’re unaware of your surroundings."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.291, 0.273, 0.309], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unoccupied Space"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.309, 0.484, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A space is unoccupied if no creatures are in it and it isn’t completely filled by objects."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.347, 0.247, 0.364], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Utilize [Action]"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.365, 0.476, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You normally interact with an object while doing something else, such as when you draw a sword as part of the Attack action. When an object requires an action for its use, you take the Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.434, 0.223, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vulnerability"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.452, 0.484, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you have Vulnerability to a damage type, damage of that type is doubled against you. Vulnerability is applied only once to an instance of damage. See also “Playing the Game” (“Damage and Healing”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.521, 0.185, 0.538], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.539, 0.452, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A weapon is an object that is in the Simple or Martial weapon category. See also “Equipment” (“Weapons”)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.593, 0.252, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon Attack"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.611, 0.44, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A weapon attack is an attack roll made with a weapon. See also “Weapon.”"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "191"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 191, "blocks": [{"type": "doc_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.107, 0.049, 0.485, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gameplay Toolbox"}], "level": 1}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.094, 0.268, 0.117], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Travel Pace"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.12, 0.486, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A group of characters can travel overland at a Normal, Fast, or Slow pace, as described in “Playing the Game.” During any journey stage, the predominant terrain determines the characters’ maximum travel pace, as shown in the Maximum Pace column of the Travel Terrain table. Certain factors can affect a group’s travel pace."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.234, 0.239, 0.253], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Good Roads"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.1, 0.258, 0.489, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The presence of a good road increases the group’s "}, {"type": "text", "content": "maximum pace by one step (from Slow to Normal or", "styles": ["underline"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " from Normal to Fast)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.312, 0.287, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slower Travelers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.336, 0.488, 0.369], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The group must move at a Slow pace if any group member’s Speed is reduced to half or less of normal."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.374, 0.281, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Extended Travel"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.397, 0.485, 0.492], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Characters can push themselves to travel for more than 8 hours per day, at the risk of tiring. At the end of each additional hour of travel beyond 8 hours, each character must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 10 plus 1 for each hour past 8 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.497, 0.302, 0.517], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Movement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.521, 0.486, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a party can travel at a high Speed for an extended time, as with a spell such as Wind Walk or a magic item such as a Carpet of Flying, translate the party’s Speed into travel rates using these rules:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.608, 0.05, 0.827, 0.066], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Miles per hour", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " = Speed ÷ 10"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.545, 0.066, 0.89, 0.099], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Miles per day", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (Normal pace) = Miles per hour × number of hours traveled (typically 8)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.547, 0.1, 0.888, 0.117], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fast pace", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " = Miles per day × 1⅓ (round down)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.544, 0.117, 0.89, 0.134], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slow pace", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " = Miles per day × 2/3 (round down)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.137, 0.893, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the characters are flying or their special movement allows them to ignore Difficult Terrain, they can move at a Fast pace regardless of the terrain."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.191, 0.617, 0.21], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vehicles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.521, 0.214, 0.902, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Characters traveling in a vehicle use the vehicle’s speed in miles per hour (as shown in “Equipment”) to determine their rate of travel, and they don’t choose a travel pace."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.287, 0.847, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creating a Background"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.521, 0.312, 0.911, 0.42], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A character’s background represents what the character did prior to becoming an adventurer. Creating a unique background or customizing an existing one can reflect the particular theme of your campaign or elements of your world. You can also create a background to help a player craft the story they have in mind for their character."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.419, 0.906, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This section describes, step by step, how you can "}, {"type": "text", "content": "create backgrounds tailored for your world and the", "styles": ["underline"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " heroes in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.473, 0.728, 0.491], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1: Choose Abilities"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.496, 0.908, 0.529], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose three abilities that seem appropriate for the background:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.533, 0.905, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Strength or Dexterity.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These abilities are ideal for a background involving physical exertion."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.565, 0.904, 0.598], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Constitution.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This ability is ideal for a background that involves endurance or long hours of activity."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.103, 0.646, 0.911, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.102, 0.629, 0.227, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Travel Terrain"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.103, 0.646, 0.911, 0.877], "content": "<table><tr><td>Terrain</td><td>Maximum Pace</td><td>Encounter Distance</td><td>Foraging DC</td><td>Navigation DC</td><td>Search DC</td></tr><tr><td>Arctic</td><td>Fast*</td><td>6d6×10 feet</td><td>20</td><td>10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Coastal</td><td>Normal</td><td>2d10×10 feet</td><td>10</td><td>5</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Desert</td><td>Normal</td><td>6d6×10 feet</td><td>20</td><td>10</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Forest</td><td>Normal</td><td>2d8×10 feet</td><td>10</td><td>15</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Grassland</td><td>Fast</td><td>6d6×10 feet</td><td>15</td><td>5</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Hill</td><td>Normal</td><td>2d10×10 feet</td><td>15</td><td>10</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Mountain</td><td>Slow</td><td>4d10×10 feet</td><td>20</td><td>15</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Swamp</td><td>Slow</td><td>2d8×10 feet</td><td>10</td><td>15</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Underdark</td><td>Normal</td><td>2d6×10 feet</td><td>20</td><td>10</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Urban</td><td>Normal</td><td>2d6×10 feet</td><td>20</td><td>15</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Waterborne</td><td>Special†</td><td>6d6×10 feet</td><td>15</td><td>10</td><td>15</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.101, 0.883, 0.623, 0.897], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "*Appropriate equipment (such as skis) is necessary to keep up a Fast pace in Arctic terrain."}]}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.101, 0.896, 0.667, 0.91], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "†Characters’ rate of travel while waterborne depends on the vehicle carrying them; see “Vehicles.”"}]}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "192"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 192, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.485, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Intelligence or Wisdom.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " One or both abilities are ideal for a background that focuses on cerebral or spiritual matters."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.096, 0.47, 0.128], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Charisma.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This ability is ideal for a background "}, {"type": "text", "content": "that involves performance or social interaction.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.134, 0.287, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2: Choose a Feat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.158, 0.479, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose one feat from the Origin category. See “Origin Feats” for examples of Origin feats."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.196, 0.405, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "3: Choose Skill Proficiencies"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.22, 0.475, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose two skills appropriate for the background. There needn’t be a relationship between the skill proficiencies a background grants and the ability scores it increases."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.289, 0.411, 0.308], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "4: Choose a Tool Proficiency"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.313, 0.459, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose one tool used in the practice of the background or often associated with it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.351, 0.335, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "5: Choose Equipment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.375, 0.479, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assemble a package of equipment worth 50 GP (including unspent gold). Don’t include Martial weapons or armor, as characters get them from their class choices."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.447, 0.376, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curses and Magical Contagions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.497, 0.488, 0.558], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A curse is a magical burden that lasts for a specified time or until it is ended by some means. A magical contagion is an adverse effect of magical origin that is contagious by definition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.558, 0.488, 0.59], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The following sections discuss curses and magical", "styles": ["underline"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " contagions in detail."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.597, 0.182, 0.614], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.619, 0.461, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A curse typically takes one of the forms detailed below."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.659, 0.235, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bestow Curse"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.676, 0.488, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The simplest curses are created by the Bestow Curse spell. The effects of such curses are limited and can be ended by the Remove Curse spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.722, 0.468, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bestow Curse provides useful benchmarks for gauging the potency of other curses. A curse that lasts for 1 minute equates to a level 3 spell, while one that lasts until dispelled equates to a level 9 spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.807, 0.27, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cursed Creatures"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.824, 0.489, 0.873], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some monsters are associated with curses, whether as part of their origins or due to their ability to spread curses—werewolves being a prime example."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.902, 0.129], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You decide how a spell like Remove Curse affects a creature with accursed origins. For example, you might decide that a mummy was created through a curse and it can be destroyed permanently only by casting Remove Curse on its corpse."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.135, 0.709, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cursed Magic Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.153, 0.904, 0.2], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cursed magic items are created deliberately or originate as the result of supernatural events. Such items are detailed in “Magic Items.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.206, 0.685, 0.223], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Narrative Curses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.224, 0.91, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A curse might manifest during an adventure when a creature’s violation of a taboo warrants supernatural punishment, such as breaking a vow, defiling a tomb, or murdering an innocent. Such a curse can have any effects you design, or it might be a customized version of another type of curse discussed in this section."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.332, 0.908, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature affected by such a curse should know why they’re being punished and be able to learn how to end their curse, likely by symbolically righting the wrong they committed. How a spell like Remove Curse affects a curse that’s part of your adventure is up to you—the spell might merely sup press the effects of the curse for a time. Regardless, narrative curses should feel like rare, potent magic rooted in the lore of your campaign."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.478, 0.73, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Environmental Curses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.495, 0.896, 0.556], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some locations are so suffused with evil that anyone who lingers there is burdened with a curse. Demonic Possession is one example of an environmental curse."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.557, 0.907, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Demonic Possession.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Demonic Possession arises from the chaos and evil of the Abyss and commonly besets creatures that interact with demonic objects or linger in desecrated locations, where demonic spirits await victims."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.634, 0.9, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that becomes the target of Demonic Possession must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma saving throw or be possessed by a bodiless demonic entity. Whenever the possessed creature rolls a 1 on a D20 Test, the demonic entity takes control of the creature and determines the creature’s behavior thereafter. At the end of each of the possessed creature’s later turns, the creature makes a DC 15 Charisma saving throw, regaining control of itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.786, 0.896, 0.865], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After finishing a Long Rest, a creature with Demonic Possession makes a DC 15 Charisma saving throw. On a successful save, the effect ends on the creature. A Dispel Evil and Good spell or any magic that removes a curse also ends the effect on it."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "193"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 193, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.313, 0.071], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magical Contagions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.075, 0.488, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alchemists, potion brewers, and areas of wild magic are credited with creating the first magical contagions. An outbreak of such a contagion can form the basis of an adventure as characters search for a cure and try to stop the contagion’s spread."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.16, 0.312, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rest and Recuperation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.177, 0.481, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a creature infected with a magical contagion spends 3 days recuperating—engaging in no activities that would interrupt a Long Rest—the creature makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw at the end of the recuperation period. On a successful save, the creature has Advantage on saving throws to fight off the magical contagion for the next 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.309, 0.292, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example Contagions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.481, 0.389], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The following examples show how magical contagions can work. Feel free to alter the saving throw DCs, effects, and other characteristics of these contagions to suit your campaign."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.395, 0.227, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cackle Fever"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.413, 0.24, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magical Contagion"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.432, 0.472, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cheaply made potions and elixirs are sometimes tainted by Cackle Fever, which affects Humanoids only (gnomes are strangely immune). A creature suffers the following effects 1d4 days after infection:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.515, 0.486, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fever.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The creature gains 1 Exhaustion level, which lasts until the contagion ends on the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.545, 0.484, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Uncontrollable Laughter.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While the creature has the Exhaustion condition, the creature makes a DC 13 Constitution saving throw each time it takes damage other than Psychic damage. On a failed save, the creature takes 5 (1d10) Psychic damage and has the Incapacitated condition as it laughs uncontrollably. At the end of each of its turns, the creature repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.707, 0.479, 0.783], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting the Contagion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " At the end of each Long Rest, an infected creature makes a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. After the creature succeeds on three of these saves, the contagion ends on it, and the creature is immune to Cackle Fever for 1 year."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.783, 0.478, 0.907], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spreading the Contagion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any Humanoid (other than a gnome) that starts its turn within a 10-foot Emanation originating from a creature infected with Cackle Fever must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or also become infected with the contagion. On a successful save, the Humanoid can’t catch the contagion from that particular infected creature for the next 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.651, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sewer Plague"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.661, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magical Contagion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.912, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fouled potions and alchemical waste can give rise to Sewer Plague, which incubates in sewers and refuse heaps and is sometimes transmitted by creatures that dwell in such areas, including otyu ghs and rats. Any Humanoid that is wounded by a creature that carries the contagion or that comes into contact with contaminated filth or offal must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or become infected with Sewer Plague. A creature suffers the following effects 1d4 days after infection:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.248, 0.876, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fatigue.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The creature gains 1 Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.525, 0.265, 0.902, 0.31], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weakness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While the creature has any Exhaustion levels, it regains only half the normal number of Hit Points from spending Hit Point Dice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.31, 0.904, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Restlessness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While the creature has any Exhaustion levels, finishing a Long Rest neither restores lost Hit Points nor reduces the creature’s Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.378, 0.907, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting the Contagion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Daily at dawn, an infected creature makes a DC 11 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature gains 1 Exhaustion level as its fatigue worsens. On a successful save, the creature’s Exhaustion level decreases by 1. If the creature’s Exhaustion level is reduced to 0, the contagion ends on the creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.494, 0.615, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sight Rot"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.511, 0.661, 0.527], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magical Contagion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.531, 0.911, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any Beast or Humanoid that drinks water tainted by Sight Rot must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Blinded condition until the contagion ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.593, 0.91, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fighting the Contagion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Magic such as a Heal or Lesser Restoration spell ends the contagion immediately. A character who is proficient with an Herbalism Kit can use it to create one dose of nonmagical ointment, which takes 1 hour. When applied to the eyes of a creature suffering from Sight Rot, the ointment suppresses the contagion on that creature for 24 hours. If the contagion is suppressed in this way for a total of 72 hours (requiring three doses and applications of the ointment), the contagion ends on the creature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.761, 0.905, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spreading the Contagion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any Humanoid that makes skin contact with a creature infected with Sight Rot must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or also become infected with the contagion. On a successful save, the Humanoid can’t catch the contagion from that particular infected creature for the next 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.03, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "194"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 194, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.412, 0.074], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Environmental Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.077, 0.241, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deep Water"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.1, 0.488, 0.195], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Swimming through deep water (more than 100 feet deep) presents additional challenges because of the water’s pressure and cold temperature. After each hour of swimming in deep water, a creature that lacks a Swim Speed must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.2, 0.258, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Extreme Cold"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.224, 0.487, 0.319], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the temperature is 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower, a creature exposed to the extreme cold must succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw at the end of each hour or gain 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures that have Resistance or Immunity to Cold damage automatically succeed on the save."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.324, 0.259, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Extreme Heat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.347, 0.488, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the temperature is 100 degrees Fahrenheit or higher, a creature exposed to the extreme heat and without access to drinkable water must succeed on a Constitution saving throw at the end of each hour or gain 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 5 for the first hour and increases by 1 for each additional hour. Creatures wearing Medium or Heavy armor have Disadvantage on the save. Creatures that have Resistance or Immunity to Fire damage automatically succeed on the save."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.508, 0.244, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Frigid Water"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.532, 0.484, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature can be immersed in frigid water for a number of minutes equal to its Constitution score before suffering any ill effects. Each additional minute spent in frigid water requires the creature to succeed on a DC 10 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level. Creatures with Resistance or Immunity to Cold damage automatically succeed on the save, as do creatures that are naturally adapted to living in ice-cold water."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.739, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Heavy Precipitation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.522, 0.074, 0.908, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Everything within an area of heavy rain or heavy snowfall is Lightly Obscured, and creatures in the area have Disadvantage on all Wisdom (Perception) checks. Heavy rain also extinguishes open flames."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.143, 0.673, 0.163], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "High Altitude"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.167, 0.909, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traveling at altitudes of 10,000 feet or higher above sea level is taxing for most creatures because of the reduced amount of oxygen in the air. Each hour such a creature spends traveling at high altitude counts as 2 hours for the purpose of determining how long that creature can travel (see “Travel Pace”)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.26, 0.902, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures can become acclimated to a high altitude by spending 30 days or more at this elevation. Creatures can’t become acclimated to elevations above 20,000 feet unless they are native to such environments."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.344, 0.655, 0.364], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slippery Ice"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.367, 0.91, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slippery ice is Difficult Terrain. A creature that moves onto slippery ice for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.436, 0.666, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Strong Wind"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.46, 0.903, 0.522], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Strong wind imposes Disadvantage on ranged attack rolls with weapons. It also extinguishes open flames and disperses fog. A flying creature in a strong wind must land at the end of its turn or fall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.523, 0.909, 0.569], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A strong wind in a desert can create a sandstorm that imposes Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.575, 0.616, 0.593], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thin Ice"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.599, 0.907, 0.692], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thin ice has a weight tolerance of 3d10 × 10 pounds per 10-foot-square area. Whenever the total weight on an area of thin ice exceeds its tolerance, the ice in that area breaks. All creatures on broken ice fall through. Below the ice is frigid water (see “Frigid Water” above)."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "195"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 195, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.426, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fear and Mental Stress"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.077, 0.489, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Due to the nature of their vocation, adventurers tend to be less susceptible to fear and mental stress than common folk. Whereas a farmer might flee in terror from a bear or an apparition, adventurers are made of sterner stuff. That said, certain creatures and game effects can terrify or fray the mind of even the most stalwart adventurer."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.183, 0.482, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you plan to use any of these rules, discuss them with your players at the start of the campaign."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.222, 0.234, 0.24], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fear Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.245, 0.49, 0.34], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever the characters encounter something that is supernaturally frightful, use the Frightened condition as the baseline effect. Fear effects typically require a Wisdom saving throw, with a save DC based on how terrifying the situation is. The Sample Fear DCs table provides some examples."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.351, 0.251, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sample Fear DCs"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.105, 0.369, 0.487, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.105, 0.369, 0.487, 0.525], "content": "<table><tr><td>Example</td><td>Save DC</td></tr><tr><td>When the characters open a sarcophagus, a harmless yet terrifying apparition appears.</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>A character triggers a magical trap that creates an illusory manifestation of that character&#x27;s worst fears, visible only to that character.</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>A portal to the Abyss opens, revealing a nightmarish realm of torment and slaughter.</td><td>20</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.533, 0.481, 0.579], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Typically, a Frightened creature repeats the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.58, 0.484, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At your discretion, a Frightened creature might be subject to other effects as long as the Frightened condition lasts. Consider these examples:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.632, 0.485, 0.678], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• The Frightened creature must take the Dash action on each of its turns and uses its movement to get farther away from the source of its fear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.679, 0.484, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Attack rolls against the Frightened creature have Advantage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.709, 0.474, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Frightened creature can do only one of the following on each of its turns: move, take an action, or take a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.752, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mental Stress Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.075, 0.907, 0.121], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a character is subjected to an effect that causes intense mental stress, Psychic damage is the best way to emulate that effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.121, 0.91, 0.245], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Sample Mental Stress Effects table provides a few examples of such effects, with suggested saving throw DCs and damage. Mental stress can usually be resisted with a successful Wisdom save, but sometimes an Intelligence or Charisma save is more appropriate. On a successful save, a character might take half as much damage instead of no damage, at your discretion."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.257, 0.769, 0.273], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sample Mental Stress Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.527, 0.276, 0.908, 0.46], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.527, 0.276, 0.908, 0.46], "content": "<table><tr><td>Example</td><td>Save DC</td><td>Psychic Damage</td></tr><tr><td>A character ingests a hallucinogenic substance that distorts the charac- ter&#x27;s perception of reality.</td><td>10</td><td>Id6</td></tr><tr><td>A character touches a fiendish idol that tears at the character&#x27;s mind, threatening to shatter it.</td><td>15</td><td>3d6</td></tr><tr><td>A magical trap flings a character into the Far Realm until the end of that character&#x27;s next turn.</td><td>20</td><td>9d6</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.477, 0.688, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Prolonged Effects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.495, 0.898, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Exposure to mental stress can cause prolonged effects. Consider the following possibilities."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.526, 0.904, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Short-Term Effects.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The character has the Frightened, Incapacitated, or Stunned condition for 1d10 minutes. This condition might be accompanied by alarming behavior or hallucinations. These effects can be suppressed with the Calm Emotions spell or removed by the Lesser Restoration spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.617, 0.908, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Long-Term Effects.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The character has Disadvantage on some or all ability checks for 1d10 × 10 hours, stemming from an unwillingness or inability to exert a particular set of abilities. The character might feel enervated and unable to exert much Strength, for example, or become so suspicious of others that Charisma checks are more difficult. These effects can be suppressed with the Calm Emotions spell or removed by the Lesser Restoration spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.77, 0.91, 0.833], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Indefinite Effects.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An indefinite effect is a longterm effect (see above) that lasts until removed by a Greater Restoration spell. It can be suppressed by a Calm Emotions spell."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "196"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 196, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.2, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.076, 0.489, 0.124], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Given their insidious and deadly nature, poisons are a favorite tool among assassins and evil creatures. Poisons come in the following four types:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.13, 0.474, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Contact.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Contact poison can be smeared on an object and remains potent until it is touched or washed off. A creature that touches contact poison with exposed skin suffers its effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.191, 0.487, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ingested.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature must swallow an entire dose of ingested poison to suffer its effects. The dose can be delivered in food or a liquid. You may decide that a partial dose has a reduced effect, such as allowing Advantage on the saving throw or dealing only half as much damage on a failed save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.283, 0.489, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inhaled.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Poisonous powders and gases take effect when inhaled. Blowing the powder or releasing the gas subjects creatures in a 5-foot Cube to its effect. The resulting cloud dissipates immediately afterward. Holding one’s breath is ineffective against inhaled poisons, as they affect nasal membranes, tear ducts, and other parts of the body."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.39, 0.485, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Injury.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Injury poison can be applied as a Bonus Action to a weapon, a piece of ammunition, or similar object. The poison remains potent until delivered through a wound or washed off. A creature that takes Piercing or Slashing damage from an object coated with the poison is exposed to its effects."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.505, 0.299, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Purchasing Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.1, 0.528, 0.489, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In some settings, laws prohibit the possession and use of poison, but an illicit dealer or unscrupulous apothecary might keep a hidden stash. Characters with criminal contacts might be able to acquire poison easily. Other characters might have to make extensive inquiries and pay bribes before they acquire the poison they seek."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.643, 0.3, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Harvesting Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.667, 0.489, 0.839], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A character can attempt to harvest poison from a venomous creature that is dead or has the Incapacitated condition. The effort takes 1d6 minutes, after which the character makes a DC 20 Intelligence (Nature) check using a Poisoner’s Kit. On a successful check, the character harvests enough poison for a single dose, and no additional poison can be harvested from that creature. On a failed check, the character is unable to extract any poison. If the character fails the check by 5 or more, the character is subjected to the creature’s poison."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.693, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sample Poisons"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.075, 0.912, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example poisons are detailed here in alphabetical order. Each poison’s description includes the suggested price for a single dose of the poison, its type (contact, ingested, inhaled, or injury), and a descrip tion of the poison’s debilitating effects."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.159, 0.76, 0.177], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assassin’s Blood (150 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.177, 0.642, 0.193], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ingested Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.197, 0.91, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Assassin’s Blood makes a DC 10 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 6 (1d12) Poison damage and has the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.282, 0.794, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Burnt Othur Fumes (500 GP) Inhaled Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.32, 0.912, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Burnt Othur Fumes must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) Poison damage, and it must repeat the save at the start of each of its turns. On each successive failed save, the creature takes 3 (1d6) Poison damage. After three successful saves, the poison ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.434, 0.752, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crawler Mucus (200 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.453, 0.637, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Contact Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.472, 0.901, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Crawler Mucus must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute. The creature also has the Paralyzed condition while Poisoned in this way. The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.587, 0.765, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Essence of Ether (300 GP) Inhaled Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.624, 0.901, 0.733], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Essence of Ether must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 8 hours. The creature also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned in this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature takes an action to shake it awake."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.74, 0.674, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Malice (250 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.758, 0.635, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inhaled Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.778, 0.89, 0.841], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Malice must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. The creature also has the Blinded condition while Poisoned in this way."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.847, 0.765, 0.865], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Midnight Tears (1,500 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.865, 0.642, 0.881], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ingested Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.884, 0.894, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that ingests Midnight Tears suffers no effect until the stroke of midnight. Any effect that"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.031, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "197"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 197, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.48, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "ends the Poisoned condition neutralizes this poison. If the poison hasn’t been neutralized before midnight, the creature makes a DC 17 Constitution saving throw, taking 31 (9d6) Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.15, 0.305, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oil of Taggit (400 GP) Contact Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.187, 0.479, 0.267], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Oil of Taggit must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 24 hours. The creature also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned in this way. It wakes up if it takes damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.272, 0.315, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pale Tincture (250 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.291, 0.22, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ingested Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.309, 0.486, 0.45], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Pale Tincture must succeed on a DC 16 Constitution saving throw or take 3 (1d6) Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition. The Poisoned creature repeats the save every 24 hours, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage on a failed save. The damage the poison deals can’t be healed by any means while the creature remains Poisoned. After seven successful saves against the poison, the creature is no longer Poisoned."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.456, 0.399, 0.474], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Purple Worm Poison (2,000 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.474, 0.202, 0.49], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Injury Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.493, 0.49, 0.556], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Purple Worm Poison makes a DC 21 Constitution saving throw, taking 35 (10d6) Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.562, 0.335, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Serpent Venom (200 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.581, 0.202, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Injury Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.6, 0.475, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Serpent Venom must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw, taking"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.894, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "10 (3d6) Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.088, 0.738, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spider’s Sting (200 GP) Injury Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.126, 0.908, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Spider’s Sting must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. If the creature fails the save by 5 or more, the creature also has the Unconscious condition while Poisoned in this way. The creature wakes up if it takes damage or if another creature takes an action to shake it awake."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.242, 0.68, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Torpor (600 GP)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.26, 0.642, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ingested Poison"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.279, 0.911, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Torpor poison must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 4d6 hours. The creature’s Speed is halved while the creature is Poisoned in this way."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.363, 0.729, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Truth Serum (150 GP) Ingested Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.401, 0.901, 0.465], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Truth Serum must succeed on a DC 11 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. The Poisoned creature can’t knowingly communicate a lie."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.47, 0.769, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wyvern Poison (1,200 GP) Injury Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.508, 0.908, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature subjected to Wyvern Poison makes a DC 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 24 (7d6) Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "198"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 198, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.052, 0.185, 0.075], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traps"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.076, 0.479, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traps should be used sparingly, lest they lose their charm. A hidden pit can be a fun surprise, but too many traps in an adventure can lead players to become overly cautious, which slows down the game."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.138, 0.479, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The best traps are fleeting distractions that skilled characters can overcome in a short amount of time or deadly puzzles that require quick thinking and teamwork to overcome. Traps that are un"}, {"type": "text", "content": "detectable and inescapable are rarely fun.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.222, 0.265, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parts of a Trap"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.246, 0.455, 0.278], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The description of a trap includes the following parts after the trap’s name:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.283, 0.49, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Severity and Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A trap is designated as a nuisance or as deadly for characters of certain levels. A nuisance trap is unlikely to seriously harm characters of the indicated levels, whereas a deadly trap can grievously damage characters of the indicated levels."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.376, 0.49, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Traps are often set to go off when a creature enters an area or touches an object. Examples of triggers include stepping on a pressure plate, crossing a trip wire, turning a doorknob, or using the wrong key in a lock."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.452, 0.489, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Some traps have durations expressed in rounds, minutes, or hours. Others specify that their effects last until the trap is destroyed or dispelled. If a trap’s duration is instantaneous, its effect is resolved instantly. If a trap resets after activating, that fact is noted in this entry. A trap is otherwise inert after activation."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.566, 0.486, 0.629], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Use caution when introducing a trap to characters of a level lower than the trap’s level range. A trap that is a nuisance at one level range could be deadly "}, {"type": "text", "content": "to characters of a lower level range.", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.635, 0.265, 0.654], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example Traps"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.659, 0.414, 0.675], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traps are presented in alphabetical order."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.682, 0.252, 0.7], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Collapsing Roof"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.7, 0.282, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deadly Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.381, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature crosses a trip wire "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.757, 0.479, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This trap uses a trip wire to collapse an unstable section of ceiling. The trip wire is 3 inches off the ground and stretches between two weak supports that topple when the trip wire is pulled."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.819, 0.49, 0.913], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first creature that crosses the trip wire causes the supports to topple and the unstable section of ceiling to collapse. Each creature beneath the unstable section of ceiling must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 11 (2d10) Bludgeoning damage on a failed save or half as much damage"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.904, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "on a successful one. Rubble from the collapse turns the trapped area into Difficult Terrain."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.082, 0.91, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Search action, a creature can examine the trapped area and make a DC 11 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the trip wire and the unstable section of ceiling on a successful check. Once detected, the trip wire can be easily cut or avoided (no ability check required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.173, 0.91, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the damage and the save DC, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.526, 0.224, 0.909, 0.298], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.526, 0.224, 0.909, 0.298], "content": "<table><tr><td>Levels</td><td>Bludgeoning Damage</td><td>Save DC</td></tr><tr><td>5-10</td><td>22 (4d10)</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>11-16</td><td>55 (10d10)</td><td>17</td></tr><tr><td>17-20</td><td>99 (18d10)</td><td>19</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.309, 0.63, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Falling Net"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.326, 0.719, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nuisance Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.346, 0.803, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger: A creature crosses a trip wire Duration: Instantaneous"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.384, 0.903, 0.445], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A falling net trap uses a trip wire to release a weighted, 10-foot-square Net suspended from the ceiling. The trip wire is 3 inches off the ground and stretches between two columns or trees."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.445, 0.907, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first creature that crosses the trip wire causes the Net to fall on it. The target must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw or have the Restrained condition until it escapes. The target succeeds automatically if it’s Huge or larger. A creature can take an action to make a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check, freeing itself or another creature within its reach from the Net on a successful check."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.568, 0.908, 0.66], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Search action, a creature can examine the trapped area and make a DC 11 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the trip wire and the suspended Net on a successful check. Once detected, the trip wire can be easily cut or avoided (no ability check required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.66, 0.902, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Destroy the Net.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reducing the Net to 0 Hit Points frees any creature trapped in it (see “Adventuring Gear” for the Net’s statistics)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.706, 0.904, 0.782], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Set the Trap.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature that has Thieves’ Tools and all the trap’s components (including a Net) can try to set a falling net trap, doing so with a successful DC 13 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check. Each attempt to set this trap takes 10 minutes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.782, 0.912, 0.86], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the weight of the Net, which increases the save DC and the DC of the Strength (Athletics) check as follows: DC 12 at levels 5–10, DC 14 at levels 11–16, or DC 16 at levels 17–20."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.867, 0.704, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire-Casting Statue"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.884, 0.704, 0.901], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deadly Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.904, 0.869, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature moves onto a pressure plate"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.03, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "199"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 199, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.468, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous, and the trap resets at the start of the next turn"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.474, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a creature moves onto this trap’s pressure plate for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, a nearby statue exhales a 15-foot Cone of magical flame. The statue can look like anything, such as a dragon or a wizard. Each creature in the Cone must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 11 (2d10) Fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.211, 0.49, 0.38], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Detect Magic spell reveals an aura of Evocation magic around the statue. As a Search action, a creature within 5 feet of the statue can examine it and make a DC 10 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting a tiny glyph on the statue on a successful check. Once the glyph is found, a character can take a Study action to examine it and make a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check, ascertaining that the glyph means “fire” on a successful check. As an action, a character can use a sharp tool to deface the glyph, which disarms the trap."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.38, 0.49, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Search action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pressure plate and make a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the pressure plate on a successful check. Wedging an Iron Spike or similar object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from triggering."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.471, 0.488, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the damage and the area of effect, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.522, 0.488, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.522, 0.488, 0.597], "content": "<table><tr><td>Levels</td><td>Fire Damage</td><td>Area of Effect</td></tr><tr><td>5-10</td><td>22 (4d10)</td><td>30-foot Cone</td></tr><tr><td>11-16</td><td>55 (10d10)</td><td>60-foot Cone</td></tr><tr><td>17-20</td><td>99 (18d10)</td><td>120-foot Cone</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.606, 0.205, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hidden Pit"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.624, 0.296, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nuisance Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.644, 0.412, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature moves onto the pit’s lid "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.681, 0.482, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This 10-foot-deep pit has a hinged lid constructed from material identical to the surrounding floor. When a creature moves onto the lid, it swings open like a trapdoor, causing the creature to fall into the pit. The lid remains open thereafter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.759, 0.452, 0.789], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that falls into the pit takes 3 (1d6) Bludgeoning damage from the fall."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.79, 0.481, 0.928], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Study action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pit’s lid and make a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check, detecting the pit on a successful check. Once the pit is detected, an Iron Spike or a similar object can be wedged between the pit’s lid and the surrounding floor to prevent the lid from opening, thereby making it safe to cross. The cover can also be held shut using Arcane Lock or similar magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.908, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Escape.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature needs a Climb Speed, climbing gear, or magic such as Spider Climb to scale the pit’s smooth walls. You can make the pit easier to escape by adding cracks in the walls big enough to serve as handholds and footholds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.127, 0.91, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the pit’s depth and damage, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.525, 0.177, 0.909, 0.252], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.525, 0.177, 0.909, 0.252], "content": "<table><tr><td>Levels</td><td>Pit Depth</td><td>Bludgeoning Damage</td></tr><tr><td>5-10</td><td>30 feet</td><td>10 (3d6)</td></tr><tr><td>11-16</td><td>60 feet</td><td>21 (6d6)</td></tr><tr><td>17-20</td><td>120 feet</td><td>42 (12d6)</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.263, 0.669, 0.279], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poisoned Darts"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.28, 0.704, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deadly Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.3, 0.892, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature moves onto a pressure plate "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous, and the trap resets at the start of the next turn if it has activated fewer than three times"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.367, 0.886, 0.458], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a creature moves onto this trap’s pressure plate for the first time on a turn, poisoned darts shoot from tubes embedded in the surrounding walls. The holes that house these tubes are obscured by dust and cobwebs or skillfully hidden amid bas-reliefs, murals, or frescoes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.459, 0.905, 0.505], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each creature in the darts’ path must succeed on a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw or be struck by 1d3 darts, taking 3 (1d6) Poison damage per dart."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.506, 0.911, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Search action, a creature can examine the walls and make a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the holes on a successful check. Plugging all the holes with wax, cloth, or detritus prevents the darts from firing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.582, 0.912, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Search action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pressure plate and make a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the pressure plate on a successful check. Wedging an Iron Spike or a similar object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from triggering."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.674, 0.91, 0.736], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing each dart’s Poison damage as follows: 7 (2d6) at levels 5–10, 14 (4d6) at levels 11–16, or 24 (7d6) at levels 17–20."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.743, 0.682, 0.759], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poisoned Needle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.76, 0.719, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nuisance Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.78, 0.898, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature opens the trap’s lock improperly or fails to disarm the trap"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.81, 0.709, 0.825], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.832, 0.902, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A poisoned needle is hidden in a lock. When a creature opens the lock with any object other than the proper key, the needle springs out and stabs the creature. The creature makes a DC 11 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 5 (1d10) Poison damage and has the Poisoned"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "200"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 200, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.481, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "condition for 1 hour. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.081, 0.437, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Avoid.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The trap doesn’t trigger if the lock is opened using a Knock spell or similar magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.113, 0.489, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Search action, a creature can examine the trapped lock and make a DC 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, detecting the needle on a successful check. Once the trap is detected, a character can take an action to try to disarm the trap, doing so with a successful DC 15 Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check. On a failed check, the creature triggers the trap."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.234, 0.488, 0.281], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the damage and the save DC, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.286, 0.488, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.286, 0.488, 0.36], "content": "<table><tr><td>Levels</td><td>Poison Damage</td><td>Save DC</td></tr><tr><td>5-10</td><td>II (2d10)</td><td>13</td></tr><tr><td>11-16</td><td>22 (4d10)</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>17-20</td><td>55 (10d10)</td><td>17</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.37, 0.227, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rolling Stone"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.388, 0.472, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deadly Trap (Levels 11–16) or Nuisance Trap (Levels 17–20)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.423, 0.448, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature moves onto a pressure plate "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Until the stone stops rolling"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.461, 0.477, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a creature moves onto a hidden pressure plate, a 5-foot-radius orb of solid stone is released from a secret compartment and begins to roll. The stone and all creatures nearby roll Initiative; the stone gets a +8 bonus on its Initiative roll."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.537, 0.484, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On its turn, the stone moves 60 feet in one direction, changing course if redirected by an obstacle. The stone can move through creatures’ spaces, and creatures can move through the stone’s space, treating it as Difficult Terrain. Whenever the stone enters a creature’s space for the first time on a turn or a creature enters the stone’s space while the stone is rolling, that creature must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 55 (10d10) Bludgeoning damage and have the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.691, 0.469, 0.767], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The stone stops when it hits a wall or similar barrier. It can’t go around corners, but creative dungeon builders incorporate curving turns into nearby passages that allow the stone to keep moving."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.767, 0.479, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Study action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pressure plate and make a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check, deducing the pressure plate’s function on a successful check. Wedging an Iron Spike or a similar object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from triggering."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.894, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Destroy the Stone.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The stone is a Large object that has AC 17, HP 100, a Damage Threshold of 10, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.097, 0.912, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slow the Stone.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As an action, a creature can try to slow down the stone with a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check. If the check is successful, the distance the stone moves on its turn is reduced by 15 feet. If that distance drops to 0, it stops moving and is no longer a threat."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.196, 0.622, 0.213], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spiked Pit"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.214, 0.704, 0.23], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deadly Trap (Levels 1–4)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.233, 0.833, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trigger:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature moves onto the pit’s lid "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Duration:", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Instantaneous"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.271, 0.91, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A 10-foot-deep pit has a hinged lid constructed from material identical to the surrounding floor. When a creature moves onto the lid, it swings open like a trapdoor, causing the creature to fall into the pit, which has sharpened wooden or metal spikes at the bottom. The lid remains open thereafter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.364, 0.879, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that falls into the pit lands at the bottom and takes 3 (1d6) Bludgeoning damage from the fall plus 9 (2d8) Piercing damage from the spikes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.425, 0.907, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Detect and Disarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Study action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pit’s lid and make a DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check, detecting the pit on a successful check. Once the hidden pit is detected, an Iron Spike or a similar object can be wedged between the pit’s lid and the surrounding floor to prevent the lid from opening, thereby making it safe to cross. The cover can also be held shut using an Arcane Lock spell or similar m"}, {"type": "text", "content": "agic", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.578, 0.907, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Escape.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A creature needs a Climb Speed, climbing gear, or magic such as a Spider Climb spell to scale the pit’s smooth walls. You can make the pit easier to escape by adding cracks in the walls big enough to serve as handholds and footholds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.655, 0.91, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "At Higher Levels.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can scale the trap for higher levels by increasing the pit’s depth and damage, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.526, 0.706, 0.908, 0.828], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.526, 0.706, 0.908, 0.828], "content": "<table><tr><td>Levels</td><td>Pit Depth</td><td>Damage</td></tr><tr><td>5-10</td><td>30 feet</td><td>10 (3d6) Bludgeoning plus 13 (3d8) Piercing</td></tr><tr><td>11-16</td><td>60 feet</td><td>21 (6d6) Bludgeoning plus 36 (8d8) Piercing</td></tr><tr><td>17-20</td><td>120 feet</td><td>42 (I2d6) Bludgeoning plus 57 (13d8) Piercing</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "201"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 201, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.384, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combat Encounters"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.076, 0.479, 0.109], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The following features can make a combat encounter more interesting or challenging:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.114, 0.491, 0.19], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Changes in Elevation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Terrain features that provide a change of elevation (such as stacks of empty crates, ledges, and balconies) reward clever positioning and encourage characters to jump, climb, fly, or teleport."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.191, 0.476, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Defensive Positions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Enemies in hard-to-reach locations or defensive positions force characters who normally attack at range to move around."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.237, 0.468, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mixed Monster Groups.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When different types of monsters work together, they can combine their abilities—just like characters with different classes and origins. A diverse force is more powerful."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.314, 0.487, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reasons to Move.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use features that encourage characters and their enemies to move around, such as chandeliers, kegs of gunpowder or oil, and rolling stone traps."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.382, 0.413, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combat Encounter Difficulty"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.406, 0.48, 0.438], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Use the following guidelines to create a combat encounter of a desired level of difficulty."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.445, 0.347, 0.461], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Step 1: Choose a Difficulty"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.463, 0.468, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Three categories describe the range of encounter difficulty:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.499, 0.479, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Low Difficulty.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An encounter of low difficulty is likely to have one or two scary moments for the players, but their characters should emerge victorious with no casualties. One or more of them might need to use healing resources, however. As a rough guideline, a single monster generally presents a low-difficulty challenge for a party of four characters whose level equals the monster’s Challenge Rating."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.638, 0.488, 0.714], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Moderate Difficulty.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Absent healing and other resources, an encounter of moderate difficulty could go badly for the adventurers. Weaker characters might get taken out of the fight, and there’s a slim chance that one or more characters might die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.714, 0.476, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "High Difficulty.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A high-difficulty encounter could be lethal for one or more characters. To survive it, the characters will need smart tactics, quick thinking, and maybe even a little luck."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.783, 0.425, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Step 2: Determine Your XP Budget"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.801, 0.481, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using the XP Budget per Character table, cross-reference the party’s level with the desired encounter difficulty. Multiply the number in the table by the number of characters in the party to get your XP budget for the encounter."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.525, 0.075, 0.91, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.054, 0.741, 0.071], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "XP Budget per Character"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.525, 0.075, 0.91, 0.496], "content": "<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Party&#x27;s Level</td><td colspan=\"3\">-Encounter Difficulty</td></tr><tr><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>50</td><td>75</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>100</td><td>150</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>150</td><td>225</td><td>400</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>250</td><td>375</td><td>500</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>500</td><td>750</td><td>1,100</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>600</td><td>1,000</td><td>1,400</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>750</td><td>1,300</td><td>1,700</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>1,000</td><td>1,700</td><td>2,100</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>1,300</td><td>2,000</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>1,600</td><td>2,300</td><td>2,600 3,100</td></tr><tr><td>ⅡI</td><td>1,900</td><td>2,900</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td></td><td>3,700</td><td>4,100</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>2,200</td><td></td><td>4,700</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>2,600</td><td>4,200</td><td>5,400</td></tr><tr><td>14 15</td><td>2,900</td><td>4,900 5,400</td><td>6,200</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>3,300 3,800</td><td>6,100</td><td>7,800 9,800</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td></td><td>7,200</td><td>11,700</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>4,500</td><td></td><td>14,200</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>5,000</td><td>8,700</td><td>17,200</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>5,500</td><td>10,700</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>6,400</td><td>13,200</td><td>22,000</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.507, 0.772, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Step 3: Spend Your Budget"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.526, 0.909, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every creature has an XP value in its stat block. When you add a creature to your combat encounter, deduct its XP from your XP budget to determine how many XP you have left to spend. Spend as much of your XP budget as you can without going over. It’s OK if you have a few unspent XP left over. Examples are given below:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.639, 0.911, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example 1.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A low-difficulty encounter for four level 1 characters has an XP budget of 50 × 4, for a total of 200 XP. With that, you could build any of the following encounters:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.709, 0.759, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 1 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bugbear Warrior", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (200 XP)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.725, 0.879, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Wasps", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (100 XP each), for 200 XP total"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.742, 0.856, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Rats", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (25 XP each), for 150 XP total"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.764, 0.912, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example 2.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A moderate-difficulty encounter for five level 3 characters has an XP budget of 225 × 5, for a total of 1,125 XP. With that, you could build either of these encounters:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.833, 0.87, 0.866], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Druids", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (450 XP each) and 9 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Stirges", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (25 XP each), for 1,125 XP total"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.867, 0.912, 0.9], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 1 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Wight", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (700 XP), 1 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Warhorse Skeleton", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (100 XP), and 6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Skeletons", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (50 XP each), for 1,100 XP total"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "202"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 202, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.05, 0.484, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Example 3.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A high-difficulty encounter for six level 15 characters has an XP budget of 7,800 × 6, for a total of 46,800 XP. With that, you could build this encounter:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.119, 0.488, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• 2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adult Red Dragons", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (18,000 XP each) and 2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Fire", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giants", "styles": ["bold", "underline"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "(5,000 XP each), for 46,000 XP total", "styles": ["underline"]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.159, 0.282, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Troubleshooting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.183, 0.458, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When creating and running combat encounters, keep the following in mind."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.222, 0.253, 0.239], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Many Creatures"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.24, 0.481, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The more creatures in an encounter, the higher the risk that a lucky streak on their part could deal more damage to the characters than you expect. If your encounter includes more than two creatures per character, include fragile creatures that can be defeated quickly. This guideline is especially important for characters of level 1 or 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.355, 0.223, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adjustments"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.373, 0.488, 0.497], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A player’s absence might warrant removing creatures from an encounter to keep it at the intended difficulty. Also, die rolls and other factors can result in an encounter being easier or harder than intended. You can adjust an encounter on the fly, such as by having creatures flee (making the encounter easier) or adding reinforcements (making the encounter harder)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.672, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "CR 0 Creatures"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.907, 0.131], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creatures that have a CR of 0, particularly ones that are worth 0 XP, should be used sparingly. If you want to include many CR 0 critters in an encounter, use swarms instead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.523, 0.138, 0.735, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Number of Stat Blocks"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.155, 0.899, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The best combat encounters often pair one kind of creature with another, such as fire giants paired with hell hounds. Be mindful of the number of stat blocks you need to run the encounter. Referencing more than two or three stat blocks for a single encounter can be daunting, particularly if the creatures are complex."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.271, 0.707, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Powerful Creatures"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.288, 0.912, 0.382], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If your combat encounter includes a creature whose CR is higher than the party’s level, be aware that such a creature might deal enough damage with a single action to take out one or more characters. For example, an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ogre", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (CR 2) can kill a level 1 Wizard with a single blow."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.389, 0.687, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unusual Features"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.406, 0.907, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a monster has a feature that lower-level characters can’t easily overcome, consider not adding that monster to an encounter for characters whose level is lower than the monster’s Challenge Rating."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.027, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "203"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.103, 0.951, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 203, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.176, 0.05, 0.418, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.091, 0.476, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic items are gleaned from the hoards of felled monsters or discovered in long-lost vaults. Such items grant capabilities a character could rarely have otherwise, or they complement their owner’s capabilities in wondrous ways."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.178, 0.419, 0.202], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Categories"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.204, 0.481, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every magic item belongs to a category. The Magic Item Categories table lists the nine categories and provides examples. Rules for the categories appear after the table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.278, 0.294, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Categories"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.297, 0.489, 0.489], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.297, 0.489, 0.489], "content": "<table><tr><td>Category</td><td>Examples</td></tr><tr><td>Armor</td><td>+1 Leather Armor, +1 Shield</td></tr><tr><td>Potions</td><td>Potion of Healing</td></tr><tr><td>Rings</td><td>Ring of Invisibility</td></tr><tr><td>Rods</td><td>Immovable Rod</td></tr><tr><td>Scrolls</td><td>Spell Scroll</td></tr><tr><td>Staffs</td><td>Staff of Striking</td></tr><tr><td>Wands</td><td>Wand of Fireballs</td></tr><tr><td>Weapons</td><td>+1 Ammunition, +1 Longsword</td></tr><tr><td>Wondrous Items</td><td>Bag of Holding, Boots of Elvenkind</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.497, 0.181, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.521, 0.488, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An item in the Armor category is typically a magical version of armor from “Equipment.” Unless an armor’s description notes otherwise, the armor must be worn for its magic to function."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.583, 0.488, 0.646], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some suits of magic armor specify the type of armor they are, such as Chain Mail or Plate Armor. If no type is specified, choose the type or determine it randomly."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.652, 0.188, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.675, 0.476, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An item in the Potion category might be a magical brew that must be imbibed or an oil that must be applied to a creature or an object. A typical potion consists of 1 ounce of liquid in a vial."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.737, 0.484, 0.829], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Potion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Potions are consumable items. Drinking a potion or administering it to another creature requires a Bonus Action. Applying an oil might take longer as specified in its description. Once used, a potion takes effect immediately, and it is used up."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.829, 0.481, 0.908], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mixing Potions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A character might drink one potion while still under the effects of another or pour several potions into a single container. The strange ingredients used in creating potions can result in unpredictable interactions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When a character mixes two potions together, roll on the Potion Miscibility table. If more than two are combined, roll again for each subsequent potion, combining the results. Unless the effects are immediately obvious, reveal them only when they become evident."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.155, 0.673, 0.171], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion Miscibility"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.527, 0.175, 0.91, 0.667], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.527, 0.175, 0.91, 0.667], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>1d100</td><td>Result</td></tr><tr><td>01</td><td>Both potions lose their effects, and the mixture creates a magical explosion in a 5-foot-radius Sphere centered on itself. Each creature in that area takes 4d10 Force damage.</td></tr><tr><td>02-08</td><td>Both potions lose their effects, and the mix-ture becomes an ingested poison of your choice (see \"Poison\" in \"Gameplay Toolbox\").</td></tr><tr><td>09-1516-2526-35</td><td>Both potions lose their effects. One potion loses its effect. Both potions work, but with their numerical effects and durations halved. If a potion has no numerical effect and no duration, it instead loses its effect.</td></tr><tr><td>36-9091-99</td><td>Both potions work normally. Both potions work, but the numerical effects and duration of one potion are doubled. If nei-ther potion has anything to double in this way, they work normally.</td></tr><tr><td>00</td><td>Only one potion works, but its effects are permanent. Choose the simplest effect to make permanent or the one that seems the most fun. For example, a Potion of Healing might increase the drinker's Hit Point maxi-mum by 2d4 + 2, or a Potion of Invisibility might give the drinker the Invisible condition indefi-nitely. At your discretion, a Dispel Magic spell or similar magic might end this lasting effect.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.674, 0.587, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rings"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.698, 0.902, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For its magic to function, an item in the Ring category must be worn on a finger or a similar digit unless its description notes otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.752, 0.584, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rods"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.776, 0.902, 0.822], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An item in the Rod category is a scepter usually made of metal, wood, or bone. A typical rod weighs 2 to 5 pounds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.822, 0.898, 0.854], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unless its description notes otherwise, a rod can be used as an Arcane Focus."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.027, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "204"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 204, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.179, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scrolls"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.075, 0.487, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An item in the Scroll category is a roll of paper or parchment, sometimes attached to wooden rods and typically kept safe in a tube of ivory, jade, leather, metal, or wood. The most prevalent scroll is the Spell Scroll, a spell stored in written form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.152, 0.48, 0.228], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using a Scroll.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Scrolls are consumable items. Unleashing the magic in a scroll requires the user to read the scroll. When its magic has been invoked, the scroll can’t be used again. Its words fade, or it crumbles into dust."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.228, 0.476, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature that can understand a written language can read a scroll and attempt to activate it unless its description notes otherwise."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.281, 0.167, 0.299], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staffs"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.306, 0.491, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Items in the Staff category vary widely in appearance: some are of nearly equal diameter throughout and smooth, others are gnarled and twisted, some are made of wood, and others are composed of polished metal or crystal. A staff weighs between 2 and 7 pounds and serves well as a walking stick or cane."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.398, 0.49, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unless its description notes otherwise, a staff can be used as a nonmagical Quarterstaff and an Arcane Focus."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.451, 0.182, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wands"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.474, 0.473, 0.536], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An item in the Wand category is typically 12 to 15 inches long and crafted of metal, bone, or wood. It is tipped with metal, crystal, stone, or some other material."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.536, 0.463, 0.568], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unless its description notes otherwise, a wand can be used as an Arcane Focus."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.575, 0.208, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapons"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.598, 0.479, 0.691], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A magic weapon is typically a magical version of a weapon from “Equipment.” Some magic weapons specify the type of weapon they are in their descriptions, such as a Longsword or Longbow. If no weapon type is specified, you may choose the type or determine it randomly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.691, 0.485, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ammunition.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If a magic weapon has the Ammunition property, ammunition fired from it is considered magical for the purpose of any rule that cares whether a weapon is magical or not."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.759, 0.285, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.783, 0.473, 0.846], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Items include wearable items such as boots, belts, capes, amulets, brooches, and circlets. Bags, carpets, figurines, horns, musical instruments, and more also fall into this category."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.539, 0.059, 0.701, 0.074], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Rules"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.538, 0.078, 0.87, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rules for identifying, attuning to, and using magic items appear in “Equipment.” Additional rules are presented below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.537, 0.124, 0.892, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attunement Prerequisites.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If a magic item has a class prerequisite, a creature must be a member of that class to attune to the item. If a creature must be a spellcaster to attune to an item, the creature qualifies if it can cast at least one spell using its traits or features, not by using a magic item or the like."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.537, 0.216, 0.89, 0.322], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Items Made for Specific Creatures.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Magic items that are meant to be worn tend to magically adjust themselves to the wearer. However, you can decide that a magic item doesn’t adjust its size to fit any wearer. For example, a particular armorer might make items usable only by folk who are sized and shaped like dwarves."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.538, 0.323, 0.895, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unusual Anatomy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Use your discretion to decide whether a creature can wear an item not made for its anatomy. A ring placed on a tentacle might work, but a yuan-ti with a snakelike tail instead of legs can’t wear magic boots."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.538, 0.4, 0.882, 0.477], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Paired Items.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can allow exceptions to the rule that paired items must both be worn. For example, a character with only one arm might be able to use a single Glove of Missile Snaring so long as the matching glove is on their person."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.509, 0.776, 0.532], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Rarity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.535, 0.902, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every magic item has a rarity, which provides a rough measure of an item’s power relative to other magic items. The rarities are shown in the Magic Item Rarities and Values table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.596, 0.906, 0.643], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Common magic items, such as a Potion of Healing, are the most plentiful. Artifacts, such as the Dragon Orb, are priceless, unique, and difficult to acquire."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.649, 0.824, 0.669], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Values by Rarity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.673, 0.912, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Common magic items can often be bought in a town or city. Uncommon and Rare magic items are usually found only in cities, and rarer magic items might be sold only in wondrous locations, such as a city on another plane of existence. If you allow characters to buy and sell magic items in your campaign, rarity can help you set prices for those items. Gold Piece values are provided in the Magic Item Rarities and Values table, though a seller might ask for a service rather than coin as payment."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.827, 0.903, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a magic item incorporates an item that has a purchase cost in “Equipment” (such as a weapon or a suit of armor), add that item’s cost to the magic item’s value. For example, +1 Armor (Plate Armor)"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.027, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "205"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 205, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.475, 0.098], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "has a value of 5,500 GP, which is the sum of a Rare magic item’s value (4,000 GP) and the cost of Plate Armor (1,500 GP)."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.128, 0.486, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.109, 0.362, 0.125], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Rarities and Values"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.128, 0.486, 0.203], "content": "<table><tr><td>Rarity</td><td>Value*</td><td>Rarity</td><td>Value*</td></tr><tr><td>Common</td><td>100 GP</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>40,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Uncommon</td><td>400 GP</td><td>Legendary</td><td>200,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>Rare</td><td>4,000 GP</td><td>Artifact</td><td>Priceless</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.1, 0.21, 0.489, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "*Halve the value for a consumable item other than a Spell Scroll. The value of a Spell Scroll is double what it costs to scribe the scroll (as specified in the “Scribing Spell Scrolls” section of “Equipment”)."}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.262, 0.433, 0.286], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Activating a Magic Item"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.1, 0.287, 0.487, 0.38], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "It usually takes a Magic action to activate a magic item. The item’s user might also need to do something special. The description of each item category or individual item details how an item is activated. Certain items use the following rules for their activation."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.386, 0.287, 0.405], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Command Word"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.41, 0.481, 0.489], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A command word is a word or short phrase that must be spoken or signed for an item to work. Spoken command words must be audible and fail to work in areas where all sound is suppressed, as in the area of the Silence spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.495, 0.305, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Consumable Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.518, 0.491, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some items are consumed—used up, in other words—when they are activated. A Potion of Healing must be swallowed, for example, while the writing vanishes from a scroll when it is read. Once used, a consumable item loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.603, 0.312, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells Cast from Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.1, 0.621, 0.488, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items allow the user to cast a spell from the item. The spell is cast at the lowest possible spell and caster level, doesn’t expend any of the user’s spell slots, and requires no components unless the item’s description notes otherwise. The spell uses its normal casting time, range, and duration, and the user of the item must concentrate if the spell requires Concentration. Many items, such as Potions, bypass the casting of a spell and confer the spell’s effects with its usual duration. Certain items make exceptions to these rules, changing the casting time, duration, or other parts of a spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.805, 0.483, 0.883], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A magic item may require the user to use their own spellcasting ability when casting a spell from the item. If the user has more than one spellcasting ability, the user chooses which one to use with the item. If the user doesn’t have a spellcasting ability,"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.521, 0.049, 0.908, 0.083], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "their spellcasting ability modifier is +0 for the item, and the user’s Proficiency Bonus applies."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.089, 0.606, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Charges"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.521, 0.107, 0.904, 0.2], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items have charges that must be expended to activate their properties. The number of charges an item has remaining is revealed when the Identify spell is cast on it. A creature attuned to an item knows how many charges the item has and how many it regains."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.208, 0.782, 0.231], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“The Next Dawn”"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.521, 0.234, 0.897, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic items often have charges or properties that recharge at the next dawn or some other specified time. If such an item is on a world or plane of existence where the specified event doesn’t occur, the GM determines when the item recharges."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.321, 0.716, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cursed Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.346, 0.913, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A magic item’s description specifies whether it bears a curse. Most methods of identifying items, including the Identify spell, fail to reveal such a curse."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.393, 0.913, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attunement to a cursed item can’t be ended voluntarily unless the curse is broken first, such as with a Remove Curse spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.449, 0.829, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Resilience"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.474, 0.901, 0.521], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A magic item is at least as durable as a nonmagical item of its kind. Most magic items, other than Potions and Scrolls, have Resistance to all damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.521, 0.905, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Artifact can be destroyed only in some special way. Otherwise, it is impervious to damage. Learning how to destroy an Artifact usually requires research or the completion of a quest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.592, 0.819, 0.616], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crafting Magic Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.521, 0.617, 0.898, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“Equipment” contains rules on brewing Potions of Healing and scribing Spell Scrolls. To create other magic items, follow the rules below. In these rules, "}, {"type": "text", "content": "“you” refers to the character crafting the magic", "styles": ["underline"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " item."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.701, 0.73, 0.72], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arcana Proficiency"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.725, 0.899, 0.758], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To craft a magic item, you and any assistants must have proficiency in the Arcana skill."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.763, 0.588, 0.782], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tools"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.521, 0.787, 0.91, 0.882], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Magic Item Tools table lists which tool is required to make a magic item of each category. You must use the required tool to make an item and have proficiency with that tool. Any assistants must also have proficiency with it. For more information on the tools, see “Equipment.”"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.027, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "206"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 206, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.076, 0.489, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.057, 0.25, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Tools"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.105, 0.076, 0.489, 0.411], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Item Category</td><td>Required Tool</td></tr><tr><td>Armor</td><td>Leatherworker's Tools, Smith's Tools, or Weaver's Tools depend-ing on the kind of armor as noted in the tools' descriptions</td></tr><tr><td>Potion</td><td>Alchemist's Supplies or Herbalism Kit</td></tr><tr><td>Ring Rod Scroll Staff Wand Weapon</td><td>Jeweler's Tools Woodcarver's Tools Calligrapher's Supplies Woodcarver's Tools Woodcarver's Tools Leatherworker's Tools, Smith's Tools, or Woodcarver's Tools de-pending on the kind of weapon as noted in the tools' descriptions</td></tr><tr><td>Wondrous Item</td><td>Tinker's Tools or the tool required to make the nonmagical item on which the magic item is based</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.418, 0.17, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.443, 0.482, 0.491], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a magic item allows its user to cast any spells from it, you must have all those spells prepared every day you spend crafting the item."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.497, 0.265, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Time and Cost"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.52, 0.479, 0.567], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crafting a magic item takes an amount of time and money based on the item’s rarity as shown in the Magic Item Crafting Time and Cost table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.567, 0.482, 0.613], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work per Day.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " For each day of crafting, you must work for 8 hours. If an item requires multiple days, those days needn’t be consecutive."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.613, 0.488, 0.69], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assistants.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Characters can combine their efforts to shorten the crafting time. Divide the time needed to create an item by the number of characters working on it. Normally, only one other character can assist you, but the GM might allow more assistants."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.69, 0.49, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Raw Materials.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The cost in the table represents the raw materials needed to make a magic item. The GM determines whether appropriate raw materials are available. In a city, there is a 75 percent chance that the materials are available, and in any other settlement, that chance is 25 percent. If materials aren’t available, you must wait at least 7 days before checking on the availability again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.812, 0.485, 0.906], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a magic item incorporates an item that has a purchase cost (such as a weapon or a suit of armor), you must also pay that entire cost or craft that item using the rules in “Equipment.” For example, to make +1 Armor (Plate Armor), you must pay 3,500 GP or pay 2,000 GP and craft the armor."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.525, 0.069, 0.91, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.821, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Item Crafting Time and Cost"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.525, 0.069, 0.91, 0.183], "content": "<table><tr><td>Item Rarity</td><td>Time* Cost*</td></tr><tr><td>5 days Common</td><td>50 GP</td></tr><tr><td>10 days Uncommon</td><td>200 GP</td></tr><tr><td>50 days Rare</td><td>2,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>125 days Very Rare</td><td>20,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>250 days Legendary</td><td>100,000 GP</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.189, 0.912, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "*The time and cost are halved for a consumable item other than a Spell Scroll, whose crafting time and cost are given in “Equipment.”"}]}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.229, 0.82, 0.252], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Magic Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.912, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some magic items have sentience and personality. Such an item might be possessed, haunted by the spirit of a previous owner, or self-aware thanks to the magic used to create it. A sentient item might be a cherished ally to its wielder or a continual thorn in the side."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.347, 0.904, 0.393], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Most sentient items are weapons, but other kinds of items can manifest sentience. Single-use items such as potions and scrolls are never sentient."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.393, 0.904, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The GM controls sentient magic items and their activated properties. A bearer who maintains a good relationship with the item can access those properties. If the relationship is strained, a conflict can ensue (see “Conflict” below)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.476, 0.81, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Magic Item Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.5, 0.892, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make a sentient magic item, you create the item’s persona much as you would create an NPC, with these exceptions."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.554, 0.605, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Abilities"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.572, 0.91, 0.635], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A sentient magic item has Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. Choose the item’s abilities, or determine them randomly as follows: roll 4d6 for each one, dropping the lowest roll and totaling the rest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.642, 0.625, 0.659], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alignment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.659, 0.901, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A sentient magic item has an alignment. Its creator or nature might suggest an alignment. Otherwise, pick an alignment or roll on the Sentient Item’s Alignment table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.729, 0.674, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Communication"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.746, 0.898, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A sentient item communicates by sharing its emotions, broadcasting its thoughts telepathically, or speaking aloud. You can choose how it communicates or roll on the Sentient Item’s Communication table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.831, 0.592, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.521, 0.848, 0.908, 0.896], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A sentient item can perceive its surroundings out to a limited range. You can choose its senses or roll on the Sentient Item’s Senses table."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "207"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 207, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.251, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Purpose"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.486, 0.193], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can give a sentient item an objective it pursues, perhaps to the exclusion of all else. As long as the wielder’s use of the item aligns with that special purpose, the item remains cooperative. Deviating from this course might cause conflict between the wielder and the item (see “Conflict” below). You can pick a special purpose or roll on the Sentient Item’s Special Purpose table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.205, 0.324, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Item’s Alignment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.223, 0.488, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.223, 0.488, 0.337], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Alignment</td><td>IdI00</td><td>Alignment</td></tr><tr><td>01-15</td><td>Lawful Good</td><td>74-85</td><td>Chaotic Neutral</td></tr><tr><td>16-35</td><td>Neutral Good</td><td>86-89</td><td>Lawful Evil</td></tr><tr><td>36-50</td><td>Chaotic Good</td><td>90-96</td><td>Neutral Evil</td></tr><tr><td>51-63</td><td>Lawful Neutral</td><td>97-00</td><td>Chaotic Evil</td></tr><tr><td>64-73</td><td>Neutral</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.352, 0.368, 0.367], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Item’s Communication"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.107, 0.371, 0.487, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.107, 0.371, 0.487, 0.494], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI0</td><td>Communication</td></tr><tr><td>1-6</td><td>The item communicates by transmitting emo- tion to the creature carrying or wielding it.</td></tr><tr><td>7-9</td><td>The item speaks one or more languages.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>The item speaks one or more languages. In ad- dition, the item can communicate telepathically with any creature that carries or wields it.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.509, 0.293, 0.524], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Item’s Senses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.119, 0.528, 0.218, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d4 Senses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.125, 0.547, 0.452, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1 Hearing and standard vision out to 30 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.125, 0.566, 0.452, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2 Hearing and standard vision out to 60 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.125, 0.585, 0.458, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "3 Hearing and standard vision out to 120 feet"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.125, 0.605, 0.432, 0.621], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "4 Hearing and Darkvision out to 120 feet"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.637, 0.368, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentient Item’s Special Purpose"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.116, 0.657, 0.281, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d10 Special Purpose"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.125, 0.675, 0.472, 0.723], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aligned.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks to defeat or destroy those of a diametrically opposed alignment. Such an item is never Neutral."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.125, 0.727, 0.459, 0.775], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bane.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks to thwart or destroy creatures of a particular type, such as Constructs, Fiends, or Undead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.123, 0.778, 0.466, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "3 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Creator Seeker.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks its creator and wants to understand why it was created."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.124, 0.814, 0.472, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "4 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Destiny Seeker.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item believes it and its bearer have key roles to play in future events."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.537, 0.056, 0.702, 0.071], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d10 Special Purpose"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.545, 0.074, 0.902, 0.108], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "5 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Destroyer.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item craves destruction and goads its user to fight arbitrarily."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.546, 0.111, 0.894, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "6 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Glory Seeker.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks renown as the greatest magic item in the world by winning fame or notoriety for its user."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.547, 0.162, 0.905, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "7 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Lore Seeker.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item craves knowledge or is determined to solve a mystery, learn a secret, or unravel a cryptic prophecy."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.547, 0.214, 0.881, 0.262], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "8 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Protector.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks to defend a particular kind of creature, such as elves or werewolves."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.546, 0.265, 0.908, 0.314], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "9 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Soulmate Seeker.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks another sentient magic item, perhaps one that is similar to itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.545, 0.318, 0.884, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "10 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Templar.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item seeks to defend the servants and interests of a particular deity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.367, 0.603, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Conflict"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.385, 0.908, 0.479], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the bearer of a sentient item acts in a manner opposed to the item’s alignment or purpose, conflict can arise. When such a conflict occurs, the item’s bearer makes a Charisma saving throw (DC 12 plus the item’s Charisma modifier). On a failed save, the item makes one or more of the following demands:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.484, 0.902, 0.529], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chase My Dreams.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item demands that its bearer pursue the item’s goals to the exclusion of all other goals."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.53, 0.904, 0.56], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Get Rid of It.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item demands that its bearer dispose of anything the item finds repugnant."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.525, 0.561, 0.882, 0.591], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "It’s Time for a Change.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item demands to be given to someone else."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.591, 0.91, 0.622], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Keep Me Close.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The item insists on being carried or worn at all times."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.628, 0.888, 0.66], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If its bearer refuses to comply with the item’s demands, the item can do any of the following:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.666, 0.89, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Make it impossible for its bearer to attune to it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.682, 0.9, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Suppress one or more of its activated properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.697, 0.907, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Attempt to take control of its bearer, whereupon the bearer makes a Charisma saving throw (DC 12 plus the item’s Charisma modifier). On a failed save, the bearer has the Charmed condition for 1d12 hours. While Charmed in this way, the bearer must try to follow the item’s commands. If the bearer takes damage, it repeats the save, ending the effect on a success. Whether or not the attempt to control its bearer succeeds, the item can’t use this power again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.027, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "208"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 208, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.343, 0.074], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Items A–Z"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.076, 0.462, 0.092], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic items are presented in alphabetical order."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.092, 0.488, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a magic item description capitalizes a creature’s name and presents it in "}, {"type": "text", "content": "bold", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " type, that’s a visual cue pointing you to the creature’s stat block. Unless the text states otherwise, the stat block is in “Monsters.” How to read and use a stat block is explained in “Monsters.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.192, 0.285, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Adamantine Armor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.209, 0.462, 0.24], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.244, 0.469, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This suit of armor is reinforced with adamantine, one of the hardest substances in existence. While you’re wearing it, any Critical Hit against you becomes a normal hit."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.314, 0.345, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ammunition, +1, +2, or +3"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.331, 0.485, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Ammunition), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2), or Very Rare (+3)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.367, 0.482, 0.443], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this piece of magic ammunition. The bonus is determined by the rarity of the ammunition. Once it hits a target, the ammunition is no longer magical."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.443, 0.486, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This ammunition is typically found or sold in quantities of ten or twenty pieces. Ten pieces of this ammunition are equivalent in value to a potion of the same rarity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.513, 0.312, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ammunition of Slaying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.531, 0.373, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Ammunition), Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.551, 0.481, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This magic ammunition is meant to slay creatures of a particular type, which the GM chooses or determines randomly by rolling on the table below. If a creature of that type takes damage from the ammunition, the creature makes a DC 17 Constitution saving throw, taking an extra 6d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much extra damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.673, 0.473, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After dealing its extra damage to a creature, the ammunition becomes nonmagical."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.708, 0.488, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.708, 0.488, 0.861], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Creature Type</td><td>IdI00</td><td>Creature Type</td></tr><tr><td>01-10</td><td>Aberrations</td><td>51-60</td><td>Fey</td></tr><tr><td>11-15</td><td>Beasts</td><td>61-70</td><td>Fiends</td></tr><tr><td>16-20</td><td>Celestials</td><td>71-75</td><td>Giants</td></tr><tr><td>21-25</td><td>Constructs</td><td>76-80</td><td>Monstrosities</td></tr><tr><td>26-35</td><td>Dragons</td><td>81-85</td><td>Oozes</td></tr><tr><td>36-45</td><td>Elementals</td><td>86-90</td><td>Plants</td></tr><tr><td>46-50</td><td>Humanoids</td><td>91-00</td><td>Undead</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.687, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Amulet of Health"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.068, 0.841, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.902, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your Constitution is 19 while you wear this amulet. It has no effect on you if your Constitution is 19 or higher without it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.143, 0.838, 0.172], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.887, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.192, 0.895, 0.24], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this amulet, you can’t be targeted by Divination spells or perceived through magical scrying sensors unless you allow it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.246, 0.718, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Amulet of the Planes"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.264, 0.876, 0.281], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.284, 0.905, 0.408], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this amulet, you can take a Magic action to name a location that you are familiar with on another plane of existence. Then make a DC 15 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a successful check, you cast Plane Shift. On a failed check, you and each creature and object within 15 feet of you travel to a random destination determined by rolling 1d100 and consulting the following table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.533, 0.412, 0.678, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d100 Destination", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.53, 0.43, 0.875, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "01–60 Random location on the plane you named"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.532, 0.45, 0.905, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "61–70 Random location on an Inner Plane determined by rolling 1d6: on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "1,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Plane of Air; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "2,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Plane of Earth; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "3,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Plane of Fire; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "4,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Plane of Water; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "5,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Feywild; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "6,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Shadowfell"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.53, 0.533, 0.905, 0.614], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "71–80 Random location on an Outer Plane determined by rolling 1d8: on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "1,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Arborea; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "2,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Arcadia; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "3,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Beastlands; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "4,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Bytopia; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "5,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Elysium; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "6,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Mechanus; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "7,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Mount Celestia; on an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "8,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Ysgard"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.531, 0.617, 0.901, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "81–90 Random location on an Outer Plane determined by rolling 1d8: on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "1,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Abyss; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "2,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Acheron; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "3,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Carceri; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "4,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Gehenna; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "5,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Hades; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "6,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Limbo; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "7,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " the Nine Hells; on an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "8,", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Pandemonium"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.53, 0.7, 0.839, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "91–00 Random location on the Astral Plane"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.727, 0.678, 0.743], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Animated Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.744, 0.872, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.765, 0.909, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you can take a Bonus Action to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animate for 1 minute, until you take a Bonus Action to end this effect, or until you die or have the Incapacitated condition, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "209"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 209, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.31, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Apparatus of the Crab"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.299, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.482, 0.242], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This item first appears to be a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful DC 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "rans", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "forms to resemble a giant lobster."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.242, 0.48, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Apparatus of the Crab is a Large object with the following statistics: AC 20; HP 200; Speed 30 ft., Swim 30 ft. (or 0 ft. for both if the legs aren’t extended); Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.303, 0.481, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus’s hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.395, 0.485, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.456, 0.484, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature in the compartment can take a Utilize action to move as many as two of the apparatus’s levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of the Crab Levers table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.555, 0.353, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Apparatus of the Crab Levers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.714, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor, +1, +2, or +3"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.9, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (+1), Very Rare (+2), or Legendary (+3)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.522, 0.103, 0.907, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a bonus to Armor Class while wearing this armor. The bonus is determined by its rarity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.523, 0.143, 0.748, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor of Invulnerability"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.16, 0.828, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Plate Armor), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.195, 0.896, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while you wear this armor."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.226, 0.901, 0.304], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Metal Shell.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to give yourself Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this property is used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.311, 0.715, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor of Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.328, 0.9, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.363, 0.899, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Resistance to one type of damage while you wear this armor. The GM chooses the type or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.526, 0.429, 0.909, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.526, 0.429, 0.909, 0.543], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI0</td><td>Damage Type</td><td>IdI0</td><td>Damage Type</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Acid</td><td>6</td><td>Necrotic</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Cold</td><td>7</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fire</td><td>8</td><td>Psychic</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Force</td><td>9</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lightning</td><td>10</td><td>Thunder</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.104, 0.574, 0.909, 0.911], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.104, 0.574, 0.909, 0.911], "content": "<table><tr><td>Lever Up</td><td></td><td>Down</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Legs extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim.</td><td>Legs retract, reducing the apparatus&#x27;s Speed and Swim Speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bo- nuses to speed.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Forward window shutter opens.</td><td>Forward window shutter closes.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Side window shutters open (two per side).</td><td>Side window shutters close (two per side).</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Two claws extend from the front side of the apparatus.</td><td>The claws retract.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage.</td><td>Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: +8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: The target has the Grappled condition (escape DC 15).</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>The apparatus walks or swims forward provided its legs are extended.</td><td>The apparatus walks or swims backward provided its legs are extended.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise provided its legs are extended.</td><td>The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise provided its legs are extended.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Eyelike fixtures emit Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet.</td><td>The light turns off.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it&#x27;s in liquid.</td><td>The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it&#x27;s in liquid.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>The rear hatch unseals and opens.</td><td>The rear hatch closes and seals.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "210"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 210, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.312, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor of Vulnerability"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.1, 0.069, 0.478, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.471, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this armor, you have Resistance to one of the following damage types: Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing. The GM chooses the type or determines it randomly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.165, 0.487, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curse.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when the Identify spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by a Remove Curse spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed, you have Vulnerability to two of the three damage types associated with the armor (not the one to which it grants Resistance)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.296, 0.315, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arrow-Catching Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.314, 0.415, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.333, 0.48, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class against ranged attack rolls while you wield this Shield. This bonus is in addition to the Shield’s normal bonus to AC."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.38, 0.484, 0.426], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever an attacker makes a ranged attack roll against a target within 5 feet of you, you can take a Reaction to become the target of the attack instead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.434, 0.224, 0.45], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bag of Beans"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.451, 0.256, 0.466], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.47, 0.482, 0.532], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This heavy cloth bag contains 3d4 dry beans when found. The bag weighs half a pound regardless of how many beans it contains and becomes a non-magical item when it no longer contains any beans."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.533, 0.487, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you dump one or more beans out of the bag, they explode in a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered on them. All the dumped beans are destroyed in the explosion, and each creature in the Sphere, including you, makes a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 5d4 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.64, 0.485, 0.717], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you remove a bean from the bag, plant it in dirt or sand, and then water it, the bean disappears as it produces an effect 1 minute later from the ground where it was planted. The GM can choose an effect from the following table or determine it randomly."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.118, 0.721, 0.226, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d100 Effect", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.122, 0.739, 0.485, 0.852], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "01 5d4 toadstools sprout. If a creature eats a toadstool, roll any die. On an odd roll, the eater must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 5d6 Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour. On an even roll, the eater gains 5d6 Temporary Hit Points for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.116, 0.856, 0.472, 0.904], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "02–10 A geyser erupts and spouts water, beer, mayonnaise, tea, vinegar, wine, or oil (GM’s choice) 30 feet into the air for 1d4 minutes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.54, 0.056, 0.647, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d100 Effect", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.527, 0.063, 0.91, 0.845], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.527, 0.063, 0.91, 0.845], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>1d100</td><td>Effect</td></tr><tr><td>11-20</td><td>A Treant sprouts. Roll any die. On an odd roll, the treant is Chaotic Evil. On an even roll, the treant is Chaotic Good.</td></tr><tr><td>21-30</td><td>An animate but immobile stone statue in your likeness rises and makes verbal threats against you. If you leave it and others come near, it describes you as the most heinous of villains and directs the newcomers to find and attack you. If you are on the same plane of existence as the statue, it knows where you are. The statue becomes inanimate after 24 hours.</td></tr><tr><td>31-40</td><td>A campfire with green flames springs forth and burns for 24 hours or until it is extinguished.</td></tr><tr><td>41-5051-60</td><td>Three Shrieker Fungi sprout. 1d4 + 4 bright-pink toads crawl forth. When-ever a toad is touched, it transforms into a Large or smaller monster of the GM's choice that acts in accordance with its alignment and nature. The monster remains for 1 min-ute, then disappears in a puff of bright-pink smoke.</td></tr><tr><td>61-7071-80</td><td>A hungry Bulette burrows up and attacks. A fruit tree grows. It has 1d10 + 20 fruit, 1d8 of which act as randomly determined po-tions. The tree vanishes after 1 hour. Picked fruit remains, retaining any magic for 30 days.</td></tr><tr><td>81-90</td><td>A nest of 1d4 + 3 rainbow-colored eggs springs up. Any creature that eats an egg makes a DC 20 Constitution saving throw. On a successful save, a creature permanently increases its lowest ability score by 1, ran-domly choosing among equally low scores. On a failed save, the creature takes 10d6 Force damage from an internal explosion.</td></tr><tr><td>91-95</td><td>A pyramid with a 60-foot-square base bursts upward. Inside is a burial chamber containing a Mummy, a Mummy Lord, or some other Undead of the GM's choice. Its sarcophagus contains treasure of the GM's choice.</td></tr><tr><td>96-00</td><td>A giant beanstalk sprouts, growing to a height of the GM's choice. The top leads where the GM chooses, such as to a great view, a cloud giant's castle, or another plane of existence.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.059, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "211"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 211, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.264, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bag of Devouring"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.069, 0.292, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.484, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This bag resembles a Bag of Holding but is a feeding orifice for a gigantic extradimensional creature. Turning the bag inside out closes the orifice."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.135, 0.49, 0.365], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The extradimensional creature attached to the bag can sense whatever is placed inside the bag. Animal or vegetable matter placed wholly in the bag is devoured and lost forever. When part of a living creature is placed in the bag, as happens when someone reaches inside it, there is a 50 percent chance that the creature is pulled inside the bag. A creature inside the bag can take an action to try to escape, doing so with a successful DC 15 Strength (Athletics) check. Another creature can take an action to reach into the bag to pull a creature out, doing so with a successful DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check, provided the puller isn’t pulled inside the bag first. Any creature that starts its turn inside the bag is devoured, its body destroyed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.365, 0.49, 0.441], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Inanimate objects can be stored in the bag, which can hold a cubic foot of such material. However, once each day, the bag swallows any objects inside it and spits them out into another plane of existence. The GM determines the time and plane."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.441, 0.467, 0.488], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the bag is pierced or torn, it is destroyed, and anything contained within it is transported to a random location on the Astral Plane."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.495, 0.241, 0.512], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bag of Holding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.514, 0.302, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.532, 0.484, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This bag has an interior space considerably larger than its outside dimensions—roughly 2 feet square and 4 feet deep on the inside. The bag can hold up to 500 pounds, not exceeding a volume of 64 cubic feet. The bag weighs 5 pounds, regardless of its contents. Retrieving an item from the bag requires a Utilize action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.64, 0.485, 0.747], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the bag is overloaded, pierced, or torn, it is destroyed, and its contents are scattered in the Astral Plane. If the bag is turned inside out, its contents spill forth unharmed, but the bag must be put right before it can be used again. The bag holds enough air for 10 minutes of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.747, 0.484, 0.887], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Placing a Bag of Holding inside an extradimensional space created by a Handy Haversack, Portable Hole, or similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. The gate originates where the one item was placed inside the other. Any creature within a 10-foot-radius Sphere centered on the gate is sucked through it to a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes. The gate is one-way and can’t be reopened."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.647, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bag of Tricks"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.724, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.904, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This bag made from gray, rust, or tan cloth appears empty. Reaching inside the bag, however, reveals the presence of a small, fuzzy object."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.135, 0.901, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to pull the fuzzy object from the bag and throw it up to 20 feet. When the object lands, it transforms into a creature you determine by rolling on the table that corresponds to the bag’s color. See “Monsters” for the creature’s stat block. The creature vanishes at the next dawn or when it is reduced to 0 Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.242, 0.906, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is Friendly to you and your allies, and it acts immediately after you on your Initiative count. You can take a Bonus Action to command how the creature moves and what action it takes on its next turn, such as attacking an enemy. In the absence of such orders, the creature acts in a fashion appropriate to its nature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.349, 0.892, 0.395], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once three fuzzy objects have been pulled from the bag, the bag can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.427, 0.911, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.525, 0.408, 0.682, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gray Bag of Tricks"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.427, 0.911, 0.52], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Weasel</td><td>5</td><td>Panther</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Giant Rat</td><td>6</td><td>Giant Badger</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Badger</td><td>7</td><td>Dire Wolf</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Boar</td><td>8</td><td>Giant Elk</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.525, 0.554, 0.911, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.537, 0.679, 0.552], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rust Bag of Tricks"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.525, 0.554, 0.911, 0.649], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Rat</td><td>5</td><td>Giant Goat</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Owl</td><td>6</td><td>Giant Boar</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Mastiff</td><td>7</td><td>Lion</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Goat</td><td>8</td><td>Brown Bear</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.682, 0.911, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.665, 0.672, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tan Bag of Tricks"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.682, 0.911, 0.777], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td><td>Id8</td><td>Creature</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Jackal</td><td>5</td><td>Black Bear</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Ape</td><td>6</td><td>Giant Weasel</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Baboon</td><td>7</td><td>Giant Hyena</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Axe Beak</td><td>8</td><td>Tiger</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.525, 0.788, 0.655, 0.803], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bead of Force"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.806, 0.678, 0.82], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.824, 0.899, 0.871], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This small black sphere measures 3/4 of an inch in diameter and weighs an ounce. Typically, 1d4 + 4 Beads of Force are found together."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.871, 0.9, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to throw the bead up to 60 feet. The bead explodes in a 10-foot-radius Sphere on impact and is destroyed. Each creature"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "212"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 212, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "in the Sphere must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 5d4 Force damage. A sphere of transparent force then encloses the area for 1 minute. Any creature that failed the save and is completely within the area is trapped inside this sphere. Creatures that succeeded on the save or are partially within the area are pushed away from the center of the sphere until they are no longer inside it. Only breathable air can pass through the sphere’s wall. No attack or other effect can pass through."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.204, 0.484, 0.282], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An enclosed creature can take a Utilize action to push against the sphere’s wall, moving the sphere up to half the creature’s Speed. The sphere can be picked up, and its magic causes it to weigh only 1 pound, regardless of the weight of creatures inside."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.289, 0.302, 0.304], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bead of Nourishment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.306, 0.285, 0.321], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Common"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.482, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This flavorless, gelatinous bead dissolves on your tongue and provides as much nourishment as 1 day of Rations."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.38, 0.295, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Belt of Dwarvenkind"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.397, 0.419, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.417, 0.451, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this belt, you gain the following benefits:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.454, 0.344, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarvish.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know Dwarvish."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.47, 0.47, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Friend of Dwarvenkind.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to interact with dwarves and duergar."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.516, 0.473, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Toughness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.553, 0.482, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, while attuned to the belt, you have a 50 percent chance each day at dawn of growing a full beard if you can grow one, or a thicker beard if you already have one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.615, 0.476, 0.647], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you aren’t a dwarf or duergar, you gain the following additional benefits while wearing the belt:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.652, 0.49, 0.682], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Darkvision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision with a range of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.683, 0.482, 0.73], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resilience.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to Poison damage. You also have Advantage on saving throws you make to avoid or end the Poisoned condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.103, 0.737, 0.307, 0.754], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Belt of Giant Strength"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.755, 0.478, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rarity Varies (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.775, 0.482, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this belt, your Strength changes to a score granted by the belt. The type of giant determines the score (see the table below). The item has no effect on you if your Strength without the belt is equal to or greater than the belt’s score."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.527, 0.055, 0.908, 0.185], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.527, 0.055, 0.908, 0.185], "content": "<table><tr><td>Belt</td><td>Str. Rarity</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Giant Strength (hill)</td><td>21</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Giant Strength (frost or stone)</td><td>23</td><td>Very Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Giant Strength (fire)</td><td>25</td><td>Very Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Giant Strength (cloud)</td><td>27</td><td>Legendary</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Giant Strength (storm)</td><td>29</td><td>Legendary</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.195, 0.664, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Berserker Axe"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.212, 0.864, 0.245], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Battleaxe, Greataxe, or Halberd), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.247, 0.907, 0.324], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, while you are attuned to this weapon, your Hit Point maximum increases by 1 for each level you have attained."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.324, 0.901, 0.416], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curse.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the weapon, keeping it within reach at all times. You also have Disadvantage on attack rolls with weapons other than this one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.416, 0.913, 0.508], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever another creature damages you while the weapon is in your possession, you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or go berserk. This berserk state ends when you start your turn and there are no creatures within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.509, 0.912, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While berserk, you regard the creature nearest to you that you can see or hear as your enemy. If there are multiple possible creatures, choose one at random. On each of your turns, you must move as close to the creature as possible and take the Attack action, targeting the creature. If you’re unable to get close enough to the creature to attack it with the weapon, your turn ends after you’ve used up all your available movement. If the creature dies or can no longer be seen or heard by you, the next nearest creature that you can see or hear becomes your new target."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.7, 0.699, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boots of Elvenkind"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.718, 0.724, 0.734], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.737, 0.883, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear these boots, your steps make no sound, regardless of the surface you are moving across. You also have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.807, 0.702, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boots of Levitation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.824, 0.841, 0.841], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.844, 0.893, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear these boots, you can cast Levitate on yourself."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "213"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 213, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.245, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boots of Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.419, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.482, 0.181], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear these boots, you can take a Bonus Action to click the boots’ heels together. If you do, the boots double your Speed, and any creature that makes an Opportunity Attack against you has Disadvantage on the attack roll. If you click your heels together again, you end the effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.181, 0.478, 0.228], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you’ve used the boots’ property for a total of 10 minutes, the magic ceases to function for you until you finish a Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.234, 0.387, 0.252], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boots of Striding and Springing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.252, 0.465, 0.269], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.272, 0.483, 0.334], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear these boots, your Speed becomes 30 feet unless your Speed is higher, and your Speed isn’t reduced by you carrying weight in excess of your carrying capacity or wearing Heavy Armor."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.334, 0.485, 0.365], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once on each of your turns, you can jump up to 30 feet by spending only 10 feet of movement."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.372, 0.337, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Boots of the Winterlands"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.389, 0.466, 0.406], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.409, 0.475, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These furred boots are snug and feel warm. While wearing them, you gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.441, 0.484, 0.501], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cold Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to Cold damage and can tolerate temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower without any additional protection."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.501, 0.474, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Winter Strider.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You ignore Difficult Terrain created by ice or snow."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.54, 0.469, 0.574], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bowl of Commanding Water Elementals Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.577, 0.485, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While this bowl is filled with water and you are within 5 feet of it, you can take a Magic action to summon a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Water Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the bowl as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The bowl can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.731, 0.469, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The bowl is about 1 foot in diameter and half as deep. It holds about 3 gallons."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.77, 0.281, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bracers of Archery"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.103, 0.787, 0.465, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.807, 0.48, 0.855], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing these bracers, you have proficiency with the Longbow and Shortbow, and you gain a +2 bonus to damage rolls made with such w"}, {"type": "text", "content": "eapons", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.701, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bracers of Defense"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.841, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.91, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing these bracers, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class if you are wearing no armor and using no Shield."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.143, 0.889, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brazier of Commanding Fire Elementals Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.18, 0.912, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you are within 5 feet of this brazier, you can take a Magic action to summon a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Fire Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the brazier as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The brazier can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.326, 0.705, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Brooch of Shielding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.343, 0.899, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) While wearing this brooch, you have Resistance to Force damage, and you have Immunity to damage from the Magic Missile spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.418, 0.674, 0.435], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Broom of Flying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.435, 0.886, 0.451], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.455, 0.91, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wooden broom functions like a mundane broom until you stand astride it and take a Magic action to make it hover beneath you, at which time it can be ridden in the air. It has a Fly Speed of 50 feet. It can carry up to 400 pounds, but its Fly Speed becomes 30 feet while carrying over 200 pounds. The broom stops hovering when you land or when you’re no longer riding it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.578, 0.908, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can send the broom to travel alone to a destination within 1 mile of you if you name the location and are familiar with it. The broom comes back to you when you take a Magic action and use a command word if the broom is still within 1 mile of you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.678, 0.715, 0.694], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Candle of Invocation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.696, 0.876, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.714, 0.896, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This candle’s magic is activated when the candle is lit, which requires a Magic action. After burning for 4 hours, the candle is destroyed. You can snuff it out early for use at a later time. Deduct the time it burned in increments of 1 minute from its total burn time."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.807, 0.898, 0.885], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While lit, the candle sheds Dim Light in a 30-foot radius. While you are within that light, you have Advantage on D20 Tests. In addition, a Cleric or Druid in the light can cast level 1 spells they have prepared without expending spell slots."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.884, 0.888, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, when you light the candle for the first time, you can cast Gate with it. Doing so destroys the candle. The portal created by the spell"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "214"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 214, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.475, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "links to a particular Outer Plane chosen by the GM or determined by rolling on the following table."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "table", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.086, 0.488, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.086, 0.488, 0.257], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Outer Plane</td><td>IdI00</td><td>Outer Plane</td></tr><tr><td>01-05</td><td>Abyss</td><td>55-59</td><td>Gehenna</td></tr><tr><td>06-10</td><td>Acheron</td><td>60-64</td><td>Hades</td></tr><tr><td>11-17</td><td>Arborea</td><td>65-69</td><td>Limbo</td></tr><tr><td>18-25</td><td>Arcadia</td><td>70-77</td><td>Mechanus</td></tr><tr><td>26-33</td><td>Beastlands</td><td>78-85</td><td>Mount Celestia</td></tr><tr><td>34-41</td><td>Bytopia</td><td>86-90</td><td>Nine Hells</td></tr><tr><td>42-46</td><td>Carceri</td><td>91-95</td><td>Pandemonium</td></tr><tr><td>47-54</td><td>Elysium</td><td>96-00</td><td>Ysgard</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.268, 0.332, 0.285], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cape of the Mountebank"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.286, 0.258, 0.301], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.305, 0.475, 0.366], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This cape smells faintly of brimstone. While wearing it, you can use it to cast Dimension Door as a Magic action. This property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.366, 0.477, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you teleport with that spell, you leave behind a cloud of smoke. The space you left is Lightly Obscured by that smoke until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.436, 0.253, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Carpet of Flying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.454, 0.292, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.473, 0.487, 0.534], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can make this carpet hover and fly by taking a Magic action and using the carpet’s command word. It moves according to your directions if you are within 30 feet of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.535, 0.49, 0.628], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Four sizes of Carpet of Flying exist. The GM chooses the size of a given carpet or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table. A carpet can carry up to twice the weight shown on the table, but its Fly Speed is halved if it carries more than its normal capacity."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.104, 0.631, 0.489, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.104, 0.631, 0.489, 0.725], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Size</td><td>Capacity</td><td>Fly Speed</td></tr><tr><td>01-20</td><td>3 ft. × 5 ft.</td><td>200 lb.</td><td>80 feet</td></tr><tr><td>21-55</td><td>4 ft. × 6 ft.</td><td>400 lb.</td><td>60 feet</td></tr><tr><td>56-80</td><td>5 ft. × 7 ft.</td><td>600 lb.</td><td>40 feet</td></tr><tr><td>81-00</td><td>6 ft. × 9 ft.</td><td>800 lb.</td><td>30 feet</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.736, 0.441, 0.769], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Censer of Controlling Air Elementals Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.773, 0.482, 0.913], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While gently swinging this censer, you can take a Magic action to summon an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Air Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the censer as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The censer can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.695, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Chime of Opening"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.679, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.907, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This hollow metal tube measures about 1 foot long and weighs 1 pound. As a Magic action, you can strike the chime to cast Knock. The spell’s customary knocking sound is replaced by the clear, ringing tone of the chime, which is audible out to 300 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.166, 0.895, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The chime can be used 10 times. After the tenth time, it cracks and becomes useless."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.204, 0.692, 0.221], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Circlet of Blasting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.222, 0.724, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.241, 0.913, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this circlet, you can cast Scorching Ray with it (+5 to hit). The circlet can’t cast this spell again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.295, 0.703, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of Arachnida"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.313, 0.876, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.333, 0.899, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This fine garment is made of black silk interwoven with faint, silvery threads. While wearing it, you gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.379, 0.907, 0.409], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Poison Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Resistance to Poison damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.41, 0.906, 0.47], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spider Climb.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed and can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings, while leaving your hands free."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.471, 0.908, 0.516], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spider Walk.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can’t be caught in webs of any sort and can move through webs as if they were Difficult Terrain."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.517, 0.909, 0.579], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Web.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can cast Web (save DC 13). The web created by the spell fills twice its normal area. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.586, 0.735, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of Displacement"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.604, 0.841, 0.62], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.623, 0.91, 0.732], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear this cloak, it magically projects an illusion that makes you appear to be standing in a place near your actual location, causing any creature to have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. If you take damage, the property ceases to function until the start of your next turn. This property is suppressed while your Speed is 0."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.738, 0.699, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of Elvenkind"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.756, 0.886, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.775, 0.885, 0.839], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear this cloak, Wisdom (Perception) checks made to perceive you have Disadvantage, and you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.846, 0.702, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of Invisibility"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.863, 0.882, 0.88], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.883, 0.909, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This cloak has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the cloak, you can take a Magic action to pull its hood over your"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "215"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 215, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.489, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "head and expend 1 charge to give yourself the Invisible condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you pull the hood down (no action required) or cease wearing the cloak."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.12, 0.286, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of Protection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.137, 0.465, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.157, 0.45, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws while you wear this cloak."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.196, 0.256, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of the Bat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.213, 0.419, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.233, 0.487, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this cloak, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. In an area of Dim Light or Darkness, you can grip the edges of the cloak and use it to gain a Fly Speed of 40 feet. If you ever fail to grip the cloak’s edges while flying in this way, or if you are no longer in Dim Light or Darkness, you lose this Fly Speed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.341, 0.482, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing the cloak in an area of Dim Light or Darkness, you can cast Polymorph on yourself, shape-shifting into a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Bat", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". While in that form, you retain your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The cloak can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.441, 0.319, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cloak of the Manta Ray"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.458, 0.491, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) While wearing this cloak, you can breathe underwater, and you have a Swim Speed of 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.517, 0.214, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crystal Ball"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.534, 0.491, 0.586], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement) While touching this crystal orb, you can cast Scrying (save DC 17) with it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.593, 0.364, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crystal Ball of Mind Reading"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.611, 0.461, 0.627], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.63, 0.488, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While touching this crystal orb, you can cast Scrying (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you can cast Detect Thoughts (save DC 17) targeting creatures you can see within 30 feet of the spell’s sensor. You don’t need to concentrate on this Detect Thoughts spell to maintain it during its duration, but it ends if the Scrying spell ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.746, 0.33, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crystal Ball of Telepathy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.764, 0.461, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.783, 0.489, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While touching this crystal orb, you can cast Scrying (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you can communicate telepathically with creatures you can see within 30 feet of the spell’s sensor. You can also cast Suggestion (save DC 17) through the sensor on one of those creatures. You don’t need to concentrate on this Suggestion to maintain it during its duration, but it ends if Scrying ends. You can’t cast Suggestion in this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.77, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Crystal Ball of True Seeing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.07, 0.913, 0.151], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement) While touching this crystal orb, you can cast Scrying (save DC 17) with it. In addition, you have Truesight with a range of 120 feet centered on the spell’s sensor."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.157, 0.659, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cube of Force"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.175, 0.841, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.195, 0.907, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This cube is about an inch across. Each face has a distinct marking on it. You can press one of those faces, expend the number of charges required for it, and thereby cast the spell associated with it (save DC 17), as shown in the Cube of Force Faces table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.272, 0.888, 0.305], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The cube starts with 10 charges, and it regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.315, 0.698, 0.331], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cube of Force Faces"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.526, 0.334, 0.91, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.526, 0.334, 0.91, 0.467], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell                                    Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Mage Armor                                   I</td></tr><tr><td>Shield                                          一</td></tr><tr><td>Tiny Hut                                       3</td></tr><tr><td>Private Sanctum                                4</td></tr><tr><td>Resilient Sphere                                4</td></tr><tr><td>Wall of Force                                   5</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.477, 0.632, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cubic Gate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.495, 0.72, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.514, 0.907, 0.591], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This cube is 3 inches across and radiates palpable magical energy. The six sides of the cube are each "}, {"type": "text", "content": "keyed", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " to a different plane of existence, one of which is the Material Plane. The other sides are linked to planes determined by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.592, 0.908, 0.653], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The cube has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. As a Magic action, you can expend 1 of the cube’s charges to cast one of the following spells using the cube."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.653, 0.905, 0.698], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gate.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Pressing one side of the cube, you cast Gate, opening a portal to the plane of existence keyed to that side."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.699, 0.902, 0.746], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plane Shift.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Pressing one side of the cube twice, you cast Plane Shift, transporting the targets to the plane of existence keyed to that side."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.754, 0.689, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dagger of Venom"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.771, 0.695, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Dagger), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.79, 0.908, 0.821], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.822, 0.909, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Bonus Action to magically coat the blade with poison. The poison remains for 1 minute or until an attack using this weapon hits a creature. That creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or take 2d10 Poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute. The weapon can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "216"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 216, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.245, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dancing Sword"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.483, 0.101], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.479, 0.196], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Bonus Action to toss this magic weapon into the air. When you do so, the weapon begins to hover, flies up to 30 feet, and attacks one creature of your choice within 5 feet of itself. The weapon uses your attack roll and adds your ability modifier to damage rolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.196, 0.485, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While the weapon hovers, you can take a Bonus Action to cause it to fly up to 30 feet to another spot within 30 feet of you. As part of the same Bonus Action, you can cause the weapon to attack one creature within 5 feet of the weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.272, 0.48, 0.395], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After the hovering weapon attacks for the fourth time, it flies back to you and tries to return to your hand. If you have no hand free, the weapon falls to the ground in your space. If the weapon has no unobstructed path to you, it moves as close to you as it can and then falls to the ground. It also ceases to hover if you grasp it or are more than 30 feet away from it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.403, 0.352, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Decanter of Endless Water"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.421, 0.302, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.44, 0.468, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This stoppered flask sloshes when shaken, as if it contains water. The decanter weighs 2 pounds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.472, 0.489, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to remove the stopper and issue one of three command words, whereupon an amount of fresh water or salt water (your choice) pours out of the flask. The water stops pouring out at the start of your next turn. Choose from the following command words:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.57, 0.486, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Splash.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The decanter produces 1 gallon of water. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Fountain.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The decanter produces 5 gallons of water. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Geyser.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The decanter produces 30 gallons of water that gushes forth in a Line 30 feet long and 1 foot wide. If you’re holding the decanter, you can aim the geyser in one direction (no action required). One creature of your choice in the Line must succeed on a DC 13 Strength saving throw or take 1d4 Bludgeoning damage and have the Prone condition. Instead of a creature, you can target one object in the Line that isn’t being worn or carried and that weighs no more than 200 pounds. The object is knocked over by the geyser."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.777, 0.257, 0.793], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deck of Illusions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.795, 0.302, 0.811], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.814, 0.487, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This box contains a set of cards. A full deck has 34 cards: 32 depicting specific creatures and two with a mirrored surface. A deck found as treasure is usually missing 1d20 − 1 cards."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.876, 0.479, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The magic of the deck functions only if its cards are drawn at random. You can take a Magic action to draw a card at random from the deck and throw"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "it to the ground at a point within 30 feet of yourself. An illusion of a creature, determined by rolling on the Deck of Illusions table, forms over the thrown card and remains until dispelled. The illusory creature created by the card looks and behaves like a real creature of its kind, except that it can do no harm. While you are within 120 feet of the illusory creature and can see it, you can take a Magic action to move it anywhere within 30 feet of its card."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.189, 0.907, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any physical interaction with the illusory creature reveals it to be false, because objects pass through it. A creature that takes a Study action to visually inspect the illusory creature identifies it as an illusion with a successful DC 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check. The illusion lasts until its card is moved or the illusion is dispelled (using a Dispel Magic spell or a similar effect). When the illusion ends, the image on its card disappears, and that card can’t be used again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.355, 0.666, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Deck of Illusions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.526, 0.373, 0.911, 0.915], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.526, 0.373, 0.911, 0.915], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Illusion*</td></tr><tr><td>01-03</td><td>Adult Red Dragon</td></tr><tr><td>04-06</td><td>Archmage</td></tr><tr><td>07-09</td><td>Assassin</td></tr><tr><td>10-12</td><td>Bandit Captain</td></tr><tr><td>13-15</td><td>Basilisk</td></tr><tr><td>16-18</td><td>Berserker</td></tr><tr><td>19-21</td><td>Bugbear Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>22-24</td><td>Cloud Giant</td></tr><tr><td>25-27</td><td>Druid</td></tr><tr><td>28-30</td><td>Erinyes</td></tr><tr><td>31-33</td><td>Ettin</td></tr><tr><td>34-36</td><td>Fire Giant</td></tr><tr><td>37-39</td><td>Frost Giant</td></tr><tr><td>40-42</td><td>Gnoll Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>43-45</td><td>Goblin Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>46-48</td><td>Guardian Naga</td></tr><tr><td>49-51</td><td>Hill Giant</td></tr><tr><td>52-54</td><td>Hobgoblin Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>55-57</td><td>Incubus</td></tr><tr><td>58-60</td><td>Iron Golem</td></tr><tr><td>61-63</td><td>Knight</td></tr><tr><td>64-66</td><td>Kobold Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>67-69</td><td>Lich</td></tr><tr><td>70-72</td><td>Medusa</td></tr><tr><td>73-75</td><td>Night Hag</td></tr><tr><td>76-78</td><td>Ogre</td></tr><tr><td>79-81</td><td>Oni</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "217"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 217, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.053, 0.489, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.053, 0.489, 0.188], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Illusion*</td></tr><tr><td>82-84</td><td>Priest</td></tr><tr><td>85-87</td><td>Succubus</td></tr><tr><td>88-90</td><td>Troll</td></tr><tr><td>91-93</td><td>Veteran Warrior</td></tr><tr><td>94-96</td><td>Wyvern</td></tr><tr><td>97-00</td><td>The card drawer</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.195, 0.487, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "*Stat blocks for these creatures (except the card drawer) appear in “Monsters.”"}]}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.233, 0.194, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Defender"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.25, 0.464, 0.281], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.286, 0.487, 0.316], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.316, 0.485, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first time you attack with the weapon on each of your turns, you can transfer some or all of the weapon’s bonus to your Armor Class. For example, you could reduce the bonus to your attack rolls and damage rolls to +1 and gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class. The adjusted bonuses remain in effect until the start of your next turn, although you must hold the weapon to gain a bonus to AC from it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.447, 0.244, 0.463], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Demon Armor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.464, 0.444, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Light, Medium, or Heavy), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.499, 0.487, 0.606], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class, and you know Abyssal. In addition, the armor’s clawed gauntlets allow your Unarmed Strikes to deal 1d8 Slashing damage instead of the usual Bludgeoning damage, and you gain a +1 bonus to the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.1, 0.607, 0.484, 0.7], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curse.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Once you don this cursed armor, you can’t doff it unless you are targeted by a Remove Curse spell or similar magic. While wearing the armor, you have Disadvantage on attack rolls against demons and on saving throws against their spells and special abilities."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.707, 0.302, 0.723], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dimensional Shackles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.725, 0.258, 0.74], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.744, 0.485, 0.882], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Utilize action to place these shackles on a creature that has the Incapacitated condition. The shackles adjust to fit a creature of Small to Large size. The shackles prevent a creature bound by them from using any method of extradimensional movement, including teleportation or travel to a different plane of existence. They don’t prevent the creature from passing through an interdimensional portal."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.882, 0.485, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You and any creature you designate when you use the shackles can take a Utilize action to remove them. Once every 30 days, the bound creature can"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "make a DC 30 Strength (Athletics) check. On a successful check, the creature breaks free and destroys the shackles."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.105, 0.641, 0.122], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragon Orb"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.122, 0.862, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.142, 0.907, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An orb is an etched crystal globe about 10 inches in diameter. When used, it grows to about 20 inches in diameter, and mist swirls inside it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.188, 0.908, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While attuned to an orb, you can take a Magic action to peer into the orb’s depths. You must then make a DC 15 Charisma saving throw. On a successful save, you control the orb for as long as you remain attuned to it. On a failed save, the orb imposes the Charmed condition on you for as long as you remain attuned to it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.295, 0.91, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you are Charmed by the orb, you can’t voluntarily end your Attunement to it, and the orb casts Suggestion on you at will (save DC 18), urging you to work toward the evil ends it desires. The dragon essence within the orb might want many things: the annihilation of a particular society or organization, freedom from the orb, to spread suffering in the world, to advance the worship of Tiamat, or something else the GM decides."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.433, 0.908, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The orb has 7 charges and regains 1d4 + 3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you control the orb, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.526, 0.515, 0.91, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.526, 0.515, 0.91, 0.642], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cure Wounds (level 9 version)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Daylight</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Death Ward</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Detect Magic</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Scrying (save DC 18)</td><td>3</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.651, 0.907, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Call Dragons.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While you control the orb, you can take a Magic action to cause the orb to issue a telepathic call that extends in all directions for 40 miles. Chromatic dragons in range feel compelled to come to the orb as soon as possible by the most direct route. Dragon deities such as Tiamat are unaffected by this call. Chromatic dragons drawn to the orb might be Hostile toward you for compelling them against their will. Once you have used this property, it can’t be used again for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.805, 0.91, 0.851], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Destroying an Orb.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Dragon Orb has AC 20 and is destroyed if it takes damage from a +3 Weapon or a Disintegrate spell. Nothing else can harm it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.858, 0.693, 0.875], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragon Scale Mail"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.875, 0.901, 0.892], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Scale Mail), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.896, 0.904, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragon Scale Mail is made of the scales of one kind of dragon. Sometimes dragons collect their cast-off"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "218"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 218, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.482, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "scales and gift them. Other times, hunters carefully preserve the hide of a dead dragon. In either case, Dragon Scale Mail is highly valued."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.485, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class, you have Advantage on saving throws against the breath weapons of Dragons, and you have Resistance to one damage type determined by the kind of dragon that provided the scales (see the accompanying table)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.189, 0.485, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Additionally, you can focus your senses as a Magic action to discern the distance and direction to the closest dragon within 30 miles of yourself that is of the same type as the armor. This action can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.105, 0.269, 0.488, 0.383], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.105, 0.269, 0.488, 0.383], "content": "<table><tr><td>Dragon</td><td>Resistance</td><td>Dragon</td><td>Resistance</td></tr><tr><td>Black</td><td>Acid</td><td>Gold</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Blue</td><td>Lightning</td><td>Green</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>Brass</td><td>Fire</td><td>Red</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Bronze</td><td>Lightning</td><td>Silver</td><td>Cold</td></tr><tr><td>Copper</td><td>Acid</td><td>White</td><td>Cold</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.394, 0.237, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragon Slayer"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.411, 0.373, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.43, 0.487, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.462, 0.457, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The weapon deals an extra 3d6 damage of the weapon’s type if the target is a Dragon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.501, 0.312, 0.517], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dust of Disappearance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.518, 0.303, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.537, 0.49, 0.692], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This powder resembles fine sand. There is enough of it for one use. When you take a Utilize action to throw the dust into the air, you and each creature and object within a 10-foot Emanation originating from you have the Invisible condition for 2d4 minutes. The duration is the same for all subjects, and the dust is consumed when its magic takes effect. Immediately after an affected creature makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell, the Invisible condition ends for that creature."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.699, 0.255, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dust of Dryness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.717, 0.302, 0.732], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.1, 0.736, 0.488, 0.89], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This small packet contains 1d6 + 4 pinches of dust. As a Utilize action, you can sprinkle a pinch of the dust over water, turning up to a 15-foot Cube of water into one marble-sized pellet, which floats or rests near where the dust was sprinkled. The pellet’s weight is negligible. A creature can take a Utilize action to smash the pellet against a hard surface, causing the pellet to shatter and release the water the dust absorbed. Doing so destroys the pellet and ends its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.89, 0.484, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can sprinkle a pinch of the dust on an Elemental within 5 feet of yourself that"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.129], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "is composed mostly of water (such as a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Water Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "). Such a creature exposed to a pinch of the dust makes a DC 13 Constitution saving throw, taking 10d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.135, 0.799, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dust of Sneezing and Choking"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.154, 0.726, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.172, 0.898, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Found in a small container, this powder resembles Dust of Disappearance, and Identify reveals it to be such. There is enough of it for one use."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.218, 0.911, 0.31], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can throw the dust into the air, forcing yourself and every creature in a 30-foot Emanation originating from you to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. Constructs, Elementals, Oozes, Plants, and Undead succeed on the save automatically."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.311, 0.911, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On a failed save, a creature begins sneezing uncontrollably; it has the Incapacitated condition and is suffocating. The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. The effect also ends on any creature targeted by a Lesser Restoration spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.41, 0.664, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarven Plate"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.428, 0.896, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Half Plate Armor or Plate Armor), Very Rare While wearing this armor, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class. In addition, if an effect moves you against your will along the ground, you can take a Reaction to reduce the distance you are moved by up to 10 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.532, 0.698, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dwarven Thrower"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.55, 0.913, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Warhammer), Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Dwarf or a Creature Attuned to a Belt of Dwarvenkind)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.6, 0.908, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. It has the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When you hit with a ranged attack using this weapon, it deals an extra 1d8 Force damage, or an extra 2d8 Force damage if the target is a Giant. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.731, 0.673, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Efficient Quiver"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.749, 0.724, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.769, 0.912, 0.892], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each of the quiver’s three compartments connects to an extradimensional space that allows the quiver to hold numerous items while never weighing more than 2 pounds. The shortest compartment can hold up to 60 Arrows, Bolts, or similar objects. The midsize compartment holds up to 18 Javelins or similar objects. The longest compartment holds up to 6 long objects, such as bows, Quarterstaffs, or Spears."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.892, 0.89, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can draw any item the quiver contains as if doing so from a regular quiver or scabbard."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.029, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "219"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 219, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.103, 0.051, 0.232, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Efreeti Bottle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.069, 0.292, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.488, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take a Magic action to remove the stopper of this painted brass bottle, a cloud of thick smoke flows out of it. At the end of your turn, the smoke disappears with a flash of harmless fire, and an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Efreeti", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.166, 0.489, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The first time the bottle is opened, the GM rolls on the following table to determine what happens."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.115, 0.201, 0.211, 0.216], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d10 Effect"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.121, 0.22, 0.47, 0.268], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The efreeti attacks you. After fighting for 5 rounds, the efreeti disappears, and the bottle loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.115, 0.272, 0.481, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "2–9 The efreeti understands your languages and obeys your commands for 1 hour, after which it returns to the bottle, and a new stopper contains it. The stopper can’t be removed for 24 hours. The next two times the bottle is opened, the same effect occurs. If the bottle is opened a fourth time, the efreeti escapes and disappears, and the bottle loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.122, 0.402, 0.485, 0.467], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "10 The efreeti understands your languages and can cast Wish once for you. It disappears when it grants the wish or after 1 hour, and the bottle loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.477, 0.248, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elemental Gem"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.495, 0.302, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.487, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This gem contains a mote of elemental energy. When you take a Utilize action to break the gem, an elemental is summoned (see “Monsters” for its stat block), and the gem ceases to be magical. The elemental appears in an unoccupied space as close to the broken gem as possible, understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The type of gem determines the elemental, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.105, 0.704, 0.488, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.105, 0.704, 0.488, 0.797], "content": "<table><tr><td>Gem</td><td>Summoned Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Blue sapphire</td><td>Air Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Emerald</td><td>Water Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Red corundum</td><td>Fire Elemental</td></tr><tr><td>Yellow diamond</td><td>Earth Elemental</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.807, 0.244, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elixir of Health"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.826, 0.196, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.845, 0.477, 0.906], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you are cured of all magical contagions. In addition, the following conditions end on you: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, and Poisoned."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.115, 0.906, 0.481, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The clear, red liquid has tiny bubbles of light in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.637, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elven Chain"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.068, 0.805, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Chain Mail or Chain Shirt), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.909, 0.15], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while you wear this armor. You are considered trained with this armor even if you lack training with Medium or Heavy armor."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.158, 0.64, 0.175], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Energy Bow"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.176, 0.904, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Longbow or Shortbow), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.211, 0.91, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, which has no string. Each time you pull your arm back in a firing motion, a magical arrow made of golden energy appears nocked and ready to fire. An arrow produced by this weapon deals Force damage instead of Piercing damage on a hit, and it disappears after it hits or misses its target. Until it disappears, the arrow emits Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.364, 0.845, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This weapon has the following additional properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.395, 0.907, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arrow of Restraint.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whenever you use this weapon to make a ranged attack against a creature, you can try to restrain the target instead of dealing damage to it. If the arrow hits, the target must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or have the Restrained condition for 1 minute. As an action, a creature Restrained by an arrow can make a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check to try to break the restraint, ending the effect on itself on a successful check."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.549, 0.91, 0.671], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Arrow of Transport.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you can fire one energy arrow from this weapon at a target you can see within 60 feet of yourself. The target can be either a willing Medium or smaller creature or an object that isn’t being worn or carried, provided the object is small enough to fit inside a 5-foot Cube. The arrow teleports the target to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.671, 0.907, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Energy Ladder.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you can loose a flurry of energy arrows from this weapon at a wall up to 60 feet away from yourself. The arrows become glowing rungs that stick out of the wall, forming a magical ladder up to 60 feet long on the wall. This ladder lasts for 1 minute before disappearing."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.771, 0.707, 0.787], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eversmoking Bottle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.525, 0.789, 0.724, 0.804], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.808, 0.902, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can open or close this bottle."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.823, 0.899, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Opening the bottle causes thick smoke to billow out, forming a cloud that fills a 60-foot Emanation originating from the bottle. The area within the smoke is Heavily Obscured."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.885, 0.899, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each minute the bottle remains open, the size of the Emanation increases by 10 feet until it reaches its maximum size of 120 feet."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "220"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 220, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.473, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Closing the bottle causes the cloud to become fixed in place until it disperses after 10 minutes. A strong wind (such as that created by the Gust of Wind spell) disperses the cloud after 1 minute."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.12, 0.267, 0.137], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eyes of Charming"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.137, 0.465, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.157, 0.484, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. They have 3 charges. While wearing them, you can expend 1 or more charges to cast Charm Person (save DC 13). For 1 charge, you cast the level 1 version of the spell. You increase the spell’s level by one for each additional charge you expend. The lenses regain all expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.272, 0.304, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eyes of Minute Seeing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.291, 0.302, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.309, 0.489, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, your vision improves significantly out to a range of 1 foot, granting you Darkvision within that range and Advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks made to examine something within that range."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.41, 0.261, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eyes of the Eagle"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.302, 0.444], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.447, 0.485, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These crystal lenses fit over the eyes. While wearing them, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. In conditions of clear visibility, you can make out details of even extremely distant creatures and objects as small as 2 feet across."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.548, 0.24, 0.564], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feather Token"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.566, 0.315, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rarity Varies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.584, 0.49, 0.662], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This object looks like a feather. Different types of feather tokens exist, each with a different single-use effect. The GM chooses the kind of token or determines it randomly by rolling on the Feather Tokens table. The type of token determines its rarity."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.662, 0.487, 0.738], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Anchor (Uncommon).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to touch the token to a boat or ship. For the next 24 hours, the vessel can’t be moved by any means. Touching the token to the vessel again ends the effect. When the effect ends, the token disappears."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.1, 0.738, 0.492, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bird (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to toss the token 5 feet into the air. The token disappears and an enormous, multicolored bird takes its place. The bird has the statistics of a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Roc", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", but it can’t attack. It obeys your simple commands and can carry up to 500 pounds while flying at its maximum speed (16 miles per hour for a maximum of 144 miles per day, with a 1-hour rest for every 3 hours of flying) or 1,000 pounds at half that speed. The bird disappears after flying its maximum distance for a day or if it drops to 0 Hit Points. You can dismiss the bird as a Magic action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.912, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fan (Uncommon).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you are on a boat or ship, you can take a Magic action to toss the token up to 10 feet in the air. The token disappears, and a giant flapping fan takes its place. The fan floats and creates a strong wind. This wind can fill the sails of one ship, increasing its speed by 5 miles per hour for 8 hours. You can dismiss the fan as a Magic action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.158, 0.907, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Swan Boat (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to touch the token to a body of water at least 60 feet in diameter. The token disappears, and a 50-footlong, 20-foot-wide boat shaped like a swan takes its place. The boat is self-propelled and moves across water at a speed of 6 miles per hour. You can take a Magic action while on the boat to command it to move or to turn up to 90 degrees. The boat remains for 24 hours and then disappears. You can dismiss the boat as a Magic action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.311, 0.907, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tree (Uncommon).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You must be outdoors to use this token. You can take a Magic action to touch it to an unoccupied space on the ground. The token disappears, and in its place a nonmagical oak tree springs into existence. The tree is 60 feet tall and has a 5-foot-diameter trunk, and its branches at the top spread out in a 20-foot radius."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.418, 0.911, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whip (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to throw the token to a point within 10 feet of yourself. The token disappears, and a floating whip takes its place. You can then take a Bonus Action to make a melee spell attack against a creature within 10 feet of the whip, with an attack bonus of +9. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 + 5 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.526, 0.91, 0.604], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can direct the whip to fly up to 20 feet and repeat the attack against a creature within 10 feet of the whip. The whip disappears after 1 hour, when you take a Magic action to dismiss it, or when you die or have the Incapacitated condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.615, 0.658, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Feather Tokens"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.526, 0.633, 0.91, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.526, 0.633, 0.91, 0.766], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Token</td><td>Rarity</td></tr><tr><td>01-20</td><td>Anchor</td><td>Uncommon</td></tr><tr><td>21-35</td><td>Bird</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>36-50</td><td>Fan</td><td>Uncommon</td></tr><tr><td>51-65</td><td>Swan boat</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>66-90</td><td>Tree</td><td>Uncommon</td></tr><tr><td>91-00</td><td>Whip</td><td>Rare</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.777, 0.788, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Figurine of Wondrous Power"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.525, 0.795, 0.738, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rarity Varies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.814, 0.906, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Figurine of Wondrous Power is a statuette small enough to fit in a pocket. If you take a Magic action to throw the figurine to a point on the ground within 60 feet of yourself, the figurine becomes a living creature specified in the figurine’s description below. If the space where the creature would appear is occupied by other creatures or objects, or"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.059, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "221"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 221, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "if there isn’t enough space for the creature, the figurine doesn’t become a creature."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.486, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature is Friendly to you and your allies. It understands your languages, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. If you issue no commands, the creature defends itself but takes no other actions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.159, 0.487, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The creature exists for a duration specific to each figurine. At the end of the duration, the creature reverts to its figurine form. It reverts to a figurine early if its creature form drops to 0 Hit Points or if you take a Magic action while touching the creature to make it revert to figurine form. When the creature becomes a figurine again, its property can’t be used again until a certain amount of time has passed, as specified in the figurine’s description."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.296, 0.489, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bronze Griffon (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This bronze statuette is of a griffon rampant. It can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Griffon", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 6 hours. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 5 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.357, 0.491, 0.435], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ebony Fly (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This ebony statuette, carved in the likeness of a horsefly, can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Fly", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (see the accompanying stat block) for up to 12 hours and can be ridden as a mount. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 2 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.104, 0.445, 0.206, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant Fly"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.464, 0.488, 0.584], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.464, 0.488, 0.584], "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"8\">Large Beast, Unaligned AC 11 Initiative +1 (11) HP 19 (3d10 + 3) Speed 30 ft., Fly 60 ft.</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\">STR 14 +2</td><td>MOD SAVE +2</td><td>Dex 13</td><td colspan=\"2\">MOD SAVE +1 +1</td><td></td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>INT 2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td>Con 13</td><td>+l</td><td>+1</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>-4</td><td>Wis 10</td><td>+0</td><td>+0</td><td>CHA 3</td><td>-4</td><td>-4</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.593, 0.415, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses Darkvision 60 ft., Passive Perception 10 Languages None"}]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.645, 0.485, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Golden Lions (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These gold statuettes of lions are always created in pairs. You can use one figurine or both simultaneously. Each can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Lion", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 1 hour. Once a lion has been used, it can’t be used again until 7 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.722, 0.488, 0.784], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ivory Goats (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These ivory statuettes of goats are always created in sets of three. Each goat looks unique and functions differently from the others. Their properties are as follows:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.79, 0.484, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goat of Terror.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This figurine can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Goat", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 3 hours. The goat can’t attack, but you can (harmlessly) remove its horns and use them as weapons. One horn becomes a +1 Lance, and the other becomes a +2 Longsword. Removing a horn requires a Magic action, and the weapons disappear and the horns return when the goat reverts to figurine form. While you ride the goat, any Hostile creature that starts its turn within"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.535, 0.051, 0.909, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "a 30-foot Emanation originating from the goat must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition for 1 minute, until you are no longer riding the goat, or until the goat reverts to figurine form. The Frightened creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Once it succeeds on the save, a creature is immune to this effect for the next 24 hours. Once the figurine has been used, it can’t be used again until 15 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.219, 0.91, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goat of Traveling.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This figurine can become a Large goat with the same statistics as a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Riding Horse", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". It has 24 charges, and each hour or portion thereof it spends in goat form costs 1 charge. While it has charges, you can use it as often as you wish. When it runs out of charges, it reverts to a figurine and can’t be used again until 7 days have passed, when it regains all expended charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.342, 0.9, 0.389], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goat of Travail.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This figurine can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Goat", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 3 hours. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 30 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.394, 0.904, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Marble Elephant (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This marble statuette resembles a trumpeting elephant. It can become an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Elephant", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 24 hours. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 7 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.456, 0.9, 0.532], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Obsidian Steed (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This polished obsidian horse can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Nightmare", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 24 hours. The nightmare fights only to defend itself. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 5 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.532, 0.894, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The figurine has a 10 percent chance each time you use it to ignore your orders, including a command to revert to figurine form. If you mount the nightmare while it is ignoring your orders, you and the nightmare are instantly transported to a random location on the plane of Hades, where the nightmare reverts to figurine form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.64, 0.908, 0.732], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Onyx Dog (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This onyx statuette of a dog can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mastiff", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 6 hours. The mastiff has an Intelligence of 8 and can speak Common. It also has Blindsight with a range of 60 feet. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 7 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.732, 0.91, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Serpentine Owl (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This serpentine statuette of an owl can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Owl", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 8 hours. The owl can communicate telepathically with you at any range if you and it are on the same plane of existence. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 2 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.823, 0.912, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Silver Raven (Uncommon).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This silver statuette of a raven can become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Raven", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " for up to 12 hours. Once it has been used, it can’t be used again until 2 days have passed. While in raven form, the figurine grants you the ability to cast Animal Messenger on it."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "222"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 222, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.235, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flame Tongue"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.422, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Melee Weapon), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.104, 0.484, 0.244], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this magic weapon, you can take a Bonus Action and use a command word to cause flames to engulf the damage-dealing part of the weapon. These flames shed Bright Light in a 40- foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 40 feet. While the weapon is ablaze, it deals an extra 2d6 Fire damage on a hit. The flames last until you take a Bonus Action to issue the command again or until you drop, stow, or sheathe the weapon."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.223, 0.267], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Folding Boat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.268, 0.257, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.287, 0.483, 0.366], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This object appears as a wooden box that measures 12 inches long, 6 inches wide, and 6 inches deep. It weighs 4 pounds and floats. It can be opened to store items inside. This item also has three command words, each requiring a Magic action to use:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.371, 0.447, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "First Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The box unfolds into a Rowboat."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.402, 0.465, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Second Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The box unfolds into a Keelboat."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.432, 0.489, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Third Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Folding Boat folds back into a box if no creatures are aboard. Any objects in the vessel that can’t fit inside the box remain outside the box as it folds. Any objects in the vessel that can fit inside the box do so."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.515, 0.483, 0.562], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the box becomes a vessel, its weight becomes that of a normal vessel its size, and anything that was stored in the box remains in the boat."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.562, 0.472, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Statistics for the Rowboat and Keelboat appear in “Equipment.” If either vessel is reduced to 0 Hit Points, the Folding Boat is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.616, 0.216, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Frost Brand"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.633, 0.447, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.684, 0.486, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you hit with an attack roll using this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 1d6 Cold damage. In addition, while you hold the weapon, you have Resistance to Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.745, 0.487, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In freezing temperatures, the weapon sheds Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 10 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.791, 0.476, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you draw this weapon, you can extinguish all nonmagical flames within 30 feet of yourself. Once used, this property can’t be used again for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.756, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gauntlets of Ogre Power"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.887, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.904, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Your Strength is 19 while you wear these gauntlets. They have no effect on you if your Strength is 19 or higher without them."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.143, 0.698, 0.16], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gem of Brightness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.16, 0.724, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.179, 0.901, 0.241], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This prism has 50 charges. While you are holding it, you can take a Magic action and use one of three command words to cause one of the following effects:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.248, 0.908, 0.34], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "First Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The gem sheds Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. This effect doesn’t expend a charge. It lasts until you take a Bonus Action to repeat the command word or until you use another function of the gem."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.341, 0.908, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Second Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You expend 1 charge and cause the gem to fire a brilliant beam of light at one creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself. The creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Blinded condition for 1 minute. The creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.463, 0.904, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Third Command Word.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You expend 5 charges and cause the gem to flare with intense light in a 30- foot Cone. Each creature in the Cone makes a saving throw as if struck by the beam created with the second command word."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.546, 0.88, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When all of the gem’s charges are expended, the gem becomes a nonmagical jewel worth 50 GP."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.585, 0.662, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gem of Seeing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.602, 0.841, 0.619], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.623, 0.912, 0.684], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This gem has 3 charges. As a Magic action, you can expend 1 charge. For the next 10 minutes, you have Truesight out to 120 feet when you peer through the gem."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.684, 0.89, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The gem regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.722, 0.641, 0.739], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant Slayer"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.74, 0.795, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.76, 0.908, 0.791], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.791, 0.912, 0.853], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you hit a Giant with this weapon, the Giant takes an extra 2d6 damage of the weapon’s type and must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or have the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.86, 0.788, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Glamoured Studded Leather"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.878, 0.796, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Studded Leather Armor), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.897, 0.888, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this armor, you gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class. You can also take a Bonus Action to"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "223"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 223, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.487, 0.144], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "cause the armor to assume the appearance of a normal set of clothing or some other kind of armor. You decide what it looks like—including color, style, and accessories—but the armor retains its normal bulk and weight. The illusory appearance lasts until you use this property again or doff the armor."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.15, 0.332, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gloves of Missile Snaring"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.168, 0.465, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.188, 0.49, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you’re hit by an attack roll made with a Ranged or Thrown weapon while wearing these gloves, you can take a Reaction to reduce the damage by 1d10 plus your Dexterity modifier if you have a free hand. If you reduce the damage to 0, you can catch the ammunition or weapon if it is small enough for you to hold in that hand."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.303, 0.413, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gloves of Swimming and Climbing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.321, 0.465, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.34, 0.488, 0.403], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing these gloves, you have a Climb Speed and a Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and you gain a +5 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to climb or swim."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.41, 0.278, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gloves of Thievery"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.302, 0.444], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.447, 0.474, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These gloves are imperceptible while worn. While wearing them, you gain a +5 bonus to Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.502, 0.261, 0.519], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Goggles of Night"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.52, 0.302, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.538, 0.478, 0.587], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing these dark lenses, you have Darkvision out to 60 feet. If you already have Darkvision, wearing the goggles increases its range by 60 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.594, 0.339, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hammer of Thunderbolts"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.611, 0.481, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Maul or Warhammer), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.646, 0.486, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.677, 0.483, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The weapon has 5 charges. You can expend 1 charge and make a ranged attack with the weapon, hurling it as if it had the Thrown property with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the attack hits, the weapon unleashes a thunderclap audible out to 300 feet. The target and every creature within 30 feet of it other than you must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or have the Stunned condition until the end of your next turn. Immediately after hitting or missing, the weapon flies back to your hand. The weapon regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.861, 0.48, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giant’s Bane.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While you are attuned to the weapon and wearing either a Belt of Giant Strength or Gauntlets of Ogre Power to which you are also attuned, you gain the following benefits:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.91, 0.111], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giants’ Bane.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you roll a 20 on the d20 for an attack roll made with this weapon against a Giant, the creature must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.112, 0.893, 0.158], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Might of Giants.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Strength score bestowed by your Belt of Giant Strength or Gauntlets of Ogre Power increases by 4, to a maximum of 30."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.166, 0.687, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Handy Haversack"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.183, 0.679, 0.199], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.203, 0.91, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This backpack has a central pouch and two side pouches, each of which is an extradimensional space. Each side pouch can hold up to 200 pounds of material, not exceeding a volume of 25 cubic feet. The central pouch can hold up to 500 pounds of material, not exceeding a volume of 64 cubic feet. The haversack always weighs 5 pounds, regardless of its contents."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.326, 0.91, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Retrieving an item from the haversack requires a Utilize action or a Bonus Action (your choice). When you reach into the haversack for a specific item, the item is always magically on top."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.388, 0.909, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If any of its pouches is overloaded, pierced, or torn, the haversack ruptures and is destroyed. If the haversack is destroyed, its contents are lost forever, although an Artifact always turns up again somewhere. If the haversack is turned inside out, its contents spill forth unharmed, and the haversack must be put right before it can be used again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.495, 0.902, 0.541], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each pouch of the haversack holds enough air for 10 minutes of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.541, 0.909, 0.695], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Placing the haversack inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, Portable Hole, or similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. The gate originates where the one item was placed inside the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate and not behind Total Cover is sucked through it and deposited in a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes. The gate is one-way only and can’t be reopened."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.702, 0.667, 0.719], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hat of Disguise"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.72, 0.887, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) While wearing this hat, you can cast the Disguise Self spell. The spell ends if the hat is removed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.778, 0.698, 0.795], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hat of Many Spells"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.796, 0.903, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.83, 0.864, 0.846], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This pointed hat has the following properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.522, 0.846, 0.913, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting Focus.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the hat, you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus for your Wizard spells. Any spell you cast using the hat gains a special Somatic component: you must reach into the hat and “pull” the spell out of it."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "224"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 224, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.488, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unknown Spell.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the hat, you can try to cast a level 1+ spell you don’t know. The spell must be on the Wizard spell list, it must be of a level you can cast, and it can’t have Material components costing more than 1,000 GP. Once you decide on the spell, you must expend a spell slot of the spell’s level. Then, to determine whether you cast the spell, make an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC 10 plus the spell’s level). On a successful check, you cast the spell using its normal casting time, and you can’t use this property again until you finish a Short or Long Rest. On a failed check, you fail to cast the spell and a random effect occurs instead, determined by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.265, 0.461, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any spell you cast from the hat uses your spell save DC and spell attack bonus."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.11, 0.301, 0.217, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d100 Effect", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.106, 0.313, 0.487, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.106, 0.313, 0.487, 0.755], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>01-50</td><td>You cast a random spell determined by rolling</td></tr><tr><td>51-55</td><td>1d10: on a 1, Enlarge/Reduce (enlarge effect); on a 2, Enlarge/Reduce (reduce effect); on a 3, Faerie Fire; on a 4, Fireball; on a 5, Gust of Wind; on a 6, Invisibility (cast on yourself); on a 7, Lightning Bolt; on an 8, Phantasmal Force; on a 9, Polymorph; on a 10, Stinking Cloud. You have the Stunned condition until the end of your next turn, believing something awe-some just happened.</td></tr><tr><td>56-60</td><td>A harmless swarm of butterflies fills a 10-foot Cube within 30 feet of yourself. The swarm disperses after 1 minute.</td></tr><tr><td>61-65</td><td>You pull a nonmagical object out of the hat. Roll 1d4 to determine the object: on a 1, a vial of Acid; on a 2, a flask of Alchemist's Fire; on a 3, a Crowbar; on a 4, a lit Torch.</td></tr><tr><td>66-70</td><td>You suffer a bout of \"magic sickness\" and have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour.</td></tr><tr><td>71-75</td><td>You have the Petrified condition until the end of your next turn.</td></tr><tr><td>76-80</td><td>You pull a nonmagical object out of the hat. Roll 1d4 to determine the object: on a 1, a Dagger; on a 2, a Rope with a Grappling Hook tied to one end; on a 3, a bag of Caltrops; on a 4, a gem worth 50 GP.</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.107, 0.76, 0.482, 0.887], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "81–85 A creature appears in an unoccupied space as close to you as possible. The creature isn’t under your control and acts as it normally would, and it disappears after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 Hit Points. Roll 1d4 to determine the creature: on a 1, a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Camel", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "; on a 2, a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Constrictor Snake", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "; on a 3, an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Elephant", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "; on a 4, a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Mule", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.532, 0.056, 0.638, 0.07], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "1d100 Effect", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.53, 0.074, 0.89, 0.107], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "86–90 A Hostile "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Swarm of Bats", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " flies out of the hat, occupies your space, and attacks you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.529, 0.11, 0.896, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "91–95 A vertical, 10-foot-diameter, two-way portal to another plane of existence opens in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of you and remains open until the end of your next turn. The GM determines where it leads."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.528, 0.193, 0.905, 0.29], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "96–00 You pull a magic item out of the hat. Roll 1d6 to determine the item’s rarity: on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "1–3", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", Common; on a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "4–5", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", Uncommon; on a 6, Rare. The GM chooses the item, which disappears after 1 hour if it’s not consumed or destroyed before then."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.524, 0.3, 0.724, 0.315], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Headband of Intellect"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.523, 0.318, 0.891, 0.384], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) Your Intelligence is 19 while you wear this headband. It has no effect on you if your Intelligence is 19 or higher without it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.391, 0.692, 0.407], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Helm of Brilliance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.523, 0.41, 0.91, 0.49], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement) This helm is set with 1d10 diamonds, 2d10 rubies, 3d10 fire opals, and 4d10 opals. Any gem pried from the helm crumbles to dust. When all the gems are removed or destroyed, the helm loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.49, 0.905, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain the following benefits while wearing the helm."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.523, 0.521, 0.892, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Diamond Light.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As long as it has at least one diamond, the helm emits a 30-foot Emanation. When at least one Undead is within that area, the Emanation is filled with Dim Light. Any Undead that starts its turn in that area takes 1d6 Radiant damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.91, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire Opal Flames.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As long as the helm has at least one fire opal, you can take a Magic action to cause one weapon you are holding to burst into flames. The flames emit Bright Light in a 10-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 10 feet. The flames are harmless to you and the weapon. When you hit with an attack using the blazing weapon, the target takes an extra 1d6 Fire damage. The flames last until you take a Bonus Action to extinguish them or until you drop or stow the weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.766, 0.903, 0.797], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ruby Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As long as the helm has at least one ruby, you have Resistance to Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.797, 0.914, 0.888], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can cast one of the following spells (save DC 18), using one of the helm’s gems of the specified type as a component: Daylight (opal), Fireball (fire opal), Prismatic Spray (diamond), or Wall of Fire (ruby). The gem is destroyed when the spell is cast and disappears from the helm."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.889, 0.913, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Taking Fire Damage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Roll 1d20 if you are wearing the helm and take Fire damage as a result of failing"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "225"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 225, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.484, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "a saving throw against a spell. On a roll of 1, the helm emits beams of light from its remaining gems and is then destroyed. Each creature within a 60- foot Emanation originating from you must succeed on a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw or be struck by a beam, taking Radiant damage equal to the number of gems in the helm."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.166, 0.428, 0.199], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Helm of Comprehending Languages Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.203, 0.479, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this helm, you can cast Comprehend Languages from it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.242, 0.274, 0.259], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Helm of Telepathy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.259, 0.465, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.279, 0.483, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this helm, you have telepathy with a range of 30 feet, and you can cast Detect Thoughts or Suggestion (save DC 13) from the helm. Once either spell is cast from the helm, that spell can’t be cast from it again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.365, 0.31, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Helm of Teleportation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.382, 0.419, 0.398], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.401, 0.478, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This helm has 3 charges. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Teleport from it. The helm regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.457, 0.232, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Avenger"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.473, 0.485, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.509, 0.488, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit a Fiend or an Undead with it, that creature takes an extra 2d10 Radiant damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.57, 0.49, 0.678], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you hold the drawn weapon, it creates a 10-foot Emanation originating from you. You and all creatures Friendly to you in the Emanation have Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects. If you have 17 or more levels in the Paladin class, the size of the Emanation increases to 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.685, 0.256, 0.702], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Horn of Blasting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.103, 0.703, 0.257, 0.719], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.722, 0.485, 0.878], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to blow the horn, which emits a thunderous blast in a 30-foot Cone that is audible out to 600 feet. Each creature in the Cone makes a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 5d8 Thunder damage and has the Deafened condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. Glass or crystal objects in the Cone that aren’t being worn or carried take 10d8 Thunder damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.887, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each use of the horn’s magic has a 20 percent chance of causing the horn to explode. The explosion deals 10d6 Force damage to the user and destroys the horn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.676, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Horn of Valhalla"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.137, 0.868, 0.17], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Silver or Brass), Very Rare (Bronze), or Legendary (Iron)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.172, 0.911, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to blow this horn. In response, warrior spirits from the plane of Ysgard appear in unoccupied spaces within 60 feet of you. Each spirit uses the "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Berserker", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " stat block and returns to Ysgard after 1 hour or when it drops to 0 Hit Points. The spirits look like living, breathing warriors, and they have Immunity to the Charmed and Frightened conditions. Once you use the horn, it can’t be used again until 7 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.311, 0.904, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Four types of Horn of Valhalla are known to exist, each made of a different metal. The horn’s type determines how many spirits it summons, as well as the requirement for its use. The GM chooses the horn’s type or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.403, 0.905, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you blow the horn without meeting its requirement, the summoned spirits attack you. If you meet the requirement, they are Friendly to you and your allies and follow your commands."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.469, 0.909, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.525, 0.469, 0.909, 0.61], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Horn Type</td><td>Spirits</td><td>Requirement</td></tr><tr><td>01-40</td><td>Silver</td><td>2</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>41-75</td><td>Brass</td><td>3</td><td>Proficiency with all Simple weapons</td></tr><tr><td>76-90</td><td>Bronze</td><td>4</td><td>Training with all Medium armor</td></tr><tr><td>91-00</td><td>Iron</td><td>5</td><td>Proficiency with all Martial weapons</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.621, 0.744, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Horseshoes of a Zephyr"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.525, 0.639, 0.715, 0.654], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.658, 0.898, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These horseshoes come in a set of four. As a Magic action, you can touch one of the horseshoes to the hoof of a horse or similar creature, whereupon the horseshoe affixes itself to the hoof. Removing a horseshoe also takes a Magic action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.735, 0.903, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While all four shoes are affixed to the hooves of a horse or similar creature, they allow the creature to move normally while floating 4 inches above a surface. This effect means the creature can cross or stand above nonsolid or unstable surfaces, such as water or lava. The creature leaves no tracks and ignores Difficult Terrain. In addition, the creature can travel for up to 12 hours a day without gaining Exhaustion levels from extended travel."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "226"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 226, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.298, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Horseshoes of Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.069, 0.258, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.476, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These horseshoes come in a set of four. As a Magic action, you can touch one of the horseshoes to the hoof of a horse or similar creature, whereupon the horseshoe affixes itself to the hoof. Removing a horseshoe also takes a Magic action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.166, 0.459, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While all four horseshoes are attached to the same creature, its Speed is increased by 30 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.204, 0.249, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immovable Rod"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.222, 0.223, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.242, 0.49, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This iron rod has a button on one end. You can take a Utilize action to press the button, which causes the rod to become magically fixed in place. Until you or another creature takes a Utilize action to push the button again, the rod doesn’t move, even if it defies gravity. The rod can hold up to 8,000 pounds of weight. More weight causes the rod to deactivate and fall. A creature can take a Utilize action to make a DC 30 Strength (Athletics) check, moving the fixed rod up to 10 feet on a successful check."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.403, 0.252, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instant Fortress"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.421, 0.419, 0.436], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.44, 0.483, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can place this 1-inch adamantine statuette on the ground and, using a command word, cause it to grow rapidly into a square adamantine tower. Repeating the command word causes the tower to revert to statuette form, which works only if the tower is empty. Each creature in the area where the tower appears is pushed to an unoccupied space outside but next to the tower. Objects in the area that aren’t being worn or carried are also pushed clear of the tower."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.594, 0.485, 0.747], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The tower is 20 feet on a side and 30 feet high, with arrow slits on all sides and a battlement atop it. Its interior is divided into two floors, with a ladder, staircase, or ramp (your choice) connecting them. This ladder, staircase, or ramp ends at a trapdoor leading to the roof. When created, the tower has a single door at ground level on the side facing you. The door opens only at your command, which you can issue as a Bonus Action. It is immune to the Knock spell and similar magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.747, 0.482, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic prevents the tower from being tipped over. The roof, the door, and the walls each have AC 20; HP 100; Immunity to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage except that which is dealt by siege equipment; and Resistance to all other damage. Shrinking the tower back down to statuette form doesn’t repair damage to the tower. Only a Wish spell can repair the tower (this use of the spell counts as replicating a spell of level 8 or lower). Each casting of Wish causes the tower to regain all its Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.628, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ioun Stone"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.9, 0.15], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rarity Varies (Requires Attunement) Roughly marble sized, Ioun Stones are named after Ioun, a god of knowledge and prophecy revered on some worlds. Many types of Ioun Stones exist, each type a distinct combination of shape and color."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.15, 0.908, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you take a Magic action to toss an Ioun Stone into the air, the stone orbits your head at a distance of 1d3 feet, conferring its benefit to you while doing so. You can have up to three Ioun Stones orbiting your head at the same time."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.227, 0.909, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each Ioun Stone orbiting your head is considered to be an object you are wearing. The orbiting stone avoids contact with other creatures and objects, adjusting its orbit to avoid collisions and thwarting all attempts by other creatures to attack or snatch it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.304, 0.892, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Utilize action, you can seize and stow any number of Ioun Stones orbiting your head. If your Attunement to an Ioun Stone ends while it’s orbiting your head, the stone falls as though you had dropped it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.38, 0.858, 0.41], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The type of stone determines its rarity and effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.411, 0.906, 0.517], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Absorption (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While this pale lavender ellipsoid orbits your head, you can take a Reaction to cancel a spell of level 4 or lower cast by a creature you can see. A canceled spell has no effect, and any resources used to cast it are wasted. Once the stone has canceled 20 levels of spells, it burns out, turns dull gray, and loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.518, 0.898, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Agility (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this deep-red sphere orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.564, 0.911, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Awareness (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While this dark-blue rhomboid orbits your head, you have Advantage on Initiative rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.61, 0.89, 0.656], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fortitude (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this pink rhomboid orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.656, 0.91, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Greater Absorption (Legendary).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While this marbled lavender and green ellipsoid orbits your head, you can take a Reaction to cancel a spell of level 8 or lower cast by a creature you can see. A canceled spell has no effect, and any resources used to cast it are wasted. Once the stone has canceled 20 levels of spells, it burns out, turns dull gray, and loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.778, 0.907, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Insight (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this incandescent blue sphere orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.824, 0.912, 0.87], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Intellect (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Intelligence increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this marbled scarlet and blue sphere orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.87, 0.911, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Leadership (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Charisma increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this marbled pink and green sphere orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "227"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 227, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.487, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mastery (Legendary).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Proficiency Bonus increases by 1 while this pale green prism orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.481, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protection (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class while this dusty-rose prism orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.128, 0.478, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regeneration (Legendary).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You regain 15 Hit Points at the end of each hour this pearly white spindle orbits your head if you have at least 1 Hit Point."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.189, 0.485, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reserve (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This vibrant purple prism stores spells cast into it, holding them until you use them. The stone can store up to 4 levels of spells at a time. When found, it contains 1d4 levels of stored spells chosen by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.265, 0.487, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature can cast a spell of level 1 through 4 into the stone by touching it as the spell is cast. The spell has no effect, other than to be stored in the stone. If the stone can’t hold the spell, the spell is expended without effect. The level of the slot used to cast the spell determines how much space it uses."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.358, 0.485, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While this stone orbits your head, you can cast any spell stored in it. The spell uses the slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability of the original caster but is otherwise treated as if you cast the spell. The spell cast from the stone is no longer stored in it, freeing up s"}, {"type": "text", "content": "pace", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.449, 0.485, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Strength (Very Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, while this pale blue rhomboid orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.495, 0.485, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sustenance (Rare).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You don’t need to eat or drink while this clear spindle orbits your head."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.534, 0.206, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Iron Bands"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.551, 0.257, 0.566], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.571, 0.488, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This rusty iron sphere measures 3 inches in diameter and weighs 1 pound. You can take a Magic action to throw the sphere at a Huge or smaller creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself. As the sphere moves through the air, it opens into a tangle of metal bands."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.663, 0.489, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a ranged attack roll with an attack bonus equal to your Dexterity modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. On a hit, the target has the Restrained condition until you take a Bonus Action to issue a command that releases it. Doing so or missing with the attack causes the bands to contract and become a sphere once more."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.771, 0.489, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A creature that can touch the bands, including the one Restrained, can take an action to make a DC 20 Strength (Athletics) check to break the iron bands. On a successful check, the item is destroyed, and the Restrained creature is freed. On a failed check, any further attempts made by that creature a"}, {"type": "text", "content": "utomati", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "cally fail until 24 hours have elapsed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.878, 0.482, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once the bands are used, they can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.619, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Iron Flask"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.72, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.912, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this brass-stoppered iron flask, you can take a Magic action to target a creature that you can see within 60 feet of yourself. If the flask is empty and the target is native to a plane of existence other than the one you’re on, the target must succeed on a DC 17 Wisdom saving throw or be trapped in the flask. If the target has been trapped by the flask before, it has Advantage on the save. Once trapped, a creature remains in the flask until released. The flask can hold only one creature at a time. A creature trapped in the flask doesn’t age and doesn’t need to breathe, eat, or drink."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.273, 0.91, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to remove the flask’s stopper and release the creature in the flask. The creature then obeys your commands for 1 hour, understanding those commands even if it doesn’t know the language in which the commands are given. If you issue no commands or give the creature a command that is likely to result in its death or imprisonment, it defends itself but otherwise takes no actions. At the end of the duration, the creature acts in accordance with its normal disposition and alignment."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.441, 0.904, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An Identify spell reveals if the flask contains a creature, but the only way to determine the type of creature is to open the flask. A newly discovered Iron Flask might already contain a creature chosen by the GM."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.526, 0.7, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Javelin of Lightning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.544, 0.736, 0.559], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Javelin), Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.563, 0.91, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each time you make an attack roll with this magic weapon and hit, you can have it deal Lightning damage instead of Piercing damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.61, 0.908, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning Bolt.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you throw this weapon at a target no farther than 120 feet from you, you can forgo making a ranged attack roll and instead turn the weapon into a bolt of lightning. This bolt forms a 5-foot-wide Line between you and the target. The target and each other creature in the Line (excluding you) makes a DC 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 4d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. Immediately after dealing this damage, the weapon reappears in your hand. This property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.801, 0.723, 0.834], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lantern of Revealing Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.838, 0.91, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While lit, this hooded lantern burns for 6 hours on 1 pint of oil, shedding Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet. Invisible creatures and objects are visible as long as they are in the lantern’s Bright Light. You can take a Utilize"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "228"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 228, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.491, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "action to lower the hood, reducing the lantern’s light to Dim Light in a 5-foot radius."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.207, 0.105], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Luck Blade"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.107, 0.482, 0.153], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, Sickle, or Shortsword), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.157, 0.486, 0.218], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. While the weapon is on your person, you also gain a +1 bonus to saving throws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.488, 0.295], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Luck.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the weapon is on your person, you can call on its luck (no action required) to reroll one failed D20 Test if you don’t have the Incapacitated condition. You must use the second roll. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.296, 0.488, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wish.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The weapon has 1d3 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge and cast Wish from it. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn. The weapon loses this property if it has no charges."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.38, 0.281, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mace of Disruption"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.397, 0.421, 0.414], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Mace), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.417, 0.484, 0.525], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you hit a Fiend or an Undead with this magic weapon, that creature takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage. If the target has 25 Hit Points or fewer after taking this damage, it must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or be destroyed. On a successful save, the creature has the Frightened condition until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.525, 0.486, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Light.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While you hold this weapon, it sheds Bright Light in a 20-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 20 feet."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.579, 0.253, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mace of Smiting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.597, 0.259, 0.613], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Mace), Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.616, 0.477, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The bonus increases to +3 when you use the weapon to attack a Construct."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.677, 0.481, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you roll a 20 on an attack roll made with this weapon, the target takes an extra 7 Bludgeoning damage, or 14 Bludgeoning damage if it’s a Construct. If a Construct has 25 Hit Points or fewer after taking this damage, it is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.762, 0.245, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mace of Terror"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.78, 0.421, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Mace), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.8, 0.475, 0.909], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This magic weapon has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding the weapon, you can take a Magic action and expend 1 charge to release a wave of terror from it. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition for 1 minute. While"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.907, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Frightened in this way, a creature must spend its turns trying to move as far away from you as it can, and it can’t make Opportunity Attacks. For its action, it can use only the Dash action or try to escape from an effect that prevents it from moving. If it has nowhere it can move, the creature can take the Dodge action. At the end of each of its turns, a creature repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.196, 0.765, 0.213], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mantle of Spell Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.214, 0.841, 0.23], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.234, 0.911, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Advantage on saving throws against spells while you wear this cloak."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.272, 0.745, 0.289], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Manual of Bodily Health"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.291, 0.715, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.31, 0.902, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book contains health and nutrition tips, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Constitution increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.425, 0.767, 0.442], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Manual of Gainful Exercise"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.443, 0.715, 0.459], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.463, 0.91, 0.556], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book describes fitness exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.563, 0.693, 0.579], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Manual of Golems"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.581, 0.714, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.6, 0.91, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This tome contains information and incantations necessary to make a particular type of golem. The GM chooses the type or determines it randomly by rolling on the accompanying table. To decipher and use the manual, you must be a spellcaster with at least two level 5 spell slots. A creature that can’t use a Manual of Golems and attempts to read it takes 6d6 Psychic damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.523, 0.723, 0.91, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To create a golem, you must spend the time shown on the table, working without interruption with the manual at hand and resting no more than 8 hours per day. You must also pay the specified cost to purchase supplies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.8, 0.913, 0.893], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once you finish creating the golem, the book is consumed in eldritch flames. The golem becomes animate when the ashes of the manual are sprinkled on it. See “Monsters” for the golem’s stat block. The golem is under your control, and it understands and obeys your commands."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "229"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 229, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.479, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.479, 0.149], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id20</td><td>Time Golem</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>1-5</td><td>30 days Clay Golem</td><td>65,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>6-17</td><td>60 days Flesh Golem</td><td>50,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>I20 days Iron Golem</td><td>100,000 GP</td></tr><tr><td>19-20</td><td>90 days Stone Golem</td><td>80,000 GP</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.16, 0.382, 0.193], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Manual of Quickness of Action Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.197, 0.475, 0.306], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book contains coordination and balance exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.313, 0.29, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Marvelous Pigments"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.331, 0.292, 0.346], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.349, 0.48, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This fine wooden box contains 1d4 pots of pigment and a brush (weighing 1 pound in total)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.381, 0.484, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Using the brush and expending 1 pot of pigment, you can paint any number of three-dimensional objects and terrain features (such as walls, doors, trees, flowers, weapons, webs, and pits), provided these elements are all confined to a 20-foot Cube. The effort takes 10 minutes (regardless of the number of elements you create), during which time you must remain in the Cube, and requires Concentration. If your Concentration is broken or you leave the Cube before the work is done, all the painted elements vanish, and the pot of pigment is wasted."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.549, 0.489, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the work is done, all the painted objects and terrain features become real. Thus, painting a door on a wall creates an actual door, which can be opened to whatever is beyond. Painting a pit creates a real pit, the entire depth of which must lie within the 20-foot Cube."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.641, 0.487, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "No object created by a pot of pigment can have a value greater than 25 GP, and the total value of all objects created by a pot of pigment can’t exceed 500 GP. If you paint objects of greater value (such as a large pile of gold), they look authentic, but close inspection reveals they’re made from paste, cookies, or some other worthless material."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.749, 0.484, 0.796], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you paint a form of energy such as fire or lightning, the energy dissipates as soon as you complete the painting, doing no harm."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.802, 0.308, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Medallion of Thoughts"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.82, 0.465, 0.836], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.84, 0.49, 0.903], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The medallion has 5 charges. While wearing it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Detect Thoughts (save DC 13) from it. The medallion regains 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.737, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mirror of Life Trapping Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.904, 0.181], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When this 4-foot-tall, 2-foot-wide mirror is viewed indirectly, its surface shows faint images of creatures. The mirror weighs 50 pounds, and it has AC 11, HP 10, Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage, and Vulnerability to Bludgeoning damage. It shatters and is destroyed when reduced to 0 Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.181, 0.907, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the mirror is hanging on a vertical surface and you are within 5 feet of it, you can take a Magic action and use a command word to activate it. It remains activated until you take a Magic action and repeat the command word to deactivate it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.257, 0.908, 0.38], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature other than you that sees its reflection in the activated mirror while within 30 feet of the mirror must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma saving throw or be trapped, along with anything it is wearing or carrying, in one of the mirror’s twelve extradimensional cells. A creature that knows the mirror’s nature makes the save with Advantage, and Constructs succeed on the save automatically."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.38, 0.892, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An extradimensional cell is an infinite expanse filled with thick fog that reduces visibility to 10 feet. Creatures trapped in the mirror’s cells don’t age, and they don’t need to eat, drink, or sleep. A creature trapped within a cell can escape using magic that permits planar travel. Otherwise, the creature is confined to the cell until freed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.487, 0.907, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the mirror traps a creature but its twelve extradimensional cells are already occupied, the mirror frees one trapped creature at random to accommodate the new prisoner. A freed creature appears in an unoccupied space within sight of the mirror but facing away from it. If the mirror is shattered, all creatures it contains are freed and appear in unoccupied spaces near it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.61, 0.908, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While within 5 feet of the mirror, you can take a Magic action to name one creature trapped in it or call out a particular cell by number. The creature named or contained in the named cell appears as an image on the mirror’s surface. You and the creature can then communicate."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.702, 0.903, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In a similar way, you can take a Magic action and use a second command word to free one creature trapped in the mirror. The freed creature appears, along with its possessions, in the unoccupied space nearest to the mirror and facing away from it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.778, 0.91, 0.918], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Placing the mirror inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, Portable Hole, or similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. The gate originates where the one item was placed inside the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate and not behind Total Cover is sucked through it to a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes. The gate is one-way only and can’t be reopened."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "230"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 230, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.241, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mithral Armor"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.068, 0.461, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Any Medium or Heavy, Except Hide Armor), Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.489, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mithral is a light, flexible metal. Armor made of this substance can be worn under normal clothes. If the armor normally imposes Disadvantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks or has a Strength requirement, the mithral version of the armor doesn’t."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.189, 0.261, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mysterious Deck"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.206, 0.299, 0.222], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.225, 0.486, 0.318], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Usually found in a box or pouch, this deck contains a number of cards made of ivory or vellum. Most (75 percent) of these decks have thirteen cards, but some have twenty-two. Use the appropriate column of the Mysterious Deck table when randomly determining cards drawn from the deck."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.318, 0.488, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Before you draw a card, you must declare how many cards you intend to draw and then draw them randomly. Any cards drawn in excess of this number have no effect. Otherwise, as soon as you draw a card from the deck, its magic takes effect. You must draw each card no more than 1 hour after the pre-vious draw. If you fail to draw the chosen number, the remaining number of cards fly from the deck on their own and take effect all at once."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.456, 0.48, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once a card is drawn, it disappears. Unless the card is the Fool or Jester, the card reappears in the deck, making it possible to draw the same card twice. (Once the Fool or Jester has left the deck, reroll on the table if that card comes up again.)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.546, 0.247, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mysterious Deck"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.104, 0.561, 0.489, 0.919], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.104, 0.561, 0.489, 0.919], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00 (13-Card Deck)</td><td>IdI00 (22-Card Deck)</td><td>Card</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>01-05</td><td>Balance</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>06-10</td><td>Comet</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>11-14</td><td>Donjon</td></tr><tr><td>01-08</td><td>15-18</td><td>Euryale</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>19-23</td><td>Fates</td></tr><tr><td>09-16</td><td>24-27</td><td>Flames</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>28-31</td><td>Fool</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>32-36</td><td>Gem</td></tr><tr><td>17-24</td><td>37-41</td><td>Jester</td></tr><tr><td>25-32</td><td>42-46</td><td>Key</td></tr><tr><td>33-40</td><td>47-51</td><td>Knight</td></tr><tr><td>41-48</td><td>52-56</td><td>Moon</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>57-60</td><td>Puzzle</td></tr><tr><td>49-56</td><td>61-64</td><td>Rogue</td></tr><tr><td>57-64</td><td>65-68</td><td>Ruin</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>69-73</td><td>Sage</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.525, 0.054, 0.91, 0.214], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.525, 0.054, 0.91, 0.214], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00 (13-Card Deck)</td><td>IdI00 (22-Card Card Deck)</td></tr><tr><td>74-77 65-72</td><td>Skull</td></tr><tr><td>73-80</td><td>Star 78-82</td></tr><tr><td>81-88</td><td>Sun 83-87</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>88-91 Talons</td></tr><tr><td>89-96</td><td>92-96 Throne</td></tr><tr><td>97-00</td><td>97-00 Void</td></tr></table>"}, {"type": "table_footnote", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.537, 0.224, 0.815, 0.239], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each card’s effect is described below."}]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.24, 0.903, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Balance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can increase one of your ability scores by 2, to a maximum of 22, provided you also decrease another one of your ability scores by 2. You can’t decrease an ability that has a score of 5 or lower. Alternatively, you can choose not to adjust your ability scores, in which case this card has no effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.347, 0.909, 0.469], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Comet.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The next time you enter combat against one or more Hostile creatures, you can select one of them as your foe when you roll Initiative. If you reduce your foe to 0 Hit Points during that combat, you have Advantage on Death Saving Throws for 1 year. If someone else reduces your chosen foe to 0 Hit Points or you don’t choose a foe, this card has no effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.469, 0.908, 0.623], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Donjon.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You disappear and become entombed in a state of suspended animation in an extradimensional sphere. Everything you’re wearing and carrying disappears with you except for Artifacts, which stay behind in the space you occupied when you disappeared. You remain imprisoned until you are found and removed from the sphere. You can’t be located by any Divination magic, but a Wish spell can reveal the location of your prison. You draw no more cards."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.623, 0.892, 0.685], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Euryale.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The card’s medusa-like visage curses you. You take a −2 penalty to saving throws while cursed in this way. Only a god or the magic of the Fates card can end this curse."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.684, 0.91, 0.761], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fates.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Reality’s fabric unravels and spins anew, allowing you to avoid or erase one event as if it never happened. You can use the card’s magic as soon as you draw the card or at any other time before you die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.761, 0.904, 0.822], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Flames.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A powerful devil becomes your enemy. The devil seeks your ruin and torments you, savoring your suffering before attempting to slay you. This enmity lasts until either you or the devil dies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.822, 0.912, 0.868], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fool.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Disadvantage on D20 Tests for the next 72 hours. Draw another card; this draw doesn’t count as one of your declared draws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.868, 0.913, 0.915], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gem.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Twenty-five pieces of jewelry worth 2,000 GP each or fifty gems worth 1,000 GP each appear at your feet."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.06, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "231"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 231, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Jester.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on D20 Tests for the next 72 hours, or you can draw two additional cards beyond your declared draws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.481, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Key.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Rare or rarer magic weapon with which you are proficient appears on your person. The GM chooses the weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.143, 0.49, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Knight.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain the service of a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Knight", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", who magically appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of yourself. The knight has the same alignment as you and serves you loyally until death, believing the two of you have been drawn together by fate. Work with your GM to create a name and backstory for this NPC. The GM can use a different stat block to represent the knight, as desired."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.115, 0.265, 0.484, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Moon.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain the ability to cast Wish 1d3 times."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.281, 0.485, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Puzzle.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Permanently reduce your Intelligence or Wisdom by 1d4 + 1 (to a minimum score of 1). You can draw one additional card beyond your declared draws."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.342, 0.488, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rogue.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An NPC of the GM’s choice becomes Hostile toward you. You don’t know the identity of this NPC until they or someone else reveals it. Nothing less than a Wish spell or divine intervention can end the NPC’s hostility toward you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.418, 0.481, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ruin.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " All forms of wealth that you carry or own, other than magic items, are lost to you. Portable property vanishes. Businesses, buildings, and land you own are lost in a way that alters reality the least. Any documentation that proves you should own something lost to this card also disappears."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.51, 0.489, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " At any time you choose within one year of drawing this card, you can ask a question in meditation and mentally receive a truthful answer to that question."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.571, 0.49, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skull.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " An "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Avatar of Death", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " (see the accompanying stat block) appears in an unoccupied space as close to you as possible. The avatar targets only you with its attacks, appearing as a ghostly skeleton clad in a tattered black robe and carrying a spectral scythe. The avatar disappears when it drops to 0 Hit Points or you die. If an ally of yours deals damage to the avatar, that ally summons another "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Avatar of Death", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The new avatar appears in an unoccupied space as close to that ally as possible and targets only that ally with its attacks. You and your allies can each summon only one avatar as a consequence of this draw. A creature slain by an avatar can’t be restored to life."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.786, 0.482, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Star.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Increase one of your ability scores by 2, to a maximum of 24."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.817, 0.488, 0.864], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sun.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A magic item (chosen by the GM) appears on your person. In addition, you gain 10 Temporary Hit Points daily at dawn until you die."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.893, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talons.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Every magic item you wear or carry disintegrates. Artifacts in your possession vanish instead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.096, 0.906, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Throne.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain proficiency and Expertise in your choice of History, Insight, Intimidation, or Persuasion. In addition, you gain rightful ownership of a small keep somewhere in the world. However, the keep is currently home to one or more monsters, which must be cleared out before you can claim the keep as yours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.204, 0.913, 0.327], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Void.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your soul is drawn from your body and contained in an object in a place of the GM’s choice. One or more powerful beings guard the place. While your soul is trapped in this way, your body is inert, ceases aging, and requires no food, air, or water. A Wish spell can’t return your soul to your body, but the spell reveals the location of the object that holds your soul. You draw no more cards."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.338, 0.703, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Avatar of Death"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.36, 0.726, 0.376], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Medium Undead, Neutral evil"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.381, 0.812, 0.397], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 20 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Initiative", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " +3 (13)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.398, 0.81, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Half the HP maximum of its summoner "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 60 ft., Fly 60 ft. (hover)"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.53, 0.428, 0.909, 0.474], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.53, 0.428, 0.909, 0.474], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"2\">MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 16 +3</td><td>+3 De</td><td>x 16 +3 +3 Co</td><td>n16 +3 +3</td></tr><tr><td>Int 16 +3</td><td>+3 Wi</td><td>s 16 +3 +3 Ch</td><td>a 16 +3 +3</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.481, 0.906, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immunities", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Necrotic, Poison; Charmed, Exhaustion, Frightened, Paralyzed, Petrified, Poisoned, Unconscious "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Senses", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Truesight 60 ft., Passive Perception 13 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " All languages known to its summoner "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " None (XP 0; PB equals its summoner’s)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.565, 0.579, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.586, 0.908, 0.649], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Incorporeal Movement.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The avatar can move through other creatures and objects as if they were Difficult Terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if it ends its turn inside an object."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.656, 0.595, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.676, 0.912, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The avatar makes a number of Reaping Scythe attacks equal to half the summoner’s Proficiency Bonus (rounded up)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.728, 0.911, 0.776], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reaping Scythe.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: Automatic hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (1d8 + 3) Slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) Necrotic damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.781, 0.742, 0.798], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Necklace of Adaptation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.801, 0.911, 0.881], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) While wearing this necklace, you can breathe normally in any environment, and you have Advantage on saving throws made to avoid or end the Poisoned condition."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "232"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 232, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.295, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Necklace of Fireballs"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.069, 0.258, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.488, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This necklace has 1d6 + 3 beads hanging from it. You can take a Magic action to detach a bead and throw it up to 60 feet away. When it reaches the end of its trajectory, the bead detonates as a level 3 Fireball (save DC 15)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.166, 0.482, 0.228], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can hurl multiple beads, or even the whole necklace, at one time. When you do so, increase the damage of the Fireball by 1d6 for each bead after the first (maximum 12d6)."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.235, 0.338, 0.251], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Necklace of Prayer Beads"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.252, 0.445, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Cleric, Druid, or Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.287, 0.487, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This necklace has 1d4 + 2 magic beads made from aquamarine, black pearl, or topaz. It also has many nonmagical beads made from stones such as amber, bloodstone, citrine, coral, jade, pearl, or quartz. If a magic bead is removed from the necklace, that bead loses its magic."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.379, 0.488, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Six types of magic beads exist. The GM decides the type of each bead on the necklace or determines it randomly by rolling on the table below. A necklace can have more than one bead of the same type. To use one, you must be wearing the necklace. Each bead contains a spell that you can cast from it as a Bonus Action (using your spell save DC if a save is necessary). Once a magic bead’s spell is cast, that bead can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.521, 0.489, 0.686], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.521, 0.489, 0.686], "content": "<table><tr><td>Id20</td><td>Bead</td><td>Spell</td></tr><tr><td>1-6</td><td>Bead of Blessing</td><td>Bless</td></tr><tr><td>7-12</td><td>Bead of Curing</td><td>Cure Wounds (level 2 version)</td></tr><tr><td>13-16</td><td>Bead of Favor</td><td>Greater Restoration</td></tr><tr><td>17-18</td><td>Bead of Smiting</td><td>Shining Smite</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Bead of Summons</td><td>Guardian of Faith</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Bead of Wind Walking</td><td>Wind Walk</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.697, 0.272, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Nine Lives Stealer"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.714, 0.479, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.749, 0.487, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.781, 0.485, 0.936], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Life Stealing.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The weapon has 1d8 + 1 charges. When you attack a creature that has fewer than 100 Hit Points with this weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the attack roll, the creature must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be slain instantly as the sword tears its life force from its body. Constructs and Undead succeed on the save automatically. The weapon loses 1 charge if the creature is slain. When the weapon has no charges remaining, it loses this property."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.615, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oathbow"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.903, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Longbow or Shortbow), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.103, 0.908, 0.242], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you nock an arrow on this bow, it whispers in Elvish, “Swift defeat to my enemies.” When you use this weapon to make a ranged attack, you can utter or sign the following command words: “Swift death to you who have wronged me.” The target of your attack becomes your sworn enemy until it dies or until dawn 7 days later. You can have only one such sworn enemy at a time. When your sworn enemy dies, you can choose a new one after the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.242, 0.908, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you make a ranged attack roll with this weapon against your sworn enemy, you have Advantage on the roll. In addition, your target gains no benefit from Half Cover or Three-Quarters Cover, and you suffer no Disadvantage due to long range. If the attack hits, your sworn enemy takes an extra 3d6 Piercing damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.349, 0.887, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While your sworn enemy lives, you have Disadvantage on attack rolls with all other weapons."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.388, 0.701, 0.404], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oil of Etherealness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.406, 0.618, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.425, 0.909, 0.517], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it’s wearing and carrying (one additional vial is required for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes. The affected creature then gains the effect of the Etherealness spell for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.517, 0.898, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beads of this cloudy, gray oil form on the outside of its container and quickly evaporate."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.556, 0.678, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oil of Sharpness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.574, 0.653, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.593, 0.908, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One vial of this oil can coat one Melee weapon or twenty pieces of ammunition, but only ammunition and Melee weapons that are nonmagical and deal Slashing or Piercing damage are affected. Applying the oil takes 1 minute, after which the oil magically seeps into whatever it coats, turning the coated weapon into a +3 Weapon or the coated ammunition into +3 Ammunition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.716, 0.861, 0.747], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This clear, gelatinous oil sparkles with tiny, ultrathin silver shards."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.754, 0.693, 0.771], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oil of Slipperiness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.772, 0.663, 0.788], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.792, 0.909, 0.884], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One vial of this oil can cover one Medium or smaller creature, along with the equipment it’s wearing and carrying (one additional vial is required for each size category above Medium). Applying the oil takes 10 minutes. The affected creature then gains the effect of the Freedom of Movement spell for 8 hours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.885, 0.907, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, the oil can be poured on the ground as a Magic action, where it covers a 10-foot square,"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "233"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 233, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.487, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "duplicating the effect of the Grease spell in that area for 8 hours."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.081, 0.479, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This sticky, black unguent is thick and heavy, but it flows quickly when poured."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.12, 0.242, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pearl of Power"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.137, 0.48, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.172, 0.472, 0.235], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While this pearl is on your person, you can take a Magic action to regain one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower. Once you use the pearl, it can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.242, 0.263, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Periapt of Health"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.259, 0.465, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.279, 0.484, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this pendant, you can take a Magic action to regain 2d4 + 2 Hit Points. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.486, 0.372], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, you have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition while you wear this pendant."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.38, 0.385, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Periapt of Proof against Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.397, 0.419, 0.413], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.417, 0.49, 0.464], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This delicate silver chain has a brilliant-cut black gem pendant. While you wear it, you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition and Poison damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.471, 0.344, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Periapt of Wound Closure"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.489, 0.483, 0.539], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement) While wearing this pendant, you gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.539, 0.485, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Life Preservation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whenever you make a Death Saving Throw, you can change a roll of 9 or lower to a 10, turning a failed save into a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.585, 0.485, 0.632], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Natural Healing Boost.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Whenever you roll a Hit Point Die to regain Hit Points, double the number of Hit Points it restores."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.639, 0.241, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Philter of Love"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.657, 0.241, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.676, 0.484, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The next time you see a creature within 10 minutes after drinking this philter, you are charmed by that creature and have the Charmed condition for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.738, 0.474, 0.77], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This rose-hued, effervescent liquid contains one easy-to-miss bubble shaped like a heart."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.777, 0.268, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pipes of Haunting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.103, 0.795, 0.302, 0.81], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.101, 0.814, 0.49, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. You can take a Magic action to play them and expend 1 charge to create an eerie, spellbinding tune. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet of you must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Frightened condition for 1 minute. A creature that fails the save"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.899, 0.113], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "repeats it at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that succeeds on its save is immune to the effect of these pipes for 24 hours."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.12, 0.707, 0.136], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pipes of the Sewers"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.137, 0.887, 0.154], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.158, 0.907, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While these pipes are on your person, ordinary rats and giant rats are Indifferent toward you and won’t attack you unless you threaten or harm them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.204, 0.908, 0.371], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The pipes have 3 charges and regain 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. If you play the pipes as a Magic action, you can take a Bonus Action to expend 1 to 3 charges, calling forth one "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Swarm of Rats", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " with each expended charge if enough rats are within half a mile of you to be called in this fashion (as determined by the GM). If there aren’t enough rats to form a swarm, the charge is wasted. Called swarms move toward the music by the shortest available route but aren’t under your control otherwise."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.372, 0.908, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Swarm of Rats", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " that isn’t under another creature’s control comes within 30 feet of you while you are playing the pipes, the swarm makes a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the swarm behaves as it normally would and can’t be swayed by the pipes’ music for the next 24 hours. On a failed save, the swarm is swayed by the pipes’ music and becomes Friendly to you and your allies for as long as you continue to play the pipes each round as a Magic action. A Friendly swarm obeys your commands. If you issue no commands to a Friendly swarm, it defends itself but otherwise takes no actions. If a Friendly swarm starts its turn more than 30 feet away from you, your control over that swarm ends, and the swarm behaves as it normally would and can’t be swayed by the pipes’ music for the next 24 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.523, 0.64, 0.786, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plate Armor of Etherealness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.658, 0.899, 0.69], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Half Plate Armor or Plate Armor), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.522, 0.693, 0.912, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you’re wearing this armor, you can take a Magic action and use a command word to gain the effect of the Etherealness spell. The spell ends immediately if you remove the armor or take a Magic action to repeat the command word. This property of the armor can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.794, 0.657, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Portable Hole"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.811, 0.679, 0.826], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.83, 0.9, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This fine black cloth, soft as silk, is folded up to the dimensions of a handkerchief. It unfolds into a circular sheet 6 feet in diameter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.877, 0.873, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to unfold a Portable Hole and place it on or against a solid surface, whereupon the Portable Hole creates an"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "234"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 234, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.482, 0.127], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "extradimensional hole 10 feet deep. The cylindrical space within the hole exists on a different plane of existence, so it can’t be used to create open passages. Any creature inside an open Portable Hole can exit the hole by climbing out of it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.473, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to close a Portable Hole by taking hold of the edges of the cloth and folding it up. Folding the cloth closes the hole, and any creatures or objects within remain in the extradimensional space. No matter what’s in it, the hole weighs next to nothing."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.219, 0.49, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the hole is folded up, a creature within the hole’s extradimensional space can take an action to make a DC 10 Strength (Athletics) check. On a successful check, the creature forces its way out and appears within 5 feet of the Portable Hole. A closed Portable Hole holds enough air for 1 hour of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.49, 0.481], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Placing a Portable Hole inside an extradimensional space created by a Bag of Holding, Handy Haversack, or similar item instantly destroys both items and opens a gate to the Astral Plane. The gate originates where the one item was placed inside the other. Any creature within 10 feet of the gate and not behind Total Cover is sucked through it and deposited in a random location on the Astral Plane. The gate then closes. The gate is one-way only and can’t be reopened."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.487, 0.358, 0.504], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Animal Friendship"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.505, 0.241, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.525, 0.49, 0.556], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you can cast the level 3 version of the Animal Friendship spell (save DC 13)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.556, 0.488, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Agitating this potion’s muddy liquid brings little bits into view: a fish scale, a hummingbird feather, a cat claw, or a squirrel hair."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.61, 0.312, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Clairvoyance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.628, 0.196, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.647, 0.479, 0.679], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the Clairvoyance spell (no Concentration required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.679, 0.475, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "An eyeball bobs in this potion’s yellowish liquid but vanishes when the potion is opened."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.716, 0.276, 0.734], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Climbing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.735, 0.224, 0.75], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Common"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.754, 0.489, 0.815], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed for 1 hour. During this time, you have Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to climb."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.816, 0.48, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion is separated into brown, silver, and gray layers resembling bands of stone. Shaking the bottle fails to mix the colors."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.719, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Diminution"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.618, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.901, 0.134], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the “reduce” effect of the Enlarge/Reduce spell for 1d4 hours (no Concentration required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.135, 0.902, 0.197], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The red in the potion’s liquid continuously contracts to a tiny bead and then expands to color the clear liquid around it. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.204, 0.67, 0.221], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Flying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.222, 0.654, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.241, 0.902, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed for 1 hour and can hover. If you’re in the air when the potion wears off, you fall unless you have some other means of staying aloft."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.303, 0.901, 0.349], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s clear liquid floats at the top of its container and has cloudy white impurities drifting in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.356, 0.747, 0.373], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Gaseous Form"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.375, 0.618, 0.39], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.394, 0.907, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the Gaseous Form spell for 1 hour (no Concentration required) or until you end the effect as a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.455, 0.876, 0.487], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s container seems to hold fog that moves and pours like water."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.494, 0.75, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Giant Strength"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.512, 0.676, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rarity Varies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.531, 0.911, 0.608], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, your Strength score changes for 1 hour. The type of giant determines the score (see the table below). The potion has no effect on you if your Strength is equal to or greater than that score."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.608, 0.909, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s transparent liquid has floating in it a sliver of light resembling a giant’s fingernail."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.527, 0.644, 0.909, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.527, 0.644, 0.909, 0.774], "content": "<table><tr><td>Potion</td><td>Str.</td><td>Rarity</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Giant Strength (hill)</td><td>21</td><td>Uncommon</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Giant Strength (frost or stone)</td><td>23</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Giant Strength (fire)</td><td>25</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Giant Strength (cloud)</td><td>27</td><td>Very Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Giant Strength (storm)</td><td>29</td><td>Legendary</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.783, 0.688, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Growth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.801, 0.663, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.82, 0.909, 0.867], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the “enlarge” effect of the Enlarge/Reduce spell for 10 minutes (no Concentration required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.867, 0.881, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The red in the potion’s liquid continuously expands from a tiny bead to color the clear liquid around it and then contracts. Shaking the bottle fails to interrupt this process."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "235"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 235, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.273, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potions of Healing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.254, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rarity Varies"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.469, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You regain Hit Points when you drink this potion. The number of Hit Points depends on the potion’s rarity, as shown in the table below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.135, 0.486, 0.165], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whatever its potency, the potion’s red liquid glimmers when agitated."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.17, 0.488, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.105, 0.17, 0.488, 0.313], "content": "<table><tr><td>Potion</td><td>HP Regained</td><td>Rarity</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Healing</td><td>2d4 + 2</td><td>Common</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Healing (greater)</td><td>4d4 + 4</td><td>Uncommon</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Healing (superior)</td><td>8d4 + 8</td><td>Rare</td></tr><tr><td>Potion of Healing (supreme)</td><td>10d4 + 20</td><td>Very Rare</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.103, 0.322, 0.273, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Heroism"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.34, 0.196, 0.355], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.359, 0.486, 0.421], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain 10 Temporary Hit Points that last for 1 hour. For the same duration, you are under the effect of the Bless spell (no Concentration required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.42, 0.481, 0.452], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s blue liquid bubbles and steams as if boiling."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.459, 0.285, 0.476], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Invisibility"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.478, 0.196, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.497, 0.473, 0.575], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s container looks empty but feels as though it holds liquid. When you drink the potion, you have the Invisible condition for 1 hour. The effect ends early if you make an attack roll, deal damage, or cast a spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.582, 0.323, 0.599], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Invulnerability"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.6, 0.196, 0.615], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.619, 0.472, 0.65], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For 1 minute after you drink this potion, you have Resistance to all damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.649, 0.459, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s syrupy liquid looks like liquefied iron."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.688, 0.282, 0.706], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Longevity"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.707, 0.231, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.726, 0.488, 0.803], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, your physical age is reduced by 1d6 + 6 years, to a minimum of 13 years. Each time you subsequently drink a Potion of Longevity, there is 10 percent cumulative chance that you instead age by 1d6 + 6 years."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.803, 0.49, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Suspended in this amber liquid is a tiny heart that, against all reason, is still beating. These ingredients vanish when the potion is opened."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.739, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Mind Reading"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.618, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.893, 0.135], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the Detect Thoughts spell (save DC 13) for 10 minutes (no Concentration required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.135, 0.881, 0.166], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s dense, purple liquid has an ovoid cloud of pink floating in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.677, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Poison"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.191, 0.663, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.21, 0.905, 0.272], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This concoction looks, smells, and tastes like a Potion of Healing or another beneficial potion. However, it is actually poison masked by illusion magic. Identify reveals its true nature."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.272, 0.91, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you drink this potion, you take 4d6 Poison damage and must succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw or have the Poisoned condition for 1 hour."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.326, 0.712, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.343, 0.664, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.363, 0.904, 0.425], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you have Resistance to one type of damage for 1 hour. The GM chooses the type or determines it randomly by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.429, 0.909, 0.544], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.429, 0.909, 0.544], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI0</td><td>Damage Type</td><td>IdI0</td><td>Damage Type</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Acid</td><td>6</td><td>Necrotic</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Cold</td><td>7</td><td>Poison</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fire</td><td>8</td><td>Psychic</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Force</td><td>9</td><td>Radiant</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lightning</td><td>10</td><td>Thunder</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.553, 0.673, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.571, 0.653, 0.587], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.522, 0.59, 0.904, 0.652], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, you gain the effect of the Haste spell for 1 minute (no Concentration required) without suffering the wave of lethargy that typically occurs when the effect ends."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.652, 0.893, 0.683], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s yellow fluid is streaked with black and swirls on its own."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.691, 0.683, 0.708], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Vitality"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.524, 0.709, 0.653, 0.725], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.728, 0.91, 0.805], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you drink this potion, it removes any Exhaustion levels you have and ends the Poisoned condition on you. For the next 24 hours, you regain the maximum number of Hit Points for any Hit Point Die you spend."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.523, 0.805, 0.908, 0.837], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s crimson liquid regularly pulses with dull light, calling to mind a heartbeat."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.524, 0.844, 0.769, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion of Water Breathing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.524, 0.862, 0.663, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Potion, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.523, 0.88, 0.871, 0.913], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can breathe underwater for 24 hours after drinking this potion."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "236"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 44, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 236, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.476, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This potion’s cloudy green fluid smells of the sea and has a jellyfish-like bubble floating in it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.089, 0.359, 0.105], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Quarterstaff of the Acrobat"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.107, 0.416, 0.137], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Quarterstaff), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.142, 0.489, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.173, 0.477, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this weapon, you can cause it to emit green Dim Light out to 10 feet, either as a Bonus Action or after you roll Initiative, or you can extinguish the light as a Bonus Action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.234, 0.488, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this weapon, you can take a Bonus Action to alter its form, turning it into a 6-inch rod (for ease of storage) or a 10-foot pole, or reverting it a Quarterstaff; the weapon will elongate only as far as the surrounding space allows."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.311, 0.487, 0.341], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In certain forms, the weapon has the following additional properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.342, 0.482, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Acrobatic Assist (Quarterstaff and 10-Foot Pole Forms Only).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding this weapon, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.388, 0.486, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Deflection (Quarterstaff Form Only).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you are hit by an attack while holding the weapon, you can take a Reaction to twirl the weapon around you, gaining a +5 bonus to your Armor Class against the triggering attack, potentially causing the attack to miss you. You can’t use this property again until you finish a Short or Long Rest."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.495, 0.482, 0.572], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ranged Weapon (Quarterstaff Form Only).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This weapon has the Thrown property with a normal range of 30 feet and a long range of 120 feet. Immediately after you make a ranged attack with the weapon, it flies back to your hand."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.579, 0.327, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Animal Influence"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.597, 0.182, 0.613], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.617, 0.483, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This ring has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the ring, you can expend 1 charge to cast one of the following spells (save DC 13) from it:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.685, 0.256, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Animal Friendship"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.103, 0.7, 0.31, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Fear (affects Beasts only)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.103, 0.716, 0.266, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Speak with Animals"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.103, 0.739, 0.341, 0.756], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Djinni Summoning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.757, 0.385, 0.773], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.776, 0.49, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can take a Magic action to summon a particular "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Djinni", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " from the Elemental Plane of Air. The djinni appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 120 feet of yourself. It remains as long as you maintain Concentration, to a maximum of 1 hour, or until it drops to 0 Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.869, 0.49, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While summoned, the djinni is Friendly to you and your allies, and it obeys your commands. If you fail to command it, the djinni defends itself against attackers but takes no other actions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.05, 0.902, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "After the djinni departs, it can’t be summoned again for 24 hours, and the ring becomes nonmagical if the djinni dies."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.096, 0.911, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rings of Djinni Summoning are often created by the djinn they summon and given to mortals as gifts of friendship or tokens of esteem."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.15, 0.788, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Elemental Command"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.168, 0.806, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.188, 0.907, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each Ring of Elemental Command is linked to one of the four Elemental Planes. The GM chooses or randomly determines the linked plane. For example, a Ring of Elemental Command (air) is linked to the Elemental Plane of Air."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.264, 0.901, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every Ring of Elemental Command has the following two properties:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.302, 0.904, 0.363], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elemental Bane.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While wearing the ring, you have Advantage on attack rolls against Elementals and they have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.363, 0.899, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elemental Compulsion.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While wearing the ring, you can take a Magic action to try to compel an Elemental you see within 60 feet of yourself. The Elemental makes a DC 18 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the Elemental has the Charmed condition until the start your next turn, and you determine what it does with its move and action on its next turn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.493, 0.91, 0.54], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elemental Focus.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While wearing the ring, you benefit from additional properties corresponding to the ring’s linked Elemental Plane:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.546, 0.902, 0.591], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Air.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know Auran, you have Resistance to Lightning damage, and you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed and can hover."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.592, 0.902, 0.729], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Earth.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know Terran, and you have Resistance to Acid damage. Terrain composed of rubble, rocks, or dirt isn’t Difficult Terrain for you. In addition, you can move through solid earth or rock as if those areas were Difficult Terrain without disturbing the matter through which you pass. If you end your turn in solid earth or rock, you are shunted out to the nearest unoccupied space you last occupied."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.73, 0.887, 0.76], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fire.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know Ignan, and you have Immunity to Fire damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.76, 0.901, 0.792], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Water.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You know Aquan, you gain a Swim Speed of 60 feet, and you can breathe underwater."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.798, 0.904, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The ring has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the ring, you can cast a spell from it. Choose the spell from the list of available spells based on the Elemental Plane the ring is linked to, as shown in the following table. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell, which has a save DC of 18."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "237"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 237, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.487, 0.263], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.487, 0.263], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Plane</td><td>Spells (Charges)</td></tr><tr><td>Air</td><td>Chain Lightning (3 charges), Feather Fall (0 charges), Gust of Wind (2 charges), Wind Wall (1 charge)</td></tr><tr><td>Earth</td><td>Earthquake (5 charges), Stone Shape (2 charges), Stoneskin (3 charges), Wall of Stone (3 charges)</td></tr><tr><td>Fire</td><td>Burning Hands (1 charge), Fireball (2 charges), Fire Storm (4 charges), Wall of Fire (3 charges)</td></tr><tr><td>Water</td><td>Create or Destroy Water (1 charge), Ice Storm (2 charges), Tsunami (5 charges), Wall of Ice (3 charges), Water Walk (2 charges)</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.245, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Evasion"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.289, 0.344, 0.305], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.308, 0.485, 0.386], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This ring has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. When you fail a Dexterity saving throw while wearing the ring, you can take a Reaction to expend 1 charge to succeed on that save instead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.393, 0.31, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Feather Falling"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.411, 0.344, 0.427], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.43, 0.482, 0.463], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you fall while wearing this ring, you descend 60 feet per round and take no damage from falling."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.469, 0.284, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Free Action"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.487, 0.344, 0.503], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.507, 0.479, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear this ring, Difficult Terrain doesn’t cost you extra movement. In addition, magic can neither reduce any of your Speeds nor cause you to have the Paralyzed or Restrained condition."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.103, 0.576, 0.267, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Invisibility"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.594, 0.385, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.614, 0.49, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can take a Magic action to give yourself the Invisible condition. You remain Invisible until the ring is removed or until you take a Bonus Action to become visible again."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.103, 0.683, 0.249, 0.701], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Jumping"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.701, 0.39, 0.717], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.72, 0.478, 0.753], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can cast Jump from it, but can target only yourself when you do so."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.76, 0.308, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Mind Shielding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.777, 0.39, 0.793], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.101, 0.797, 0.481, 0.889], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you are immune to magic that allows other creatures to read your thoughts, determine whether you are lying, know your alignment, or know your creature type. Creatures can telepathically communicate with you only if you allow it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.889, 0.485, 0.921], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to cause the ring to become imperceptible until you take another Magic"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.899, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "action to make it perceptible, until you remove the ring, or until you die."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.081, 0.907, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you die while wearing the ring, your soul enters it, unless it already houses a soul. You can remain in the ring or depart for the afterlife. As long as your soul is in the ring, you can telepathically communicate with any creature wearing it. A wearer can’t prevent this telepathic communication."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.181, 0.695, 0.198], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Protection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.199, 0.766, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.523, 0.218, 0.87, 0.251], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class and saving throws while wearing this ring."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.257, 0.719, 0.274], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Regeneration"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.274, 0.801, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.294, 0.908, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you regain 1d6 Hit Points every 10 minutes if you have at least 1 Hit Point. If you lose a body part, the ring causes the missing part to regrow and return to full functionality after 1d6 + 1 days if you have at least 1 Hit Point the whole time."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.394, 0.693, 0.412], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Resistance"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.413, 0.604, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.432, 0.909, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Resistance to one damage type while wearing this ring. The gemstone in the ring indicates the type, which the GM chooses or determines randomly by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.499, 0.91, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.525, 0.499, 0.91, 0.709], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI0</td><td>Damage Type</td><td>Gemstone</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>Acid</td><td>Pearl</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Cold</td><td>Tourmaline</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Fire</td><td>Garnet</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Force</td><td>Sapphire</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lightning</td><td>Citrine</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Necrotic</td><td>Jet</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Poison</td><td>Amethyst</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Psychic</td><td>Jade</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Radiant</td><td>Topaz</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Thunder</td><td>Spinel</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.719, 0.73, 0.737], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Shooting Stars"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.737, 0.801, 0.753], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.756, 0.895, 0.772], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can cast Dancing Lights or Light from the ring."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.523, 0.772, 0.904, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The ring has 6 charges and regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. You can expend its charges to use the properties below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.524, 0.818, 0.895, 0.848], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Faerie Fire.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can expend 1 charge to cast Faerie Fire from the ring."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.849, 0.899, 0.895], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning Spheres.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can expend 2 charges as a Magic action to create up to four 3-foot-diameter spheres of lightning."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.895, 0.898, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each sphere appears in an unoccupied space you can see within 120 feet of yourself. The spheres"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "238"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 238, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.476, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "last as long as you maintain Concentration, up to 1 minute. Each sphere sheds Dim Light in a 30-foot radius."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.49, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can move each sphere up to 30 feet, but no farther than 120 feet away from yourself. The first time the sphere comes within 5 feet of a creature other than you that isn’t behind Total Cover, the sphere discharges lightning at that creature and disappears. That creature makes a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes Lightning damage based on the number of spheres you created, as shown in the following table. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.105, 0.27, 0.486, 0.338], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.105, 0.27, 0.486, 0.338], "content": "<table><tr><td>Number of Spheres</td><td>Lightning Damage</td><td>Number of Spheres</td><td>Lightning Damage</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>4dl2</td><td>3</td><td>2d6</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>5d4</td><td>4</td><td>2d4</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.347, 0.488, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shooting Stars.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can expend 1 to 3 charges as a Magic action. For every charge you expend, you launch a glowing mote of light from the ring at a point you can see within 60 feet of yourself. Each creature in a 15-foot Cube originating from that point is showered in sparks and makes a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 5d4 Radiant damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.493, 0.292, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Spell Storing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.512, 0.344, 0.528], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.531, 0.488, 0.607], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This ring stores spells cast into it, holding them until the attuned wearer uses them. The ring can store up to 5 levels worth of spells at a time. When found, it contains 1d6 − 1 levels of stored spells chosen by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.608, 0.49, 0.7], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Any creature can cast a spell of level 1 through 5 into the ring by touching the ring as the spell is cast. The spell has no effect other than to be stored in the ring. If the ring can’t hold the spell, the spell is expended without effect. The level of the slot used to cast the spell determines how much space it uses."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.7, 0.487, 0.794], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can cast any spell stored in it. The spell uses the slot level, spell save DC, spell attack bonus, and spellcasting ability of the original caster but is otherwise treated as if you cast the spell. The spell cast from the ring is no longer stored in it, freeing up space."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.8, 0.295, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Spell Turning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.818, 0.385, 0.834], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.837, 0.49, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells. If you succeed on the save for a spell of level 7 or lower, the spell has no effect on you. If that spell targeted only you and didn’t create an area of effect, you can take a Reaction to deflect the spell back at the spell’s caster; the"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.896, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "caster must make a saving throw against the spell using their own spell save DC."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.692, 0.107], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Swimming"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.108, 0.65, 0.123], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.126, 0.912, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a Swim Speed of 40 feet while wearing this ring."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.165, 0.697, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Telekinesis"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.183, 0.801, 0.2], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.202, 0.883, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can cast Telekinesis from it."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.241, 0.675, 0.259], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of the Ram"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.259, 0.765, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.279, 0.913, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This ring has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the ring, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 to 3 charges to make a ranged spell attack against one creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself. The ring produces a spectral ram’s head and makes its attack roll with a +7 bonus. On a hit, for each charge you spend, the target takes 2d10 Force damage and is pushed 5 feet away from you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.417, 0.905, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alternatively, you can expend 1 to 3 of the ring’s charges as a Magic action to try to break a nonmagical object you can see within 60 feet of yourself that isn’t being worn or carried. The ring makes a Strength check with a +5 bonus for each charge you spend."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.517, 0.724, 0.534], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Three Wishes"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.535, 0.647, 0.551], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Legendary"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.554, 0.907, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can expend 1 of its 3 charges to cast Wish from it. The ring becomes non-magical when you use the last charge."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.608, 0.675, 0.625], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Warmth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.626, 0.812, 0.642], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.646, 0.911, 0.677], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you take Cold damage while wearing this ring, the ring reduces the damage you take by 2d8."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.677, 0.889, 0.724], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, while wearing this ring, you and everything you wear and carry are unharmed by temperatures of 0 degrees Fahrenheit or lower."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.731, 0.736, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of Water Walking"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.749, 0.65, 0.765], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.523, 0.768, 0.899, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you cast Water Walk from it, targeting only yourself."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.524, 0.807, 0.71, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring of X-ray Vision"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.825, 0.766, 0.841], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ring, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.522, 0.844, 0.896, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this ring, you can take a Magic action to gain X-ray vision with a range of 30 feet for 1 minute. To you, solid objects within that radius appear transparent and don’t prevent light from passing through them. The vision can penetrate 1"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "239"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 239, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.49, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or up to 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances or a thin sheet of lead block the vision."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.476, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you use the ring again before taking a Long Rest, you must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.151, 0.224, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe of Eyes"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.103, 0.168, 0.419, 0.184], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.188, 0.478, 0.22], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This robe is adorned with eyelike patterns. While you wear the robe, you gain the following benefits:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.225, 0.488, 0.287], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "All-Around Vision.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The robe gives you Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Special Senses.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Darkvision and Truesight, both with a range of 120 feet."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.293, 0.492, 0.387], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Drawbacks.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Light spell cast on the robe or a Daylight spell cast within 5 feet of the robe gives you the Blinded condition for 1 minute. At the end of each of your turns, you make a Constitution saving throw (DC 11 for Light or DC 15 for Daylight), ending the condition on yourself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.394, 0.353, 0.411], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe of Scintillating Colors"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.411, 0.455, 0.428], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.43, 0.487, 0.631], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This robe has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While you wear it, you can take a Magic action and expend 1 charge to cause the garment to display a shifting pattern of dazzling hues until the end of your next turn. During this time, the robe sheds Bright Light in a 30-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 30 feet, and creatures that can see you have Disadvantage on attack rolls against you. Any creature in the Bright Light that can see you when the robe’s power is activated must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Stunned condition until the effect ends."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.639, 0.23, 0.654], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe of Stars"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.103, 0.656, 0.454, 0.672], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.675, 0.469, 0.722], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This black or dark-blue robe is embroidered with small white or silver stars. You gain a +1 bonus to saving throws while you wear it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.722, 0.484, 0.814], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Six stars, located on the robe’s upper-front portion, are particularly large. While wearing this robe, you can take a Magic action to remove one of the stars and expend it to cast the level 5 version of Magic Missile. Daily at dusk, 1d6 removed stars reappear on the robe."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.1, 0.814, 0.485, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear the robe, you can take a Magic action to enter the Astral Plane along with everything you are wearing and carrying. You remain there until you take a Magic action to return to the plane you were on. You reappear in the last space you occupied or, if that space is occupied, the nearest unoccupied space."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.727, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe of the Archmagi"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.908, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.103, 0.895, 0.134], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This elegant garment is made from exquisite cloth and adorned with runes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.134, 0.892, 0.181], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain these benefits while wearing the robe. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Armor.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you aren’t wearing armor, your base Armor Class is 15 plus your Dexterity modifier."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.181, 0.905, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Magic Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.211, 0.908, 0.243], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "War Mage.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Your spell save DC and spell attack bonus each increase by 2."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.25, 0.719, 0.266], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Robe of Useful Items"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.268, 0.724, 0.283], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.287, 0.901, 0.379], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This robe has cloth patches of various shapes and colors covering it. While wearing the robe, you can take a Magic action to detach one of the patches, causing it to become the object or creature it represents. Once the last patch is removed, the robe becomes an ordinary garment."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.537, 0.379, 0.907, 0.395], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The robe has two of each of the following patches:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.401, 0.775, 0.417], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Bullseye Lantern (filled and lit)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.525, 0.418, 0.602, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Dagger"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.525, 0.433, 0.601, 0.446], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Mirror"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.525, 0.448, 0.582, 0.462], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Pole"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.525, 0.463, 0.645, 0.478], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Rope (coiled)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.525, 0.479, 0.585, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Sack"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.5, 0.906, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "In addition, the robe has 4d4 other patches. The GM chooses the patches or determines them randomly by rolling on the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.527, 0.553, 0.91, 0.874], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.527, 0.553, 0.91, 0.874], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00 Patch</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>01-08</td><td>Bag of 100 GP</td></tr><tr><td>09-15</td><td>Silver coffer (I foot long, 6 inches wide and deep) worth 500 GP</td></tr><tr><td>16-22</td><td>Iron door (up to 10 feet wide and 10 feet high, barred on one side of your choice), which you can place in an opening you can reach; it con- forms to fit the opening, attaching and hinging itself</td></tr><tr><td>23-30</td><td>10 gems worth 100 GP each</td></tr><tr><td>31-44</td><td>Wooden ladder (24 feet long)</td></tr><tr><td>45-51</td><td>Riding Horse with a Riding Saddle</td></tr><tr><td>52-59</td><td>Open pit (a l0-foot Cube), which you can place on the ground within 10 feet of yourself</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>60–68 4 Potions of Healing</td></tr><tr><td>69-75</td><td>Rowboat (12 feet long)</td></tr><tr><td>76-83</td><td>Spell Scroll containing one spell of level 1, 2, or 3 (your choice)</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "240"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 240, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.106, 0.056, 0.487, 0.162], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.106, 0.056, 0.487, 0.162], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Patch</td></tr><tr><td>84-90</td><td>2 Mastiffs</td></tr><tr><td>91-96</td><td>Window (2 feet by 4 feet, up to 2 feet deep), which you can place on a vertical surface you can reach</td></tr><tr><td>97-00 Portable Ram</td><td></td></tr></table>"}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.172, 0.275, 0.189], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Absorption"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.19, 0.374, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.21, 0.486, 0.394], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this rod, you can take a Reaction to absorb a spell that is targeting only you and doesn’t create an area of effect. The absorbed spell’s effect is canceled, and the spell’s energy—not the spell itself—is stored in the rod. The energy has the same level as the spell when it was cast. A canceled spell dissipates with no effect, and any resources used to cast it are wasted. The rod can absorb and store up to 50 levels of energy over the course of its existence. Once the rod absorbs 50 levels of energy, it can’t absorb more. If you are targeted by a spell that the rod can’t store, the rod has no effect on that spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.394, 0.49, 0.455], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you become attuned to the rod, you know how many levels of energy the rod has absorbed over the course of its existence and how many levels of spell energy it currently has stored."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.455, 0.488, 0.577], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you are a spellcaster holding the rod, you can convert energy stored in it into spell slots to cast spells you have prepared or know. You can create spell slots only of a level equal to or lower than your own spell slots, up to a maximum of level 5. You use the stored levels in place of your slots but otherwise cast the spell as normal. For example, you can use 3 levels stored in the rod as a level 3 spell slot."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.577, 0.471, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A newly found rod typically has 1d10 levels of spell energy stored in it. A rod that can no longer absorb spell energy and has no energy remaining becomes nonmagical."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.647, 0.259, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Alertness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.664, 0.375, 0.68], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.684, 0.384, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This rod has the following properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.7, 0.476, 0.745], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alertness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the rod, you have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks and on Initiative rolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.746, 0.485, 0.777], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the rod, you can cast the following spells from it:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.783, 0.274, 0.798], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Detect Evil and Good"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.104, 0.8, 0.221, 0.813], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Detect Magic"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.104, 0.814, 0.31, 0.829], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• Detect Poison and Disease"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.104, 0.83, 0.23, 0.845], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "• See Invisibility"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.852, 0.487, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protective Aura.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you can plant the haft end of the rod in the ground, whereupon the rod’s head sheds Bright Light in a 60-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 60 feet. While in that Bright Light, you and your allies gain a +1"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.893, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "bonus to Armor Class and saving throws and can sense the location of any Invisible creature that is also in the Bright Light."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.096, 0.896, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rod’s head stops glowing and the effect ends after 10 minutes or when a creature takes a Magic action to pull the rod from the ground. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.181, 0.71, 0.198], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Lordly Might"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.199, 0.802, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.218, 0.903, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This rod has a flanged head, and it functions as a magic Mace that grants a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. The rod has properties associated with six different buttons that are set in a row along the haft. It has three other properties as well, detailed below."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.311, 0.896, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Buttons.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can press one of the following buttons as a Bonus Action; a button’s effect lasts until you push a different button or until you push the same button again, which causes the rod to revert to its normal form:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.394, 0.902, 0.486], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 1.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A fiery blade sprouts from the end opposite the rod’s flanged head. The flames shed Bright Light in a 40-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 40 feet, and the blade functions as a magic Longsword or Shortsword (your choice) that deals an extra 2d6 Fire damage on a hit."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.525, 0.486, 0.91, 0.561], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 2.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The rod’s flanged head folds down and two crescent-shaped blades spring out, transforming the rod into a magic Battleaxe that grants a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.563, 0.896, 0.654], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 3.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The rod’s flanged head folds down, a spear point springs from the rod’s tip, and the rod’s handle lengthens into a 6-foot haft, transforming the rod into a magic Spear that grants a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.525, 0.655, 0.905, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 4.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The rod transforms into a climbing pole up to 50 feet long (you specify the length), though the rod’s buttons remain within your reach. In s"}, {"type": "text", "content": "urfaces", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " as hard as granite, a spike at the bottom and three hooks at the top anchor the pole. Horizontal bars 3 inches long fold out from the sides, 1 foot apart, forming a ladder. The pole can bear up to 4,000 pounds. More weight or lack of solid anchoring causes the rod to revert to its normal form."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.525, 0.808, 0.884, 0.869], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 5.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The rod transforms into a handheld battering ram and grants its user a +10 bonus to Strength (Athletics) checks made to break through doors, barricades, and other barriers."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.525, 0.87, 0.902, 0.916], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Button 6.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The rod assumes or remains in its normal form and indicates magnetic north. (Nothing happens if this function of the rod is used in a"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.059, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "241"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.373, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 241, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.114, 0.05, 0.487, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "location that has no magnetic north.) The rod also gives you knowledge of your approximate depth beneath the ground or your height above it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.103, 0.487, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Drain Life.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a creature with a melee attack using the rod, you can force the target to make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes an extra 4d6 Necrotic damage, and you regain a number of Hit Points equal to half that Necrotic damage. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.211, 0.486, 0.333], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Paralyze.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit a creature with a melee attack using the rod, you can force the target to make a DC 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target has the Paralyzed condition for 1 minute. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.333, 0.48, 0.472], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Terrify.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the rod, you can take a Magic action to force each creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself to make a DC 17 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a target has the Frightened condition for 1 minute. A Frightened target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.48, 0.29, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Resurrection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.497, 0.381, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.516, 0.488, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rod has 5 charges. While you hold it, you can cast one of the following spells from it: Heal (expends 1 charge) or Resurrection (expends 5 charges)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.563, 0.486, 0.61], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rod regains 1 expended charge daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the rod disappears in a harmless burst of radiance."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.617, 0.258, 0.634], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Rulership"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.634, 0.339, 0.65], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.1, 0.654, 0.488, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to present the rod and command obedience from each creature of your choice that you can see within 120 feet of yourself. Each target must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the Charmed condition for 8 hours. While Charmed in this way, the creature regards you as its trusted leader. If harmed by you or your allies or commanded to do something contrary to its nature, a target ceases to be Charmed in this way. Once used, this property can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.831, 0.247, 0.847], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod of Security"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.848, 0.214, 0.864], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rod, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.868, 0.485, 0.931], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this rod, you can take a Magic action to activate it. The rod then instantly transports you and up to 199 other willing creatures you can see to a demiplane. You choose the form the demiplane"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.051, 0.91, 0.204], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "takes. It could be a tranquil garden, a cheery tavern, an immense palace, a tropical island, a fantastic carnival, or whatever else you can imagine. Regardless of its nature, the demiplane contains enough water and food to sustain its visitors, and the demiplane’s e"}, {"type": "text", "content": "nvironment", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " can’t harm its occupants. Everything else that can be interacted with there can exist only there. For example, a flower picked from a garden there disappears if it is taken outside the demiplane."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.204, 0.908, 0.296], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For each hour spent in the demiplane, a visitor regains Hit Points as if it had spent 1 Hit Point Die. Also, creatures don’t age while there, although time passes normally. Visitors can remain there for up to 200 days divided by the number of creatures present (round down)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.296, 0.91, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When the time runs out or you take a Magic action to end the effect, all visitors reappear in the location they occupied when you activated the rod or an unoccupied space nearest that location. Once used, this property can’t be used again until 10 days have passed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.395, 0.724, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rope of Climbing Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.433, 0.913, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This 60-foot length of rope can hold up to 3,000 pounds. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a Magic action to command the other end of the rope to animate and move toward a destination you choose, up to the rope’s length away from you. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet at the start of each of your subsequent turns until reaching its destination or until you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or to unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.602, 0.91, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. While knotted, the rope shortens to a 50-foot length and grants Advantage on ability checks made to climb using the rope."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.663, 0.911, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rope has AC 20, HP 20, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 Hit Point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 Hit Point. If the rope drops to 0 Hit Points, it is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.732, 0.73, 0.766], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Rope of Entanglement Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.769, 0.908, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This rope is 30 feet long. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a Magic action to command the other end to dart forward and entangle one creature you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity saving throw or have the Restrained condition. You can release the target by letting go of your end of the rope (causing the rope to coil up in the target’s space) or by using a Bonus Action to repeat the command (causing the rope to coil up in your hand)."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "242"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 242, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.49, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A target Restrained by the rope can take an action to make its choice of a DC 15 Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check. On a successful check, the target is no longer Restrained by the rope. If you’re still holding onto the rope when a target escapes from it, you can take a Reaction to command the rope to coil up in your hand; otherwise, the rope coils up in the target’s space."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.173, 0.489, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rope has AC 20, HP 20, and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 Hit Point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 Hit Point. If the rope drops to 0 Hit Points, it is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.243, 0.295, 0.258], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scarab of Protection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.26, 0.461, 0.276], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.28, 0.481, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This beetle-shaped medallion provides three benefits while it is on your person."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.115, 0.311, 0.45, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Defense.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You gain a +1 bonus to Armor Class."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.326, 0.488, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Preservation.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a Necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an Undead, you can take a Reaction to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a successful one. The scarab c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "rum", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "bles into powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.434, 0.475, 0.465], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Resistance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You have Advantage on saving throws against spells."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.472, 0.267, 0.489], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scimitar of Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.489, 0.478, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Scimitar), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.509, 0.492, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a Bonus Action on each of your turns."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.579, 0.245, 0.595], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sending Stones"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.597, 0.302, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.616, 0.489, 0.723], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sending Stones come in pairs, with each stone carved to match the other so the pairing is easily recognized. While you touch one stone, you can cast Sending from it. The target is the bearer of the other stone. If no creature bears the other stone, you know that fact as soon as you use the stone, and you don’t cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.724, 0.487, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once Sending is cast using either stone, the stones can’t be used again until the next dawn. If one of the stones in a pair is destroyed, the other one becomes nonmagical."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.793, 0.242, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sentinel Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.811, 0.299, 0.827], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.83, 0.472, 0.877], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you have Advantage on Initiative rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks. The Shield is emblazoned with a symbol of an eye."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.709, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shield, +1, +2, or +3", "styles": ["bold"]}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.069, 0.879, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2), or Very Rare (+3)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.103, 0.907, 0.151], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you have a bonus to Armor Class determined by the Shield’s rarity, in addition to the Shield’s normal bonus to AC."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.158, 0.773, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shield of Missile Attraction"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.176, 0.836, 0.192], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.195, 0.901, 0.226], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you have Resistance to damage from attacks made with Ranged weapons."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.226, 0.903, 0.334], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Curse.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This Shield is cursed. Attuning to it curses you until you are targeted by a Remove Curse spell or similar magic. Removing the Shield fails to end the curse on you. Whenever an attack with a Ranged weapon targets a creature within 10 feet of you, the curse causes you to become the target instead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.341, 0.723, 0.358], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Shield of the Cavalier"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.359, 0.872, 0.375], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.378, 0.912, 0.424], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you have a +2 bonus to Armor Class. This bonus is in addition to the Shield’s normal bonus to AC."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.523, 0.425, 0.91, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Shield has the following additional properties that you can use while holding it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.456, 0.91, 0.609], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Forceful Bash.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you take the Attack action, you can make one of the attack rolls using the Shield against a target within 5 feet of yourself. Apply your Proficiency Bonus and Strength modifier to the attack roll. On a hit, the Shield deals Force damage to the target equal to 2d6 + 2 plus your Strength modifier, and if the target is a creature, you can push it up to 10 feet directly away from yourself. If the creature is your size or smaller, you can also knock it down, giving it the Prone condition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.609, 0.915, 0.871], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Protective Field.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Reaction, when you or an ally you can see within 5 feet of you is targeted by an attack or makes a saving throw against an area of effect, you can use the Shield to create an immobile 5-foot Emanation originating from you. When the Emanation appears, any creatures or objects not fully contained within it are pushed into the nearest unoccupied spaces outside it. The attack or area of effect that triggered the Reaction has no effect on creatures and objects inside the Emanation, which lasts as long as you maintain Concentration, up to 1 minute. Nothing can pass into or out of the Emanation. A creature or object inside the Emanation can’t be damaged by attacks or effects originating from outside, nor can a creature inside the Emanation damage anything outside it. Once this property is used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "243"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 243, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.353, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Slippers of Spider Climbing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.465, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.088, 0.487, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While you wear these light shoes, you can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings, while leaving your hands free. You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. However, the slippers don’t allow you to move this way on a slippery surface, such as one covered by ice or oil."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.189, 0.245, 0.206], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sovereign Glue"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.206, 0.299, 0.222], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.226, 0.488, 0.303], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This viscous, milky-white substance can form a permanent adhesive bond between any two objects. It must be stored in a jar or flask that has been coated inside with Oil of Slipperiness. When found, a container contains 1d6 + 1 ounces."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.303, 0.49, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "One ounce of the glue can cover a 1-foot square surface. Applying an ounce of Sovereign Glue takes a Utilize action, and the applied glue takes 1 minute to set. Once it has done so, the bond it creates can be broken only by the application of Universal Solvent or Oil of Etherealness, or with a Wish spell."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.402, 0.263, 0.419], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellguard Shield"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.42, 0.45, 0.437], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor (Shield), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.437, 0.469, 0.502], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this Shield, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects, and spell attack rolls have Disadvantage against you."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.509, 0.21, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Scroll"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.527, 0.248, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Scroll, Rarity Varies"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.546, 0.488, 0.67], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A Spell Scroll bears the words of a single spell, written in a mystical cipher. If the spell is on your spell list, you can read the scroll and cast its spell without Material components. Otherwise, the scroll is unintelligible. Casting the spell by reading the scroll requires the spell’s normal casting time. Once the spell is cast, the scroll crumbles to dust. If the casting is interrupted, the scroll isn’t lost."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.669, 0.487, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the spell is on your spell list but of a higher level than you can normally cast, you make an ability check using your spellcasting ability to determine whether you cast the spell. The DC equals 10 plus the spell’s level. On a failed check, the spell disappears from the scroll with no other effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.761, 0.485, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The level of the spell on the scroll determines the spell’s saving throw DC and attack bonus, as well as the scroll’s rarity, as shown in the following table."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.105, 0.812, 0.488, 0.905], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.105, 0.812, 0.488, 0.905], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell Level</td><td>Rarity</td><td>Save DC</td><td>Attack Bonus</td></tr><tr><td>Cantrip</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Common</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>13</td><td>+5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Uncommon</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.525, 0.055, 0.909, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.525, 0.055, 0.909, 0.188], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell Level</td><td>Rarity</td><td>Save DC</td><td>Attack Bonus</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Rare</td><td>15</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>17</td><td>+9</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Very Rare</td><td>18</td><td>+10</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Legendary</td><td>19</td><td>+11</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.202, 0.906, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Copying a Scroll into a Spellbook.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Wizard spell on a Spell Scroll can be copied into a spellbook. When a spell is copied in this way, the copier must succeed on an Intelligence (Arcana) check with a DC equal to 10 plus the spell’s level. On a successful check, the spell is copied. Whether the check succeeds or fails, the Spell Scroll is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.318, 0.731, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sphere of Annihilation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.336, 0.721, 0.352], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.523, 0.355, 0.886, 0.402], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This 2-foot-diameter black sphere is a hole in the multiverse, hovering in space and stabilized by a magical field surrounding it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.402, 0.912, 0.509], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The sphere obliterates all matter it passes through and all matter that passes through it. Artifacts are the exception. Unless an Artifact is susceptible to damage from a Sphere of Annihilation, it passes through the sphere unscathed. Anything else that touches the sphere but isn’t wholly engulfed and obliterated by it takes 8d10 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.523, 0.509, 0.908, 0.647], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Controlling the Sphere.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A Sphere of Annihilation is stationary until someone takes control of it. If you are within 60 feet of a sphere, you can take a Magic action to make a DC 25 Intelligence (Arcana) check. On a successful check, you control the sphere until the start of your next turn, and if it was under another creature’s control, that creature loses control of the sphere. On a failed check, the sphere moves 10 feet toward you in a straight line."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.647, 0.899, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While in control of the sphere, you can take a Bonus Action to cause it to move in one direction of your choice, up to a number of feet equal to 5 times your Intelligence modifier (minimum 5 feet). Any creature whose space the sphere enters must succeed on a DC 19 Dexterity saving throw or be touched by it, taking 8d10 Force damage. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage is obliterated, leaving its possessions behind but no other physical remains."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.8, 0.913, 0.879], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sphere Interactions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the sphere comes into contact with a planar portal (such as that created by the Gate spell) or an extradimensional space (such as that within a Portable Hole), the GM determines randomly what happens using the following table."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "244"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 244, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.105, 0.055, 0.488, 0.178], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.105, 0.055, 0.488, 0.178], "content": "<table><tr><td>IdI00</td><td>Result</td></tr><tr><td>01-50</td><td>The sphere is destroyed.</td></tr><tr><td>51-85</td><td>The sphere moves through the portal or into the extradimensional space.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>86–00 A spatial rift sends the sphere and each crea- ture and object within 180 feet of the sphere to a random plane of existence.</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.187, 0.267, 0.205], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Charming"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.206, 0.461, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.24, 0.469, 0.273], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 10 charges. While holding the staff, you can use any of its properties:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.278, 0.475, 0.325], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cast Spell.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can expend 1 of the staff’s charges to cast Charm Person, Command, or Comprehend Languages from it using your spell save DC."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.325, 0.476, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reflect Enchantment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you succeed on a saving throw against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, you can take a Reaction to expend 1 charge from the staff and turn the spell back on its caster as if you had cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.401, 0.478, 0.479], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resist Enchantment.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If you fail a saving throw against an Enchantment spell that targets only you, you can turn your failed save into a s"}, {"type": "text", "content": "uccess", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "ful one. You can’t use this property of the staff again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.484, 0.49, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d8 + 2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff crumbles to dust and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.553, 0.213, 0.57], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Fire"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.571, 0.453, 0.603], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.606, 0.482, 0.637], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Resistance to Fire damage while you hold this staff."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.637, 0.488, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff has 10 charges. While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.105, 0.719, 0.486, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.105, 0.719, 0.486, 0.786], "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Charge</td><td colspan=\"2\">Charge</td></tr><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Cost</td><td>Spell</td><td>Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Burning Hands</td><td>I</td><td>Wall of Fire</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball</td><td>3</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.796, 0.49, 0.86], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff crumbles into cinders and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.648, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Frost"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.875, 0.1], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.103, 0.904, 0.134], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have Resistance to Cold damage while you hold this staff."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.134, 0.909, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff has 10 charges. While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.527, 0.217, 0.908, 0.285], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.527, 0.217, 0.908, 0.285], "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Charge</td><td colspan=\"2\"></td></tr><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Cost</td><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cone of Cold</td><td>5</td><td>Ice Storm</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Fog Cloud</td><td>1</td><td>Wall of Ice</td><td>4</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.293, 0.912, 0.356], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff turns to water and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.363, 0.668, 0.38], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Healing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.523, 0.38, 0.902, 0.412], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Bard, Cleric, or Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.415, 0.909, 0.494], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 10 charges. While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spellcasting ability modifier. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.527, 0.497, 0.909, 0.604], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.527, 0.497, 0.909, 0.604], "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=\"2\">Spell Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cure Wounds</td><td>I charge per spell level (maximum 4 for a level 4 spell)</td></tr><tr><td>Lesser Restoration</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Mass Cure Wounds</td><td>5</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.612, 0.904, 0.676], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff vanishes in a flash of light, lost forever."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.682, 0.658, 0.699], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Power"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.7, 0.893, 0.732], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.735, 0.906, 0.812], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 20 charges and can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class, saving throws, and spell attack rolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.812, 0.913, 0.875], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "245"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 245, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.489, 0.26], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.489, 0.26], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Cone of Cold</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball (level 5 version)</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Globe of Invulnerability</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>Hold Monster</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Levitate</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Lightning Bolt (level 5 version)</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Magic Missile</td><td>I</td></tr><tr><td>Ray of Enfeeblement</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Wall of Force</td><td>5</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.269, 0.484, 0.361], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 2d8 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff retains its +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls but loses all other properties. On a 20, the staff regains 1d8 + 2 charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.1, 0.361, 0.488, 0.562], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Retributive Strike.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface. The staff is destroyed and releases its magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot Emanation originating from itself. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion. If you fail to avoid the effect, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. Each other creature in the area makes a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes Force damage equal to 4 times the number of charges in the staff. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.568, 0.248, 0.585], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Striking"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.585, 0.38, 0.602], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.605, 0.47, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.651, 0.459, 0.713], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The staff has 10 charges. When you hit with a melee attack using it, you can expend up to 3 charges. For each charge you expend, the target takes an extra 1d6 Force damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.713, 0.477, 0.776], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.782, 0.334, 0.799], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Swarming Insects"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.8, 0.459, 0.832], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Bard, Cleric, Druid, Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.834, 0.293, 0.85], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 10 charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.851, 0.47, 0.929], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Insect Cloud.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you can take a Magic action and expend 1 charge to cause a swarm of harmless flying insects to fill a 30- foot Emanation originating from you. The insects remain for 10 minutes, making the area Heavily"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.896, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Obscured for creatures other than you. A strong wind (like that created by Gust of Wind) disperses the swarm and ends the effect."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.096, 0.91, 0.174], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC and spell attack modifier. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.527, 0.177, 0.91, 0.247], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.527, 0.177, 0.91, 0.247], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Giant Insect</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Insect Plague</td><td>5</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.255, 0.899, 0.319], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, a swarm of insects consumes and destroys the staff, then disperses."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.325, 0.678, 0.342], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of the Magi"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.342, 0.901, 0.374], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Sorcerer, Warlock, or Wizard)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.377, 0.906, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 50 charges and can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. While you hold it, you gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.44, 0.907, 0.592], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Absorption.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you have Advantage on saving throws against spells. In addition, you can take a Reaction when another creature casts a spell that targets only you. If you do, the staff absorbs the magic of the spell, canceling its effect and gaining a number of charges equal to the absorbed spell’s level. However, if doing so brings the staff’s total number of charges above 50, the staff explodes as if you activated its Retributive Strike (see below)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.592, 0.912, 0.655], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.661, 0.91, 0.922], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.525, 0.661, 0.91, 0.922], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Arcane Lock</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Conjure Elemental</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Detect Magic</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Dispel Magic</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Enlarge/Reduce</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Fireball (level 7 version)</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Flaming Sphere</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Ice Storm</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Invisibility</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Knock</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Light</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Lightning Bolt (level 7 version)</td><td>7</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "246"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 246, "blocks": [{"type": "table", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.489, 0.222], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.104, 0.055, 0.489, 0.222], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Mage Hand</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Passwall</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Plane Shift</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Protection from Evil and Good</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Telekinesis</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Wall of Fire</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Web</td><td>2</td></tr></table>"}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.229, 0.49, 0.291], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 4d6 + 2 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 20, the staff regains 1d12 + 1 charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.291, 0.488, 0.493], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Retributive Strike.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to break the staff over your knee or against a solid surface. The staff is destroyed and releases its magic in an explosion that fills a 30-foot Emanation originating from itself. You have a 50 percent chance to instantly travel to a random plane of existence, avoiding the explosion. If you fail to avoid the effect, you take Force damage equal to 16 times the number of charges in the staff. Each other creature in the area makes a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes Force damage equal to 6 times the number of charges in the staff. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.498, 0.278, 0.515], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of the Python"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.516, 0.392, 0.533], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.536, 0.486, 0.629], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Magic action, you can throw this staff so that it lands in an unoccupied space within 10 feet of you, causing the staff to become a "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Giant Constrictor Snake", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " in that space. The snake is under your control and shares your Initiative count, taking its turn immediately after yours."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.628, 0.488, 0.751], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "On your turn, you can mentally command the snake (no action required) if it is within 60 feet of you and you don’t have the Incapacitated condition. You decide what action the snake takes and where it moves during its turn, or you can issue it a general command, such as to attack your enemies or guard a location. Absent commands from you, the snake defends itself."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.751, 0.483, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As a Bonus Action, you can command the snake to revert to staff form in its current space, and you can’t use the staff’s property again for 1 hour. If the snake is reduced to 0 Hit Points, it dies and reverts to its staff form; the staff then shatters and is destroyed. If the snake reverts to staff form before losing all its Hit Points, it regains all of them."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.737, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of the Woodlands"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.523, 0.068, 0.842, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Druid)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.522, 0.088, 0.907, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 6 charges and can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. While holding it, you have a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.149, 0.913, 0.212], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the staff, you can cast one of the spells on the following table from it, using your spell save DC. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.526, 0.216, 0.91, 0.4], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.526, 0.216, 0.91, 0.4], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Animal Friendship</td><td>I</td></tr><tr><td>Awaken</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Barkskin</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Locate Animals or Plants</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Pass without Trace</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Speak with Animals</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Speak with Plants</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Wall of Thorns</td><td>6</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.522, 0.41, 0.906, 0.594], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tree Form.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to plant one end of the staff in earth in an unoccupied space and expend 1 charge to transform the staff into a healthy tree. The tree is 60 feet tall and has a 5-foot-diameter trunk, and its branches at the top spread out in a 20-foot radius. The tree appears ordinary but radiates a faint aura of Transmutation magic that can be discerned with the Detect Magic spell. While touching the tree and using a Magic action, you return the staff to its normal form. Any creature in the tree falls when the tree reverts to a staff."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.594, 0.913, 0.657], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The staff regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the staff loses its properties and becomes a nonmagical Quarterstaff."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.523, 0.663, 0.804, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Thunder and Lightning Staff, Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.701, 0.892, 0.778], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff that grants a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with it. It also has the following additional properties. Once one of these properties is used, it can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.778, 0.898, 0.824], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause the target to take an extra 2d6 Lightning damage (no action required)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.823, 0.91, 0.917], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thunder.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " When you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can cause the staff to emit a crack of thunder audible out to 300 feet (no action required). The target you hit must succeed on a DC 17 Constitution saving throw or have the Stunned condition until the end of your next turn."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "247"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 247, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.483, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thunder and Lightning.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Immediately after you hit with a melee attack using the staff, you can take a Bonus Action to use the Lightning and Thunder properties (see above) at the same time. Doing so doesn’t expend the daily use of those properties, only the use of this one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.143, 0.482, 0.234], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lightning Strike.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to cause a bolt of lightning to leap from the staff’s tip in a Line that is 5 feet wide and 120 feet long. Each creature in that Line makes a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw, taking 9d6 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.234, 0.487, 0.359], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thunderclap.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can take a Magic action to cause the staff to produce a thunderclap audible out to 600 feet. Every creature within a 60-foot Emanation originating from you makes a DC 17 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d6 Thunder damage and has the Deafened condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.365, 0.271, 0.382], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff of Withering"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.383, 0.345, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Staff, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.402, 0.478, 0.433], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This staff has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.433, 0.482, 0.557], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The staff can be wielded as a magic Quarterstaff. On a hit, it deals damage as a normal Quarterstaff, and you can expend 1 charge to deal an extra 2d10 Necrotic damage to the target and force it to make a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the target has Disadvantage for 1 hour on any ability check or saving throw that uses Strength or Constitution."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.564, 0.45, 0.597], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stone of Controlling Earth Elementals Wondrous Item, Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.1, 0.6, 0.492, 0.741], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While touching this 5-pound stone to the ground, you can take a Magic action to summon an "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Earth Elemental", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ". The elemental appears in an unoccupied space you choose within 30 feet of yourself, obeys your commands, and takes its turn immediately after you on your Initiative count. The elemental disappears after 1 hour, when it dies, or when you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. The stone can’t be used this way again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.747, 0.399, 0.764], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stone of Good Luck (Luckstone)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.765, 0.465, 0.781], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.785, 0.487, 0.817], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While this polished agate is on your person, you gain a +1 bonus to ability checks and saving throws."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.823, 0.198, 0.84], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sun Blade"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.84, 0.464, 0.876], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Longsword), Rare (Requires Attunement) This item appears to be a sword hilt."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.876, 0.47, 0.924], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Blade of Radiance.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While grasping the hilt, you can take a Bonus Action to cause a blade of pure radiance to spring into existence or make the"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.904, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "blade disappear. While the blade exists, this magic weapon functions as a Longsword with the Finesse property. If you are proficient with Longswords or Shortswords, you are proficient with the Sun Blade."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.523, 0.113, 0.898, 0.188], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this weapon, which deals Radiant damage instead of Slashing damage. When you hit an Undead with it, that target takes an extra 1d8 Radiant damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.189, 0.906, 0.297], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sunlight.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The sword’s luminous blade emits Bright Light in a 15-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 15 feet. The light is sunlight. While the blade persists, you can take a Magic action to expand or reduce its radius of Bright Light and Dim Light by 5 feet each, to a maximum of 30 feet each or a minimum of 10 feet each."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.303, 0.726, 0.32], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sword of Life Stealing"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.522, 0.321, 0.906, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.357, 0.909, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you attack a creature with this magic weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the attack roll, that target takes an extra 15 Necrotic damage if it isn’t a Construct or an Undead, and you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to the amount of Necrotic damage taken."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.456, 0.708, 0.473], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sword of Sharpness"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.474, 0.906, 0.506], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Very Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.509, 0.902, 0.555], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you attack an object with this magic weapon and hit, maximize your weapon damage dice against the target."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.555, 0.902, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you attack a creature with this weapon and roll a 20 on the d20 for the attack roll, that target takes an extra 14 Slashing damage and gains 1 Exhaustion level."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.625, 0.709, 0.641], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Sword of Wounding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.642, 0.905, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.677, 0.913, 0.785], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you hit a creature with an attack using this magic weapon, the target takes an extra 2d6 Necrotic damage and must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be unable to regain Hit Points for 1 hour. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.793, 0.736, 0.809], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talisman of Pure Good"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.81, 0.909, 0.842], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement by a Cleric or Paladin)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.846, 0.906, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This talisman is a mighty symbol of goodness. A Fiend or an Undead that touches the talisman takes 8d6 Radiant damage and takes the damage again each time it ends its turn holding or carrying the talisman."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "248"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 248, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.05, 0.475, 0.096], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Symbol.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use the talisman as a Holy Symbol. You gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls while you wear or hold it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.097, 0.49, 0.328], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pure Rebuke.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The talisman has 7 charges. While wearing or holding the talisman, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge and target one creature you can see on the ground within 120 feet of yourself. A flaming fissure opens under the target, and the target makes a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw. If the target is a Fiend or an Undead, it has Disadvantage on the save. On a failed save, the target falls into the fissure and is destroyed, leaving no remains. On a successful save, the target isn’t cast into the fissure but takes 4d6 Psychic damage from the ordeal. In either case, the fissure then closes, leaving no trace of its existence. When you expend the last charge, the talisman disperses into motes of golden light and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.335, 0.315, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talisman of the Sphere"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.352, 0.461, 0.368], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.371, 0.486, 0.496], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding or wearing this talisman, you have Advantage on any Intelligence (Arcana) check you make to control a Sphere of Annihilation. In addition, when you start your turn in control of a Sphere of Annihilation, you can take a Magic action to move it 10 feet plus a number of additional feet equal to 10 times your Intelligence modifier. This movement doesn’t have to be in a straight line."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.503, 0.333, 0.518], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talisman of Ultimate Evil"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.52, 0.461, 0.537], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.54, 0.478, 0.617], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This item symbolizes unrepentant evil. A creature that isn’t a Fiend or an Undead that touches the talisman takes 8d6 Necrotic damage and takes the damage again each time it ends its turn holding or carrying the talisman."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.617, 0.475, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Holy Symbol.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use the talisman as a Holy Symbol. You gain a +2 bonus to spell attack rolls while you wear or hold it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.663, 0.489, 0.894], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ultimate End.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The talisman has 6 charges. While wearing or holding the talisman, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge and target one creature you can see on the ground within 120 feet of yourself. A flaming fissure opens under the target, and the target makes a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw. If the target is a Celestial, it has Disadvantage on the save. On a failed save, the target falls into the fissure and is destroyed, leaving no remains. On a successful save, the target isn’t cast into the fissure but takes 4d6 Psychic damage from the ordeal. In either case, the fissure then closes, leaving no trace of its existence. When you expend the last charge, the talisman dissolves into foul-smelling slime and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.734, 0.067], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Thunderous Greatclub"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.522, 0.068, 0.909, 0.181], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Greatclub), Very Rare (Requires Attunement) While you are attuned to this magic weapon, your Strength is 20 unless your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score. The weapon deals an extra 1d8 Thunder damage to any creature it hits and an extra 3d8 Thunder damage to objects it hits that aren’t being worn or carried."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.524, 0.181, 0.841, 0.211], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The weapon has the following additional properties."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.523, 0.211, 0.909, 0.333], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Clap of Thunder.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you can strike the weapon against a hard surface to create a loud clap of thunder audible out to 300 feet. You also create a 30-foot Cone of thunderous energy. Each creature in the Cone must succeed on a DC 15 Strength saving throw or have the Prone condition. Nonmagical objects in the Cone that aren’t being worn or carried take 3d8 Thunder damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.334, 0.913, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Earthquake.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " As a Magic action, you can strike the weapon against the ground to create an intense seismic disturbance in a 50-foot-radius circle centered on the point of impact. Structures in contact with the ground in that area take 50 Bludgeoning damage, and each creature on the ground in that area must succeed on a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw or have the Prone condition. If that creature is also concentrating, it must succeed on a DC 20 Constitution saving throw, or its Concentration is broken. In addition, you can cause a 30-foot-deep, 10-foot-wide fissure to open up on the ground anywhere in the area. Any creature on a spot where the fissure opens must make a DC 20 Dexterity saving throw, falling into the fissure on a failed save or moving with the fissure’s edge on a successful one. Any structure on a spot where the fissure opens collapses into the fissure. Once you use this property, it can’t be used again until the next dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.633, 0.741, 0.667], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tome of Clear Thought Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.522, 0.67, 0.908, 0.78], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book contains memory and logic exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Intelligence increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.786, 0.833, 0.819], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tome of Leadership and Influence Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.823, 0.908, 0.902], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book contains guidelines for influencing and c"}, {"type": "text", "content": "harming", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " others, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Charisma increases by 2, to"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.028, 0.953, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "249"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 249, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.476, 0.084], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic but regains it in a century."}], "continues_prev": true}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.09, 0.321, 0.107], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tome of Understanding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.103, 0.108, 0.293, 0.124], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Very Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.127, 0.479, 0.237], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This book contains intuition and insight exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book’s contents and practicing its guidelines, your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.243, 0.338, 0.259], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Trident of Fish Command"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.26, 0.481, 0.277], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Trident), Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.28, 0.479, 0.358], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This magic weapon has 3 charges, and it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While you carry it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Dominate Beast (save DC 15) from it on a Beast that has a Swim Speed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.103, 0.366, 0.267, 0.382], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Universal Solvent"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.103, 0.383, 0.298, 0.399], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.101, 0.402, 0.481, 0.434], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This tube holds milky liquid with a strong alcohol smell. When found, a tube contains 1d6 + 1 o"}, {"type": "text", "content": "unces", "styles": ["subscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": "."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.434, 0.485, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Utilize action to pour 1 or more ounces of solvent from the tube onto a surface within reach. Each ounce instantly dissolves up to 1 square foot of adhesive it touches, including Sovereign Glue."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.518, 0.255, 0.535], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vicious Weapon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.103, 0.536, 0.373, 0.552], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Rare"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.555, 0.468, 0.604], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This magic weapon deals an extra 2d6 damage to any creature it hits. This extra damage is of the same type as the weapon’s normal damage."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.102, 0.61, 0.231, 0.626], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Vorpal Sword"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.627, 0.484, 0.659], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Glaive, Greatsword, Longsword, or Scimitar), Legendary (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.102, 0.663, 0.482, 0.709], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, the weapon ignores Resistance to Slashing damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.709, 0.489, 0.91], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "When you use this weapon to attack a creature that has at least one head and roll a 20 on the d20 for the attack roll, you cut off one of the creature’s heads. The creature dies if it can’t survive without the lost head. A creature is immune to this effect if it has Immunity to Slashing damage, if it doesn’t have or need a head, or if the GM decides that the creature is too big for its head to be cut off with this weapon. Such a creature instead takes an extra 30 Slashing damage from the hit. If the creature has Legendary Resistance, it can expend one daily use of that trait to avoid losing its head, taking the extra damage instead."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.68, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Binding"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.774, 0.086], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.089, 0.713, 0.104], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.104, 0.898, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the wand, you can cast one of the spells (save DC 17) on the following table from it. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.527, 0.171, 0.91, 0.239], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.527, 0.171, 0.91, 0.239], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Hold Monster</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Hold Person</td><td>2</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.248, 0.896, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.318, 0.77, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Enemy Detection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.336, 0.775, 0.352], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.355, 0.905, 0.478], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge. For 1 minute, you know the direction of the nearest creature Hostile to you within 60 feet, but not its distance from you. The wand can sense the presence of Hostile creatures that are Invisible, ethereal, disguised, or hidden, as well as those in plain sight. The effect ends if you stop holding the wand."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.478, 0.896, 0.541], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.547, 0.654, 0.563], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Fear"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.565, 0.774, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.524, 0.584, 0.714, 0.6], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.523, 0.6, 0.898, 0.663], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spells.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While holding the wand, you can cast one of the spells (save DC 15) on the following table from it. The table indicates how many charges you must expend to cast the spell."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.528, 0.668, 0.909, 0.735], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.528, 0.668, 0.909, 0.735], "content": "<table><tr><td>Spell</td><td>Charge Cost</td></tr><tr><td>Command (“flee” or “grovel” only)</td><td>I</td></tr><tr><td>Fear (60-foot Cone)</td><td>3</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.523, 0.744, 0.895, 0.807], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.813, 0.688, 0.83], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Fireballs"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.831, 0.886, 0.848], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.522, 0.85, 0.913, 0.93], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can expend no more than 3 charges to cast Fireball (save DC 15) from it. For 1 charge, you cast the level 3 version of the spell. You can increase the spell’s level by 1 for each additional charge you expend."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "250"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 250, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.101, 0.051, 0.473, 0.114], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.121, 0.325, 0.138], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Lightning Bolts"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.138, 0.465, 0.155], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.159, 0.478, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can expend no more than 3 charges to cast Lightning Bolt (save DC 15) from it. For 1 charge, you cast the level 3 version of the spell. You can increase the spell’s level by 1 for each additional charge you expend."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.251, 0.474, 0.313], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.32, 0.338, 0.337], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Magic Detection"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.103, 0.338, 0.237, 0.354], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.357, 0.481, 0.405], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 3 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Detect Magic from it. The wand regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.411, 0.316, 0.429], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Magic Missiles"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.429, 0.236, 0.445], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.448, 0.487, 0.526], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can expend no more than 3 charges to cast Magic Missile from it. For 1 charge, you cast the level 1 version of the spell. You can increase the spell’s level by 1 for each additional charge you expend."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.526, 0.474, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.595, 0.269, 0.612], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Paralysis"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.612, 0.465, 0.629], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.632, 0.485, 0.755], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge to cause a thin blue ray to streak from the tip toward a creature you can see within 60 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or have the Paralyzed condition for 1 minute. At the end of each of the target’s turns, it repeats the save, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.755, 0.473, 0.818], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.71, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Polymorph"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.523, 0.069, 0.837, 0.101], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Very Rare (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.104, 0.898, 0.15], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Polymorph (save DC 15) from it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.523, 0.151, 0.896, 0.213], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.22, 0.679, 0.236], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Secrets"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.238, 0.659, 0.253], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Uncommon"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.257, 0.904, 0.336], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 3 charges and regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge, and if a secret door or trap is within 60 feet of you, the wand pulses and points at the one nearest to you."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.343, 0.902, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of the War Mage, +1, +2, or +3", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Wand, Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2), or Very Rare (+3) (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster) While holding this wand, you gain a bonus to spell attack rolls determined by the wand’s rarity. In addition, you ignore Half Cover when making a spell attack roll."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.463, 0.656, 0.48], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Web"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.523, 0.482, 0.847, 0.513], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Uncommon (Requires Attunement by a Spellcaster)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.517, 0.898, 0.548], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast Web (save DC 13) from it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.523, 0.548, 0.896, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Regaining Charges.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The wand regains 1d6 + 1 expended charges daily at dawn. If you expend the wand’s last charge, roll 1d20. On a 1, the wand crumbles into ashes and is destroyed."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.617, 0.688, 0.633], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand of Wonder"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.634, 0.775, 0.651], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wand, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.654, 0.907, 0.823], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This wand has 7 charges. While holding it, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge while choosing a point within 120 feet of yourself. That location becomes the point of origin of a spell or other magical effect determined by rolling on the Wand of Wonder Effects table. Spells cast from the wand have a save DC of 15. If a spell’s maximum range is normally less than 120 feet, it be