ox": [0.102, 0.069, 0.488, 0.101], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon (+1), Rare (+2), or Very Rare (+3)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.104, 0.475, 0.152], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have a bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. The bonus is determined by the weapon’s rarity."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.158, 0.291, 0.176], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon of Warning"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.176, 0.489, 0.207], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Weapon (Any Simple or Martial), Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.211, 0.488, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "As long as this weapon is within your reach and you are attuned to it, you and allies within 30 feet of you gain the following benefits."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.257, 0.483, 0.318], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alarm.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The weapon magically awakens each subject who is sleeping naturally when combat begins. This benefit doesn’t wake a subject from magically induced sleep."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.319, 0.49, 0.351], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Supernatural Readiness.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Each subject has Advantage on its Initiative rolls."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.357, 0.299, 0.374], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Well of Many Worlds"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.103, 0.375, 0.299, 0.391], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Legendary"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.394, 0.478, 0.44], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This fine black cloth, soft as silk, is folded up to the dimensions of a handkerchief. It unfolds into a circular sheet 6 feet in diameter."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.44, 0.482, 0.578], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "You can take a Magic action to unfold the Well of Many Worlds and place it on a solid surface, whereupon it forms a two-way, 6-foot-diameter, circular portal to another world or plane of existence. Each time the item opens a portal, the GM decides where it leads. The portal remains open until a creature within 5 feet of it takes a Magic action to close it by taking hold of the edges of the cloth and folding it up."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.578, 0.485, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Once the Well of Many Worlds has opened a portal, it can’t do so again for 1d8 hours."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.618, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wind Fan"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.524, 0.069, 0.724, 0.085], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.089, 0.901, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While holding this fan, you can cast Gust of Wind (save DC 13) from it. Each subsequent time the fan is used before the next dawn, it has a cumulative 20 percent chance of not working; if the fan fails to work, it tears into useless, nonmagical tatters."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.66, 0.191], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Winged Boots"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.191, 0.886, 0.208], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Uncommon (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.522, 0.211, 0.895, 0.305], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These boots have 4 charges and regain 1d4 expended charges daily at dawn. While wearing the boots, you can take a Magic action to expend 1 charge, gaining a Fly Speed of 30 feet for 1 hour. If you are flying when the duration expires, you descend at a rate of 30 feet per round until you land."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.311, 0.669, 0.329], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wings of Flying"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.329, 0.841, 0.345], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.348, 0.909, 0.458], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While wearing this cloak, you can take a Magic action to turn the cloak into a pair of wings on your back. The wings lasts for 1 hour or until you end the effect early as a Magic action. The wings give you a Fly Speed of 60 feet. If you are aloft when the wings disappear, you fall. When the wings disappear, you can’t use them again for 1d12 hours."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.061, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "253"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.103, 0.952, 0.374, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 253, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.202, 0.051, 0.392, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monsters"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.095, 0.395, 0.116], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Stat Block Overview"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.12, 0.472, 0.167], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster has a stat block that contains the rules necessary to use it in the game. Stat blocks are divided into the following parts:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.173, 0.481, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Name and General Details.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The name of the monster is followed by its size, creature type (along with any descriptive tags), and alignment."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.219, 0.487, 0.249], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Combat Highlights.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Armor Class, Hit Points, Speed, and Initiative are provided here."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.25, 0.471, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " A monster’s ability scores, ability modifiers, and saving throws are listed here."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.28, 0.487, 0.357], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Other Details.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The monster’s Senses, Languages, and CR entries appear here. Additional details appear in some monsters, such as skill proficiencies, Resistances, Immunities, and Gear. If a monster lacks those details, entries for them don’t appear."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.357, 0.488, 0.388], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Monster characteristics that are active at all times or during certain situations appear here."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.102, 0.388, 0.476, 0.418], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The monster can take the actions here in addition to those in “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.418, 0.478, 0.449], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This section provides a monster’s Bonus Actions, if any."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.102, 0.449, 0.487, 0.481], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reactions and Legendary Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " These sections provide Reactions and Legendary Actions, if any."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.49, 0.393, 0.511], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Parts of a Stat Block"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.1, 0.514, 0.489, 0.547], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The rules for a stat block are detailed in “Rules Glossary” and in this section."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.554, 0.152, 0.571], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Size"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.577, 0.473, 0.64], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster is Tiny, Small, Medium, Large, Huge, or Gargantuan. If size options are presented, you choose the creature’s size from those options. See “Playing the Game” for information on size."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.102, 0.646, 0.263, 0.665], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Creature Type"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.669, 0.482, 0.731], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Each monster has a tag that identifies the type of creature it is. Certain spells, magic items, class features, and other effects in the game interact in special ways with creatures of a particular type."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.102, 0.731, 0.475, 0.763], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The game includes the following creature types, which have no rules of their own:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.768, 0.475, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aberrations", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are utterly alien beings, such as aboleths and cloakers."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.102, 0.8, 0.484, 0.83], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beasts", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are non-Humanoid natural creatures, like horses and wolves, as well as most giant animals."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.102, 0.831, 0.49, 0.861], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Celestials", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are magical creatures, such as angels and pegasi, with ties to the Upper Planes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.102, 0.861, 0.488, 0.891], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Constructs", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are magically created creatures such as homunculi and shield guardians."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.892, 0.48, 0.923], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dragons", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are scaly beings of ancient origin, such as red dragons and wyverns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.524, 0.05, 0.898, 0.081], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Elementals", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are beings from the Elemental Planes, such as efreet and water elementals."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.524, 0.081, 0.897, 0.112], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fey", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are creatures tied to the Feywild or the forces of nature, such as dryads and goblins."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.112, 0.863, 0.142], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Fiends", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are creatures tied to terrifying Lower Planes, such as balors and hell hounds."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.524, 0.143, 0.908, 0.173], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Giants", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are towering beings with humanlike shapes, like fire giants and trolls."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.173, 0.907, 0.219], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Humanoids", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are people defined by their roles and professions, such as mages, pirates, and warriors. They include members of varied species."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.219, 0.879, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monstrosities", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are unnatural creatures with strange origins, such as mimics and owlbears."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.25, 0.879, 0.28], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Oozes", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are gelatinous creatures, including black puddings and gelatinous cubes."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.525, 0.28, 0.91, 0.311], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Plants", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are sentient vegetation and fungal monsters, such as shambling mounds and treants."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.311, 0.898, 0.343], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Undead", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " are spirits and the reanimated dead, such as ghosts, vampires, and zombies."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.524, 0.349, 0.679, 0.366], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Descriptive Tags"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.522, 0.367, 0.912, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster might have one or more tags in parentheses following its type. Such tags provide additional categorization and have no rules of their own, but certain game effects might refer to them."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.436, 0.641, 0.456], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Alignment"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.521, 0.459, 0.912, 0.582], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The alignment specified in a monster’s stat block is a default suggestion of how to roleplay the monster, inspired by its traditional role in the game or realworld folklore. Change a monster’s alignment to suit your storytelling needs. The Neutral alignment, in particular, is an invitation for you to consider whether an individual leans toward one of the other alignments."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.523, 0.582, 0.879, 0.614], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“Character Creation” describes the nine alignments and unaligned creatures."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 37, "bbox": [0.523, 0.621, 0.665, 0.639], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Armor Class"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 38, "bbox": [0.522, 0.644, 0.907, 0.692], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s Armor Class (AC) includes its natural armor, Dexterity, gear, and other defenses. See “Playing the Game” for information on Armor Class."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 39, "bbox": [0.523, 0.697, 0.623, 0.716], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 40, "bbox": [0.521, 0.721, 0.909, 0.845], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Initiative entry specifies the monster’s Initiative modifier followed by the monster’s Initiative score in parentheses. Use the modifier when you roll to determine a monster’s Initiative. A monster’s Initiative modifier is typically equal to its Dexterity modifier, but some monsters have additional modifiers, such as Proficiency Bonus, applied to that number."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 41, "bbox": [0.521, 0.845, 0.908, 0.907], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If you don’t want to roll a monster’s Initiative, use the Initiative score as the monster’s Initiative in combat. Initiative is further detailed in “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 42, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "254"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 43, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 254, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.215, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.075, 0.491, 0.182], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s Hit Points are presented as a number followed by parentheses, where the monster’s Hit Point Dice are provided, along with any contribution from its Constitution. Either use the number for the monster’s Hit Points or roll the die expression in parentheses to determine the monster’s Hit Points randomly; don’t use both."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.182, 0.489, 0.229], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s size typically determines the die used to calculate its Hit Points, as shown in the Hit Dice by Size table."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.242, 0.241, 0.257], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit Dice by Size"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "table", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.26, 0.488, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.104, 0.26, 0.488, 0.392], "content": "<table><tr><td>Monster Size</td><td>Hit Die</td><td>Average HP per Die</td></tr><tr><td>Tiny</td><td>d4</td><td>2/2</td></tr><tr><td>Small</td><td>d6</td><td>3/2</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>d8</td><td>41/2</td></tr><tr><td>Large</td><td>d10</td><td>51/2</td></tr><tr><td>Huge</td><td>d12</td><td>6/2</td></tr><tr><td>Gargantuan</td><td>d20</td><td>10/2</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.401, 0.479, 0.478], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s Constitution modifier is multiplied by the number of Hit Dice it possesses, and the result is added to its Hit Points. For example, if a monster has a Constitution of 12 (+1 modifier) and 2d8 Hit Dice, it has 2d8 + 2 Hit Points (average 11)."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.115, 0.478, 0.468, 0.495], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "For more on Hit Points, see “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.501, 0.174, 0.52], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.524, 0.487, 0.589], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Speed entry specifies a monster’s Speed. Some monsters have one or more of the following speeds: Burrow, Climb, Fly, Swim. Rules for Speed and these specials speeds appear in “Rules Glossary.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.594, 0.256, 0.613], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ability Scores"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.617, 0.475, 0.681], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Every monster has six ability scores along with corresponding ability score modifiers and saving throw modifiers. For more information on ability scores and saving throws, see “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.686, 0.163, 0.704], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skills"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.71, 0.488, 0.82], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Skills entry specifies a monster’s skill proficiencies, if any. For example, a monster that is very perceptive and stealthy might have bonuses to Wisdom (Perception) and Dexterity (Stealth) checks. A skill bonus is the sum of a monster’s relevant ability modifier and its Proficiency Bonus. Other modifiers might apply."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.102, 0.825, 0.432, 0.844], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Resistances and Vulnerabilities"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.849, 0.482, 0.896], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "These entries list a monster’s Resistances and Vulnerabilities, if any. See “Playing the Game” for more information."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.539, 0.057, 0.724, 0.073], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Running a Monster"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.538, 0.076, 0.883, 0.108], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "To ensure a monster acts in accordance with its Challenge Rating, follow these rules during combat:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.539, 0.111, 0.89, 0.203], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Special Abilities.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster has a special ability that deals a lot of damage but has a limited number of uses, such as a recharging breath weapon or a spell it can cast only once per day, have it use that special ability as quickly and as often as possible."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.539, 0.203, 0.889, 0.25], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster has Multiattack, have it use Multiattack on any of its turns in which it’s not using one of its more powerful abilities."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.539, 0.25, 0.895, 0.312], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Actions, Reactions, Legendary Actions.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the monster has Bonus Actions, Reactions, or Legendary Actions in its stat block, make sure it uses them as often as it can."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.328, 0.648, 0.347], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Immunities"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.522, 0.351, 0.906, 0.415], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This entry lists the monster’s Immunities, if any. If the monster has damage and condition Immunities, the damage types are listed before the conditions. See “Playing the Game” for details."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.524, 0.421, 0.584, 0.439], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Gear"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.521, 0.445, 0.908, 0.583], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monsters have proficiency with their equipment. If a monster has equipment that can be given away or retrieved, the items are listed in the Gear entry. The monster’s stat block might include special flourishes that happen when the monster uses an item, and the stat block might ignore the rules in “Equipment” for that item. When used by someone else, a retrievable item uses its “Equipment” rules, ignoring any special flourishes in the stat block."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.583, 0.9, 0.645], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Gear entry doesn’t necessarily list all of a monster’s equipment. For example, a monster that wears clothes is assumed to be dressed appropriately, and those clothes aren’t in this entry."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.645, 0.91, 0.692], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipment mentioned outside the Gear entry is considered to be supernatural or highly specialized, and it is unusable when the monster is defeated."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.523, 0.698, 0.828, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Ammunition and Ranged Attacks"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.716, 0.898, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster that requires ammunition to make ranged attacks carries the necessary ammunition."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.754, 0.905, 0.849], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Equipping a Monster with Other Items", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " You may equip monsters with additional gear however you like, using the items in “Equipment” for inspiration. You decide how much of a monster’s equipment is recoverable after the creature is slain and whether any of that equipment is still usable."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.849, 0.906, 0.927], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Beware of giving a monster combat-oriented magic items, since those might alter the monster’s Challenge Rating. If you do give a monster a magic item, the monster can have Attunement with magic items as noted in “Equipment.” A monster with"}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "255"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 255, "blocks": [{"type": "text", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.1, 0.05, 0.462, 0.082], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "a class tag after its creature type is considered a member of that class for Attunement purposes."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.102, 0.088, 0.18, 0.106], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.101, 0.111, 0.481, 0.175], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The Senses entry specifies a monster’s Passive Perception score, as well as any special senses the monster possesses. Passive Perception and special senses are described in “Rules Glossary.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.182, 0.218, 0.201], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Languages"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.101, 0.205, 0.484, 0.284], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "This entry lists languages that the monster can use to communicate. Sometimes a monster can understand a language but can’t communicate with it, which is noted in its entry. “None” indicates that a creature doesn’t comprehend any language."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.102, 0.29, 0.197, 0.307], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathy"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.307, 0.484, 0.37], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Telepathy is a magical ability that allows a creature to communicate mentally with another creature within a specified range. See “Rules Glossary” for more information."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.376, 0.287, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Challenge Rating"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.399, 0.475, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Challenge Rating is defined in “Rules Glossary,” while guidance on using CR to plan potential combat encounters is in “Gameplay Toolbox.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.454, 0.27, 0.471], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Experience Points"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.472, 0.466, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The number of Experience Points (XP) a monster is worth is based on its CR, as detailed in the Experience Points by Challenge Rating table. XP is awarded for defeating the monster in combat or otherwise neutralizing it."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.101, 0.549, 0.489, 0.596], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Unless a rule says otherwise, a monster summoned by a spell or another magical ability is worth the XP noted in its stat block."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.104, 0.625, 0.489, 0.912], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.102, 0.607, 0.426, 0.624], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Experience Points by Challenge Rating"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.104, 0.625, 0.489, 0.912], "content": "<table><tr><td>CR</td><td>XP</td><td>CR</td><td>XP</td></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>0 or 10</td><td>14</td><td>11,500</td></tr><tr><td>1/8</td><td>25</td><td>15</td><td>13,000</td></tr><tr><td>1/4</td><td>50</td><td>16</td><td>15,000</td></tr><tr><td>1/2</td><td>100</td><td>17</td><td>18,000</td></tr><tr><td>I</td><td>200</td><td>18</td><td>20,000</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>450</td><td>19</td><td>22,000</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>700</td><td>20</td><td>25,000</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1,100</td><td>21</td><td>33,000</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>1,800</td><td>22</td><td>41,000</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2,300</td><td>23</td><td>50,000</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>2,900</td><td>24</td><td>62,000</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>3,900</td><td>25</td><td>75,000</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>5,000</td><td>26</td><td>90,000</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>5,900</td><td>27</td><td>105,000</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.525, 0.054, 0.91, 0.13], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.525, 0.054, 0.91, 0.13], "content": "<table><tr><td>CR</td><td>XP</td><td>CR</td><td>XP</td></tr><tr><td>ⅡI</td><td>7,200</td><td>28</td><td>120,000</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>8,400</td><td>29</td><td>135,000</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>10,000</td><td>30</td><td>155,000</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.524, 0.142, 0.691, 0.159], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Proficiency Bonus"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.521, 0.159, 0.898, 0.238], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s Proficiency Bonus (PB) is determined by its CR, as shown in the Proficiency Bonus by Challenge Rating table, and is reflected in saving t"}, {"type": "text", "content": "hrows", "styles": ["superscript"]}, {"type": "text", "content": ", skills, and other statistics where the monster’s exceptional aptitude is a factor."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.267, 0.909, 0.361], "content": [{"type": "table_caption", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.524, 0.249, 0.847, 0.265], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Proficiency Bonus by Challenge Rating"}]}, {"type": "table_body", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.525, 0.267, 0.909, 0.361], "content": "<table><tr><td>CR</td><td>PB</td><td>CR</td><td>PB</td></tr><tr><td>0-4</td><td>+2</td><td>17-20</td><td>+6</td></tr><tr><td>5-8</td><td>+3</td><td>21-24</td><td>+7</td></tr><tr><td>9-12</td><td>+4</td><td>25-28</td><td>+8</td></tr><tr><td>13-16</td><td>+5</td><td>29-30</td><td>+9</td></tr></table>"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.373, 0.592, 0.392], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.522, 0.397, 0.89, 0.43], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s traits, if any, are features that are active at all times or in certain situations."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.524, 0.436, 0.611, 0.454], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.459, 0.904, 0.507], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster can take the actions in this section or take one of the actions available to all creatures, as described in “Playing the Game.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.523, 0.514, 0.678, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Attack Notation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.521, 0.531, 0.911, 0.638], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The entry for a monster’s attack identifies whether the attack is a melee or a ranged attack and then provides the attack roll’s bonus, its reach or range, and what happens on a hit. An attack is against one target unless its entry says otherwise. For details on different kinds of attacks, see “Playing the Game” and “Spells.”"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.522, 0.639, 0.912, 0.685], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Any damage dealt or other effects that occur as a result of an attack hitting a target are described after the “Hit:” notation."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.685, 0.898, 0.715], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Miss.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If an attack has an effect that occurs on a miss, that information follows the “Miss:” notation."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.522, 0.715, 0.902, 0.762], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Hit or Miss.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If an attack has an effect that occurs regardless of whether it hits or misses its target, that information follows the “Hit or Miss:” notation."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.524, 0.769, 0.798, 0.786], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Saving Throw Effect Notation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.522, 0.787, 0.907, 0.863], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If an effect forces a saving throw, the effect identifies the kind of save required and then provides the save’s DC, a description of which creatures make the save, and an explanation of what happens on a failed or successful save."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.522, 0.863, 0.907, 0.926], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "“Half damage only” on a successful save means the target takes half as much damage (round down) as targets that fail the save, while also ignoring all other parts of the effect."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "256"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.969], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 256, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.102, 0.051, 0.27, 0.068], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Damage Notation"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.101, 0.069, 0.49, 0.147], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A stat block usually provides both a number and a die expression for each instance of damage. For example, an attack might deal 4 (1d4 + 2) damage on a hit. You decide whether to use the number or the die expression in parentheses; don’t use both."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.102, 0.154, 0.212, 0.169], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.101, 0.171, 0.478, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some creatures can make more than one attack when they take the Attack action. Such creatures have the Multiattack entry in the “Actions” section of their stat block. This entry details the attacks a creature can make, as well as any additional abilities it can use, as part of the Attack action."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.102, 0.271, 0.215, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spellcasting"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.101, 0.289, 0.487, 0.396], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a monster can cast any spells, its stat block lists the spells and provides the monster’s spellcasting ability, spell save DC (if any spells require a saving throw), and spell attack bonus (if any spells require an attack roll). Unless noted otherwise, a spell of level 1 or higher is always cast at its lowest possible level and can’t be cast at a higher level."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.101, 0.396, 0.488, 0.457], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "A monster’s spell can have special rules or restrictions. For example, a green hag can cast the Invisibility spell, but the spell has a “self only” restriction, which means the spell affects only the hag."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.101, 0.457, 0.488, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Spell Components.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The Spellcasting trait notes whether the monster’s spellcasting ignores the need for certain spell components. If any spell components are required, describe the monster’s use of Verbal, Somatic, or Material components to signal to characters that it is casting a spell. A monster that requires Material components has them."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.101, 0.565, 0.488, 0.673], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Casting Times of 1+ Minutes.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If a spell has a casting time of 1 minute or more yet is listed in a spellcasting action, the monster doesn’t cast the spell in just one action unless the action’s description states otherwise; the monster must take the Magic action on each of its turns and maintain Concentration to cast the spell, as described in “Rules Glossary.”"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.679, 0.25, 0.697], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Bonus Action"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.703, 0.485, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If a monster has Bonus Action options, they are listed in this section. See “Playing the Game” for details on Bonus Actions."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.524, 0.051, 0.633, 0.069], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Reactions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.522, 0.075, 0.91, 0.122], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the monster has Reaction options, those are listed in this section along with their triggers. See “Playing the Game” for details on Reactions."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.524, 0.129, 0.728, 0.149], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Legendary Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.522, 0.152, 0.905, 0.275], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "If the monster has Legendary Action options, those are listed in this section. A Legendary Action is an action that a monster can take immediately after another creature’s turn. Only one of these actions can be taken at a time and only after another creature’s turn ends. The monster can’t take a Legendary Action if it has the Incapacitated condition or is otherwise unable to take actions."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.522, 0.275, 0.903, 0.353], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The monster has a limited number of Legendary Action uses, and that number is specified in the stat block. The monster expends one use whenever it takes a Legendary Action, and it regains all expended uses at the start of each of its turns."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.524, 0.359, 0.682, 0.378], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Limited Usage"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.522, 0.383, 0.898, 0.431], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Some parts of a stat block have restrictions on the number of times they can be used. Here are the most common ways that usage is limited:"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.523, 0.435, 0.904, 0.543], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "X/Day.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This notation means the stat block part can be used a certain number of times (represented by X) and that a monster must finish a Long Rest to regain expended uses. For example, a Reaction that includes “1/Day” means the Reaction can be taken once and that the monster must finish a Long Rest to take it again."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.524, 0.543, 0.908, 0.712], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Recharge X–Y.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This notation means a monster can use the stat block part once. At the start of each of the monster’s turns, roll 1d6. If the roll is within the number range given in the notation (represented by X–Y), the monster regains the use of that part, which also recharges when the monster finishes a Short or Long Rest. For example, “Recharge 5–6” in an action means a monster can take the action once. Then, at the start of each of the monster’s turns, it regains the use of that action if it rolls a 5 or 6 on 1d6."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.524, 0.712, 0.892, 0.774], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Recharge after a Short or Long Rest.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " This notation means the monster can use the stat block part once and must then finish a Short or Long Rest to use it again."}]}, {"type": "page_number", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.028, 0.952, 0.062, 0.967], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "257"}]}, {"type": "footer", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.102, 0.952, 0.375, 0.968], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "System Reference Document 5.2.1"}]}]}, {"page_idx": 257, "blocks": [{"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 0, "bbox": [0.153, 0.05, 0.441, 0.08], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Monsters A–Z"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 1, "bbox": [0.103, 0.094, 0.219, 0.117], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aboleth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 2, "bbox": [0.104, 0.124, 0.195, 0.143], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Aboleth"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 3, "bbox": [0.102, 0.147, 0.294, 0.163], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Aberration, Lawful Evil"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 4, "bbox": [0.103, 0.168, 0.148, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 17"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 5, "bbox": [0.277, 0.169, 0.39, 0.183], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " +7 (17)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 6, "bbox": [0.102, 0.184, 0.245, 0.198], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 150 (20d10 + 40)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 7, "bbox": [0.102, 0.2, 0.268, 0.215], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 ft., Swim 40 ft."}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.217, 0.487, 0.264], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 8, "bbox": [0.104, 0.217, 0.487, 0.264], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 21 +5 +5</td><td>Dex 9 -1 +3</td><td>Con15 +2 +6</td></tr><tr><td>Int 18 +4 +8</td><td>Wis 15 +2 +6</td><td>Cha18 +4 +4</td></tr></tbody></table>"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 9, "bbox": [0.102, 0.272, 0.33, 0.288], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Skills", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " History +12, Perception +10"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 10, "bbox": [0.101, 0.285, 0.422, 0.335], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Senses", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Darkvision 120 ft.; Passive Perception 20 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Languages", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Deep Speech; telepathy 120 ft. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "CR", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 (XP 5,900, or 7,200 in lair; PB +4)"}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 11, "bbox": [0.102, 0.343, 0.156, 0.36], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Traits"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 12, "bbox": [0.101, 0.364, 0.465, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Amphibious.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The aboleth can breathe air and water."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 13, "bbox": [0.101, 0.385, 0.463, 0.448], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Eldritch Restoration.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If destroyed, the aboleth gains a new body in 5d10 days, reviving with all its Hit Points in the Far Realm or another location chosen by the GM."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 14, "bbox": [0.101, 0.452, 0.471, 0.499], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Legendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Lair).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the aboleth fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 15, "bbox": [0.101, 0.503, 0.488, 0.611], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Mucus Cloud.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " While underwater, the aboleth is surrounded by mucus. Constitution Saving Throw: DC 14, each creature in a 5-foot Emanation originating from the aboleth at the end of the aboleth’s turn. Failure: The target is cursed. Until the curse ends, the target’s skin becomes slimy, the target can breathe air and water, and it can’t regain Hit Points unless it is underwater."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 16, "bbox": [0.101, 0.611, 0.481, 0.674], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "While the cursed creature is outside a body of water, the creature takes 6 (1d12) Acid damage at the end of every 10 minutes unless moisture is applied to its skin before those minutes have passed."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 17, "bbox": [0.101, 0.678, 0.485, 0.726], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Probing Telepathy.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If a creature the aboleth can see communicates telepathically with the aboleth, the aboleth learns the creature’s greatest desires."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 18, "bbox": [0.102, 0.733, 0.172, 0.749], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 19, "bbox": [0.101, 0.753, 0.485, 0.8], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Multiattack.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The aboleth makes two Tentacle attacks and uses either Consume Memories or Dominate Mind if available."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 20, "bbox": [0.101, 0.805, 0.476, 0.868], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Tentacle.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Melee Attack Roll: +9, reach 15 ft. Hit: 12 (2d6 + 5) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the Grappled condition (escape DC 14) from one of four tentacles."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 21, "bbox": [0.101, 0.872, 0.487, 0.92], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Consume Memories.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Intelligence Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature within 30 feet that is Charmed or Grappled by the aboleth. Failure: 10 (3d6) Psychic damage."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 22, "bbox": [0.522, 0.05, 0.902, 0.097], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Success: Half damage. Failure or Success: The aboleth gains the target’s memories if the target is a Humanoid and is reduced to 0 Hit Points by this action."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 23, "bbox": [0.522, 0.102, 0.904, 0.24], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Dominate Mind (2/Day).", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " Wisdom Saving Throw: DC 16, one creature the aboleth can see within 30 feet. Failure: The target has the Charmed condition until the aboleth dies or is on a different plane of existence from the target. While Charmed, the target acts as an ally to the aboleth and is under its control while within 60 feet of it. In addition, the aboleth and the target can communicate telepathically with each other over any distance."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 24, "bbox": [0.522, 0.24, 0.906, 0.302], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "The target repeats the save whenever it takes damage as well as after every 24 hours it spends at least 1 mile away from the aboleth, ending the effect on itself on a success."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 25, "bbox": [0.524, 0.309, 0.684, 0.326], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Legendary Actions"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 26, "bbox": [0.522, 0.328, 0.898, 0.381], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Legendary Action Uses: 3 (4 in Lair). Immediately after another creature’s turn, the aboleth can expend a use to take one of the following actions. The aboleth regains all expended uses at the start of each of its turns."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 27, "bbox": [0.524, 0.385, 0.841, 0.401], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Lash.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " The aboleth makes one Tentacle attack."}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 28, "bbox": [0.522, 0.406, 0.904, 0.453], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Psychic Drain.", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " If the aboleth has at least one creature Charmed or Grappled, it uses Consume Memories and regains 5 (1d10) Hit Points."}]}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 29, "bbox": [0.524, 0.461, 0.72, 0.484], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Air Elemental"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "paragraph_title", "index": 30, "bbox": [0.525, 0.491, 0.679, 0.51], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Air Elemental"}], "level": 2}, {"type": "text", "index": 31, "bbox": [0.524, 0.514, 0.69, 0.53], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Large Elemental, Neutral"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 32, "bbox": [0.525, 0.535, 0.57, 0.549], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "AC", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 15"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 33, "bbox": [0.698, 0.535, 0.812, 0.55], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Initiative", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " +5 (15)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 34, "bbox": [0.524, 0.55, 0.657, 0.565], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "HP", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 90 (12d10 + 24)"}]}, {"type": "text", "index": 35, "bbox": [0.524, 0.566, 0.724, 0.581], "content": [{"type": "text", "content": "Speed", "styles": ["bold"]}, {"type": "text", "content": " 10 ft., Fly 90 ft. (hover)"}]}, {"type": "table", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.525, 0.583, 0.91, 0.63], "content": [{"type": "table_body", "index": 36, "bbox": [0.525, 0.583, 0.91, 0.63], "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td><td>MOD SAVE</td></tr><tr><td>Str 14 +2 +2</td><td>De